// Content for The Talks, Age by Age (node g64, Parent Layer, Chapter 8): NEW v2 build to GDD 64
// (mechanic-embodying), the KEYSTONE of the Parent Layer and the hinge of the generational loop: a parent guided
// here becomes the trusted adult the kids' journey always assumed. The core reframe: it isn't one dreaded "talk",
// it's many small, age-right conversations, and you can do them. 84 researched, India-grounded scenarios across
// how-to-talk → early-years → middle-years → the-teen-talks → facts-and-values → tools-and-help, each encoded as
// one of the shared v2 play actions (role-play / strike-rewrite / branch / sort / reflect / match / spot): no
// binary "tap the right card". Lead: role-play (say it), strike-rewrite (bust the myth), branch (your move). Six
// modes: how to talk (start early, stay calm, answer "I don't know" honestly, be the askable open door), the early
// years (correct body-part names (which protect against abuse and aid disclosure) body safety & consent basics,
// no body secrets, where-babies-come-from simply, consent in greetings), the middle years (prepare for puberty
// BEFORE it starts, periods and wet dreams for ALL children, online basics & reporting scary content), the teen
// talks (consent, online & porn-literacy against the manosphere, respect in relationships, staying askable through
// the eye-rolls), facts and your values (give honest facts AND share your values rather than choosing between
// them: silence cedes the field to peers and the algorithm), tools & help (age-by-age guides, ready scripts, the
// open-door habit, and routing any child-safety concern to Be the Safe Adult g69). Protective and evidence-based:
// correct names and talking make children SAFER, not more at risk; age-appropriate, accurate, non-explicit
// guidance is expert-reviewed; respects family values while keeping facts honest and NEVER shames a parent for not
// knowing. Builds on (and mirrors) the kids' journey from My Body, My Rules (g02); around it sit the
// positive-parenting pillars (g65-g69). India: these conversations are too often never had, and silence and "log
// kya kahenge" leave the internet and the manosphere to teach instead: the node gently breaks the cycle with
// culturally-aware scripts, mindful of grandparents and joint families. gameId "the-talks".
import type { V2GameConfig, Scenario } from "./v2-schema";

const SCENARIOS: Scenario[] = [
  {"id":"tk-001","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"There's one big, dreaded 'talk' you have to get perfectly right.\"","myth":{"un":"There's one big, dreaded 'talk' you have to get perfectly right.","re":"It isn't one talk; it's many small, age-right conversations over years, and you can absolutely do those.","why":"Lots of small chats beat one terrifying lecture."},"relearn":"It's not one big talk; it's many small, age-right conversations over time, and you can do those.","persona":"Vikram","source":"many small talks"},
  {"id":"tk-002","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If I talk to my child about bodies and relationships, I'll encourage them too early.\"","myth":{"un":"If I talk to my child about bodies and relationships, I'll encourage them too early.","re":"Research shows honest, age-appropriate talks lead to later, safer choices, not earlier ones; silence is the real risk.","why":"Talking protects; it doesn't push."},"relearn":"Honest, age-appropriate talks lead to later and safer choices, not earlier ones; talking protects kids.","persona":"Divya","source":"talking protects"},
  {"id":"tk-003","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"stay calm","hook":"Your seven-year-old Aarush asks why his penis gets hard sometimes. You feel a jolt of panic.","steps":[{"prompt":"He asks at breakfast, spoon halfway to his mouth. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Take a breath, and say it's normal and happens to all boys","then":"Aarush nods and goes back to his cereal. \"Okay,\" he says.","best":true},{"text":"Tell him to just finish his breakfast and stop being silly","then":"Aarush goes red and eats the rest in silence."},{"text":"Say 'Ask me later' and hurry out of the room","then":"Aarush looks puzzled, and asks the older boy next door that afternoon."},{"text":"Launch into a long, detailed biology lesson","then":"Aarush's eyes glaze over halfway, and his cereal goes soggy."}],"why":"A calm, simple answer at his level keeps you his go-to source."},{"prompt":"That evening, Aarush says an older boy told him it means something's wrong with him. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say nothing's wrong, bodies do that, and he can always ask","then":"Aarush relaxes. \"So it's like hiccups?\" he asks. You laugh and nod.","best":true},{"text":"Say only naughty boys think about things like that","then":"Aarush looks frightened, and stops asking you about it."},{"text":"Say he'll understand it all when he's a bit older, not now","then":"Aarush frowns, still worried."},{"text":"Tell him to ask the doctor about it at his next check-up","then":"Aarush nods, and spends the weeks until then worrying."}],"why":"Reassurance with the facts turns worry into curiosity."},{"prompt":"A week later, your wife says Aarush asked her the same question. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Agree together on simple, calm words you'll both use","then":"She nods. \"Good. Then he gets the same answer from both of us.\"","best":true},{"text":"Tell her to shut the topic down if he asks again","then":"She frowns. \"Then where will he take his questions?\""},{"text":"Leave it to her, since she's better at these talks","then":"She sighs, and answers his next few questions on her own."},{"text":"Say you've handled it already, so she needn't bother","then":"She lets it go. Aarush hears two different answers anyway."}],"why":"Two calm, matching answers double his safe doors."},{"prompt":"Months later, Aarush brings you another body question, about hair growing. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Answer simply and calmly, and thank him for asking you","then":"Aarush grins. \"I've got another one,\" he says.","best":true},{"text":"Sigh, 'Again with these questions?'","then":"Aarush shrugs. \"Never mind,\" he says, and walks off."},{"text":"Hand him a book, and leave him to read it alone","then":"Aarush flips through it, alone with his questions."},{"text":"Answer quickly, then change the subject to the cricket score","then":"Aarush gets half an answer and a cricket score."}],"why":"Every calm answer makes the next, harder question easier to ask."}],"debrief":"Meet a child's question calmly and answer simply at their level, rather than shutting it down.","relearn":"Answer kids' body questions calmly and simply; shutting them down just sends them elsewhere."},
  {"id":"tk-004","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If I don't know the answer, I shouldn't say anything at all.\"","myth":{"un":"If I don't know the answer, I shouldn't say anything at all.","re":"'I don't know, let's find out together' is a great answer; it models honesty and keeps the door open.","why":"Not-knowing handled well builds trust."},"relearn":"'I don't know, let's find out together' is a great answer; you don't need every answer ready.","persona":"Divya","source":"I don't know"},
  {"id":"tk-005","type":"match","persona":"any","source":"talk skills","hook":"Match each conversation skill to what it does.","pairs":[{"left":"Staying calm and unshocked","right":"Keeps your child willing to ask"},{"left":"Answering at their level","right":"Makes the answer land"},{"left":"Saying 'great question'","right":"Rewards them for coming to you"},{"left":"'Let's find out together'","right":"Models honesty when you don't know"},{"left":"Many small chats over years","right":"Beats one dreaded big talk"}],"relearn":"Staying calm, answering at their level and welcoming questions keep your child coming to you.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-006","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: the aim isn't a perfect speech; it's being the askable parent your child keeps coming back to. Sit right?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Sits right","Be askable","Keep the door open"],"affirm":"The goal isn't a flawless talk but being the askable, open-door parent a child keeps returning to.","relearn":"The aim is to be the askable parent your child keeps coming back to, not to give a perfect speech.","persona":"any","source":"be askable"},
  {"id":"tk-007","type":"spot","persona":"any","source":"keep them asking","hook":"Spot the two reactions that send a child away instead of keeping them asking.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Calm, warm, honest answers","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Shock, anger or 'you're too young'","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Welcoming even awkward questions","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"A shaming 'why would you ask that?'","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"'I'm glad you came to me'","trick":false}],"why":"Shock or 'too young' and a shaming 'why ask that' send a child away; calm, welcoming answers keep them asking.","relearn":"Keep a child asking by answering calmly and welcoming even awkward questions, not by shaming them.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-008","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"branch","persona":"Divya","source":"never too late","hook":"Your daughter Sana is eight, and you've never talked about bodies or safety. It feels too late to start.","steps":[{"prompt":"A school note says a body-safety class is coming next week. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Start today, with one small, simple chat before the class","then":"Sana is surprised, then curious. \"Why now?\" she asks.","best":true},{"text":"Decide the school class will cover everything she needs","then":"The class happens. Sana comes home with questions, unsure who to ask."},{"text":"Decide the window has closed, and stay quiet","then":"The week passes in silence, and the distance feels a little wider."},{"text":"Plan one big, perfect talk for her ninth birthday","then":"The date gets closer, and so does your dread. Nothing is said yet."}],"why":"It's never too late, and a small chat now opens the door at any age."},{"prompt":"One evening, Sana asks why the class used words like 'vulva' and 'penis'. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say they're the proper names, and admit you left it late","then":"Sana nods. \"They said it keeps us safe,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"Say the school really shouldn't be teaching such things","then":"Sana looks confused, and decides the class was something shameful."},{"text":"Laugh and say kids these days seem to know everything","then":"Sana laughs too, but her question goes unanswered."},{"text":"Say they're correct, then change the subject fast","then":"Sana nods, but notices how quickly you moved on."}],"why":"Backing the names honestly, late or not, shows her you're someone to ask."},{"prompt":"Sana asks why you never talked about any of this before. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say nobody taught you, but you want to talk now","then":"Sana thinks. \"We can learn it together, then,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"Say she was far too young to know until now","then":"Sana frowns. \"The class said kids should know from little.\""},{"text":"Say it's not something families talk about","then":"Sana nods slowly. \"Then who am I meant to ask?\""},{"text":"Apologise at length for being such a bad parent","then":"Sana looks worried, and ends up comforting you."}],"why":"An honest, guilt-free answer shows her the door is open now."},{"prompt":"Next week, Sana brings home a friend's question about periods. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Answer it simply, and say she can bring you any question","then":"Sana nods. \"Can I ask about boys' stuff too?\" she asks.","best":true},{"text":"Tell her she'll learn about periods when hers start","then":"Sana shrugs, and gets her answer from the friend instead."},{"text":"Say her friend shouldn't be talking about periods","then":"Sana goes quiet, and stops sharing what friends say."},{"text":"Promise a proper talk soon, and then keep putting it off","then":"Sana asks twice more, then gives up."}],"why":"Answering the next question simply turns one late start into a habit."},{"prompt":"A month later, your sister says it's too late for Sana since she's 'already eight'. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say it's never too late, and small talks work at any age","then":"Your sister is quiet. \"Maybe I'll try with mine,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"Agree, and say the school can handle it now","then":"Your sister nods. Sana's next question goes to her classmates."},{"text":"Say you'll wait for a better moment to start it all","then":"Your sister nods. The better moment keeps not arriving."},{"text":"Say you feel terrible for having left it all so very late","then":"Your sister pats your hand, and the talk becomes about guilt, not Sana."}],"why":"Any age is the right age to open the door, and every small talk counts."}],"debrief":"It's never too late to start the conversations; begin now rather than deciding the window has closed.","relearn":"Start the talks now whatever your child's age; it's never too late to open the door."},
  {"id":"tk-009","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"role-play","persona":"Priya","source":"honour the question","hook":"It's the school-morning rush, and you're packing tiffins with one eye on the clock.","setup":"Your child appears at your elbow, looking thoughtful.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"Why do girls get breasts and boys don't?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Shh, we don't talk about that. Not now, not ever.\"","then":"They go quiet. \"Sorry,\" they mumble."},{"text":"\"Bodies grow differently. Now shoes on, quickly.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, though they clearly wanted more."},{"text":"\"Good question. Let's talk properly after school.\"","then":"\"Promise?\" they ask, already hunting for their shoes.","best":true},{"text":"\"Because. Now go and find your socks.\"","then":"\"That's not an answer,\" they grumble, heading off."}],"why":"Honouring the question and naming a time keeps it safe to ask, even in a rush."},{"prompt":"After school, your child asks: \"Is it rude to ask about bodies?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Only if it's something really important.\"","then":"\"How do I know if it's important?\" they ask, unsure."},{"text":"\"Not at all. I'm always glad when you ask me.\"","then":"They grin. \"Even when you're packing tiffins?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Some things are better left unasked, beta.\"","then":"They frown. \"But I still want to know about the breast thing.\""},{"text":"\"Not rude, but grown-ups might get embarrassed.\"","then":"\"Are you embarrassed, then?\" they ask, watching your face."}],"why":"Telling them plainly that asking is welcome keeps the door wide open."},{"prompt":"Snack in hand, your child asks: \"So why do girls get breasts, then?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Maybe tomorrow. I'm far too tired right now.\"","then":"\"You always say tomorrow,\" they sigh."},{"text":"\"Girls grow breasts as they grow up. Boys change too.\"","then":"\"How do boys change?\" they ask, settling in beside you.","best":true},{"text":"\"I'll tell you, but you mustn't tell your friends, okay?\"","then":"They nod slowly. \"Is it a secret, then?\""},{"text":"\"Ask your teacher. She'll explain it better.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, in a voice that means they won't."}],"why":"A simple, true answer when they ask again shows the question was always welcome."}],"relearn":"Honouring the question, even if you park it briefly, keeps it safe to ask, rather than teaching shame."},
  {"id":"tk-010","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: every calm answer makes the next, harder question easier for your child to ask. Worth it?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Worth it","Builds the habit","Yes"],"affirm":"Each calm answer builds the trust that makes the next, harder question easier for your child to bring you.","relearn":"Every calm answer makes the next, harder question easier for your child to ask.","persona":"any","source":"each answer builds"},
  {"id":"tk-011","type":"sort","persona":"any","source":"open vs close","hook":"Sort: an approach that opens the conversation, or one that closes it?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Honest, calm, age-right answers"},{"id":"b","text":"Shame, panic or avoidance"},{"id":"c","text":"Little chats as they come up"},{"id":"d","text":"Waiting for one perfect big talk"},{"id":"e","text":"Welcoming awkward questions"},{"id":"f","text":"Reacting with shock or anger"}],"bins":[{"id":"opens","label":"Opens it up","valence":"pos"},{"id":"closes","label":"Shuts it down","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"opens","b":"closes","c":"opens","d":"closes","e":"opens","f":"closes"},"relearn":"Honest calm answers and little ongoing chats open the conversation; shame and waiting for one big talk shut it down.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-012","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"open invitation","hook":"You feel awkward, but you want to start small, open talks with your child about growing up.","setup":"It's Sunday, and you're washing the car together.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child says: \"Why are you being weird? You keep looking at me.\"","options":[{"text":"\"I want you to know you can ask me anything about growing up.\"","then":"They pause, sponge in hand. \"Anything? Even embarrassing stuff?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"If you ever have a really serious problem, you can come to me.\"","then":"\"What counts as serious?\" they ask, and return to the tyres."},{"text":"\"We'll talk about all that when you're much older.\"","then":"\"All what?\" they ask, puzzled, and go back to scrubbing."},{"text":"\"Nothing. Forget it. Pass me the bucket.\"","then":"They shrug. \"Okay. Here.\" The moment slides away."}],"why":"Saying plainly that any question is welcome opens the door, even when you feel awkward."},{"prompt":"A little later, your child says: \"Rohan's dad talked to him about growing up. Did anyone tell you?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Not really, and I turned out fine.\"","then":"\"So I don't need to know either?\" they say, half joking."},{"text":"\"That's not your business, beta.\"","then":"\"Sorry,\" they mumble. Then, quietly: \"I only wondered.\""},{"text":"\"We didn't need to. We just figured things out.\"","then":"\"Oh. So I should figure it out too?\" they ask."},{"text":"\"Not really. I want it to be different for you.\"","then":"They think about that. \"That sounds lonely,\" they say quietly.","best":true}],"why":"Being honest about your own silence shows why your door is open now."},{"prompt":"As you finish, your child asks: \"If I had a really weird question, who could I ask?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Me. No question is weird with me. Ever.\"","then":"They grin. \"Deal. I'm saving up a list.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Me, and if it's weird, we'll have a good laugh.\"","then":"They laugh. \"Maybe I'll keep the weird ones to myself.\""},{"text":"\"Your teacher, maybe. Try to keep them normal.\"","then":"\"What's normal?\" they ask, and let it drop."},{"text":"\"Me. I might be shocked, but I'll try not to show it.\"","then":"They wrinkle their nose. \"So you will be shocked?\""}],"why":"Promising no question is weird makes the next, harder one easier to ask."}],"relearn":"An open invitation that no question is silly starts the lifelong door, even if you feel awkward doing it."},
  {"id":"tk-013","cat":"early-years","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Teaching little kids the correct names for private body parts is inappropriate.\"","myth":{"un":"Teaching little kids the correct names for private body parts is inappropriate.","re":"Correct names are a protection: children who know them are likelier to be left alone by abusers and to tell clearly if something happens.","why":"Right words are a safety tool, not a loss of innocence."},"relearn":"Teaching correct body-part names protects children; it helps prevent abuse and helps them disclose clearly.","persona":"Divya","source":"correct names protect"},
  {"id":"tk-014","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a body-safety basic for a young child, or not age-appropriate yet?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Correct names for body parts"},{"id":"b","text":"Explicit details of sex"},{"id":"c","text":"Private parts are private; safe vs unsafe touch"},{"id":"d","text":"Adult relationship complexities"},{"id":"e","text":"“You're the boss of your own body”"},{"id":"f","text":"Graphic content from the internet"}],"bins":[{"id":"now","label":"Right for young kids","valence":"pos"},{"id":"later","label":"For when older","valence":"uhoh"}],"key":{"a":"now","b":"later","c":"now","d":"later","e":"now","f":"later"},"relearn":"Correct names, safe-vs-unsafe touch and body ownership suit young children; explicit details and adult complexities come much later.","persona":"any","source":"now vs later","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-015","type":"match","hook":"Match each early body-safety idea to a simple way to teach it.","pairs":[{"left":"Your body belongs to you","right":"“You're the boss of your own body.”"},{"left":"Private parts are private","right":"“These are just for you, not for others.”"},{"left":"Tell a safe grown-up","right":"“If it feels wrong, tell me, no trouble.”"},{"left":"No body secrets","right":"“No one should ask you to keep a body secret.”"},{"left":"You can say no","right":"“You can say no to a hug, even to family.”"}],"relearn":"Ownership, privacy, telling, no body secrets and 'you can say no' are each taught simply, in a child's words.","persona":"Divya","source":"teach it simply","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-016","cat":"early-years","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Kids should keep 'body secrets' to be polite to adults.\"","myth":{"un":"Kids should keep 'body secrets' to be polite to adults.","re":"Teach that no one should ask them to keep a secret about their body, and they can always say no and tell you.","why":"Body secrets are a grooming red flag."},"relearn":"No one should ask a child to keep a body secret; teach them they can always say no and tell you.","persona":"Divya","source":"no body secrets"},
  {"id":"tk-017","cat":"early-years","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"simple true answer","hook":"Your five-year-old Ayaan spots a pregnant neighbour and asks where babies come from. Your mind goes blank.","steps":[{"prompt":"He's waiting, eyes on you. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say babies grow in a part of the body called the womb","then":"Ayaan nods, satisfied, and asks if he was in a womb too.","best":true},{"text":"Say the stork brings them, and ask what he wants for lunch","then":"Ayaan asks for dal-chawal, happy for now. He'll hear a different story at school soon."},{"text":"Say babies come from the hospital, which is partly true","then":"Ayaan nods. That evening he asks if you can buy him a baby brother there."},{"text":"Say he's too young for that and can ask when he's older","then":"His face falls. The next day he asks the neighbour's teenage son instead."}],"why":"A short, true answer at his level satisfies him and shows the question is welcome."},{"prompt":"A week later, Ayaan says a friend told him babies come out of a mummy's tummy. He asks if it's true. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say most come out through the vagina, and some through a cut in the tummy","then":"Ayaan thinks it over. \"So my friend was a bit right,\" he says, and goes back to his cars.","best":true},{"text":"Say yes, babies come out of the tummy, to keep it simple for him","then":"Ayaan now pictures babies sitting in a stomach next to his lunch."},{"text":"Say his friend is being silly, and quickly change the topic to cars","then":"Ayaan goes quiet. He decides his friend knows more than you do."},{"text":"Say it isn't a nice thing for little boys to be talking about","then":"Ayaan looks embarrassed and drops it, for now."}],"why":"The true facts, said simply, answer him and keep you the person he checks things with."},{"prompt":"At bedtime, Ayaan asks how a baby gets inside a mummy in the first place. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say a tiny egg and a tiny sperm join and grow into a baby","then":"\"That's so small!\" Ayaan says, and yawns. He asks what else is tiny.","best":true},{"text":"Say it happens when two people love each other very much","then":"Ayaan asks if he'll get a baby because he loves his best friend."},{"text":"Say that's enough questions for one week","then":"He pulls the blanket up and doesn't ask you anything like it for a long time."},{"text":"Explain everything in full detail to get it over with","then":"Ayaan looks lost and a little worried, and falls asleep with more questions than before."}],"why":"One small true fact fits his age and leaves the door open for the next question."}],"debrief":"Answer 'where do babies come from?' simply and truthfully at the child's level, not with a myth or a shutdown.","relearn":"Give little kids a simple true answer about where babies come from, not a stork story or silence."},
  {"id":"tk-018","cat":"early-years","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Forcing a child to hug relatives teaches good manners.\"","myth":{"un":"Forcing a child to hug relatives teaches good manners.","re":"Letting a child choose how to greet people teaches consent, that their yes and no about their body count.","why":"Bodily choice now builds consent for life."},"relearn":"Letting a child choose whether to hug teaches consent; forcing affection overrides their bodily 'no'.","persona":"Priya","source":"consent in greetings"},
  {"id":"tk-019","cat":"early-years","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: 'you're the boss of your body' is consent, taught at age four. Powerful, isn't it?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Powerful","Consent early","Love that"],"affirm":"Teaching a small child that they're the boss of their own body plants the roots of consent for life.","relearn":"'You're the boss of your body' is consent taught at age four, the foundation for everything later.","persona":"any","source":"consent at four"},
  {"id":"tk-020","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two lessons that DON'T keep a young child safer.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Knowing correct body-part names","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Being told their body isn't theirs to control","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Knowing they can always tell you","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Being told to keep a body secret to be polite","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Knowing private parts are just for them","trick":false}],"why":"Teaching a child their body isn't theirs, or to keep a body secret, removes safety; names, an open door and privacy protect.","relearn":"Safety comes from correct names, an open door and privacy, not from 'your body isn't yours' or 'keep a body secret'.","persona":"Divya","source":"safer early","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-021","cat":"early-years","type":"role-play","persona":"Divya","source":"back the names","hook":"At your mother's house, your four-year-old Myra proudly tells everyone her doll has a vulva.","setup":"Nani's neighbour is visiting too, and has gone silent.","steps":[{"prompt":"Nani gasps and says: \"Where is she learning such words? Stop her.\"","options":[{"text":"\"They're the proper names. We teach them to keep her safe.\"","then":"Nani blinks. \"Safe? How is a word safe?\" she asks.","best":true},{"text":"\"Sorry, Ma. I'll teach her not to say that.\"","then":"Nani nods. \"Good. Some words aren't for children.\" Myra's smile fades."},{"text":"\"Myra, that's enough now. Go and play outside.\"","then":"Nani sniffs as Myra trails out. \"At least she listens to you.\""},{"text":"\"She's only four, Ma. She doesn't even know what it means.\"","then":"Nani frowns. \"Then why teach it to her at all?\""}],"why":"Backing her calmly, with the reason, keeps the safety word and doesn't shame her."},{"prompt":"Nani turns to her neighbour: \"In our day, no child said such words. We turned out fine.\"","options":[{"text":"\"I know. But the words help children tell us if something's wrong.\"","then":"Nani goes quiet. \"We never had words for anything,\" she says slowly.","best":true},{"text":"\"Times have changed, Ma. You just wouldn't understand these things.\"","then":"Nani stiffens. \"Oh, I wouldn't understand?\""},{"text":"\"You're right, Ma. I'll just say 'private parts' from now on.\"","then":"Nani nods, pleased. \"Much better. Private is private.\""},{"text":"\"Can we please not do this in front of everyone?\"","then":"Nani glances around the room. \"Fine. But we'll talk later.\""}],"why":"Naming the safety reason, gently, answers her worry instead of dismissing it."},{"prompt":"Later, in the kitchen, Nani asks: \"What if she says it at school? People will talk.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Then her teacher hears a proper word. That's all it is.\"","then":"Nani laughs despite herself. \"You were always stubborn,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"\"You're right, Ma. I'll tell her to say it only at home.\"","then":"Nani nods. \"Good. Home is the place for such things.\""},{"text":"\"Let them talk. I don't care what anyone thinks.\"","then":"Nani shakes her head. \"You'll care when it's your name they say.\""},{"text":"\"She'll grow out of saying it so much. Don't worry.\"","then":"Nani sighs. \"I hope so. For all our sakes.\""}],"why":"Treating the word as ordinary, calmly, is what keeps it useful to her."}],"relearn":"Calmly backing the correct names protects your child's safety tool instead of shaming them into silence."},
  {"id":"tk-022","cat":"early-years","type":"branch","persona":"Priya","source":"respect their no","hook":"Your four-year-old Meher says she doesn't want Bua to bathe her any more. Bua is staying with you this month.","steps":[{"prompt":"Bua is already running the bath water. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say you'll do her bath tonight, and take her no seriously","then":"Meher's shoulders drop. She holds your hand all the way to the bathroom.","best":true},{"text":"Tell Meher that Bua is family, so she must be good and go","then":"Meher goes in stiff and silent, and won't look at you afterwards."},{"text":"Ask Meher, in front of Bua, what her problem is","then":"Meher hides behind your legs and says nothing. Bua looks hurt."},{"text":"Let it go tonight and hope she settles down","then":"Meher cries through the bath. Bua says she's just being fussy."}],"why":"Taking her no seriously in the moment shows her that her body and her voice count."},{"prompt":"At bedtime Meher whispers, \"I just didn't like it.\" What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Thank her and say she can always say no, and tell you","then":"Meher snuggles in. \"Even about grown-ups?\" she asks. You say yes.","best":true},{"text":"Ask her lots of questions about exactly what Bua did","then":"Meher gets muddled, says \"I don't know,\" and turns to the wall."},{"text":"Say Bua loves her very much and was only trying to help","then":"Meher nods slowly and doesn't say anything more."},{"text":"Say she hurt Bua's feelings and should say sorry","then":"Her eyes fill. She whispers sorry and tells you nothing else."}],"why":"Thanks and a clear 'you can always tell me' keep her talking, without pressing her for details."},{"prompt":"Over breakfast, Bua says Meher is getting fussy and needs a firm hand. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say you'll do Meher's baths now, and she can choose","then":"Bua raises an eyebrow but lets it go. Meher eats her breakfast in peace.","best":true},{"text":"Agree that Meher needs to learn to behave","then":"Bua nods. Meher, listening from the doorway, learns her no doesn't count."},{"text":"Say it's a phase and Bua can try again next week","then":"Bua agrees. Meher goes quiet whenever next week comes up."},{"text":"Snap at Bua in front of Meher that she's upsetting her","then":"The kitchen goes tense. Meher looks frightened, as if she caused the fight."}],"why":"Backing her choice calmly protects Meher, and keeps her telling you if anything feels wrong."}],"debrief":"Take a child's 'no' about their body seriously, even with family. It's never their fault; if they share more, stay calm, believe them: Childline 1098.","relearn":"Respect a child's 'no' about their body, even toward family; overriding it erodes their safety instinct."},
  {"id":"tk-023","cat":"middle-years","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"You should wait until puberty starts to explain puberty.\"","myth":{"un":"You should wait until puberty starts to explain puberty.","re":"Prepare children before the changes begin, ideally by around nine, so periods, wet dreams and body changes never come as a frightening shock.","why":"Forewarned is far less frightening."},"relearn":"Explain puberty before it starts (by around nine) so the changes never come as a frightening shock.","persona":"Divya","source":"prep before puberty"},
  {"id":"tk-024","cat":"middle-years","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: worth covering before puberty hits, or leave for the teen years?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Periods and wet dreams are normal"},{"id":"b","text":"Body changes that are coming"},{"id":"c","text":"Detailed adult relationship advice"},{"id":"d","text":"Basic online safety and privacy"},{"id":"e","text":"Sweat, hair and mood changes"},{"id":"f","text":"In-depth adult contraception choices"}],"bins":[{"id":"before","label":"Cover before puberty","valence":"pos"},{"id":"later","label":"Later","valence":"uhoh"}],"key":{"a":"before","b":"before","c":"later","d":"before","e":"before","f":"later"},"relearn":"Periods, wet dreams, coming changes and online basics suit pre-puberty; detailed adult advice waits.","persona":"any","source":"before or later"},
  {"id":"tk-025","cat":"middle-years","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Only girls need to know about periods, and only boys about wet dreams.\"","myth":{"un":"Only girls need to know about periods, and only boys about wet dreams.","re":"All children benefit from understanding everyone's puberty; it builds empathy and ends shame and teasing.","why":"Shared knowledge ends shame."},"relearn":"All children should learn about everyone's puberty, periods and wet dreams alike; it builds empathy and ends shame.","persona":"Priya","source":"everyone learns"},
  {"id":"tk-026","cat":"middle-years","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"online basics","hook":"Your nine-year-old is getting your old phone for online classes, and the internet is opening up.","steps":[{"prompt":"The phone is charged and ready. What do you do before handing it over?","options":[{"text":"Talk about privacy, kindness and scary stuff","then":"They roll their eyes but listen, then ask what counts as 'scary'.","best":true},{"text":"Hand it over. They'll learn as they go","then":"They vanish into it within minutes, tapping whatever pops up."},{"text":"Set up parental controls and leave it at that","then":"The filters block some things. Your child has no idea what to do if something slips through."},{"text":"Lock every app and hand over a long list of rules","then":"They nod at the rules, then start looking for ways round the locks."}],"why":"A first device plus a simple talk starts their online safety net early."},{"prompt":"A week later, your child is added to a class WhatsApp group full of forwards. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Pull them out of the group straight away, to be safe","then":"Their friends ask why they left. They feel left out and embarrassed."},{"text":"Tell them never to forward anything to anyone, ever","then":"They agree, but don't know why, or what to do with the weird ones."},{"text":"Go through the group together and talk about sharing","then":"They point out a forward that seemed odd, and you talk it through.","best":true},{"text":"Leave them to it. It's only classmates","then":"Soon they're passing on forwards they don't understand."}],"why":"Looking together teaches judgement they'll carry into every group."},{"prompt":"One evening, your child says a game asked for their school name and address. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Quietly fix the privacy settings yourself later","then":"The settings are fixed. Your child still doesn't know why it mattered."},{"text":"Thank them, and explain why those details stay private","then":"They nod. 'So I just skip that bit?' they ask, and you show them how.","best":true},{"text":"Fill the details in for them so the game can finally start","then":"The game starts, and their details sit with a company you know nothing about."},{"text":"Delete the game at once and tell them off for it","then":"They go quiet. You suspect the next thing like this won't reach you."}],"why":"Thanking them and explaining why builds the habit of keeping personal details private."},{"prompt":"A month in, you're tempted to check the phone secretly every night. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Ask an older cousin to keep an eye on their chats","then":"The cousin agrees, and your child starts to feel watched by everyone."},{"text":"Stop checking. They've been fine so far","then":"It goes quiet. You no longer know what they're seeing online."},{"text":"Agree on open check-ins together, and keep talking","then":"They grumble, then show you a funny video they found. The talking goes on.","best":true},{"text":"Read their chats every night without telling them","then":"One day they notice. They start deleting things before bed."}],"why":"Open check-ins keep trust and keep them telling you things, where snooping makes them hide."}],"debrief":"Start simple online-safety talks (privacy, kindness, telling you anything scary) as a child goes online.","relearn":"Pair a first device with simple online-safety talks, not a silent handover."},
  {"id":"tk-027","cat":"middle-years","type":"match","hook":"Match each pre-teen topic to a calm way in.","pairs":[{"left":"Periods","right":"\"It's a normal, healthy sign of growing up.\""},{"left":"Wet dreams","right":"\"This happens to bodies, nothing's wrong.\""},{"left":"Online strangers","right":"\"Tell me about anyone who makes you uneasy.\""},{"left":"Body odour","right":"\"Time for a daily wash routine, that's all.\""},{"left":"Growing taller","right":"\"Everyone grows at their own pace.\""}],"relearn":"Periods, wet dreams, online strangers, odour and growth each have a calm, normalising way to open the conversation.","persona":"any","source":"calm ways in"},
  {"id":"tk-028","cat":"middle-years","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: a child told about periods before their first one feels prepared, not terrified. Worth it?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Worth it","Prepared not scared","Yes"],"affirm":"Preparing a child for puberty before it starts replaces fear and shame with readiness and confidence.","relearn":"A child prepared for puberty before it starts feels ready, not terrified.","persona":"Divya","source":"prepared"},
  {"id":"tk-029","cat":"middle-years","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two pre-teen messages that would undermine safety and confidence.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"These changes are normal and healthy\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"We don't talk about such dirty things\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"Tell me about anything online that scares you\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"Sort it out yourself, don't bother me\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"You can come to me with any worry\"","trick":false}],"why":"\"Dirty things\" and \"sort it out yourself\" shut a child out; normalising changes and inviting them to tell you build safety.","relearn":"Pre-teen safety comes from normalising changes and inviting them to tell you, not from shame.","persona":"any","source":"build safety"},
  {"id":"tk-030","cat":"middle-years","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"thank them for telling","hook":"At dinner, your pre-teen mentions a video in their feed that clearly left them shaken.","steps":[{"prompt":"They say it showed kids at another school fighting badly. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Stay calm, thank them, and talk it through","then":"They let out a breath and say they couldn't stop thinking about it.","best":true},{"text":"Take the phone away as punishment for watching it","then":"They stare at their plate. 'I didn't even search for it,' they mutter."},{"text":"Tell them to just scroll past things like that","then":"They nod, but the picture of the fight stays with them tonight."},{"text":"Say 'This is why I hate these phones' and fume","then":"They go quiet and wish they hadn't mentioned it."}],"why":"Staying calm and thanking them teaches that telling you is safe and worth it."},{"prompt":"Later, they wonder aloud whether to send the video to friends as a warning. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say it's none of their business what others watch","then":"They shrug. The video keeps doing the rounds without them."},{"text":"Suggest reporting it instead, and show them how","then":"They find the report button, press it, and look relieved.","best":true},{"text":"Tell them to delete it and forget all about it","then":"They delete it, not knowing a report could get it taken down."},{"text":"Say yes, their friends should see what's out there","then":"The video spreads further through their class group."}],"why":"Reporting, not sharing, is a simple online habit that protects others too."},{"prompt":"A week later, you notice they seem jumpy after their evening scroll. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Check their search history while they sleep","then":"You find nothing clear, and now you're hiding something from them too."},{"text":"Ask gently whether anything else has upset them","then":"They hesitate, then tell you about another clip. 'I wasn't sure I should say.'","best":true},{"text":"Assume it's nothing and let it be","then":"They go to bed early and stay quiet at breakfast."},{"text":"Ban the phone after dinner, without explaining why","then":"They sulk, and start scrolling at night under the blanket."}],"why":"A gentle check-in keeps the telling habit going when something still bothers them."}],"debrief":"When a child reports something unsettling online, stay calm and thank them so they keep telling you.","relearn":"Thank a child for reporting scary content and talk it through; anger teaches them to hide it."},
  {"id":"tk-031","cat":"middle-years","type":"role-play","persona":"Divya","source":"prep for periods","hook":"You want to prepare your daughter for periods, calmly and positively, before they start.","setup":"You're folding laundry together on a quiet Sunday.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your daughter asks: \"Why are there pads in your cupboard?\"","options":[{"text":"\"You'll find out about all that when it happens.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" she shrugs, and goes back to folding."},{"text":"\"They're a grown-up thing. I'll tell you another time.\"","then":"\"When?\" she asks, and waits for an answer that doesn't come."},{"text":"\"For periods. One day you'll get them too. It's normal.\"","then":"\"Periods,\" she repeats slowly. \"Riya's sister has those.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"They're nothing. Don't go through my things.\"","then":"She flushes. \"Sorry. I was just asking.\""}],"why":"Using a natural moment to explain makes periods feel ordinary, not secret."},{"prompt":"Later, your daughter asks: \"Riya says periods really hurt. Do they?\"","options":[{"text":"\"It hurts a lot, but you just have to bear it.\"","then":"She goes quiet. \"So I shouldn't say if it hurts?\""},{"text":"\"It can ache. If it hurts a lot, we'll get help.\"","then":"She lets out a breath. \"Okay. I'll tell you if it's bad.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Don't worry about all of that right now, beta.\"","then":"\"But I am worried,\" she says quietly."},{"text":"\"No, it doesn't hurt at all. Not one bit.\"","then":"\"Oh, good,\" she says, and believes you completely."}],"why":"An honest answer, with help if it hurts a lot, prepares her without scaring her."},{"prompt":"Your daughter asks: \"What if it starts at school?\"","options":[{"text":"\"It won't. It almost always starts at home.\"","then":"\"Oh, okay,\" she says, and stops thinking about it."},{"text":"\"Then just come home straight away, and rest.\"","then":"\"And miss class?\" she asks, worried."},{"text":"\"We'll pack a kit for your bag, and you can call me.\"","then":"She nods. \"Can I choose the pouch?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Then ask your class teacher. She'll know how to help.\"","then":"\"But what if she's busy, and I've got nothing with me?\" she asks."}],"why":"A plan and a kit make her first period feel expected and supported."}],"relearn":"A warm, matter-of-fact heads-up makes a first period feel expected and supported, not frightening or shameful."},
  {"id":"tk-032","cat":"middle-years","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: the years just before puberty are the golden window, prepared kids handle it so much better. Agree?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Agree","Golden window","Prepare them"],"affirm":"The years just before puberty are the ideal window to prepare a child so the changes feel manageable.","relearn":"The years just before puberty are the golden window; prepared kids handle the changes far better.","persona":"any","source":"golden window"},
  {"id":"tk-033","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Once they're teens and online, it's too late and pointless to talk.\"","myth":{"un":"Once they're teens and online, it's too late and pointless to talk.","re":"Teens still want a trusted adult; staying askable about relationships, consent and online life matters most now.","why":"The door matters more, not less, in the teen years."},"relearn":"Teens still need a trusted adult; staying askable about relationships, consent and online life matters most now.","persona":"Vikram","source":"not too late"},
  {"id":"tk-034","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"sort","persona":"any","source":"have the talk","hook":"Sort: a teen-years talk worth having, or one to skip?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"What consent really means"},{"id":"b","text":"How online porn distorts real sex and bodies"},{"id":"c","text":"Respect in dating and breakups"},{"id":"d","text":"Nothing, they'll figure it out alone"},{"id":"e","text":"Staying safe with online strangers"},{"id":"f","text":"Leave it to their friends to explain"}],"bins":[{"id":"have","label":"Worth having","valence":"pos"},{"id":"skip","label":"Don't skip the talks","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"have","b":"have","c":"have","d":"skip","e":"have","f":"skip"},"relearn":"Consent, porn-literacy, respect and online safety are worth talking about; leaving teens to 'figure it out alone' or to friends isn't."},
  {"id":"tk-035","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"What teens see online about sex and relationships is a fine substitute for talking to me.\"","myth":{"un":"What teens see online about sex and relationships is a fine substitute for talking to me.","re":"Online content and the manosphere often teach distortion and disrespect; your honest voice is the antidote.","why":"If you stay silent, the algorithm fills the gap."},"relearn":"Online content often distorts sex and respect; if you stay silent the algorithm teaches instead, so your voice matters.","persona":"Vikram","source":"your voice is the antidote"},
  {"id":"tk-036","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"through the eye-rolls","hook":"Your son Kabir, 15, rolls his eyes the moment you mention relationships.","steps":[{"prompt":"He mutters that he already knows everything. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Hand him a good book on relationships, and leave it at that","then":"He tosses it on his desk. He never hears what you actually think."},{"text":"Insist he sits through the whole talk, since it matters","then":"He sits, arms folded, and answers everything with \"Yeah, I know.\""},{"text":"Say fair enough, share one thing you believe, then let it go","then":"He shrugs, but you catch him turning over what you said.","best":true},{"text":"Drop the topic. If he knows it all, he won't need you","then":"Kabir looks relieved, and you both let the subject drop."}],"why":"One short, warm thought respects what he knows and still gives him your view."},{"prompt":"A week later, a song in the car jokes that a girl's no means yes. Kabir hums along. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say nothing. He'll only roll his eyes again","then":"The song ends. Kabir skips to the next one, and the line goes unexamined."},{"text":"Turn it down and ask what he makes of that line","then":"He shrugs. \"It's just a song.\" After a pause: \"Okay, it's a bit off.\"","best":true},{"text":"Switch it off and say the song is disgusting","then":"\"It's just a song,\" he says, and puts his earphones in."},{"text":"Explain why that line is wrong, all the way home","then":"By the second minute, Kabir is staring out of the window, nodding without listening."}],"why":"A curious question invites him to think aloud, which a lecture shuts down."},{"prompt":"Months later, Kabir asks, half joking, how you know if someone likes you back. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Laugh and tease him about who the lucky girl might be","then":"Kabir goes red, says \"Forget it,\" and leaves the room."},{"text":"Seize the moment for the full, proper talk you'd been planning","then":"He listens for a minute, then remembers he has homework."},{"text":"Answer honestly, briefly, and say he can ask you anything","then":"He grins, embarrassed, and asks one more question before he goes.","best":true},{"text":"Tell him he's far too young to be worrying about that","then":"He shrugs. \"Fine. I'll just ask my friends.\""}],"why":"Answering simply when he asks shows the door he rolled his eyes at is still open."}],"debrief":"With an eye-rolling teen, stay warm and share your view without lecturing, and you stay a quiet resource.","relearn":"Stay open and non-lecturing with a resistant teen; that keeps you a resource even through the eye-rolls."},
  {"id":"tk-037","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"match","persona":"any","source":"respectful openers","hook":"Match each teen topic to an opener that respects them.","pairs":[{"left":"Consent","right":"\"Both people freely wanting it, every time, matters.\""},{"left":"Online porn","right":"\"A lot of it isn't real; let's talk about what is.\""},{"left":"A first relationship","right":"\"I'm here, no judgement, whenever you want to talk.\""},{"left":"A breakup","right":"\"This hurts, and I'm right here with you.\""},{"left":"Online strangers","right":"\"People aren't always who they claim. Show me.\""}],"relearn":"Consent, porn-literacy, first relationships, breakups and online strangers each have a respectful opener that keeps a teen listening."},
  {"id":"tk-038","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: a teen who can come to you about sex and relationships is a safer teen. Feel the stakes?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Feel it","Safer teen","Worth staying open"],"affirm":"A teen who can bring you questions about sex and relationships is safer than one left to the internet.","relearn":"A teen who can come to you about sex and relationships is a safer teen.","persona":"any","source":"safer teen"},
  {"id":"tk-039","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Talking to my teen about consent will give them ideas.\"","myth":{"un":"Talking to my teen about consent will give them ideas.","re":"Teaching consent gives them respect and safety, not ideas; it's among the most protective talks you can have.","why":"Consent knowledge protects, never encourages."},"relearn":"Teaching a teen consent gives them respect and safety, not 'ideas'; it's a deeply protective talk.","persona":"Vikram","source":"consent protects"},
  {"id":"tk-040","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"spot","persona":"any","source":"safe and connected","hook":"Spot the two things that push a teen away and online.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Honest, non-judgemental conversations","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Shaming them about bodies or crushes","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Being a calm, askable resource","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Punishing them for asking questions","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Welcoming hard questions without judgement","trick":false}],"why":"Shaming them and punishing questions push a teen away and online; honest talks and being askable keep them connected.","relearn":"Shaming a teen and punishing their questions push them away and online; honest, askable parenting keeps them connected."},
  {"id":"tk-041","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"stay open teen","hook":"Driving home, your son Rohan, 14, asks you something about sex that catches you off guard.","setup":"You grip the wheel a little tighter.","steps":[{"prompt":"Rohan asks: \"Is it true you can't get pregnant the first time?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Ask me when you're older. You're too young for this.\"","then":"\"Everyone else already knows,\" he mutters, and looks out of the window."},{"text":"\"Good question. No, that's a myth. Glad you asked me.\"","then":"Rohan nods. \"Oh. My friend said you can't.\" He waits, wanting more.","best":true},{"text":"\"Where did you hear that? You shouldn't be thinking about this.\"","then":"Rohan shrugs. \"Nowhere. Forget it.\" He puts his earphones in."},{"text":"\"Ha. Why? Is there something you want to tell me?\"","then":"Rohan goes red. \"No! Forget I asked.\""}],"why":"Welcoming the question and giving the true answer keeps you his source, not his friends."},{"prompt":"A few minutes later, Rohan tries again: \"So how does it actually work, then?\"","options":[{"text":"\"It's mostly luck, honestly. Some people just don't.\"","then":"Rohan nods, satisfied, and carries a wrong idea home with him."},{"text":"\"That's enough for today. You know the main thing now.\"","then":"Rohan shrugs. \"Okay.\" He'll look it up on his phone later."},{"text":"\"I'll tell you what I know, and we can look up the rest.\"","then":"Rohan listens closely, then asks if you can find a good site together tonight.","best":true},{"text":"\"You'll learn all that in biology class soon enough.\"","then":"\"They skip that chapter,\" Rohan says. \"Everyone knows they do.\""}],"why":"Sharing what you know and finding the rest together beats bluffing or brushing him off."},{"prompt":"A week later, Rohan says: \"My friends think it's weird I talk to you about this.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Your friends are being silly. Just ignore them.\"","then":"Rohan frowns. \"They're my friends,\" he says, and the chat ends."},{"text":"\"Oh. Then maybe we should stop talking about this stuff.\"","then":"Rohan hesitates. \"Okay,\" he says, and doesn't ask again for months."},{"text":"\"Weird? I'm the coolest parent you know.\"","then":"Rohan laughs, then drops it. You never find out what he meant."},{"text":"\"Maybe. But you can always ask me, and I won't judge.\"","then":"Rohan smiles a little. \"Yeah. It's kind of nice, actually.\"","best":true}],"why":"A calm, open reply shows his questions are welcome, whatever his friends think."}],"relearn":"Welcoming a tough teen question, and finding answers together, keeps you their trusted source over the internet."},
  {"id":"tk-042","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: every awkward, honest teen talk is a small vote for them trusting you over the algorithm. Worth it?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Worth it","Over the algorithm","Keep talking"],"affirm":"Each honest teen conversation builds the trust that keeps your child coming to you rather than the algorithm.","relearn":"Every honest teen talk is a vote for them trusting you over the algorithm.","persona":"any","source":"over the algorithm"},
  {"id":"tk-043","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"I have to choose between honest facts and my family's values.\"","myth":{"un":"I have to choose between honest facts and my family's values.","re":"You can give accurate facts and share your values; kids can hold both, the facts to stay safe and your values to guide them.","why":"Facts and values are partners, not rivals."},"relearn":"You don't choose between honest facts and your values; give both, the facts for safety and your values to guide.","persona":"Vikram","source":"facts and values"},
  {"id":"tk-044","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: an honest fact every child needs, or a value you choose to share?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"How bodies work and how to stay safe"},{"id":"b","text":"What your family believes about timing"},{"id":"c","text":"Accurate names and basic health facts"},{"id":"d","text":"Your hopes and guidance for them"},{"id":"e","text":"What consent is and how to ask for it"},{"id":"f","text":"The faith and traditions you cherish"}],"bins":[{"id":"facts","label":"Honest facts","valence":"pos"},{"id":"values","label":"Your values","valence":"tell"}],"key":{"a":"facts","b":"values","c":"facts","d":"values","e":"facts","f":"values"},"relearn":"Body facts, consent and safety are honest facts every child needs; timing, hopes and traditions are values you share.","persona":"any","source":"facts vs values"},
  {"id":"tk-045","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Withholding facts will keep my child innocent and safe.\"","myth":{"un":"Withholding facts will keep my child innocent and safe.","re":"Missing facts make children more vulnerable, not safer; honest information plus your values is what truly protects them.","why":"Knowledge is a shield, not a threat."},"relearn":"Withholding facts makes children more vulnerable; honest information plus your values protects them.","persona":"Divya","source":"facts protect"},
  {"id":"tk-046","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"both together","hook":"A condom ad comes on during the cricket, and your thirteen-year-old Arnav asks what it's for.","steps":[{"prompt":"He's looking right at you, waiting. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Tell him plainly what it's for, then share your own view","then":"Arnav listens, a bit red-faced, and asks what you mean by 'ready'.","best":true},{"text":"Change the channel and say it's nothing for boys his age","then":"Arnav rolls his eyes, and looks it up on his phone that night."},{"text":"Say he doesn't need to know, because good boys wait anyway","then":"Arnav shrugs. He learns what it is from a friend's forwarded video."},{"text":"Give him the plain facts, and keep your own views out of it","then":"Arnav gets the facts, but has no idea what you think or why."}],"why":"Honest facts keep him safe, and your view, given as yours, guides him."},{"prompt":"A few days later, Arnav asks why grown-ups keep saying to wait for the right person. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Share what you believe and why, as your view, not an order","then":"Arnav thinks about it. \"So you'd trust me to decide?\" he asks.","best":true},{"text":"Say 'because I said so', and leave it there","then":"Arnav nods, and quietly decides your rules come without reasons."},{"text":"Say there's no right way, so he can do whatever he likes","then":"Arnav shrugs, and fills the gap with what his friends think."},{"text":"Tell him scary stories about boys who didn't wait","then":"Arnav looks uneasy, and decides not to raise the topic again."}],"why":"Values shared with reasons give him something to weigh, which lasts longer than an order."},{"prompt":"At dinner, your mother says boys shouldn't even know about such things. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say kindly that Arnav needs the facts and your values, both","then":"Your mother sniffs, but lets it go. Arnav gives you a small nod.","best":true},{"text":"Agree with her, and promise not to talk to him about it again","then":"Your mother is pleased. Arnav, across the table, stops meeting your eye."},{"text":"Argue with her loudly across the dinner table","then":"Dinner turns tense. Arnav slips away to his room."},{"text":"Say nothing now, and keep the talks going quietly later","then":"The peace holds, but Arnav hears only his grandmother's view tonight."}],"why":"Naming 'both' kindly, in front of him, shows Arnav the facts aren't a secret."},{"prompt":"Later, Arnav says a friend claims condoms don't really work. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say they work well when used correctly, and he can ask you","then":"Arnav nods. \"He's wrong about loads of stuff,\" he says, grinning.","best":true},{"text":"Say his friend is right, so it's best to avoid all of it","then":"Arnav believes you, and now carries a false fact into his future."},{"text":"Tell him to stop spending so much time with that friend","then":"Arnav goes quiet. He and the friend keep talking, just not near you."},{"text":"Say you're not really sure, and change the subject","then":"Arnav shrugs, and takes his friend's word for it."}],"why":"Correcting a false fact keeps him safe, whatever your values say about when."}],"debrief":"Give the honest facts and share your values as your perspective; don't hide facts to enforce values.","relearn":"Offer honest facts and your values together; hiding facts just leaves a child unsafe."},
  {"id":"tk-047","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"match","hook":"Match each tricky moment to a facts-plus-values response.","pairs":[{"left":"'What does that word mean?'","right":"Define it simply, then share your view"},{"left":"'When is it okay to date?'","right":"Give the facts, then your family's values"},{"left":"'My friend has a boyfriend'","right":"Discuss respect and safety, and your hopes"},{"left":"'Why do people do that?'","right":"Honest answer first, then what we believe"},{"left":"'Is that normal?'","right":"Reassure with facts, add your guidance"}],"relearn":"Each tricky question gets honest facts first, then your family's values, so a child has both safety and guidance.","persona":"any","source":"facts plus values"},
  {"id":"tk-048","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: your child can know the facts to stay safe and still carry the values you raise them with. Resonate?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Resonates","Both at once","That works"],"affirm":"Children can hold accurate facts for safety alongside the values their family raises them with; it isn't either/or.","relearn":"Your child can know the facts to stay safe and carry your values too; it's not either/or.","persona":"any","source":"hold both"},
  {"id":"tk-049","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If I stay silent on values, my child won't be influenced by anyone.\"","myth":{"un":"If I stay silent on values, my child won't be influenced by anyone.","re":"If you don't share your values, peers, media and the algorithm will fill the gap; your voice belongs in the mix.","why":"Silence cedes the field to everyone else."},"relearn":"Silence on values doesn't keep a child neutral; peers and the algorithm fill the gap, so share your voice.","persona":"Vikram","source":"share your voice"},
  {"id":"tk-050","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two approaches that leave a child exposed, not protected.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Honest facts plus your shared values","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Silence and hoping for the best","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Open conversation, no shame","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Letting the feed teach instead of you","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Answering questions calmly and truthfully","trick":false}],"why":"Silence and ceding to the feed leave a child exposed; honest facts, shared values and open, calm talk protect them.","relearn":"Children are protected best by honest facts plus shared values and open talk, not by silence or the feed.","persona":"any","source":"protects best"},
  {"id":"tk-051","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: breaking the family silence doesn't betray your culture; it lets you pass on the best of it. Sit right?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Sits right","Pass on the best","Not a betrayal"],"affirm":"Breaking the silence around these topics lets parents pass on their values intentionally, rather than ceding them.","relearn":"Breaking the silence doesn't betray your culture; it lets you pass on the best of it, on purpose.","persona":"any","source":"pass it on"},
  {"id":"tk-052","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","persona":"Divya","source":"ready scripts","hook":"Your daughter Mira, 4, has started asking about bodies. Twice this week, you froze.","steps":[{"prompt":"You want to feel ready next time. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Wait and wing it. You'll find the words in the moment","then":"The next question comes at the dentist's, and you freeze again."},{"text":"Prepare a few simple, age-right answers to common questions","then":"You note three short answers on your phone, and feel calmer already.","best":true},{"text":"Plan one big, proper talk for when she's a bit older","then":"Mira keeps asking now, and your answer keeps being \"later\"."},{"text":"Read up on everything first, before you say anything more to her","then":"Weeks pass in reading, and Mira's questions go unanswered."}],"why":"A few ready answers stop the freeze without waiting for perfect knowledge."},{"prompt":"At the park, Mira loudly asks why boys stand up to pee. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Hush her quickly and whisper that you'll talk about it at home","then":"Mira looks confused, and learns that her question was embarrassing."},{"text":"Laugh and tell her that's just how it is, beta","then":"Mira frowns, not satisfied, and asks the same thing at dinner."},{"text":"Say simply that boys have a penis and girls have a vulva","then":"Mira nods, satisfied, and runs back to the slide.","best":true},{"text":"Tell her that's not a nice thing to ask in public","then":"Mira's face falls, and she stays quiet for the rest of the park trip."}],"why":"A calm, simple answer with the correct names keeps her questions coming to you."},{"prompt":"That night, Mira asks where babies come from. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Tell her a stork brings babies, like in the storybooks","then":"Mira believes you, until a cousin laughs at her for it."},{"text":"Say she's too young, and to ask again when she's big","then":"Mira shrugs, and asks her older cousin instead."},{"text":"Tell her everything, start to finish, in one go","then":"By the second minute, Mira's eyes glaze over and she wanders off."},{"text":"Give a short, true answer: a baby grows in a uterus","then":"Mira thinks, says \"Oh,\" and asks for one more story.","best":true}],"why":"A short, true, age-right answer satisfies her and keeps the door open."}],"debrief":"Keep a few simple, age-right answers ready so common questions don't catch you off guard.","relearn":"Ready a few age-right scripts; winging every hard question invites the freeze that closes the door."},
  {"id":"tk-053","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each tool to what it gives a parent.","pairs":[{"left":"Age-by-age guides","right":"What to cover, and when"},{"left":"Ready scripts","right":"Words when you're caught off guard"},{"left":"The open-door habit","right":"A child who keeps coming to you"},{"left":"Learning alongside them","right":"Answers you didn't have before"},{"left":"The safeguarding route","right":"Help when a worry is about safety"}],"relearn":"Age-by-age guides, ready scripts, the open-door habit, learning alongside and the safeguarding route are the core tools of guiding a child's RSE.","persona":"any","source":"the toolkit"},
  {"id":"tk-054","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"My own gaps and embarrassment mean I can't guide my child at all.\"","myth":{"un":"My own gaps and embarrassment mean I can't guide my child at all.","re":"You can learn alongside your child; nobody starts an expert, and your willingness matters more than perfect knowledge.","why":"Willingness beats expertise."},"relearn":"Your own gaps don't disqualify you; you can learn alongside your child, and willingness matters more than expertise.","persona":"Vikram","source":"learn alongside"},
  {"id":"tk-055","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a green-flag move for guiding your child, or one to rethink?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Many small, calm, honest talks"},{"id":"b","text":"One panicked lecture, then silence"},{"id":"c","text":"Learning the facts you're unsure of"},{"id":"d","text":"Shaming questions away"},{"id":"e","text":"Repairing it when you get one wrong"},{"id":"f","text":"Pretending you never heard the question"}],"bins":[{"id":"green","label":"Green-flag move","valence":"pos"},{"id":"rethink","label":"Rethink it","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"green","b":"rethink","c":"green","d":"rethink","e":"green","f":"rethink"},"relearn":"Small calm talks, learning the facts and repairing fumbles are green flags; a panicked lecture, shaming and ignoring questions need a rethink.","persona":"any","source":"green or rethink"},
  {"id":"tk-056","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","persona":"Meena","source":"safeguard route","hook":"At bathtime, your son Neel, 7, says someone at swimming class plays a 'secret game' he doesn't like.","steps":[{"prompt":"He says it quietly, not looking at you. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Ask him to tell you exactly what happened, step by step","then":"Neel gets flustered, says \"I don't know,\" and stops talking."},{"text":"Stay calm: \"I'm glad you told me. It's not your fault.\"","then":"Neel nods, and his shoulders drop. \"Okay,\" he says quietly.","best":true},{"text":"Tell him gently he's probably mixing things up","then":"\"Maybe,\" Neel whispers, and goes quiet."},{"text":"Gasp, and say you're going to the pool right now","then":"Neel starts to cry, frightened that he's caused trouble."}],"why":"Staying calm and believing him tells him it's not his fault, and keeps him talking."},{"prompt":"Next morning is a swimming day. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Send him anyway, so nothing seems out of the ordinary","then":"Neel clings to the car door, and goes in with red eyes."},{"text":"Go with him and watch the changing room yourself","then":"Neel spends the class looking at you, tense and unhappy."},{"text":"Keep him home from swimming until you've got advice","then":"Neel looks relieved when you say he can stay home today.","best":true},{"text":"Ask him again whether it's really true before deciding","then":"Neel's lip trembles. \"I told you already,\" he whispers."}],"why":"Keeping him away from the risk while you get advice keeps him safe."},{"prompt":"That afternoon, the worry won't leave you. Who do you turn to?","options":[{"text":"Call Childline 1098 for guidance on what to do next","then":"The counsellor listens, and explains the next steps and who else should know.","best":true},{"text":"Storm into the class and demand answers from the coach","then":"The coach gets defensive, and the whole class hears Neel's name."},{"text":"Post a warning in the parents' WhatsApp group tonight","then":"The group explodes with rumours, and another parent forwards it on."},{"text":"Ask the family elders first, and do whatever they say","then":"Dadi says to keep it quiet for the family's sake, and you're stuck."}],"why":"Expert guidance helps you act the right way, for Neel and for other children."},{"prompt":"A week later, Neel asks if he did something bad by telling. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"That it's all over now, so let's forget about it","then":"Neel nods, but still wonders if it was his fault."},{"text":"That he did well, but next time he must tell you sooner","then":"Neel's face falls. He hears that he got it wrong."},{"text":"That telling was brave, and none of it was his fault","then":"Neel smiles a little. \"Not my fault,\" he repeats, and hugs you.","best":true},{"text":"That he mustn't talk about it with anyone else, ever","then":"Neel nods solemnly. Another secret, just a different one."}],"why":"Hearing it's not his fault, and that telling was brave, keeps him telling."}],"debrief":"Take a child's safety worry seriously: believe them, say it's not their fault, and seek guidance (see Be the Safe Adult).","relearn":"Act on a child-safety worry by taking it seriously and seeking guidance; don't brush it off."},
  {"id":"tk-057","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: the scripts you give your child are the ones you may never have got yourself, and that's the cycle breaking. Feel it?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Feel it","Cycle breaking","Giving what I missed"],"affirm":"Giving your child the words and openness you may never have received is exactly how the silence cycle breaks.","relearn":"The scripts you give your child are the ones you never got; that's the cycle breaking.","persona":"any","source":"cycle breaking"},
  {"id":"tk-058","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two moves that aren't sustainable, among the ways that guide a child's RSE for years.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Ongoing small talks as they grow","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"One big talk and never again","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Staying askable for years","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Waiting till you feel fully expert","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Answering questions as they come up","trick":false}],"why":"'One big talk and done' and 'wait till you're an expert' are the red flags.","relearn":"Guiding a child's RSE is ongoing small talks and an open door over years, not one big talk or waiting to feel expert.","persona":"any","source":"sustainable guidance"},
  {"id":"tk-059","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match a parent's worry to the reassuring tool.","pairs":[{"left":"'I'll freeze on a hard question'","right":"A ready, simple script"},{"left":"'I don't know enough'","right":"Learn it together, age by age"},{"left":"'Something my child said worries me'","right":"Safeguarding guidance (Be the Safe Adult)"},{"left":"'I already fumbled one answer'","right":"Go back and repair it"},{"left":"'I'm doing this all alone'","right":"Invite your co-parent to be askable too"}],"relearn":"Each parent worry has a tool: a script, learning together, safeguarding guidance, repairing a fumble, or inviting a co-parent in.","persona":"any","source":"worry to tool"},
  {"id":"tk-060","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: the goal isn't one perfect talk. It's staying the askable parent across hundreds of small moments. Land for you?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Lands","Stay askable","Many small moments"],"affirm":"There is no single perfect talk; what protects a child is a parent who stays approachable across many small everyday moments.","relearn":"It was never one big talk. It's staying the parent your child can come back to, over and over.","persona":"any","source":"the long game"},
  {"id":"tk-061","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"bring co-parent in","hook":"Your partner Ravi wants you to handle every awkward talk with your son Ansh, 11.","setup":"He says it while you both fold laundry.","steps":[{"prompt":"Ravi says: \"You're better at this stuff. I'd just make it weird.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Fine. I'll handle all the awkward stuff myself, then.\"","then":"Ravi looks relieved. You fold the rest of the laundry in silence."},{"text":"\"Let's do it together. Just being calm and askable matters.\"","then":"Ravi sighs. \"Calm and askable. I could maybe do that.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"You're his parent too. It's your job as much as mine.\"","then":"Ravi bristles. \"I didn't say I wouldn't. I said it's awkward.\""},{"text":"\"Honestly, you're right. You'd probably make it a bit weird.\"","then":"Ravi laughs, a little hurt, and the job stays yours."}],"why":"Lowering the bar to calm and askable makes it possible for him to join in."},{"prompt":"Ravi asks: \"But what would I even say if he asked me something?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Just tell him to come and ask me instead, like always.\"","then":"Ravi agrees, relieved, with no words ready if Ansh asks him anyway."},{"text":"\"Just wing it. You'll work it out in the moment.\"","then":"Ravi looks more nervous than before."},{"text":"\"Say 'good question', then keep it short and true.\"","then":"Ravi nods slowly. \"Good question, short and true. Okay.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"I'll write you a full script to learn by heart.\"","then":"Ravi reads the first page and groans. \"I'll never remember this.\""}],"why":"One simple formula gives him confidence without needing to be an expert."},{"prompt":"A week later, Ravi admits: \"Ansh asked me about wet dreams and I froze.\"","options":[{"text":"\"See? This is exactly why I should just do it all.\"","then":"Ravi's face falls, and he quietly steps back from the talks."},{"text":"\"Oh no. Now he'll never ask you anything again.\"","then":"Ravi winces, and feels worse than before."},{"text":"\"Don't worry. I'll talk to Ansh tonight instead.\"","then":"Ravi nods, grateful, and misses his chance to repair it."},{"text":"\"That happens. Go back and say, 'Let's talk now.'\"","then":"Ravi looks relieved. \"I can go back? Okay. I'll try tonight.\"","best":true}],"why":"Showing that a fumble can be repaired keeps him in, not out."},{"prompt":"Weeks later, Ravi says: \"Ansh came to me with a question today. I actually answered it.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Great. So you'll take all the talks from now on?\"","then":"Ravi laughs uneasily. \"Let's not get carried away.\""},{"text":"\"That's huge. Now Ansh has two of us he can ask.\"","then":"Ravi grins. \"Two doors, then,\" he says. \"I like that.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"What did you tell him? Let me check you got it right.\"","then":"Ravi's smile fades as you go through his answer line by line."},{"text":"\"Good. Let's not make a big deal of it, though.\"","then":"Ravi shrugs. The moment passes without him feeling proud."}],"why":"Celebrating his effort shows how much a second trusted door is worth."}],"relearn":"Inviting a co-parent to simply be calm and askable shares the job and doubles a child's trusted doors."},
  {"id":"tk-062","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"role-play","persona":"Priya","source":"graceful in public","hook":"Guests are over for chai when your child asks a blunt body question, and the room goes quiet.","setup":"Every eye in the room turns to you.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child asks again: \"Why do boys have a penis and girls don't?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Don't be rude. We never discuss that in this house.\"","then":"Their face goes red. \"Sorry,\" they whisper, near tears."},{"text":"\"Ha! Kids say the funniest things, don't they?\"","then":"The guests laugh. \"What's funny?\" your child asks, unsure."},{"text":"\"Great question. I'll answer it after the guests go.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, and go back to their biscuit.","best":true},{"text":"\"Good question, but not now. Off you go and play.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they mumble, and trail off to play."}],"why":"A calm park-it-for-later keeps the question safe without shaming your child in front of others."},{"prompt":"A guest laughs and says: \"Such a modern child! In our day, we'd get a slap.\"","options":[{"text":"\"I know. I'll have a word with them later.\"","then":"The guest nods approvingly. \"Good. Nip it in the bud.\""},{"text":"\"Ha, yes. They do ask the strangest things.\"","then":"Everyone laughs. \"Mine were just the same,\" another guest adds."},{"text":"\"We like them to ask us. It keeps them safe.\"","then":"The guest blinks, then shrugs. \"Times change, I suppose.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"And look how well that worked out for all of you.\"","then":"The guest's smile vanishes. \"Well, excuse me,\" she says stiffly."}],"why":"A calm, short stand backs your child without starting a fight with guests."},{"prompt":"After the guests leave, your child asks: \"Did I do something bad?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Not bad, but questions like that embarrass people.\"","then":"They nod slowly. \"So I shouldn't ask about bodies?\""},{"text":"\"No. It was a good question, and I'm glad you asked.\"","then":"Their face clears. \"So will you tell me now?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Let's not talk about it anymore, okay?\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say quietly, though they still look puzzled."},{"text":"\"A little. You embarrassed me in front of everyone.\"","then":"Their eyes fill. \"I didn't mean to.\""}],"why":"Telling them the question was good stops them feeling shamed for asking."},{"prompt":"Your child climbs up beside you and asks quietly: \"So why are boys and girls different?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Boys and girls just have different private places, beta.\"","then":"\"But what are they called?\" they ask."},{"text":"\"You're too young for that. Maybe when you're ten or so.\"","then":"They look away. \"Everyone always says I'm too young.\""},{"text":"\"Boys have a penis and girls a vulva. Both are private.\"","then":"\"Private means just mine?\" they ask.","best":true},{"text":"\"That's just how it is. Now go and play.\"","then":"They sigh. \"That's not a real answer.\""}],"why":"Proper names, said calmly, give a true answer and help keep your child safe."}],"relearn":"A graceful park-it-for-later keeps the question safe to ask without shaming the child in front of others."},
  {"id":"tk-063","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"right-sized answers","hook":"You over-explain when you're nervous. Your six-year-old Vihaan asks what 'sex' means, after hearing it in a film.","steps":[{"prompt":"He asks during the ad break, eyes still on the TV. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Give one short, true answer, and see if he wants more","then":"Vihaan nods. \"Okay,\" he says, and turns back to the film.","best":true},{"text":"Deliver a full, nervous lecture on bodies and babies","then":"Vihaan fidgets, then asks if the film is back on yet."},{"text":"Say he's too young, and change the channel","then":"Vihaan shrugs, and asks his cousin at the weekend."},{"text":"Ask him to wait until you've read up on it properly","then":"Vihaan shrugs. You spend all evening reading up for a one-line answer."}],"why":"A short, true answer is what a six-year-old can take in."},{"prompt":"Next morning, Vihaan asks whether animals have babies too. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say yes, lots of animals make babies too, and stop there","then":"Vihaan nods. \"Like our neighbour's puppies,\" he says, satisfied.","best":true},{"text":"Explain how dozens of different animals make babies","then":"Vihaan's eyes glaze over somewhere around the fish."},{"text":"Ask him why he's asking so many questions lately","then":"Vihaan shrugs. \"I just wondered,\" he says, a little warier."},{"text":"Say yes, exactly the same way people do, and leave it at that","then":"Vihaan nods, picturing cows at a wedding."}],"why":"Answering only what he asked lets him set the pace."},{"prompt":"That weekend, Vihaan asks why you looked nervous when he asked. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say it's new for you too, but you're glad he asks","then":"Vihaan grins. \"I can teach you,\" he offers.","best":true},{"text":"Say you weren't nervous at all, not one bit","then":"Vihaan squints. \"You were a bit,\" he says."},{"text":"Say those questions make all grown-ups uncomfortable","then":"Vihaan nods, and files the topic under 'makes Papa nervous'."},{"text":"Say you'll be much better at it once he's older","then":"Vihaan shrugs, unsure whether to ask again before then."}],"why":"Being honest about your nerves shows him questions are still welcome."},{"prompt":"A month later, Vihaan asks a new body question just before bed. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Answer just what he asked, briefly, and say ask anytime","then":"Vihaan yawns. \"Okay. Night,\" he says, and snuggles down.","best":true},{"text":"Cover everything you think he'll need for the next year","then":"Twenty minutes later, Vihaan is asleep and you're still talking."},{"text":"Say it's too late at night for questions","then":"Vihaan sighs and rolls over."},{"text":"Answer briefly, but warn him not to ask at school","then":"Vihaan nods, and wonders what's wrong with asking."}],"why":"Short answers, with the door left open, bring him back for more."}],"debrief":"Answer just the question asked, simply, and let your child come back for more, rather than over-explaining.","relearn":"Answer the actual question simply; over-explaining overwhelms a child and closes the door."},
  {"id":"tk-064","cat":"early-years","type":"role-play","persona":"Divya","source":"name it plainly","hook":"You're changing the baby's nappy while your four-year-old Aarav watches closely.","setup":"He leans in, curious, as she kicks her legs.","steps":[{"prompt":"Aarav points and asks: \"What's that called? She doesn't have a willy like me.\"","options":[{"text":"\"That's her vulva. Yours is called a penis. Proper names.\"","then":"Aarav tries the words out. \"Vulva. Penis.\" He nods, very serious.","best":true},{"text":"\"We don't say words like that, beta. It's rude.\"","then":"\"But what IS it?\" Aarav whines, and asks again, louder."},{"text":"\"That's just her su-su. Now pass me the wipes.\"","then":"\"Su-su,\" Aarav repeats. \"Is mine a su-su too?\""},{"text":"\"Girls and boys are just made differently down there, beta.\"","then":"Aarav frowns. \"But what's it called, though?\""}],"why":"Plain names, said like elbow or knee, remove the shame and give him words that keep him safe."},{"prompt":"Aarav says: \"My friend Kunal calls it a willy. Is that the real name?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Lots of people say that. The real name is penis.\"","then":"Aarav looks proud. \"I'll tell Kunal the real one,\" he says.","best":true},{"text":"\"Kunal shouldn't be talking about things like that.\"","then":"\"Why? Is it naughty?\" Aarav asks, looking worried."},{"text":"\"Willy is fine. You don't need the proper word.\"","then":"Aarav nods. \"Okay, willy,\" he says, and the proper word is gone."},{"text":"\"Don't listen to Kunal. Only ask me about these things.\"","then":"Aarav shrugs. \"But Kunal knows lots of stuff.\""}],"why":"Accepting the nickname while giving the real word keeps it simple and honest."},{"prompt":"Aarav asks: \"Can I show Kunal mine at school?\"","options":[{"text":"\"No. Private parts are just for you. We keep them covered.\"","then":"Aarav thinks. \"And Kunal's are just for Kunal?\" You nod.","best":true},{"text":"\"Chhi! What a dirty idea. Don't ever say that again, Aarav.\"","then":"Aarav's face crumples. \"I didn't know,\" he whispers."},{"text":"\"No, because everyone will laugh at you.\"","then":"\"Why would they laugh?\" Aarav asks, confused."},{"text":"\"Ask your teacher tomorrow what she thinks.\"","then":"\"Okay!\" Aarav says, already planning to ask in front of everyone."}],"why":"Privacy as 'just for you' is a clear rule that doesn't make his body shameful."}],"relearn":"Naming body parts as plainly as elbows removes shame and gives a child the words that keep them safe."},
  {"id":"tk-065","cat":"early-years","type":"role-play","persona":"Divya","source":"safe grown-up rule","hook":"Your four-year-old Tara starts playschool next week. You want her to know the safe grown-up rule.","setup":"At bedtime, she's full of school questions.","steps":[{"prompt":"Tara asks: \"Will the teachers be the boss of me?\"","options":[{"text":"\"They'll help you. But you're the boss of your body.\"","then":"Tara thinks about it. \"Only me? Even at school?\" she asks.","best":true},{"text":"\"Yes. Just be good and do whatever grown-ups say.\"","then":"Tara nods seriously. \"Whatever they say. Okay.\""},{"text":"\"Yes, and if you're naughty, they'll tell me.\"","then":"Tara looks worried. \"What if I'm naughty by mistake?\""},{"text":"\"Don't worry about that. School is going to be fun!\"","then":"Tara grins. \"Is there a slide?\" she asks, and forgets her question."}],"why":"Naming her body as hers is the base the rest of the rule stands on."},{"prompt":"Tara asks: \"What if someone touches me somewhere I don't like?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Say no, get away, tell me. If you couldn't, still tell.\"","then":"Tara repeats it. \"No, go away, tell.\" She counts on her fingers.","best":true},{"text":"\"Nobody at your school would ever do that, beta.\"","then":"Tara looks unsure. \"But what if they did?\""},{"text":"\"Just stay close to your teacher, and you'll be safe.\"","then":"Tara thinks. \"What if she's busy with the other kids?\""},{"text":"\"Don't be scared, beta. Just be good and you'll be fine.\"","then":"Tara goes quiet. \"So if I'm good, nobody will?\""}],"why":"Simple steps ending with you, and 'still tell' means it's never her fault if she couldn't."},{"prompt":"Tara asks: \"What if a grown-up says it's a secret?\"","options":[{"text":"\"No one should ask you to keep a body secret. Tell me.\"","then":"Tara nods. \"Body secrets get told,\" she says, trying it out.","best":true},{"text":"\"Then keep it. Grown-ups usually know best.\"","then":"Tara nods. \"Okay. Grown-ups know best.\""},{"text":"\"Why would anyone say that to you? Who said that, Tara?\"","then":"Tara looks startled. \"Nobody! I was just asking.\""},{"text":"\"Secrets are bad. Never keep any secret at all.\"","then":"Tara looks upset. \"Not even Papa's birthday surprise?\""}],"why":"A clear 'no body secrets' rule is one of the strongest protections a child can carry."},{"prompt":"Tara asks, sleepily: \"Will you be cross if I tell you?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Never. I'll be glad you told me, whatever it is.\"","then":"Tara smiles and closes her eyes. \"Good,\" she mumbles.","best":true},{"text":"\"Only if you've done something naughty.\"","then":"Tara goes quiet. \"Then I might not tell,\" she whispers."},{"text":"\"That depends on what it is, doesn't it?\"","then":"Tara frowns. \"Then I don't know,\" she mumbles, pulling up the blanket."},{"text":"\"Let's hope nothing like that ever happens to you.\"","then":"Tara yawns. \"But what if it does?\""}],"why":"A promise that telling never gets her into trouble is what makes a child tell."}],"relearn":"A clear 'tell me, and you'll never be in trouble' rule gives a child permission to disclose, unlike 'obey grown-ups'."},
  {"id":"tk-066","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: teaches a young child body safety, or accidentally undermines it?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"‘You can say no to unwanted touch’"},{"id":"b","text":"‘Always let elders hug and kiss you’"},{"id":"c","text":"‘Tell me anything, no secrets about bodies’"},{"id":"d","text":"‘Good kids never refuse adults’"},{"id":"e","text":"‘Your body belongs to you’"},{"id":"f","text":"‘Keep this just between us, don't tell’"}],"bins":[{"id":"safety","label":"Builds safety","valence":"pos"},{"id":"undermine","label":"Undermines it","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"safety","b":"undermine","c":"safety","d":"undermine","e":"safety","f":"undermine"},"relearn":"'Say no', 'no body secrets' and 'your body is yours' build safety; 'always let elders', 'never refuse adults' and 'keep this secret' undermine it.","persona":"any","source":"safety or not","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-067","type":"match","hook":"Match each young-child question to a simple, honest answer.","pairs":[{"left":"'Why is my body different from my sibling's?'","right":"Bodies come in different kinds, both are normal"},{"left":"'What's that for?'","right":"A calm, correct, one-line answer"},{"left":"'Can I say no to a hug?'","right":"Yes, your body is yours"},{"left":"'Where do babies come from?'","right":"A simple, true answer at your level"},{"left":"'Is it okay to feel curious?'","right":"Yes, and you can always ask me"}],"relearn":"Young children's body questions each have a simple, honest, shame-free answer that keeps them curious and safe.","persona":"Priya","source":"honest little answers","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-068","cat":"middle-years","type":"role-play","persona":"Divya","source":"normalise changes","hook":"Your pre-teen has started wearing baggy clothes and seems embarrassed about their changing body.","setup":"Today they're refusing to dress for a cousin's birthday party.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child mumbles: \"Everything about me looks weird now.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Everyone goes through an awkward phase. It passes.\"","then":"\"So I'm awkward,\" they say, flatly."},{"text":"\"What's happening to your body is normal and healthy.\"","then":"They glance up. \"Even the spots? And the hair?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"You're being far too sensitive about all this.\"","then":"They pull the hood over their head. \"Forget it.\""},{"text":"\"Nonsense, you look fine. Hurry up and get dressed.\"","then":"\"You're not even listening,\" they mutter."}],"why":"Naming the changes as normal and healthy replaces embarrassment with reassurance."},{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"Did you feel like this at my age?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Yes, often. And I wish I'd had someone to ask.\"","then":"\"Really?\" They sit up a little. \"What was it like?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"A bit, but it's different for your generation.\"","then":"\"So you don't really get it,\" they say."},{"text":"\"That's not important. Just get ready.\"","then":"They shrug. \"Whatever,\" they say, turning away."},{"text":"\"No. We didn't make such a fuss back then.\"","then":"\"So it's just me,\" they sigh."}],"why":"Sharing your own feelings shows them they're not alone."},{"prompt":"Before the party, your child asks: \"Can I ask you body stuff without it being weird?\"","options":[{"text":"\"It'll always be a bit weird. That's life.\"","then":"\"Great,\" they mutter, and go to change."},{"text":"\"Only if it's something important.\"","then":"\"How do I know what's important?\" they ask."},{"text":"\"Anytime. Ask me anything. It won't be weird.\"","then":"They smile, just a little. \"Okay. Later, then.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Sure, but only when it's just the two of us.\"","then":"\"So it is kind of secret,\" they say."}],"why":"An open invitation keeps them bringing the changes to you."}],"relearn":"Warmly normalising the changes and inviting questions replaces embarrassment with reassurance."},
  {"id":"tk-069","cat":"middle-years","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a healthy pre-teen online habit to encourage, or a risk to address?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Telling you about anything that feels off"},{"id":"b","text":"Sharing private info with strangers"},{"id":"c","text":"Keeping passwords and privacy"},{"id":"d","text":"Meeting online 'friends' alone"},{"id":"e","text":"Asking before downloading new apps"},{"id":"f","text":"Posting their location for all to see"}],"bins":[{"id":"encourage","label":"Encourage it","valence":"pos"},{"id":"address","label":"Address the risk","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"encourage","b":"address","c":"encourage","d":"address","e":"encourage","f":"address"},"relearn":"Telling you, keeping privacy and asking first are healthy; sharing info, meeting strangers and open location are risks.","persona":"Vikram","source":"encourage or address"},
  {"id":"tk-070","cat":"middle-years","type":"branch","persona":"Divya","source":"answer honestly","hook":"Your pre-teen asks, point-blank, what sex actually is. You didn't expect it this early.","steps":[{"prompt":"They're waiting, half embarrassed and half curious. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Answer honestly and simply, without any shame","then":"They listen, cheeks pink, then nod. 'Okay. That makes sense.'","best":true},{"text":"Laugh and say they'll understand when they're older","then":"They force a laugh too, and ask a friend instead."},{"text":"Act shocked and refuse to answer","then":"They mumble 'forget it'. Later you see them searching on the tablet."},{"text":"Answer, but make it sound scary so they stay away","then":"They look alarmed, and now the whole topic feels frightening."}],"why":"An honest, age-right answer keeps their trust and gives them safe, true information."},{"prompt":"A few days later, they ask whether people only have sex to make babies. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say it's also about closeness, when both people want it","then":"They think about that. 'So both people have to want it?' they ask.","best":true},{"text":"Say it's only ever for making babies","then":"They nod. Friends will soon tell them something different."},{"text":"Say that's quite enough questions on that topic now","then":"They drop it, and take the next question somewhere else."},{"text":"Say it's for married couples, and leave it there","then":"They nod, but still don't know whether it's only about babies."}],"why":"Honest facts plus 'both people want it' give truth and consent in one answer."},{"prompt":"Your sister hears about these talks and worries they'll make your child try it sooner. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Tell her she has no idea what kids face today","then":"She bristles, and the chat turns into a sulk."},{"text":"Say they'd find it all online anyway, so why not","then":"She frowns. 'That's not much of a reason,' she says."},{"text":"Say honest talks make children safer, not more eager","then":"She pauses. 'I wish someone had talked to us,' she says.","best":true},{"text":"Agree, and decide to say nothing more for a few years","then":"She nods, relieved. You feel uneasy about what you'll say next time."}],"why":"Talking makes children safer, not earlier, and that's worth sharing with family too."},{"prompt":"A month later, your pre-teen asks how old people should be before having sex. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Share your view, and say both must be old enough and want it","then":"They nod slowly. 'So age and choice both matter,' they say.","best":true},{"text":"Name an age, and say that's the end of the questions","then":"They note the number, and the door closes on everything else."},{"text":"Say it's entirely up to them, whatever they feel","then":"They look a little lost. 'But what do you think?' they ask."},{"text":"Share your values, then quickly change the subject to school","then":"They hear your view, but nothing about choice or staying safe."}],"why":"Your values, plus the fact that both must be old enough and want it, guide them with consent at the centre."}],"debrief":"Answer an earlier-than-expected frank question honestly and age-appropriately, without shame.","relearn":"Answer frank pre-teen questions honestly and without shame; being scandalised just sends them elsewhere."},
  {"id":"tk-071","cat":"middle-years","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two moves that leave a pre-teen unprepared for the years ahead.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Honest prep before changes and online life","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Leaving them to learn from peers and feeds","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"An open door for any worry","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Saying nothing until problems show up","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Pairing a first phone with safety chats","trick":false}],"why":"Leaving them to peers/feeds and staying silent until problems hit leave a child exposed; honest prep and an open door ready them.","relearn":"Prepare a pre-teen with honest prep and an open door, not by leaving them to peers and the feed.","persona":"any","source":"best prep"},
  {"id":"tk-072","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"unflustered teen","hook":"An explicit clip pops up in your daughter Isha's class group. She's 13, and she saw it.","setup":"She comes to find you, looking shaken.","steps":[{"prompt":"Isha asks: \"Why would people even do that? It looked horrible.\"","options":[{"text":"\"That's disgusting. I don't want to hear another word.\"","then":"Isha flinches. \"I didn't post it,\" she says, and leaves."},{"text":"\"Just forget you ever saw it. It's really nothing.\"","then":"Isha nods, but the image stays with her all evening."},{"text":"\"Thank you for asking me. Most of that isn't real life.\"","then":"Isha exhales. \"Okay. I really didn't want to see it.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Which boy posted it? Give me his name right now.\"","then":"Isha panics. \"Please don't. Everyone will know I told.\""}],"why":"Thanking her keeps you her first stop, and the honest fact takes the fear out."},{"prompt":"Later, Isha asks: \"Am I in trouble for seeing it?\"","options":[{"text":"\"No. You didn't choose to see it. Telling me was brave.\"","then":"Isha's shoulders drop. \"Okay. I was so scared you'd be cross.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Not this time. But leave that group right now.\"","then":"\"So it's my fault if they post again?\" she asks, confused."},{"text":"\"You will be, if you ever see something like that again.\"","then":"Isha nods, and decides next time she'll keep quiet."},{"text":"\"Let me keep your phone for a while, just in case.\"","then":"Isha hands it over, and learns that telling you costs her the phone."}],"why":"Saying she's not in trouble makes it safe for her to tell you next time."},{"prompt":"The next morning, Isha says: \"My friends say it's still going round. What do we do?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Let's report it on the app together, and tell your class teacher.\"","then":"Isha nods. \"Okay, together.\" You report it, and her teacher tells the class to delete it.","best":true},{"text":"\"Just stay out of it. It's not your problem to fix.\"","then":"Isha shrugs. \"Okay.\" The clip keeps going round, from group to group."},{"text":"\"I'll post about it in the class parents' group tonight.\"","then":"The parents' group explodes, and by morning everyone is asking who told."},{"text":"\"Message whoever posted it and ask them to take it down.\"","then":"Isha hesitates. \"They'll just screenshot my message and laugh at me.\""}],"why":"Reporting it with her, and telling the school, helps stop the spread and shows her what to do."},{"prompt":"A few days later, Isha asks: \"Why do the boys in class keep laughing about it?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Boys will be boys. Just keep away from them.\"","then":"Isha shrugs. She starts to think it's just normal."},{"text":"\"Some think it's cool. Respect is caring how others feel.\"","then":"Isha thinks. \"Yeah. The girls in class hate it, and nobody asks them.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Just ignore them. That kind of thing isn't your concern, beta.\"","then":"Isha drops it, but the laughing still bothers her."},{"text":"\"Because they're awful. Don't talk to any of them.\"","then":"Isha frowns. \"Not all of them. Kabir said it was gross.\""}],"why":"Naming respect gives her a way to judge what she sees, beyond the laughter."}],"relearn":"Meeting an explicit question with calm porn-literacy keeps you the trusted source over the algorithm."},
  {"id":"tk-073","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"support not control","hook":"Your son Arjun, 16, admits his girlfriend keeps asking him for a private photo.","setup":"He mumbles it over late-night chai.","steps":[{"prompt":"Arjun says: \"She says everyone does it. Maybe I'm being a baby.\"","options":[{"text":"\"That's it. You're not seeing her again. End of discussion, Arjun.\"","then":"Arjun's jaw sets. \"You don't get it,\" he says, and texts her under the table."},{"text":"\"Glad you told me. No one should pressure you. What do you want?\"","then":"Arjun looks up. \"I don't want to. I just don't want her angry.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Honestly, it's normal at your age. Just be careful.\"","then":"Arjun nods slowly, less sure than before about saying no."},{"text":"\"Boys don't get pressured. Just say no and move on.\"","then":"Arjun reddens. \"Right. Okay.\" He stares into his chai."}],"why":"Believing him and asking what he wants keeps him talking. Her pushing is not his fault."},{"prompt":"Arjun asks: \"But what do I even say to her without a fight?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Just tell her your parents check your phone, so you really can't.\"","then":"Arjun likes it, but she keeps asking, now for when you're not around."},{"text":"\"Send her something silly instead, and turn it into a joke.\"","then":"She laughs, then asks again the next day."},{"text":"\"Just: 'I'm not okay with that.' Someone who cares accepts it.\"","then":"Arjun repeats it under his breath. \"Okay. That's not so hard.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Give me your phone. I'll message her myself, right now.\"","then":"Arjun clutches it. \"No way. That would be so embarrassing.\""}],"why":"His own clear no teaches him his limits count, and gives him words to hold on to."},{"prompt":"Days later, Arjun says: \"She called me boring. She might break up with me.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Good riddance, honestly. You're better off without her.\"","then":"Arjun bristles. \"You don't even know her,\" he says."},{"text":"\"Then break up with her first, before she can do it.\"","then":"Arjun frowns. \"That's not what I want either.\""},{"text":"\"Ouch. But pressure isn't love. I'm with you either way.\"","then":"Arjun nods slowly. \"I'm not sending it,\" he says. \"Whatever she decides.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Don't worry about it. She'll forget about it in a week.\"","then":"Arjun isn't sure, and checks his phone every few minutes."}],"why":"Naming that pressure isn't love, and backing whatever he decides, supports him without control."}],"relearn":"Supporting their agency while offering help keeps a pressured teen talking to you, unlike taking over."},
  {"id":"tk-074","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"sort","persona":"any","source":"come or hide","hook":"Sort: keeps a teen coming to you, or pushes them to hide things?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Calm, non-judgemental listening"},{"id":"b","text":"Punishing them for honesty"},{"id":"c","text":"Respecting their growing autonomy"},{"id":"d","text":"Snooping and shaming"},{"id":"e","text":"Thanking them for telling you hard things"},{"id":"f","text":"Threatening to tell the whole family"}],"bins":[{"id":"comes","label":"Keeps them coming","valence":"pos"},{"id":"hides","label":"Makes them hide","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"comes","b":"hides","c":"comes","d":"hides","e":"comes","f":"hides"},"relearn":"Calm listening, respecting autonomy and thanking them keep a teen coming to you; punishing honesty, snooping and threats make them hide."},
  {"id":"tk-075","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"keep the door open","hook":"Your daughter Riya, 16, tells you she's dating a classmate. You'd hoped she would wait till college.","steps":[{"prompt":"She's watching your face for a reaction. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say she has to end it now or lose her phone for good","then":"Riya's face closes. \"Fine,\" she says. Her phone stays face down from then on."},{"text":"Thank her for telling you, and say you'd hoped she'd wait","then":"Riya relaxes a little. \"I know. But he's really nice. Can I tell you about him?\"","best":true},{"text":"Smile and say it's fine, keeping your worries to yourself","then":"Riya beams and hugs you. Your worry sits unspoken between you."},{"text":"Go quiet and leave the room to think it over alone","then":"Riya stands alone in the hallway, unsure if she's in trouble."}],"why":"Thanking her keeps her talking, and naming your hope shares your view without a fight."},{"prompt":"A few days later, Riya asks to go to a Saturday movie with friends. You know he'll be there. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Refuse, since you know he'll be there","then":"Riya says \"Fine.\" On Saturday she tells you she's at a friend's house."},{"text":"Say yes without asking anything, to show you trust her","then":"Riya is thrilled. You spend Saturday wondering where they are and how she'll get back."},{"text":"Talk through the plan: who, when, and how she gets home","then":"Riya rolls her eyes at the questions, answers them all, and texts when she's home.","best":true},{"text":"Say yes, then check her location every half hour","then":"Riya notices the checks and switches her phone off halfway through the film."}],"why":"Agreeing a plan together keeps her safe and keeps you in the loop, without spying."},{"prompt":"A month later, Riya comes home upset and admits they've had a fight. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say you knew this would happen and she should end it","then":"\"I knew you'd say that,\" Riya says, and goes to her room."},{"text":"Tell her it's only puppy love and not worth the tears","then":"She wipes her eyes. \"Forget it. You don't get it.\""},{"text":"Help her out by telling her exactly what to text him tonight","then":"Riya listens, says she'll handle it, and you're not sure she will."},{"text":"Listen first, then ask what she thinks a fair partner does","then":"Riya talks for an hour. At the end she says, \"He wasn't very fair, was he?\"","best":true}],"why":"Listening first, then asking, helps her judge the relationship for herself."}],"debrief":"Stay connected and share your view on a teen's choice while keeping the door open, rather than issuing ultimatums.","relearn":"Keep the door open on choices you dislike; ultimatums cost you both influence and trust."},
  {"id":"tk-076","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"both honestly","hook":"Your family holds strong views on relationships before marriage, and your fourteen-year-old Yash has noticed.","setup":"He brings it up while you're both washing the car.","steps":[{"prompt":"Yash asks: \"Do people really have sex before marriage? Our family says it's wrong.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Yes, some do. Here's what we believe, and why.\"","then":"Yash leans in. \"Okay. Why, then?\" he asks.","best":true},{"text":"\"Never mind what others do. Just do as we say.\"","then":"Yash mutters, \"So that's a yes, then.\""},{"text":"\"No. Decent people would never, ever do that, Yash.\"","then":"Yash frowns. \"But my friend's cousin did.\""},{"text":"\"Yes, some do. Everyone decides for themselves.\"","then":"Yash looks at you. \"So you don't mind either way?\""}],"why":"The honest fact, with your belief beside it, gives him both truth and guidance."},{"prompt":"Yash asks: \"But why does our family think it matters so much?\"","options":[{"text":"\"We believe it belongs with deep trust. That's our hope.\"","then":"Yash nods slowly. \"Deep trust. Okay, that makes sense.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Because that's simply how it's always been in this family.\"","then":"Yash shrugs. \"That's not really a reason.\""},{"text":"\"Because anything else brings shame on all of us.\"","then":"Yash frowns. \"So it's about what people think?\""},{"text":"\"Ask your grandfather. He explains it much better.\"","then":"Yash groans. \"He'll just give me a lecture.\""}],"why":"A real reason, shared as your hope, is something he can weigh and keep."},{"prompt":"Yash asks: \"What if I don't agree with you when I'm older?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Then we talk. I'd still want you safe and respectful.\"","then":"Yash smiles a little. \"Okay. That's fair,\" he says.","best":true},{"text":"\"Then don't expect any support from us.\"","then":"Yash goes quiet. \"Okay,\" he says, and looks away."},{"text":"\"You will agree, beta. You'll see when you're older.\"","then":"Yash frowns. \"What if I don't, though?\""},{"text":"\"That's years away. Let's not worry about it now.\"","then":"Yash shrugs. \"But I'm asking now.\""}],"why":"Keeping the door open, even on disagreement, keeps you his trusted voice."}],"relearn":"Pairing the honest facts with your stated values gives a child both safety and your guidance to weigh."},
  {"id":"tk-077","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: an honest fact a child needs for safety, or a value you choose to share?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"How conception and contraception work"},{"id":"b","text":"When your family feels is the right time"},{"id":"c","text":"Consent and how to stay safe"},{"id":"d","text":"Your hopes for their relationships"},{"id":"e","text":"What a healthy, respectful body is owed"},{"id":"f","text":"The role you hope marriage plays one day"}],"bins":[{"id":"fact","label":"Safety fact","valence":"pos"},{"id":"value","label":"Shared value","valence":"tell"}],"key":{"a":"fact","b":"value","c":"fact","d":"value","e":"fact","f":"value"},"relearn":"How bodies, consent and respect work are safety facts; the 'right time' and your hopes are values you choose to share.","persona":"any","source":"fact or value"},
  {"id":"tk-078","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: protects a child, or leaves them exposed?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Honest facts plus your values"},{"id":"b","text":"Silence to 'protect innocence'"},{"id":"c","text":"An open, shame-free door"},{"id":"d","text":"Letting the feed teach instead"},{"id":"e","text":"Answering questions calmly and truthfully"},{"id":"f","text":"Shutting down a question with anger"}],"bins":[{"id":"protects","label":"Protects them","valence":"pos"},{"id":"exposed","label":"Leaves them exposed","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"protects","b":"exposed","c":"protects","d":"exposed","e":"protects","f":"exposed"},"relearn":"Honest facts with values, an open door and calm answers protect; silence, the feed and anger leave a child exposed.","persona":"any","source":"protect or expose"},
  {"id":"tk-079","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"facts over silence","hook":"Your parents live with you, and they believe puberty talk should wait until your nine-year-old Tanya 'needs it'.","steps":[{"prompt":"You've planned to tell Tanya about periods this weekend. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Go ahead with the talk, and tell your parents kindly why","then":"Tanya asks lots of questions. Your father clears his throat but says nothing.","best":true},{"text":"Wait until her periods actually start, to keep the peace at home","then":"Your parents relax. Tanya still has no idea what's coming."},{"text":"Do it in secret and hope your parents never find out","then":"Tanya looks confused when you ask her not to mention it to Dadi."},{"text":"Leave a book in her room and say nothing about it","then":"Tanya flicks through it, blushing, and keeps her questions to herself for now."}],"why":"Preparing her before the changes, kindly and openly, means her first period won't be a shock."},{"prompt":"At dinner, Tanya asks about periods, and your mother says, 'In our house we don't discuss such things.' What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say you respect her, but Tanya's safety needs the facts","then":"Your mother looks away. \"Nobody told me either,\" she says quietly.","best":true},{"text":"Apologise and promise never to bring it up again","then":"Your mother nods, satisfied. Tanya takes her questions to school friends."},{"text":"Tell her those days are over and she's out of touch","then":"Your mother's face falls, and she leaves the room without a word."},{"text":"Say it's really the school's job, so you'll let them handle it","then":"Your mother agrees. Tanya waits for a class that may come too late."}],"why":"Respect for elders and safety facts for your child can go together."},{"prompt":"Next week, Tanya asks why Dadi went quiet when she said 'period'. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say Dadi grew up without these talks, and the word is fine","then":"Tanya nods. \"Maybe I can teach Dadi,\" she says, grinning.","best":true},{"text":"Say Dadi's right, and it's better not to say it aloud","then":"Tanya nods, and learns that periods are something to hide."},{"text":"Say Dadi is old-fashioned, so she can ignore her","then":"Tanya giggles, and next time she's rude to Dadi about it."},{"text":"Say not to mention it in front of Dadi again, to be safe","then":"Tanya nods, and wonders what's so dangerous about the word."}],"why":"Explaining Dadi kindly keeps both the word and the respect."},{"prompt":"A year later, at a cousin's wedding, Tanya whispers that her period has started. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Take her aside, help with a pad, and say it's normal","then":"Tanya breathes out. \"Okay. It's normal,\" she says, and rejoins the dancing.","best":true},{"text":"Hurry her home before any of the relatives find out","then":"Tanya misses the sangeet, feeling she's done something shameful."},{"text":"Hand her over to Dadi, and stay out of it yourself","then":"Dadi takes over with hushed instructions, and Tanya feels it's a secret."},{"text":"Give her a pad and tell her not to tell anyone","then":"Tanya manages, but spends the evening terrified someone will notice."}],"why":"Calm, practical help makes a first period feel expected and supported."}],"debrief":"Give your child the safety facts they need while handling elders kindly; don't withhold them to keep the peace.","relearn":"Prioritise your child's safety facts over keeping the silence elders prefer; do it kindly, but do it."},
  {"id":"tk-080","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"match","hook":"Match a values-laden question to a both-and reply.","pairs":[{"left":"'Is it wrong to want that?'","right":"Here are the facts; here's what we believe"},{"left":"'Everyone's doing it'","right":"Let's separate facts from pressure, and our values"},{"left":"'Why can't I yet?'","right":"The honest reasons, plus our family's view"},{"left":"'You're being old-fashioned'","right":"Fair, here's the fact and why we still feel it"},{"left":"'My friends are allowed'","right":"Their facts may differ; here's ours and our values"}],"relearn":"Values-laden questions each get a both-and reply: honest facts first, then your family's view.","persona":"any","source":"both-and replies"},
  {"id":"tk-081","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","persona":"Divya","source":"repair a fumble","hook":"Yesterday your daughter Zara, 6, asked what 'gay' means. You froze and changed the subject.","setup":"Today she's drawing at the table.","steps":[{"prompt":"Zara says: \"Look, I drew our whole family!\"","options":[{"text":"\"It's lovely! And let's just forget what you asked yesterday.\"","then":"Zara nods, puzzled, and colours a little harder."},{"text":"\"It's lovely. Can we talk about your question from yesterday?\"","then":"Zara looks up, pleased. \"About what gay means? Okay!\"","best":true},{"text":"\"It's lovely, beta. Let's go and put it up on the fridge.\"","then":"Zara beams. \"Okay!\" Then she stops, still thinking about yesterday."},{"text":"\"Lovely. But don't ask me questions like yesterday's again.\"","then":"Zara's face falls. \"Was it a bad question?\""}],"why":"Reopening it yourself shows her no question closes the door for good."},{"prompt":"Zara puts her crayon down and asks: \"So what does gay mean?\"","options":[{"text":"\"It's a grown-up thing. You're too little to understand.\"","then":"Zara frowns. \"I'm six,\" she says, and asks her cousin instead."},{"text":"\"It's a word people use to be mean. Don't say it.\"","then":"Zara nods seriously, and decides it's a bad word."},{"text":"\"It means happy. That's what it used to mean, anyway.\"","then":"Zara looks confused. \"But Vir said it's about two boys.\""},{"text":"\"It's when a man loves a man, or a woman loves a woman.\"","then":"Zara nods. \"Oh. Like my friend Tia's two papas.\"","best":true}],"why":"A simple, true answer at her level is all she needs, and all she asked."},{"prompt":"At dinner, Zara brings it up, and Dadi frowns: \"Who's been teaching her these things?\"","options":[{"text":"\"She asked me. I want her to get simple, true answers.\"","then":"Dadi purses her lips. \"Hm. Well. As long as it's simple,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"\"Not me. She must have picked it up at school.\"","then":"Zara looks at you, puzzled. She knows she asked you."},{"text":"\"Sorry. I'll make sure she doesn't talk like that again.\"","then":"Zara stares at her plate, sure she's said something wrong."},{"text":"\"That's between me and my daughter. Please leave it.\"","then":"Dadi goes stiff, and the rest of dinner is silent."}],"why":"Owning your answer calmly shows Zara her question was okay to ask."}],"relearn":"Going back to repair a fumbled answer models honesty and shows your child the door is genuinely always open."},
  {"id":"tk-082","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a realistic, sustainable parenting-talk habit, or an unrealistic one?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Tiny talks in the car or at bedtime"},{"id":"b","text":"One scheduled formal lecture"},{"id":"c","text":"Answering as questions arise"},{"id":"d","text":"Waiting until you feel fully expert"},{"id":"e","text":"Using everyday cues to start"},{"id":"f","text":"Cramming everything into a single talk"}],"bins":[{"id":"real","label":"Realistic habit","valence":"pos"},{"id":"unreal","label":"Unrealistic","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"real","b":"unreal","c":"real","d":"unreal","e":"real","f":"unreal"},"relearn":"Tiny everyday talks, answering as questions arise and using cues are realistic; a formal lecture, waiting to feel expert and cramming aren't.","persona":"any","source":"realistic habit"},
  {"id":"tk-083","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two moves that make a parent less askable, among the ones that build trust over time.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Welcoming questions without shame","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Reacting with anger or panic","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Repairing when you get one wrong","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Mocking a question as silly","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Thanking them for coming to you","trick":false}],"why":"Anger or panic and mocking a question are the red flags that make you less askable.","relearn":"Become more askable by welcoming questions, repairing missteps and thanking them, not by reacting with anger or mocking.","persona":"any","source":"more askable"},
  {"id":"tk-084","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each age to the headline focus of the talks.","pairs":[{"left":"Around 3-6","right":"Correct names, body safety, consent basics"},{"left":"Around 9-12","right":"Prepare for puberty and online life"},{"left":"13+","right":"Consent, online-literacy, respect in relationships"},{"left":"Any age, after a fumble","right":"Repair it and reopen the door"},{"left":"Any age, a safety worry","right":"Route to help and take it seriously"}],"relearn":"Each age has a headline focus: body safety young, puberty prep before, consent in the teens, plus repair and routing worries at any age.","persona":"any","source":"age to focus"},
  {"id":"tk-900","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Divya","source":"names aren't dirty","hook":"“Using pet names like 'susu-place' keeps it innocent; real names sound dirty.”","myth":{"un":"Using pet names for private parts keeps it innocent; real names sound dirty.","re":"Real names aren't dirty. They let a child describe clearly what happened and who touched where.","why":"A clear word is a safety tool; a vague pet name can hide a disclosure."},"relearn":"Pet names can blur a disclosure; correct names let a child say clearly what happened, which keeps them safer.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-901","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Priya","source":"curiosity is normal","hook":"“A young child who touches their own body or asks about it is misbehaving.”","myth":{"un":"A young child who touches their own body or asks about it is misbehaving.","re":"Body curiosity is normal at this age; calmly teach privacy ('that's something we do in private') without shame.","why":"Shaming normal curiosity teaches secrecy, which makes a child less safe, not more."},"relearn":"Body curiosity is normal; redirect to privacy calmly instead of shaming, so a child stays open with you.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-902","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"any","source":"no exception for family","hook":"“Safe-touch rules are for strangers; you don't need them for family.”","myth":{"un":"Safe-touch rules are for strangers; you don't need them for family.","re":"Most who harm a child are known to them, so the same rules apply to everyone, family included.","why":"'Stranger danger' alone leaves a child unprotected from the people they actually meet."},"relearn":"Safe-touch rules apply to everyone a child knows, not just strangers. 'Stranger danger' alone isn't enough.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-903","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"any","source":"start small not at school","hook":"“Body-safety talk can wait until school teaches it.”","myth":{"un":"Body-safety talk can wait until school teaches it.","re":"Start at home, in tiny everyday moments, like bath time or getting dressed, long before any class covers it.","why":"A child needs these words before they ever face a situation, not after."},"relearn":"Body safety starts at home in small everyday moments, well before school covers it. Don't outsource it.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-904","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Divya","source":"private not shameful","hook":"“Telling a child their private parts are 'private' will make them feel ashamed of their body.”","myth":{"un":"Calling private parts 'private' will make a child feel ashamed of their body.","re":"'Private' means just-for-you, like a diary. It's about boundaries, not shame, and you can say it warmly.","why":"Framed as a boundary, not a flaw, privacy protects without teaching disgust."},"relearn":"'Private' means just-for-you, a boundary not a shame. Framed warmly it protects a child without disgust.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-905","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Priya","source":"tickling counts too","hook":"“If a child laughs while being tickled, it can't be unwanted touch.”","myth":{"un":"If a child laughs while being tickled, it can't be unwanted touch.","re":"A laugh can be a reflex, not a yes. If they say 'stop', stop, so they learn their 'stop' is always honoured.","why":"Honouring 'stop' even in play is how a child learns their no counts everywhere."},"relearn":"A laugh isn't consent. Stopping a tickle when a child says 'stop' teaches them their no is always honoured.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-906","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"any","source":"boys need it too","hook":"“Body-safety and consent talks are really only needed for daughters.”","myth":{"un":"Body-safety and consent talks are really only needed for daughters.","re":"Boys are harmed too and grow into the adults who must respect a no. Every child needs both.","why":"Skipping sons leaves them unprotected and unprepared to respect others."},"relearn":"Body-safety and consent are for every child, not only daughters. Sons are harmed too and must learn to respect a no.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-907","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Divya","source":"repeat not once","hook":"“Once I've told my child the safe-touch rule, the job is done.”","myth":{"un":"Once I've told my child the safe-touch rule, the job is done.","re":"Little ones forget; revisit it lightly and often, like 'look both ways', until it's simply known.","why":"Repetition over years is what makes a safety rule stick at this age."},"relearn":"Safe-touch isn't a one-time talk. Revisit it lightly and often until it's as automatic as looking both ways.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-908","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"any","source":"answer beats silence","hook":"“If I just ignore my child's body question, they'll forget they asked.”","myth":{"un":"If I ignore my child's body question, they'll forget they asked.","re":"They won't forget. They'll learn you're not the place to ask and take the question elsewhere.","why":"Silence doesn't end curiosity; it just redirects it away from you."},"relearn":"Ignoring a body question doesn't end it. It teaches a child to ask someone, or something, less safe than you.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-909","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Priya","source":"feelings have a no","hook":"“Making a child finish a kiss for grandma is just teaching respect.”","myth":{"un":"Making a child finish a kiss for grandma is just teaching respect.","re":"Offer a choice, like a hug, wave or high-five, so respect and a child's bodily 'no' both get to be real.","why":"Forcing affection teaches a child their body's no can be overruled by a grown-up."},"relearn":"Let a child pick how to greet, like a hug, wave or high-five, so they learn respect without losing the right to say no.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-910","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Divya","source":"calm keeps the door","hook":"“Acting shocked when my toddler says a body word will teach them not to say it.”","myth":{"un":"Acting shocked when my toddler says a body word will teach them not to say it.","re":"Shock teaches the word is dangerous and you're not safe to ask. Stay calm and just name it plainly.","why":"A calm face keeps you the person they bring the next, bigger thing to."},"relearn":"Reacting with shock teaches a child the topic is unsafe with you. A calm, plain answer keeps the door open.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-911","type":"sort","persona":"any","source":"safe vs unsafe touch","hook":"Sort each touch as one a young child can flag as safe, or one to tell about.","items":[{"id":"a","text":"A doctor checking you with a parent in the room"},{"id":"b","text":"Someone touching your private parts"},{"id":"c","text":"A hug you said yes to"},{"id":"d","text":"Being asked to keep a touch secret"},{"id":"e","text":"A high-five from a friend"},{"id":"f","text":"A touch that makes you feel 'uh-oh' inside"}],"bins":[{"id":"safe","label":"Safe touch","valence":"pos"},{"id":"tell","label":"Tell a grown-up","valence":"tell"}],"key":{"a":"safe","b":"tell","c":"safe","d":"tell","e":"safe","f":"tell"},"relearn":"Wanted hugs, high-fives and a checkup with a parent are safe; private-part touches, 'keep it secret' and an 'uh-oh' feeling are ones to tell about.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-912","type":"sort","persona":"Divya","source":"now vs later names","hook":"Sort: a body fact a four-year-old is ready for, or one for when they're older?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"The correct name for each private part"},{"id":"b","text":"How pregnancy actually happens"},{"id":"c","text":"Private parts are covered by swimwear"},{"id":"d","text":"What contraception is"},{"id":"e","text":"Everyone's body is a bit different"},{"id":"f","text":"The mechanics of sex"}],"bins":[{"id":"now","label":"Ready now","valence":"pos"},{"id":"later","label":"For later","valence":"uhoh"}],"key":{"a":"now","b":"later","c":"now","d":"later","e":"now","f":"later"},"relearn":"Correct names, the swimwear rule and 'bodies differ' fit a four-year-old; how pregnancy happens, contraception and the mechanics of sex come later.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-913","type":"sort","persona":"any","source":"who is a safe grown-up","hook":"Sort: a 'safe grown-up' a young child could tell, or not a good safety pick?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"A parent or guardian"},{"id":"b","text":"A grown-up who told them to keep a secret"},{"id":"c","text":"A trusted teacher"},{"id":"d","text":"Anyone who gives them sweets"},{"id":"e","text":"A grandparent they feel easy with"},{"id":"f","text":"Whoever says 'don't tell your parents'"}],"bins":[{"id":"safe","label":"A safe grown-up","valence":"pos"},{"id":"no","label":"Not a safe pick","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"safe","b":"no","c":"safe","d":"no","e":"safe","f":"no"},"relearn":"A parent, trusted teacher or easy grandparent are safe grown-ups; anyone wanting secrets, bribing with sweets or saying 'don't tell your parents' is not.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-914","type":"sort","persona":"Divya","source":"good answer vs not","hook":"Sort a reply to a toddler's body question: keeps the door open, or closes it?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"“Great question! That's called a vulva.”"},{"id":"b","text":"“That's rude, don't ask that.”"},{"id":"c","text":"“I don't know. Let's find out together.”"},{"id":"d","text":"“You're too little to know.”"},{"id":"e","text":"“Let's talk about it after lunch.”"},{"id":"f","text":"“We never talk about that here.”"}],"bins":[{"id":"open","label":"Keeps door open","valence":"pos"},{"id":"shut","label":"Closes the door","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"open","b":"shut","c":"open","d":"shut","e":"open","f":"shut"},"relearn":"Naming it calmly, 'let's find out' and 'let's talk after lunch' keep the door open; 'that's rude', 'too little' and 'we never talk about that' close it.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-915","type":"sort","persona":"any","source":"consent moments","hook":"Sort each everyday moment: it can teach a young child consent, or it overrides it?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Letting them choose a hug or a wave"},{"id":"b","text":"Forcing a kiss for a relative"},{"id":"c","text":"Asking before you tickle them"},{"id":"d","text":"Making them sit on a lap they shrink from"},{"id":"e","text":"Pausing a game when they say stop"},{"id":"f","text":"Telling them their no doesn't count with family"}],"bins":[{"id":"teach","label":"Teaches consent","valence":"pos"},{"id":"over","label":"Overrides it","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"teach","b":"over","c":"teach","d":"over","e":"teach","f":"over"},"relearn":"Offering a choice, asking before tickling and pausing at 'stop' teach consent; a forced kiss, a forced lap or 'your no doesn't count' override it.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-916","type":"sort","persona":"Priya","source":"red flag or normal","hook":"Sort what a child reports: a normal moment, or an 'uh-oh' to take seriously?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"“Auntie hugged me, it was nice.”"},{"id":"b","text":"“He touched me and said don't tell.”"},{"id":"c","text":"“My friend and I played tag.”"},{"id":"d","text":"“Uncle says our game is our secret.”"},{"id":"e","text":"“The doctor checked my ear today.”"},{"id":"f","text":"“Someone showed me a scary picture.”"}],"bins":[{"id":"ok","label":"Normal","valence":"pos"},{"id":"uhoh","label":"Take seriously","valence":"uhoh"}],"key":{"a":"ok","b":"uhoh","c":"ok","d":"uhoh","e":"ok","f":"uhoh"},"relearn":"A wanted hug, tag and an ear check are normal; a 'don't tell' touch, a 'secret game' and a scary picture are 'uh-oh' reports to take seriously.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-917","type":"sort","persona":"Vikram","source":"underwear rule","hook":"Sort: fits the simple 'underwear rule' for a young child, or doesn't belong in it?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Parts under your swimsuit are private"},{"id":"b","text":"You must obey every adult, always"},{"id":"c","text":"No one should ask to see or touch them"},{"id":"d","text":"Keep nice secrets and bad secrets alike"},{"id":"e","text":"If someone tries, tell a safe grown-up"},{"id":"f","text":"It's your fault if something happens"}],"bins":[{"id":"in","label":"Part of the rule","valence":"pos"},{"id":"out","label":"Doesn't belong","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"in","b":"out","c":"in","d":"out","e":"in","f":"out"},"relearn":"The underwear rule: private parts are private, no one may ask to see or touch them, and you tell a safe grown-up. It's never your fault.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-918","type":"sort","persona":"Divya","source":"feelings name it","hook":"Sort each body-feeling word a young child can learn to name, or one that isn't a feeling?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Safe and comfy"},{"id":"b","text":"The colour blue"},{"id":"c","text":"An 'uh-oh' tummy feeling"},{"id":"d","text":"The number seven"},{"id":"e","text":"Squirmy and wanting to leave"},{"id":"f","text":"A type of fruit"}],"bins":[{"id":"feel","label":"A body-feeling","valence":"pos"},{"id":"not","label":"Not a feeling","valence":"neutral"}],"key":{"a":"feel","b":"not","c":"feel","d":"not","e":"feel","f":"not"},"relearn":"Naming body-feelings, like safe, an 'uh-oh' tummy, or squirmy, helps a child notice and flag unsafe touch; colours, numbers and fruit aren't feelings.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-919","type":"match","persona":"Divya","source":"name each part","hook":"Match each gentle teaching moment to the correct, plain word to use.","pairs":[{"left":"Bath time, washing","right":"“We wash your vulva and your bottom.”"},{"left":"Getting dressed","right":"“Underwear covers your private parts.”"},{"left":"A scrape near the groin","right":"“Let's clean near your penis.”"},{"left":"Pointing at a picture","right":"“That's a belly button, this is a nipple.”"},{"left":"A toddler's question","right":"“Those are the proper names, like elbow.”"}],"relearn":"Everyday moments, like bath, dressing, a scrape, a picture, or a question, are all chances to use the plain, correct word with no fuss.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-920","type":"match","persona":"any","source":"rule to reason","hook":"Match each body-safety rule to the simple reason a young child can grasp.","pairs":[{"left":"Private parts are private","right":"They're just for you, not for others"},{"left":"No body secrets","right":"Secrets about bodies aren't safe to keep"},{"left":"You can say no","right":"Your body belongs to you"},{"left":"Tell a safe grown-up","right":"They'll help and you won't be in trouble"},{"left":"Trust the 'uh-oh' feeling","right":"It warns you something isn't right"}],"relearn":"Each rule pairs with a child-sized reason: privacy, no body secrets, your body is yours, telling helps, and the 'uh-oh' feeling is a warning.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-921","type":"match","persona":"Priya","source":"calm reply scripts","hook":"Match each tricky toddler question to a calm one-line reply.","pairs":[{"left":"'Why is mummy's body different?'","right":"“Grown-up and child bodies differ.”"},{"left":"'What's a period?'","right":"“A normal thing many bodies do.”"},{"left":"'Why can't I be naked outside?'","right":"“Private parts stay private in public.”"},{"left":"'Did I grow in your tummy?'","right":"“Yes, in a place called the womb.”"},{"left":"'Can boys have long hair?'","right":"“Yes, hair's for everyone.”"}],"relearn":"Each toddler question has a calm, true one-liner ready: no perfect speech needed, just a plain honest answer.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-922","type":"match","persona":"any","source":"safe vs unsafe sort","hook":"Match each touch a young child might meet to whether it's safe or one to tell about.","pairs":[{"left":"A hug you wanted","right":"A safe touch"},{"left":"A touch on a private part","right":"Tell a safe grown-up"},{"left":"A doctor checking, parent present","right":"A safe, okay touch"},{"left":"A 'keep it secret' touch","right":"Tell, even if asked not to"},{"left":"A high-five from a pal","right":"A friendly, safe touch"}],"relearn":"Wanted hugs, a parent-present checkup and a high-five are safe; private-part touches and 'keep it secret' touches are always ones to tell about.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-923","type":"match","persona":"Divya","source":"feeling to action","hook":"Match each body-feeling a young child notices to what they can do about it.","pairs":[{"left":"Feeling safe and happy","right":"Enjoy it, you're okay"},{"left":"An 'uh-oh' tummy feeling","right":"Move away and tell someone"},{"left":"Squirmy, wanting to leave","right":"You're allowed to say 'stop'"},{"left":"Confused by what an adult did","right":"Ask a safe grown-up about it"},{"left":"Scared to tell a secret","right":"Tell anyway, you won't be in trouble"}],"relearn":"A child can pair each feeling with an action: enjoy safe, move away from 'uh-oh', say stop when squirmy, ask when confused, and tell even scary secrets.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-924","type":"match","persona":"Vikram","source":"good answer model","hook":"Match each parent move to what it teaches a young child.","pairs":[{"left":"Answering calmly, no fuss","right":"This topic is safe to ask about"},{"left":"Using the correct names","right":"My body has real, plain words"},{"left":"Respecting their 'no' to a hug","right":"My body belongs to me"},{"left":"Saying 'tell me anything'","right":"I won't get in trouble for telling"},{"left":"Admitting 'I'll find out'","right":"Not knowing is okay"}],"relearn":"Each calm parent move teaches a lesson: the topic is safe, bodies have real words, my body is mine, telling is safe, and not-knowing is fine.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-925","type":"match","persona":"any","source":"myth to truth","hook":"Match each common worry to the reassuring early-years truth.","pairs":[{"left":"'Correct names sound dirty'","right":"They're a protection, like elbow or knee"},{"left":"'Talking gives them ideas'","right":"It makes them safer, not earlier"},{"left":"'They're too young for this'","right":"Body safety starts around age four"},{"left":"'Only girls need consent talks'","right":"Every child needs them"},{"left":"'School will handle it'","right":"It starts at home, in small moments"}],"relearn":"Each worry has a calm truth: names protect, talking makes kids safer, it starts at four, every child needs it, and it begins at home.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-926","type":"match","persona":"Priya","source":"where babies come from","hook":"Match each age-step of 'where do babies come from?' to a simple true answer.","pairs":[{"left":"First, simplest version","right":"“Babies grow in a special place inside.”"},{"left":"'How does it get out?'","right":"“Through an opening, or by surgery.”"},{"left":"'How does it start?'","right":"“From a tiny cell from two grown-ups.”"},{"left":"If you don't know what to say","right":"“Good question! Let's find out.”"},{"left":"What never to say","right":"A stork story or 'don't ask that'"}],"relearn":"'Where do babies come from?' builds in simple true steps: grows inside, comes out a real way, starts from two cells.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-927","cat":"early-years","type":"branch","persona":"Divya","source":"toddler in the supermarket","hook":"In a busy supermarket queue, your three-year-old Reyansh loudly asks what a penis is.","steps":[{"prompt":"People nearby turn to look. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Quietly name it as a body part boys have, and carry on","then":"Reyansh says \"Oh,\" and goes back to pointing at the sweets.","best":true},{"text":"Shush him quickly and whisper, 'We don't say that in shops'","then":"Reyansh looks stung, then says it again, louder, to see what happens."},{"text":"Laugh, and quickly point out the balloons","then":"Reyansh gets distracted. The question waits for another day."},{"text":"Give him a cute nickname instead, like 'your su-su', and move on","then":"Reyansh repeats \"su-su\" happily. The proper word stays a mystery."}],"why":"A calm, quiet, plain answer keeps the word ordinary, so he keeps asking you."},{"prompt":"At the counter, the cashier chuckles, \"Such questions from a little one!\" What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Smile and say you want him to learn the proper names","then":"The cashier shrugs and smiles back. Reyansh grins, pleased with himself.","best":true},{"text":"Apologise and say he picks up odd things somewhere","then":"Reyansh looks up at you, puzzled, as if the word got him in trouble."},{"text":"Tell Reyansh off quietly for embarrassing you","then":"His lip trembles. He clings to your leg for the rest of the queue."},{"text":"Say nothing, pay fast and hurry out","then":"You escape the moment, but Reyansh notices how quickly you left."}],"why":"Owning the proper names in public shows him they're nothing to hide."},{"prompt":"In the car home, Reyansh asks whether girls have a penis too. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say girls have a vulva, and both are private parts","then":"Reyansh repeats \"vulva\" twice and then asks for a song.","best":true},{"text":"Say that's enough questions for today","then":"Reyansh sighs and looks out of the window, his question unanswered."},{"text":"Say girls just don't have anything there","then":"He tells his cousin girls have nothing there, and she's upset."},{"text":"Say girls have a different part, and leave the name out","then":"Reyansh asks, \"What's it called?\" You say you'll tell him later."}],"why":"Naming both parts plainly keeps the words normal and gives him the words that keep children safe."}],"debrief":"A calm, quiet, plain answer keeps you askable; shushing or dodging teaches the topic is shameful.","relearn":"Answer a loud public body question calmly and plainly. Shushing or dodging teaches it's shameful."},
  {"id":"tk-928","cat":"early-years","type":"branch","persona":"Priya","source":"relative gasps at the word","hook":"At Sunday lunch, your five-year-old Anaya says 'vulva' and your mother-in-law looks horrified.","steps":[{"prompt":"Everyone at the table turns to you. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Calmly say you teach proper names to keep her safe","then":"Your mother-in-law purses her lips but says nothing. Anaya goes back to her roti.","best":true},{"text":"Apologise and promise she'll stop using 'those words'","then":"Your mother-in-law nods, satisfied. Anaya stares down at her plate."},{"text":"Scold Anaya for embarrassing you in front of everyone","then":"Anaya bursts into tears and is silent for the rest of lunch."},{"text":"Laugh it off and quickly pass the dal","then":"The moment passes. Anaya looks unsure whether she said something wrong."}],"why":"Backing her calmly, with the reason, protects her safety words without a fight."},{"prompt":"After lunch, your mother-in-law says quietly that such words spoil a child's innocence. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Explain kindly that the words help her speak up if something's wrong","then":"She's quiet for a moment. \"Nobody gave us any words,\" she says slowly.","best":true},{"text":"Agree with her, just to keep the peace at home","then":"She pats your arm, pleased. You feel the safety lesson slip away."},{"text":"Tell her firmly that she's old-fashioned and it's none of her business","then":"Her face tightens. She barely speaks to you for the rest of the day."},{"text":"Say you'll think about it, and change the subject","then":"She takes it as a yes and mentions it to your husband that evening."}],"why":"A kind reason, not a fight or a surrender, keeps the names and the relationship."},{"prompt":"That night, Anaya asks if vulva was a rude word. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say it's the proper name, like elbow, and fine to say","then":"Anaya smiles. \"Elbow, knee, vulva,\" she chants, and giggles.","best":true},{"text":"Tell her to use it only at home so nobody gets upset","then":"Anaya nods seriously and files the word away as something to hide."},{"text":"Suggest a nicer word, like 'down there'","then":"Anaya agrees. The proper word quietly drops out of her vocabulary."},{"text":"Say Dadi was just surprised, and leave it there","then":"Anaya still isn't sure. She doesn't say the word again for weeks."}],"why":"A plain 'no, it's the right word' keeps her safety word and keeps her asking you."}],"debrief":"Calmly backing the names protects your child; apologising or scolding trades safety for comfort.","relearn":"Back the proper names calmly when a relative gasps. Don't apologise them away or scold."},
  {"id":"tk-929","cat":"early-years","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"child resists a relative","hook":"At a cousin's engagement party, your four-year-old Kiara clings to you when Tauji holds out his arms for a hug.","steps":[{"prompt":"Tauji waits, arms still out. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say Kiara can wave or high-five instead","then":"Kiara gives a tiny wave from behind you. Tauji waves back.","best":true},{"text":"Nudge her forward gently so Tauji doesn't feel hurt","then":"Kiara lets herself be hugged, stiff as a board, then runs back to you."},{"text":"Promise her a laddoo if she gives Tauji a hug","then":"Kiara hugs him for the sweet. Next time, she asks what she'll get first."},{"text":"Say she's just shy today, and steer her away","then":"Tauji laughs it off. Kiara hears that her no was only shyness."}],"why":"Offering another greeting respects her no and still lets her be polite."},{"prompt":"Later, Tauji's wife says children must be made to hug elders, or they grow up rude. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say a namaste or a wave is her way of respecting elders","then":"Tauji's wife shrugs. \"In our time it was different,\" she says, and lets it go.","best":true},{"text":"Agree, and promise Kiara will hug everyone next time","then":"Tauji's wife nods. Kiara, listening nearby, looks down at the floor."},{"text":"Tell her how you raise your child is none of her business","then":"Her smile vanishes, and the whole table goes quiet."},{"text":"Laugh, and say Kiara is just going through a shy phase","then":"The aunt nods. The real point, that Kiara gets to choose, goes unspoken."}],"why":"Explaining that a wave is respect too backs your child without a fight."},{"prompt":"In the car home, Kiara asks if she has to hug everyone at functions. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say her body is hers, and she can always choose a wave","then":"Kiara sits up. \"Even with Tauji?\" she asks. You say yes.","best":true},{"text":"Say yes, or relatives like Tauji will feel sad","then":"Kiara looks worried and goes quiet for the rest of the drive."},{"text":"Say only the elders, since they deserve respect","then":"Kiara nods. At the next function, she hugs every elder quickly to be good."},{"text":"Say not to worry about it just now, and turn up the music","then":"Kiara hums along, still unsure whether saying no was allowed."}],"why":"Telling her plainly the choice was hers makes her 'no' something she'll keep using."}],"debrief":"Respecting a child's 'no', even with family, protects them; pushing or bribing overrules it.","relearn":"Let a child choose a wave over a hug, even with family. Pushing or bribing overrules their bodily no."},
  {"id":"tk-930","cat":"early-years","type":"branch","persona":"Meena","source":"child hints at a secret","hook":"While colouring, your six-year-old Kabir says, 'Uncle and I have a secret game I can't tell.'","steps":[{"prompt":"Your stomach tightens. What do you do right now?","options":[{"text":"Calmly say nobody should ask him to keep secrets from you","then":"Kabir keeps colouring. \"Not even Uncle?\" he asks. You say not even Uncle.","best":true},{"text":"Fire off questions about the game and when they play it","then":"Kabir's face closes. \"I'm not allowed to say,\" he mumbles."},{"text":"Say 'that's nice' and go back to your phone","then":"Kabir keeps colouring. The word secret stays with you all evening."},{"text":"Tell him you'll ask Uncle about the game yourself","then":"Kabir looks scared. \"Don't tell him I told!\" he begs."}],"why":"Staying calm and naming the no-secrets rule keeps him talking and tells him he can come to you."},{"prompt":"At bedtime Kabir says Uncle told him grown-ups wouldn't understand the game. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say you're glad he told you, and none of it is his fault","then":"Kabir lets out a long breath and holds your hand until he falls asleep.","best":true},{"text":"Ask him to show you exactly how the game goes, step by step","then":"Kabir gets confused and upset, and says he's forgotten."},{"text":"Tell him off for keeping a secret from you","then":"Kabir starts crying. \"I won't play it again,\" he says, and stops talking."},{"text":"Promise you won't tell anyone, so he feels safe","then":"Kabir relaxes, but now you've promised silence about something that worries you."}],"why":"Thanks and 'not your fault' keep him safe to talk, while finding out details is the helpers' job."},{"prompt":"Kabir is asleep, and Uncle is due to visit on Sunday. What do you do next?","options":[{"text":"Call Childline 1098, and keep Kabir from being alone with him","then":"The counsellor listens and talks you through the next steps, one at a time.","best":true},{"text":"Confront Uncle on Sunday in front of the family","then":"The visit erupts into shouting, and Kabir hides, sure it's his fault."},{"text":"Wait and watch for more signs before you do anything at all","then":"Sunday comes. Uncle offers to take Kabir to the park while you cook."},{"text":"Ask your mother-in-law quietly what she thinks you should do","then":"She says children make up stories, and asks you not to make a fuss."}],"why":"Getting guidance and keeping Kabir from being alone with Uncle protects him without you acting alone."}],"debrief":"Stay calm, thank your child, say it's not their fault and get guidance from Childline 1098; never brush it off.","relearn":"A hinted 'secret game' can be a grooming sign: stay calm, reaffirm no body secrets and get guidance, never brush it off."},
  {"id":"tk-931","cat":"early-years","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"caught looking at bodies","hook":"You open the bedroom door and find your five-year-old Zoya and her friend Tanvi curiously comparing bodies.","steps":[{"prompt":"They look up at you, startled. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Calmly ask them to get dressed, and suggest a game","then":"The girls pull their clothes on and are soon arguing over the blocks.","best":true},{"text":"Shout at them both that it's dirty","then":"Both girls burst into tears. Tanvi asks to go home right away."},{"text":"Close the door and pretend you saw nothing","then":"The giggling carries on. You're not sure what to do with what you saw."},{"text":"Sit them down right then for a long talk about privacy","then":"The girls squirm with embarrassment, and Tanvi hides her face."}],"why":"Calm redirection keeps curiosity ordinary, and the privacy chat works better later, one to one."},{"prompt":"That evening, Tanvi's mother calls. She's heard about it and sounds upset. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say it's normal at this age, and share how you'll teach privacy","then":"She's quiet, then relieved. \"I wasn't sure what to say to her,\" she admits.","best":true},{"text":"Apologise, and say the girls won't be playing together for a while","then":"Tanvi's mother softens, but Zoya loses her best friend over nothing."},{"text":"Say it was all Tanvi's idea","then":"The call turns frosty, and Tanvi's mother hangs up upset."},{"text":"Laugh and say it's really nothing to worry about","then":"She feels brushed off, and says she'll handle it her own way."}],"why":"Calling it normal and sharing the privacy plan settles the worry without blame."},{"prompt":"At bath time, Zoya asks if she was naughty. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say curiosity is normal, and private parts are just for her","then":"Zoya thinks it over. \"So Tanvi's are just for Tanvi?\" she asks. You nod.","best":true},{"text":"Say yes, and she must never do that again","then":"Zoya's eyes fill. She won't let you help her dry off tonight."},{"text":"Say you'd rather not talk about it","then":"Zoya drops it, but stares at the floor for the rest of bath time."},{"text":"Say it's all fine, and leave the privacy part out for now","then":"Zoya brightens. At the next play date, the same game starts up again."}],"why":"Curiosity without shame, plus a clear privacy rule, is exactly what a five-year-old needs."}],"debrief":"Normal curiosity is best met by calmly redirecting and later teaching privacy; shaming teaches disgust.","relearn":"Met with calm and a later privacy chat, body curiosity stays normal; shouting teaches disgust."},
  {"id":"tk-932","cat":"early-years","type":"branch","persona":"Divya","source":"you fumbled the answer","hook":"Worn out from night feeds, you snapped 'Don't ask that!' when your four-year-old Ishaan asked a body question.","steps":[{"prompt":"Next morning, Ishaan is quiet at breakfast. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say sorry for snapping, and invite the question again","then":"Ishaan looks up. \"Really?\" he asks, and some of the stiffness goes out of him.","best":true},{"text":"Decide it's done and never bring it up","then":"Ishaan eats in silence. The question, and the snap, stay between you."},{"text":"Say nothing, and hope he asks his father or grandmother instead","then":"He does, later. You never hear what answer he got."},{"text":"Give him an extra treat to make up for it","then":"Ishaan cheers up over the chocolate, but he doesn't ask again."}],"why":"Going back and saying sorry models honesty and reopens the door."},{"prompt":"A few days later, Ishaan quietly tries again, asking how his baby sister came out. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Thank him for asking again, then give a short, true answer","then":"Ishaan nods. \"Did it hurt?\" he asks next, and you answer that too.","best":true},{"text":"Answer, but warn him it's the last time he asks","then":"Ishaan listens, but the warning is the part he remembers."},{"text":"Say the hospital gave her to you","then":"Ishaan accepts it. You both know it wasn't the whole story."},{"text":"Answer, then add a long talk about exactly how babies are made","then":"Ishaan's attention drifts halfway, and he runs off to play."}],"why":"Thanks plus a short, true answer shows him that asking you is safe again."},{"prompt":"Another tired evening, Ishaan starts a new body question as the baby wails. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Park it till after the feed, then bring it back up","then":"At bedtime you bring it up. Ishaan is thrilled that you remembered.","best":true},{"text":"Tell him you're far too tired for any questions today","then":"Ishaan wanders off. He doesn't ask again that week."},{"text":"Answer quickly in a rush, without looking up from the baby","then":"Ishaan catches half of it and doesn't follow up."},{"text":"Tell him to go and ask his father","then":"Ishaan goes off to find his father on a call, and the question gets lost."}],"why":"Parking a question kindly, then coming back, keeps you askable even on hard days."}],"debrief":"Going back to repair a fumble reopens the door and models honesty; leaving it locks the topic away.","relearn":"You can repair a fumble. Go back, apologise and answer; leaving it teaches the topic is off-limits."},
  {"id":"tk-933","cat":"early-years","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"child says it hurt","hook":"Tying her shoes, your five-year-old Riya says quietly that a touch from someone 'felt yucky and hurt'.","steps":[{"prompt":"She's watching your face closely. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Stay calm and say, 'I'm glad you told me. This is not your fault.'","then":"Riya leans against you. \"Am I in trouble?\" she asks. You tell her no.","best":true},{"text":"Say softly, 'Are you sure? Maybe you just imagined it.'","then":"Riya's face closes. \"Never mind,\" she says, and runs off to play."},{"text":"Get upset that she didn't stop it, or didn't come and tell you sooner","then":"Riya shrinks back and starts to cry. \"I'm sorry,\" she whispers."},{"text":"Gasp, hug her tight, and start crying along with her","then":"Riya gets frightened by your tears and stops talking to comfort you."}],"why":"Calm belief and 'not your fault' tell her she was right to tell you."},{"prompt":"Later that day, Riya begs you not to tell anyone, because he'll be cross. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say you'll only tell people whose job is to keep her safe","then":"Riya thinks about it, then nods. \"Will you stay with me?\" she asks.","best":true},{"text":"Promise to keep it just between the two of you","then":"Riya relaxes, and you're left holding a secret that could leave her unsafe."},{"text":"Ask her lots of questions so you know exactly what happened","then":"Riya gets muddled and upset, and stops answering."},{"text":"Tell her not to worry because you'll sort it out yourself","then":"Riya nods, but can't tell what you'll do, and neither can you."}],"why":"An honest 'I'll tell the people who help' keeps her trust without a promise you can't keep."},{"prompt":"That night, Riya is asleep and your mind is racing. What do you do next?","options":[{"text":"Call Childline 1098 and write down Riya's own words","then":"The counsellor listens, and talks you through keeping Riya safe from tomorrow.","best":true},{"text":"Go round and confront him yourself, tonight","then":"The row turns into shouting, and he warns you to keep quiet about it."},{"text":"Wait a few days, to see if she mentions it again on her own","then":"Days pass. Riya doesn't mention it, and you still don't know if she's safe."},{"text":"Ask a friend whether you might be overreacting","then":"Your friend says children exaggerate, and you almost believe her."}],"why":"Trained help, and her own words written down, protect her better than acting alone."},{"prompt":"That week, a relative learns what Riya said, and warns that going outside the family will bring shame. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say Riya's safety comes first, and get outside help","then":"The relative looks away, unhappy. Riya gets the support she needs.","best":true},{"text":"Agree to keep it quietly inside the family, for everyone's sake","then":"The relative is relieved. Riya still has to see him at family functions."},{"text":"Quietly keep Riya at home more, and tell no one else","then":"Riya stays in, but wonders if she's being punished for telling."},{"text":"Argue with the relative until they back down","then":"The argument goes on for an hour. Riya hears the shouting from her room."}],"why":"Her safety comes before family comfort, and outside help is how children stay protected."}],"debrief":"Stay calm, believe and thank your child, say it's never their fault, and call Childline 1098 for help.","relearn":"If a child says a touch hurt, stay calm, believe and thank them. Doubt or blame teaches silence. Childline 1098 helps."},
  {"id":"tk-934","cat":"early-years","type":"branch","persona":"Priya","source":"co-parent disagrees","hook":"Your husband Rahul says teaching your four-year-old Veer about private parts is 'too soon'.","steps":[{"prompt":"He says it over dinner, and seems to mean it. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Ask what worries him, and share why it's right for Veer's age","then":"Rahul puts his spoon down. \"I just don't want him growing up too fast,\" he says.","best":true},{"text":"Drop it for now, to avoid an argument over dinner","then":"Rahul changes the subject, relieved. The talk with Veer slips back again."},{"text":"Say you'll quietly teach Veer yourself when Rahul isn't around","then":"Rahul shrugs. \"Do what you want.\" You're on your own with it now."},{"text":"Tell him he's being old-fashioned and ignorant","then":"Rahul bristles, and dinner ends in a sulky silence."}],"why":"Asking first, then explaining, is how two parents end up on the same page."},{"prompt":"A few days later, Rahul admits his real worry: it might make Veer curious too early. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say knowing the words makes children safer, not curious sooner","then":"Rahul frowns, thinking. \"So it's more like road safety?\" he asks.","best":true},{"text":"Agree it might, and say you'll wait until Veer is older","then":"Rahul relaxes. Veer is left without the words that help children speak up."},{"text":"Say his view doesn't really matter, because it's happening anyway","then":"Rahul goes quiet and leaves the room."},{"text":"Send him a long article and ask him to read it","then":"Rahul skims it and says he'll think about it. The worry never gets talked through."}],"why":"Naming the fear and answering it with the facts brings a hesitant parent on board."},{"prompt":"At bath time, with you both there, Veer asks why some parts are called private. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Answer plainly, and invite Rahul to say Veer can ask him too","then":"Rahul hesitates, then nods. \"You can ask me anything, Veer.\" Veer grins.","best":true},{"text":"Answer it yourself, and just ignore Rahul's discomfort","then":"Veer gets his answer, but notices his father staring at the tiles."},{"text":"Let Rahul quickly change the subject, to keep bath time peaceful","then":"Veer shrugs and goes on splashing, the question dropped."},{"text":"Tell Veer it's a question for when he's older","then":"Veer frowns, and asks his cousin the next day instead."}],"why":"Bringing Rahul in, even gently, shows Veer he has two safe grown-ups to ask."}],"debrief":"Aligning with a co-parent doubles a child's doors; dropping it leaves them less protected.","relearn":"Bring a hesitant co-parent on board. Two aligned parents double a child's doors; dropping it leaves them exposed."},
  {"id":"tk-935","type":"reflect","persona":"any","source":"named at four","hook":"Lensy: teaching 'you're the boss of your own body' at age four plants consent for life.","prompt":"How does that land for you?","options":["Powerful","Never thought of it that way","I can do that"],"affirm":"Telling a small child they're the boss of their own body is the first, deepest root of consent, and you're already planting it.","relearn":"'You're the boss of your own body', taught at four, is the foundation of consent for life.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-936","type":"reflect","persona":"Divya","source":"raised in silence","hook":"Lensy: many of us were raised never hearing the real words. None of that is your fault.","prompt":"What comes up for you?","options":["A bit sad","Determined to change it","Relieved to hear that"],"affirm":"Being raised in silence isn't a failing of yours, and choosing to do it differently for your child is something to be proud of.","relearn":"Being raised in silence isn't your fault; choosing to talk openly with your own child is something to be proud of.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-937","type":"reflect","persona":"any","source":"small talks not one","hook":"Lensy: it's not one dreaded 'talk' to get perfect, just many tiny, age-right chats.","prompt":"Does that feel more doable?","options":["Much less scary","Yes, I can do small","Still nervous but okay"],"affirm":"There's no big speech to nail: just lots of small, calm moments, and every one you manage already counts.","relearn":"It's not one dreaded 'talk': just many small, age-right chats, and you can do them.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-938","type":"reflect","persona":"Priya","source":"calm face matters","hook":"Lensy: your calm face is the safety net. It tells a child you're safe to come to.","prompt":"How do you feel about that?","options":["Reassuring","A lot rides on it","I'll practise staying calm"],"affirm":"You don't need perfect words. A calm face is enough to tell your child you're the safe place to bring anything.","relearn":"A calm, unshocked face keeps you the person your child brings the next, bigger thing to.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-939","type":"reflect","persona":"any","source":"i don't know is fine","hook":"Lensy: 'I don't know, but let's find out together' is a great, honest answer.","prompt":"What do you make of that?","options":["Such a relief","Takes the pressure off","I'll use that"],"affirm":"You don't have to know everything. Willingness to find out together teaches your child more than any expert ever could.","relearn":"'I don't know, but let's find out together' is a good, honest answer; willingness beats expertise.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-940","type":"reflect","persona":"Divya","source":"protection not innocence","hook":"Lensy: correct names aren't a loss of innocence. They're a shield you hand your child.","prompt":"How does that sit with you?","options":["Reframes it for me","Makes sense","I feel braver about it"],"affirm":"Teaching the real words isn't taking childhood away. It's giving your child a tool that helps keep them safe.","relearn":"Correct names aren't a loss of innocence. They're a protection you hand your child.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-941","type":"reflect","persona":"any","source":"door you are building","hook":"Lensy: every calm little answer makes the next, harder question easier for them to ask.","prompt":"What does that stir in you?","options":["Hopeful","Worth the effort","I see the long game"],"affirm":"Each small calm answer is a brick in a door your child keeps coming back through. You're building it already.","relearn":"Every calm little answer makes the next, harder question easier for your child to ask.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-942","type":"spot","persona":"Divya","source":"catch the shaming lines","hook":"Spot the two replies to a body question that shut a child down.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"“Great question! That's the proper name.”","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"“That's a dirty thing to ask.”","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"“I don't know, let's find out.”","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"“Good children don't ask that.”","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"“Let's talk about it after lunch.”","trick":false}],"why":"'That's dirty' and 'good children don't ask' shame a child into silence; the others keep the door open with a calm, honest answer.","relearn":"Calm, honest replies keep the door open; 'that's dirty' and 'good children don't ask' shame a child into taking questions elsewhere.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-943","type":"spot","persona":"any","source":"catch the grooming lines","hook":"Spot the two things an adult might say that a child should always tell you about.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"“Your parents know I'm here today.”","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"“This is our secret, don't tell.”","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"“Let's stay where mum can see us.”","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"“If you tell, you'll be in big trouble.”","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"“You can stop any time you like.”","trick":false}],"why":"'Our secret, don't tell' and 'you'll be in trouble if you tell' are grooming red flags to report; the others are safe.","relearn":"'Keep this secret' and 'you'll be in trouble if you tell' are grooming red flags to report. Open 'you can stop' talk is safe.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-944","type":"spot","persona":"any","source":"catch the unsafe rules","hook":"Spot the two 'rules' that actually make a young child less safe.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"You can say no to unwanted touch","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Always do what any grown-up says","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Tell me anything, no body secrets","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Never question or refuse an elder","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Your body belongs to you","trick":false}],"why":"'Obey any grown-up' and 'never refuse an elder' strip a child's ability to refuse harm; the others build real safety.","relearn":"'Obey every grown-up' and 'never refuse an elder' make a child less safe; 'you can say no', 'no body secrets' and 'your body is yours' protect.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-945","type":"spot","persona":"Priya","source":"catch overriding consent","hook":"Spot the two moments that override a young child's bodily 'no'.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Letting them wave instead of hug","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Forcing a kiss for a relative","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Asking before tickling them","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Making them sit on a lap they shrink from","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Stopping a game when they say stop","trick":false}],"why":"Forcing a kiss and a shrunk-from lap override a child's no; offering a wave, asking first and stopping at 'stop' teach consent.","relearn":"Forcing a kiss or a shrunk-from lap overrides a child's no; offering a wave, asking before tickling and stopping at 'stop' teach consent.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-946","type":"spot","persona":"Divya","source":"catch wrong-time facts","hook":"Spot the two things that are NOT age-right for a four-year-old.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"The correct names for private parts","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"The graphic mechanics of sex","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Private parts are private","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Explicit adult relationship details","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Safe vs unsafe touch","trick":false}],"why":"Graphic sex mechanics and explicit adult-relationship details are for much later; names, privacy and safe-vs-unsafe touch fit a four-year-old.","relearn":"Correct names, privacy and safe-vs-unsafe touch fit a four-year-old; graphic sex mechanics and explicit adult details come much later.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-947","type":"spot","persona":"any","source":"catch the myths","hook":"Spot the two statements about early body-safety that are myths.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Correct names help a child stay safe","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Talking about bodies gives kids ideas","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Body safety can start around age four","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Only girls need consent talks","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"'No body secrets' protects children","trick":false}],"why":"'Talking gives ideas' and 'only girls need consent' are myths; correct names, an early start and 'no body secrets' protect.","relearn":"'Talking gives ideas' and 'only girls need consent' are myths; correct names, an early start and 'no body secrets' protect every child.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-948","type":"spot","persona":"Meena","source":"catch the brush-offs","hook":"Spot the two reactions to a child's worry that miss a warning sign.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"“Thank you for telling me.”","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"“Stop making things up.”","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"“You're not in any trouble.”","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"“Don't be silly, he's family.”","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"“Let's talk about what happened.”","trick":false}],"why":"'Stop making things up' and 'don't be silly, he's family' brush off a warning sign; believing and gently asking keeps a child safe.","relearn":"'Stop making things up' and 'don't be silly, he's family' brush off a worry; thank, reassure and ask gently. If worried, Childline 1098.","cat":"early-years"},
  {"id":"tk-949","cat":"early-years","type":"role-play","persona":"Divya","source":"name at bathtime","hook":"At bath time, your three-year-old Siya points between her legs, curious.","setup":"She's splashing, completely unbothered.","steps":[{"prompt":"Siya asks: \"What's this one called? Is it my bum?\"","options":[{"text":"\"That's your vulva. Your bum is at the back.\"","then":"Siya pats the water. \"Vulva,\" she says, then \"Bum!\" and giggles.","best":true},{"text":"\"Never mind that. Let's get you nice and clean.\"","then":"Siya frowns. \"But what's it called?\""},{"text":"\"That's your chhi-chhi. Don't touch it.\"","then":"Siya snatches her hand away. \"Chhi-chhi is dirty?\""},{"text":"\"It's your private part, beta. Now, where's your duck?\"","then":"Siya grabs the duck. \"But what's its name?\""}],"why":"The plain name, said like elbow or knee, is a word she can use to stay safe."},{"prompt":"Siya asks: \"Does Papa have one too?\"","options":[{"text":"\"No. Papa has a penis. Bodies come in different kinds.\"","then":"Siya nods, satisfied. \"And Dadi has a vulva,\" she decides.","best":true},{"text":"\"Go and ask Papa that yourself.\"","then":"Siya shouts \"PAPA!\" towards the door at the top of her voice."},{"text":"\"Chhi, don't ask things like that.\"","then":"Siya stops splashing. \"Sorry,\" she says in a small voice."},{"text":"\"Papa has a different one, beta. Now, arms up for the towel!\"","then":"Siya lifts her arms. \"Different how?\" she asks."}],"why":"A plain, true answer keeps both words ordinary and keeps her asking you."},{"prompt":"Siya asks: \"Can anybody wash it?\"","options":[{"text":"\"You can, and I help at bath time. It's private.\"","then":"Siya thinks. \"And Papa helps?\" You nod. \"Nobody else,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"\"Whoever is looking after you, beta.\"","then":"Siya nods. \"Anybody who looks after me.\""},{"text":"\"Why do you ask? Has someone touched you there?\"","then":"Siya's lip wobbles. \"Am I in trouble?\""},{"text":"\"Nobody at all. Never let anyone near it.\"","then":"Siya looks confused. \"Not even at bath time?\""}],"why":"A simple 'private' rule that names her real helpers is one a toddler can hold on to."}],"relearn":"Naming a body part as plainly as an elbow removes shame and gives a child a word that keeps them safe."},
  {"id":"tk-950","cat":"early-years","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"teach the no-secrets rule","hook":"Your six-year-old Omar is bursting to share Dadi's birthday surprise. It's a good moment to talk about secrets.","setup":"He whispers it to you, grinning.","steps":[{"prompt":"Omar whispers: \"Is it bad if I keep a secret from Dadi?\"","options":[{"text":"\"A surprise is fine. She'll know soon. Secrets are different.\"","then":"Omar's eyes go wide. \"Different how?\" he asks.","best":true},{"text":"\"No. Secrets are fine to keep if a grown-up says so.\"","then":"Omar grins. \"Okay! Grown-ups decide,\" he says."},{"text":"\"Yes. Secrets are always bad, so go and tell her right now.\"","then":"Omar wails, \"But then I'll ruin the surprise!\""},{"text":"\"Don't worry about that, beta. Just don't tell her!\"","then":"\"Okay!\" Omar says, and runs off to hide the card."}],"why":"Separating a happy surprise from a secret gives him a line he can use."},{"prompt":"At bedtime, Omar asks: \"What's a secret, anyway? Is it like a surprise?\"","options":[{"text":"\"A surprise gets told soon. Body secrets? You always tell me.\"","then":"Omar nods. \"Body secrets get told,\" he repeats.","best":true},{"text":"\"Secrets are grown-up things. You're too young for those.\"","then":"Omar frowns. \"Like what, though?\""},{"text":"\"Secrets are what naughty children hide from their parents.\"","then":"Omar looks worried. \"I'm not naughty,\" he says."},{"text":"\"They're the same, really. Keep both if you've promised.\"","then":"Omar thinks. \"Even if it's a yucky one?\""}],"why":"A simple difference, with 'always tell me about bodies', makes the rule clear."},{"prompt":"Omar asks: \"What if someone says I'll get in trouble for telling?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Tell me anyway. You'll never be in trouble for telling me.\"","then":"Omar relaxes. \"Never ever?\" he checks. You say never ever.","best":true},{"text":"\"Then keep quiet, and just stay far away from them.\"","then":"Omar nods. \"Keep quiet. Okay.\""},{"text":"\"Who said that to you? Tell me right now.\"","then":"Omar looks startled. \"Nobody! It's just a what-if.\""},{"text":"\"Nobody would ever say such a thing to you, beta. Don't worry.\"","then":"Omar frowns. \"But if they did?\""}],"why":"'You'll never be in trouble for telling me' is what lets a child tell. It's never his fault."}],"relearn":"No one should ask a child to keep a body secret: 'tell me, and you'll never be in trouble' gives them permission to disclose."},
  {"id":"tk-951","cat":"early-years","type":"role-play","persona":"Priya","source":"redirect at the table","hook":"At a big Diwali dinner, your five-year-old Aadya asks loudly where babies come from.","setup":"Every face at the table turns to you.","steps":[{"prompt":"Aadya insists: \"Tell me! Where do they come from?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Good question. Babies grow in a womb. More after dinner.\"","then":"Aadya nods. \"After dinner,\" she says, and goes back to her puri.","best":true},{"text":"\"We don't talk about such things at the table. Eat up, now.\"","then":"Aadya slumps. \"Why not?\" she mutters into her plate."},{"text":"\"The stork brings them, beta. Now finish your food.\"","then":"Aadya giggles. \"Storks aren't real!\""},{"text":"\"Ask me later, okay? Not now, beta. Everyone's eating.\"","then":"Aadya frowns. \"Later when?\""}],"why":"A calm, true start plus 'more later' honours the question without a scene."},{"prompt":"Chachi laughs: \"Arre, such questions at her age! Where does she get them?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Kids are curious. We'd rather she asks us than anyone else.\"","then":"Chachi raises her eyebrows. \"Hmm. That's true, I suppose.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Sorry, Chachi. She picks up these things from other kids at school.\"","then":"Chachi tuts. \"Schools these days. Tch.\""},{"text":"\"At least my child asks questions, unlike some.\"","then":"Chachi's smile freezes. \"Well! Excuse me,\" she says."},{"text":"\"I don't know! Kids say the funniest things.\"","then":"Chachi laughs along. \"Too funny,\" she says, as Aadya looks puzzled."}],"why":"Saying you want her to ask you, calmly, makes the questions normal for everyone."},{"prompt":"At bedtime Aadya asks: \"So where do babies really come from?\"","options":[{"text":"\"They grow in a womb, inside the mother, until they're ready.\"","then":"Aadya pats her own tummy. \"Was I in there? In yours?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"You're still too young to understand that, Aadya.\"","then":"Aadya sighs. \"Everyone keeps saying that.\""},{"text":"\"I've told you already. Now go to sleep.\"","then":"Aadya turns over. \"But you didn't really,\" she mumbles."},{"text":"\"From the hospital, beta, where all the doctors and nurses are.\"","then":"Aadya frowns. \"But how did I get in the hospital?\""}],"why":"Coming back with a simple, true answer at bedtime shows her the question was welcome."}],"relearn":"Giving a calm true answer and a 'more later' keeps the question open instead of teaching them it's shameful to ask."},
  {"id":"tk-952","cat":"early-years","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"consent in greetings","hook":"Mamaji arrives for Raksha Bandhan and reaches for your five-year-old Dev, who stiffens and pulls back.","setup":"Dev looks up at you, waiting.","steps":[{"prompt":"Mamaji laughs: \"Come on, Dev, give Mamaji a big hug!\"","options":[{"text":"\"Dev, hug, wave or high-five? You get to choose.\"","then":"Mamaji crouches as Dev picks a high-five. \"Ooh, strong!\" he laughs.","best":true},{"text":"\"Go on, Dev, give Mamaji a hug. Don't be rude.\"","then":"Mamaji scoops up a stiff Dev. \"See? He loves me really!\""},{"text":"\"He's a bit shy, Mamaji. He'll warm up after a while.\"","then":"\"Shy? With me? Nonsense!\" Mamaji says, reaching again."},{"text":"\"Hug Mamaji, Dev, and you can have the rakhi sweets.\"","then":"Mamaji laughs. \"Bribes already! Come here, then.\""}],"why":"Offering a choice teaches Dev that his body is his, and still lets him greet his uncle."},{"prompt":"Over chai, Mamaji says: \"In our family, children hug their elders. It's respect.\"","options":[{"text":"\"He can show respect his own way. A namaste counts too.\"","then":"Mamaji considers it. \"Namaste, hm. My own father liked a namaste.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"You're right, Mamaji. I'll have a word with him later.\"","then":"Mamaji nods. \"Good. Kids need to learn these things.\""},{"text":"\"Times have changed. Nobody has to hug anyone now.\"","then":"\"So now I'm the villain?\" Mamaji says, stung."},{"text":"\"Of course. He'll give you a big hug before you leave.\"","then":"Mamaji brightens. \"I'll hold you to that!\""}],"why":"Naming another way to show respect keeps both the tradition and Dev's choice."},{"prompt":"At the door, Dev hides behind you. Mamaji sighs: \"Why let a child refuse his own family?\"","options":[{"text":"\"If he can say no to a hug, he can say no when it matters.\"","then":"Mamaji is quiet. \"I hadn't thought of it like that,\" he admits.","best":true},{"text":"\"We don't, Mamaji. He was just in a funny mood today.\"","then":"\"Then next time he hugs me properly,\" Mamaji says."},{"text":"\"Because you really can't be too careful these days, can you?\"","then":"Mamaji stiffens. \"Careful of me?\""},{"text":"\"It's what his school tells all the parents to do.\"","then":"Mamaji shrugs. \"Schools teach all sorts of things.\""}],"why":"Linking a small no to his safety explains the lesson without accusing anyone."}],"relearn":"Offering a child a choice of greeting teaches consent; forcing the hug tells them their bodily 'no' can be overruled."},
  {"id":"tk-953","cat":"early-years","type":"role-play","persona":"Divya","source":"where babies come from","hook":"Looking at old photos, your four-year-old Kavya finds one of you heavily pregnant with her.","setup":"She peers closely at the big round belly.","steps":[{"prompt":"Kavya asks: \"Why is your tummy so big? Where do babies come from?\"","options":[{"text":"\"You were growing inside me, in a place called the womb.\"","then":"Kavya stares at the photo. \"Me? Wow,\" she breathes.","best":true},{"text":"\"The stork brought you. Now off you go and play.\"","then":"Kavya frowns. \"But then why is your tummy big?\""},{"text":"\"I ate far too many laddoos that month!\"","then":"Kavya giggles. \"Silly! Tell me properly.\""},{"text":"\"That's a story for when you're much bigger, sweetheart.\"","then":"Kavya pouts. \"I AM bigger now.\""}],"why":"A simple, true answer at her level meets her curiosity and keeps her trust."},{"prompt":"Kavya taps the round belly in the photo and asks: \"Was I in there? How did I fit?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Yes. You started tiny, and my womb stretched as you grew.\"","then":"Kavya stretches her arms wide. \"This big?\" she asks, laughing.","best":true},{"text":"\"It's magic! Now let's look at the next photo.\"","then":"Kavya turns the page. \"But how?\" she asks, still looking back."},{"text":"\"Don't ask so many questions, beta.\"","then":"Kavya closes the album. \"Okay,\" she says quietly."},{"text":"\"Yes, you were a tiny seed that grew and grew and grew.\"","then":"Kavya's eyes go wide. \"Like a mango seed? Did you eat me?\""}],"why":"Plain facts at her size make sense to her, where vague pictures only bring muddles."},{"prompt":"Later, at bath time, Kavya asks: \"Can I have a baby in my tummy too?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Some grown-up bodies can. Yours is still a child's body.\"","then":"Kavya nods. \"Still growing,\" she says, and checks her height on the door.","best":true},{"text":"\"Chhi! Little girls don't talk like that, Kavya.\"","then":"Kavya's face falls. \"Sorry,\" she whispers."},{"text":"\"Yes, when you get married, you'll have lots of them!\"","then":"Kavya nods seriously. \"When I marry, babies come.\""},{"text":"\"Only if you eat all your vegetables first.\"","then":"Kavya giggles. \"Really? Then give me carrots!\""}],"why":"A true answer that fits her age answers her and leaves the rest for later."}],"relearn":"Give a little child a simple, true answer about where babies come from, not a stork story or a shutdown."},
  {"id":"tk-954","cat":"early-years","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"i don't know answer","hook":"Your seven-year-old Jay is full of body questions this week, and some of them stump you.","setup":"Tonight he's reading a body book by torchlight under the blanket.","steps":[{"prompt":"Jay asks: \"Why do older boys' voices go all croaky?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Great question. I'm not sure, so let's find out together.\"","then":"Jay sits up. \"Together? Okay!\"","best":true},{"text":"\"That's a silly thing to ask, Jay. Go to sleep now.\"","then":"\"It's not silly,\" Jay mutters, and switches off the torch."},{"text":"\"Because they shout far too much at cricket, that's why.\"","then":"Jay squints. \"Then why isn't Didi croaky?\""},{"text":"\"Ask your science teacher about it tomorrow.\"","then":"Jay shrugs. \"She'll laugh at me. You're easier.\""}],"why":"'Let's find out together' is honest, and keeps you the person he asks."},{"prompt":"Jay asks: \"Do grown-ups know everything about bodies?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Nobody knows everything. Finding out is half the fun.\"","then":"Jay grins. \"So I can stump you again?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Yes. Grown-ups know all of it, beta. Every bit.\"","then":"Jay grins. \"Then why do you always google things?\""},{"text":"\"Don't be cheeky, Jay. Grown-ups know plenty of things.\"","then":"\"Sorry,\" Jay mumbles, then peeks at his book again."},{"text":"\"I should know these things. I'm sorry, beta.\"","then":"\"It's okay,\" Jay says, unsure why you look sad."}],"why":"Owning a gap lightly shows him questions are welcome and learning never stops."},{"prompt":"Jay asks: \"Can we look it up now, on your phone?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Yes. Let's read a proper health site together.\"","then":"Jay snuggles in beside you. \"Look, there's a diagram!\" he says.","best":true},{"text":"\"Here, take the phone and search it yourself.\"","then":"Jay taps the first video he sees. \"Look, this one!\""},{"text":"\"No phones in bed. Maybe some other time.\"","then":"\"Some other time never comes,\" Jay grumbles."},{"text":"\"I'll look it up later tonight and tell you.\"","then":"Jay frowns. \"Can't I see too?\""}],"why":"Checking a trusted source side by side teaches him where good answers come from."},{"prompt":"Next morning, Jay asks: \"Will my voice go croaky too?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Yes, when you're older. That's a normal part of growing.\"","then":"Jay tries a deep voice. \"Like this?\" he booms, laughing.","best":true},{"text":"\"Let's not worry about any of that for years and years yet.\"","then":"\"But I want to know now!\" Jay says."},{"text":"\"Only if you stop drinking your milk.\"","then":"Jay frowns. \"Is that true, though?\""},{"text":"\"Maybe. Ask your uncle. He'd know that better than me.\"","then":"Jay looks puzzled. \"Why can't you just tell me?\""}],"why":"A calm 'yes, it's normal' prepares him long before the change arrives."}],"relearn":"'I'm not sure, so let's find out together' keeps you the askable parent; 'that's silly' sends the question elsewhere."},
  {"id":"tk-955","cat":"early-years","type":"role-play","persona":"Priya","source":"park a question kindly","hook":"You're frying pakoras for guests when your six-year-old Nikhil wanders in with a big body question.","setup":"The oil is spitting, and the doorbell could ring any minute.","steps":[{"prompt":"Nikhil asks: \"Why do girls and boys have different private parts?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Great question! Let's talk properly after dinner.\"","then":"Nikhil nods. \"After dinner. Don't forget!\" he says, and runs off.","best":true},{"text":"\"We don't talk about things like that in this house.\"","then":"Nikhil's face falls. \"Why not?\" he mumbles."},{"text":"\"Not now! Can't you see how busy I am?\"","then":"Nikhil backs away. \"Sorry,\" he says."},{"text":"\"Because. Bodies are just different. Now shoo, beta.\"","then":"Nikhil folds his arms. \"That's not an answer.\""}],"why":"Honouring a question and parking it briefly keeps it safe to ask."},{"prompt":"The guests arrive. Nikhil tells one what he asked, and Mrs Kapoor chuckles: \"Such questions at six!\"","options":[{"text":"\"I'm glad he asks me. We'll talk about it later.\"","then":"Mrs Kapoor smiles. \"Good for you. I never could with mine.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"I know. I have no idea where he gets it from.\"","then":"\"The internet, probably,\" Mrs Kapoor says, shaking her head."},{"text":"\"Nikhil, go to your room. Right now.\"","then":"Mrs Kapoor looks awkward. \"Oh, I didn't mean to get him into trouble.\""},{"text":"\"Boys will be boys! What to do?\"","then":"Mrs Kapoor laughs. \"Exactly. Let him be.\""}],"why":"Saying you're glad he asks, in front of guests, shows him the question was never wrong."},{"prompt":"At bedtime, Nikhil asks again: \"So why are girls and boys different down there?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Boys have a penis, girls a vulva. Both are private.\"","then":"Nikhil thinks. \"And both are just the proper names?\" You nod.","best":true},{"text":"\"That's just how it is. Now go to sleep.\"","then":"Nikhil sighs. \"That's not a real answer.\""},{"text":"\"You'll learn about it at school when you're older.\"","then":"\"But I want to know now,\" Nikhil says."},{"text":"\"Let me explain exactly how all of it works, then.\"","then":"Nikhil yawns halfway through. \"Can I just go to sleep?\""}],"why":"Coming back to it with a short, true answer keeps the door open."}],"relearn":"You can honour a question and park it briefly. That keeps it safe to ask, without a shutdown."},
  {"id":"tk-956","cat":"early-years","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"safe grown-up rule","hook":"At her check-up today, the doctor pressed your five-year-old Ananya's tummy while you held her hand.","setup":"Walking home, she's quiet, thinking hard.","steps":[{"prompt":"Ananya asks: \"Why could the doctor touch me? You said my body is mine.\"","options":[{"text":"\"A doctor can check you with me there. That's a safe touch.\"","then":"Ananya nods. \"Because you held my hand.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Because doctors are allowed to do anything they like.\"","then":"Ananya frowns. \"Anything? Even if I don't like it?\""},{"text":"\"Don't ask so many questions. The doctor was very nice.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" Ananya says, but she's still frowning."},{"text":"\"That was different, beta. Don't you worry about it at all.\"","then":"Ananya scuffs her shoe. \"Different how, though?\""}],"why":"Explaining why a check-up with you there is safe keeps her rule clear, not confusing."},{"prompt":"Ananya asks: \"So how do I know if a touch is unsafe?\"","options":[{"text":"\"If it hurts or feels wrong, or touches private parts when you don't need help.\"","then":"Ananya thinks. \"So help in the bath is okay, but not other times?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Only strangers do unsafe touches, so stay away from them.\"","then":"Ananya nods. \"So people I know are always safe?\""},{"text":"\"You're far too little to be worrying about that.\"","then":"\"But I want to know,\" Ananya insists."},{"text":"\"You'll just know. You're a clever girl.\"","then":"Ananya looks unsure. \"What if I don't know?\""}],"why":"Simple signs she can notice, with room for bath help and check-ups, let her tell safe from unsafe."},{"prompt":"Ananya asks: \"What should I do if a touch feels wrong?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Say no, move away, and tell me. Even if you couldn't, tell me.\"","then":"\"No, move, tell,\" Ananya chants. \"And tell even if I couldn't.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Just be a good girl and do what the grown-ups tell you.\"","then":"Ananya nods. \"Do what they say. Okay.\""},{"text":"\"Keep far away from that person from then on.\"","then":"Ananya thinks. \"But do I tell anyone?\""},{"text":"\"That won't ever happen to you, beta, so don't you worry.\"","then":"Ananya frowns. \"But if it does?\""}],"why":"Three steps she can remember, and 'tell me even if you couldn't' means it's never her fault."},{"prompt":"Ananya asks: \"What if it's someone we know, like a cousin?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Anyone at all. Tell me, and you'll never be in trouble.\"","then":"Ananya squeezes your hand. \"Anyone at all,\" she repeats.","best":true},{"text":"\"Family would never do something like that, beta.\"","then":"\"Oh. Okay,\" Ananya says, and tucks the idea away."},{"text":"\"Why do you ask that? Has a cousin done something to you?\"","then":"Ananya looks startled. \"No! I was only asking.\""},{"text":"\"Only tell if you're really sure they meant it.\"","then":"Ananya frowns. \"How do I know if I'm sure?\""}],"why":"'Anyone at all' covers the people children find hardest to tell about, and 'never in trouble' frees her to speak."}],"relearn":"'Tell me, and you'll never be in trouble' gives a child permission to disclose; 'obey grown-ups' takes it away."},
  {"id":"tk-957","cat":"early-years","type":"role-play","persona":"Divya","source":"repair a snap","hook":"Yesterday your six-year-old Rohan held up a sanitary pad and asked what it was. You snapped at him.","setup":"Today he's drawing quietly at the table.","steps":[{"prompt":"Rohan says, without looking up: \"I'm not asking you things any more.\"","options":[{"text":"\"I was wrong to snap. It was a good question. Ask me.\"","then":"Rohan looks up slowly. \"Really? You won't get cross?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Good. Some things just aren't for children, Rohan.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" Rohan says flatly, and keeps drawing."},{"text":"\"Let's just forget you ever asked that, okay?\"","then":"Rohan shrugs. \"Okay,\" he says, not looking up."},{"text":"\"Don't be silly, beta. Here, have a biscuit.\"","then":"Rohan takes it. \"Thanks,\" he mumbles, eyes still on his drawing."}],"why":"Owning the snap and inviting the question back shows the door is really open."},{"prompt":"Later, Rohan picks up the pad packet again and asks: \"What is it, really?\"","options":[{"text":"\"A pad. Women and older girls use them during periods.\"","then":"Rohan tilts his head, thinking hard about that.","best":true},{"text":"\"Just something for ladies. Nothing for you, beta.\"","then":"Rohan frowns. \"Why is it a secret, then?\""},{"text":"\"A kind of nappy that grown-up ladies wear sometimes.\"","then":"Rohan giggles. \"Grown-ups wear nappies?\""},{"text":"\"That's private. It's not something boys need to know.\"","then":"Rohan looks hurt. \"Why not boys?\""}],"why":"A plain, true answer is what turns yesterday's snap into trust."},{"prompt":"Rohan asks, worried: \"Is it because you're ill? Does it hurt?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Not ill. In a period, a little blood leaves the womb. It can ache.\"","then":"Rohan nods. \"Can I get you a hot water bottle when it aches?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"You're a boy, so you'll never need to know about it.\"","then":"Rohan looks confused. \"But Didi will?\""},{"text":"\"It's when ladies are unwell and unclean. Don't talk about it, beta.\"","then":"Rohan looks worried. \"Should I stay away from you?\""},{"text":"\"It's a grown-up thing. You'll learn about it at school.\"","then":"Rohan frowns. \"At school? Why not from you?\""}],"why":"Honest, calm facts about periods help every child, boys included, grow up without shame."}],"relearn":"Going back to repair a fumbled answer models honesty and shows the door is genuinely always open."},
  {"id":"tk-958","cat":"early-years","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"teach private means private","hook":"Guests are due, and your four-year-old Ira runs through the living room naked after her bath.","setup":"The doorbell rings just as you reach her.","steps":[{"prompt":"Ira protests: \"Why do I have to wear clothes? It's hot!\"","options":[{"text":"\"Private parts are just for you. We cover them around others.\"","then":"\"Just for me?\" Ira asks, and holds out her arms for her frock.","best":true},{"text":"\"Because being naked in front of people is shameful and naughty.\"","then":"Ira hides behind the sofa. \"Am I naughty?\""},{"text":"\"Because I said so, Ira. Now hurry up, quickly!\"","then":"Ira stamps her foot. \"That's not a reason!\""},{"text":"\"Because the guests will laugh at you if they see.\"","then":"Ira's eyes fill. \"Why would they laugh at me?\""}],"why":"Privacy framed as 'just for you' is a boundary, not a shame."},{"prompt":"Ira asks: \"But I can be naked with you at bath time?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Yes. Mummy or Papa helping you wash is fine.\"","then":"Ira nods. \"Bath time is for washing,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"\"No. Nobody should ever see you with no clothes on.\"","then":"Ira looks confused. \"Not even the doctor?\""},{"text":"\"Stop asking questions and put this frock on.\"","then":"Ira wriggles into the frock. \"Fine,\" she sulks."},{"text":"\"Yes, and with anyone in the family, of course.\"","then":"Ira nods. \"Anyone in the family can see me.\""}],"why":"Naming exactly who helps, and when, keeps her rule clear and safe."},{"prompt":"Dressed now, Ira asks: \"Is my body yucky?\"","options":[{"text":"\"No. Your body is lovely. Private just means it's yours.\"","then":"Ira beams and twirls. \"My lovely private body!\" she sings.","best":true},{"text":"\"Only when you run around like that without your clothes on.\"","then":"Ira looks down at herself, unsure. \"Oh.\""},{"text":"\"Don't be silly. Go and say hello to the guests.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" Ira says, still frowning as she goes."},{"text":"\"No, but girls always have to be extra careful.\"","then":"Ira frowns. \"Why only girls?\""}],"why":"Clear 'lovely and private' teaches the rule without teaching disgust."}],"relearn":"Framing privacy as 'just for you', a boundary not a shame, protects a child without teaching disgust."},
  {"id":"tk-959","cat":"early-years","type":"role-play","persona":"Meena","source":"believe a disclosure","hook":"Your seven-year-old Aryan comes home from tuition and quietly says someone touched him where he didn't like.","setup":"He's sitting very still on the edge of his bed.","steps":[{"prompt":"Aryan whispers: \"Am I in trouble?\"","options":[{"text":"\"No. I'm glad you told me. This is not your fault.\"","then":"Aryan's shoulders drop. \"I didn't know if I should tell,\" he says.","best":true},{"text":"\"Are you sure? You mustn't make up stories, Aryan.\"","then":"Aryan looks at the floor. \"Forget it,\" he says."},{"text":"\"Who was it? What did they do? Tell me everything!\"","then":"Aryan flinches and curls up. \"I don't want to say.\""},{"text":"\"Of course not. But why didn't you tell me sooner?\"","then":"Aryan's eyes fill. \"I was scared,\" he whispers."}],"why":"'This is not your fault', said calmly, is what a child most needs to hear first."},{"prompt":"Aryan says: \"Bhaiya said not to tell anyone. Will you tell?\"","options":[{"text":"\"I'll tell people whose job is to keep you safe.\"","then":"Aryan thinks. \"Not the whole family?\" You shake your head.","best":true},{"text":"\"No. I promise it stays just between us two.\"","then":"Aryan relaxes. \"Okay. Just us.\""},{"text":"\"Yes. I'm calling his parents right now to sort this.\"","then":"Aryan panics. \"No! He'll know I told!\""},{"text":"\"Let me think about it, beta. Go and wash up now.\"","then":"Aryan hesitates at the door. \"Are you cross?\""}],"why":"An honest 'I'll tell the helpers' keeps his trust without a promise that could leave him unsafe."},{"prompt":"Your husband, overhearing, says: \"Let's not make a fuss. We'll just stop the tuition.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Stopping tuition isn't enough. Let's call Childline 1098.\"","then":"He pauses, then nods. \"Okay. You call. I'll sit with Aryan.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"You're right. Let's just quietly move him to another class.\"","then":"He nods, relieved. \"Good. No need for any drama.\""},{"text":"\"How can you be so calm? I'm going there myself!\"","then":"He catches your arm. \"Wait. You'll make it worse.\""},{"text":"\"Let's wait and see if he says anything more.\"","then":"He nods. \"Yes. Maybe it was nothing.\""}],"why":"Trained help protects Aryan, and other children too, in a way moving classes can't."},{"prompt":"Next morning Aryan asks: \"Do I still have to go to tuition?\"","options":[{"text":"\"No. And telling me was exactly right.\"","then":"Aryan lets out a breath. \"Okay,\" he says, and eats his breakfast.","best":true},{"text":"\"Yes, but sit near the door this time.\"","then":"Aryan goes pale. \"But Bhaiya will be there.\""},{"text":"\"We'll see. Let's not make a big thing of it.\"","then":"Aryan goes quiet. \"Okay,\" he says."},{"text":"\"No, but don't tell your friends why you stopped.\"","then":"Aryan nods slowly. \"So it's a secret now.\""}],"why":"Keeping him away from the person, and backing his telling, keeps him safe and talking."}],"relearn":"Staying calm, believing and thanking a child keeps them talking; doubting them teaches silence. If worried, Childline 1098."},
  {"id":"tk-990","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If I just teach my values, the facts will sort themselves out.\"","myth":{"un":"If I just teach my values, the facts will sort themselves out.","re":"Values alone leave gaps a child fills from peers or the feed; pair them with honest facts so guidance has something true to stand on.","why":"Values guide; facts keep safe. A child needs both."},"relearn":"Values without facts leave gaps others fill; give the honest facts too, so your guidance stands on what's true.","persona":"any","source":"values need facts"},
  {"id":"tk-991","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Facts are cold; sharing my values would just be preaching.\"","myth":{"un":"Facts are cold; sharing my values would just be preaching.","re":"Sharing your values isn't preaching; it's offering your view alongside the facts so a child can weigh both and still feel free to choose.","why":"Said as your view, not a verdict, values invite thought."},"relearn":"Sharing your values as your view, not a verdict, isn't preaching; it gives a child something to weigh with the facts.","persona":"Priya","source":"values not preaching"},
  {"id":"tk-992","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"My child is too young for facts, so I'll just give the rule.\"","myth":{"un":"My child is too young for facts, so I'll just give the rule.","re":"A rule with no honest 'why' is easy to drop later; an age-right fact behind it makes the value stick and travel with them.","why":"'Because I said so' fades; an honest reason lasts."},"relearn":"A rule needs an age-right reason; the honest fact behind a value is what makes it stick and travel with a child.","persona":"any","source":"rule needs reason"},
  {"id":"tk-993","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If the facts and my beliefs disagree, I should hide the facts.\"","myth":{"un":"If the facts and my beliefs disagree, I should hide the facts.","re":"Hiding facts a child needs to stay safe doesn't protect your beliefs; give the facts, then share your belief honestly as your own.","why":"A hidden fact gets learned anyway, without your voice."},"relearn":"Don't hide safety facts that clash with a belief; give the facts, then share your belief honestly as your own.","persona":"Vikram","source":"don't hide facts"},
  {"id":"tk-994","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Sharing my values will pressure my child into agreeing with me.\"","myth":{"un":"Sharing my values will pressure my child into agreeing with me.","re":"Stated as 'here's what I believe and why', your values are a gift to weigh, not a command; that respect keeps a child talking to you.","why":"Offered, not imposed, values invite rather than push."},"relearn":"Offered as 'what I believe and why', your values invite thought, not pressure; that respect keeps a child talking to you.","persona":"Priya","source":"offer not impose"},
  {"id":"tk-995","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Keeping quiet keeps me neutral and lets my child decide freely.\"","myth":{"un":"Keeping quiet keeps me neutral and lets my child decide freely.","re":"Silence isn't neutral; it just lets peers, media and the feed decide for you. Your honest values belong in the mix your child weighs.","why":"Someone always fills the silence; let it be you too."},"relearn":"Silence isn't neutral; it cedes the choice to peers and the feed, so put your honest values in the mix your child weighs.","persona":"any","source":"silence not neutral"},
  {"id":"tk-996","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Talking openly about facts means I'm abandoning our family's culture.\"","myth":{"un":"Talking openly about facts means I'm abandoning our family's culture.","re":"Breaking the silence isn't betraying your culture; it lets you pass on its best parts on purpose, instead of leaving the feed to teach.","why":"Naming your values out loud is how culture passes on."},"relearn":"Open talk doesn't betray your culture; it lets you pass on its best parts on purpose, rather than ceding them to the feed.","persona":"any","source":"pass on the best"},
  {"id":"tk-997","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"My child can't handle both honest facts and our family's beliefs at once.\"","myth":{"un":"My child can't handle both honest facts and our family's beliefs at once.","re":"Children hold both with ease: the facts to stay safe and your values to guide. It's adults who treat them as a choice.","why":"'How it works' and 'what we believe' aren't rivals."},"relearn":"Children can hold both at once, the facts to stay safe and your values to guide; only adults treat them as a choice.","persona":"Divya","source":"kids hold both"},
  {"id":"tk-998","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"I'll wait for school to give the facts, then I'll add our values.\"","myth":{"un":"I'll wait for school to give the facts, then I'll add our values.","re":"Lessons may be partial or late, and the feed never waits; give the honest facts yourself, with your values, so your voice is the first they trust.","why":"Being the first trusted source is the whole advantage."},"relearn":"Don't outsource the facts and wait; give them yourself with your values, so your trusted voice is the one a child hears first.","persona":"any","source":"don't outsource"},
  {"id":"tk-999","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If I give the facts, my child will think I approve of everything.\"","myth":{"un":"If I give the facts, my child will think I approve of everything.","re":"Knowing how something works isn't the same as a green light; you can give the honest fact and clearly say where you stand on it.","why":"Information and approval are two separate messages."},"relearn":"Giving a fact isn't approval; you can explain how something works and still say clearly where your family stands on it.","persona":"Vikram","source":"facts aren't approval"},
  {"id":"tk-1000","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Strong values mean I don't really need to bother with the facts.\"","myth":{"un":"Strong values mean I don't really need to bother with the facts.","re":"The strongest values still need true information to act on; without the facts, a child can't tell where your guidance actually applies.","why":"Values point the way; facts are the ground to walk on."},"relearn":"Even strong values need true facts to act on; without them a child can't tell where your guidance really applies.","persona":"any","source":"values need ground"},
  {"id":"tk-1001","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a both-and reply that gives facts and values, or a reply that picks just one?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Here's how it works, and here's what we believe.\""},{"id":"b","text":"\"Don't ask, just follow the rule.\""},{"id":"c","text":"\"The facts are these; my hope for you is this.\""},{"id":"d","text":"\"I won't say; you'll learn it somewhere.\""},{"id":"e","text":"\"True answer first, then our family's view.\""},{"id":"f","text":"\"Facts don't matter, only what we believe.\""}],"bins":[{"id":"both","label":"Gives both","valence":"pos"},{"id":"one","label":"Picks just one","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"both","b":"one","c":"both","d":"one","e":"both","f":"one"},"relearn":"A both-and reply pairs the honest fact with your value; picking just one drops safety or your voice.","persona":"any","source":"both or one"},
  {"id":"tk-1002","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: which order makes a tricky answer land, or which order shuts it down?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Honest fact first, then our family's view"},{"id":"b","text":"\"You're too young\" before any answer"},{"id":"c","text":"Calm fact, then 'here's what I hope'"},{"id":"d","text":"A lecture before letting them ask"},{"id":"e","text":"Answer the question, then add the value"},{"id":"f","text":"Shame the question, give nothing"}],"bins":[{"id":"lands","label":"Lands well","valence":"pos"},{"id":"shuts","label":"Shuts it down","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"lands","b":"shuts","c":"lands","d":"shuts","e":"lands","f":"shuts"},"relearn":"Honest facts first, then your values, lands the answer; leading with shame or a lecture shuts the door.","persona":"any","source":"order that lands"},
  {"id":"tk-1003","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: an honest fact about respect and bodies, or a value your family shares?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"A 'no' must always be respected"},{"id":"b","text":"We hope you'll wait for someone you trust"},{"id":"c","text":"Bodies change at different times for everyone"},{"id":"d","text":"In our home, we value loyalty and honesty"},{"id":"e","text":"Saying yes must be free, not pressured"},{"id":"f","text":"We believe relationships deserve care"}],"bins":[{"id":"fact","label":"Honest fact","valence":"pos"},{"id":"value","label":"Family value","valence":"tell"}],"key":{"a":"fact","b":"value","c":"fact","d":"value","e":"fact","f":"value"},"relearn":"How consent and bodies work are honest facts; your hopes about waiting, loyalty and care are values you share.","persona":"Vikram","source":"respect facts vs values"},
  {"id":"tk-1004","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: when facts and elders' silence clash, which protects a child, which keeps the silence?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Give the safety fact kindly, but give it"},{"id":"b","text":"Stay quiet so no relative is upset"},{"id":"c","text":"Answer the child, then tell elders gently"},{"id":"d","text":"Tell the child 'we don't discuss that'"},{"id":"e","text":"Prioritise the child's safety facts"},{"id":"f","text":"Let 'log kya kahenge' decide"}],"bins":[{"id":"protect","label":"Protects the child","valence":"pos"},{"id":"silence","label":"Keeps the silence","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"protect","b":"silence","c":"protect","d":"silence","e":"protect","f":"silence"},"relearn":"Give the safety facts kindly even when elders prefer silence; safety beats 'log kya kahenge'.","persona":"Priya","source":"facts over silence sort"},
  {"id":"tk-1005","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a fact-plus-value 'both-and' reply, or a reply that hides facts to protect a belief?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"\"That's how it works; we believe in waiting.\""},{"id":"b","text":"\"I won't explain; it's against our values.\""},{"id":"c","text":"\"Here's the honest truth, and our hope.\""},{"id":"d","text":"\"Better you don't know that at all.\""},{"id":"e","text":"\"The facts are these; here's our view.\""},{"id":"f","text":"\"We don't talk facts in this family.\""}],"bins":[{"id":"bothand","label":"Both-and","valence":"pos"},{"id":"hides","label":"Hides the facts","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"bothand","b":"hides","c":"bothand","d":"hides","e":"bothand","f":"hides"},"relearn":"A both-and reply pairs the fact with your belief; hiding facts to guard a belief leaves a child unsafe.","persona":"Vikram","source":"both-and vs hide"},
  {"id":"tk-1006","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a calm 'facts + values' habit, or a habit that cedes the field to the feed?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Answer questions honestly, share your view"},{"id":"b","text":"Hope school or the internet covers it"},{"id":"c","text":"Talk early, in small everyday moments"},{"id":"d","text":"Avoid the topic till there's a crisis"},{"id":"e","text":"Pair each fact with what you believe"},{"id":"f","text":"Let the algorithm answer the hard ones"}],"bins":[{"id":"yours","label":"Your voice in the mix","valence":"pos"},{"id":"feed","label":"Cedes to the feed","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"yours","b":"feed","c":"yours","d":"feed","e":"yours","f":"feed"},"relearn":"Honest answers, early small talks and pairing fact with value keep your voice in the mix; avoiding it cedes to the feed.","persona":"any","source":"voice vs feed"},
  {"id":"tk-1007","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: an honest fact that keeps a teen safe, or a value you choose to pass on?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"What consent looks like in a real moment"},{"id":"b","text":"The kind of partner we hope you choose"},{"id":"c","text":"That a lot of online content isn't real"},{"id":"d","text":"Why we value treating people with dignity"},{"id":"e","text":"How to leave a situation that feels off"},{"id":"f","text":"Our hope that you'll never settle for less"}],"bins":[{"id":"fact","label":"Safety fact","valence":"pos"},{"id":"value","label":"Value to pass on","valence":"tell"}],"key":{"a":"fact","b":"value","c":"fact","d":"value","e":"fact","f":"value"},"relearn":"Consent, online reality and how to leave are safety facts; the partner you hope for and dignity are values to pass on.","persona":"Vikram","source":"teen facts vs values"},
  {"id":"tk-1008","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: which closes the gap others would fill, which leaves the gap wide open?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Share your honest view on a hard topic"},{"id":"b","text":"Change the subject every time it comes up"},{"id":"c","text":"Be the first to give the true answer"},{"id":"d","text":"Assume they'll 'just know' the right thing"},{"id":"e","text":"Name what your family believes and why"},{"id":"f","text":"Leave the topic to whoever asks first"}],"bins":[{"id":"closes","label":"Closes the gap","valence":"pos"},{"id":"open","label":"Leaves it open","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"closes","b":"open","c":"closes","d":"open","e":"closes","f":"open"},"relearn":"Sharing your view, answering first and naming your beliefs close the gap; avoiding it leaves it for others to fill.","persona":"any","source":"close the gap"},
  {"id":"tk-1009","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: honest facts a young child needs, or family values you choose to add?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"The correct names for body parts"},{"id":"b","text":"How we greet guests in our home"},{"id":"c","text":"That no one may touch their private parts"},{"id":"d","text":"The traditions we love to celebrate"},{"id":"e","text":"They can always tell a safe grown-up"},{"id":"f","text":"The kindness we hope they show others"}],"bins":[{"id":"fact","label":"Honest fact","valence":"pos"},{"id":"value","label":"Family value","valence":"tell"}],"key":{"a":"fact","b":"value","c":"fact","d":"value","e":"fact","f":"value"},"relearn":"Correct names, body safety and telling a safe adult are facts a young child needs; greetings and traditions are values.","persona":"Divya","source":"early facts vs values"},
  {"id":"tk-1010","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a reply that respects a child's freedom to think, or one that shuts thinking down?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Here's what I believe, and here's why.\""},{"id":"b","text":"\"Believe exactly what I say, full stop.\""},{"id":"c","text":"\"These are the facts; what do you think?\""},{"id":"d","text":"\"There's nothing for you to think about.\""},{"id":"e","text":"\"I'll share my view; you can weigh it.\""},{"id":"f","text":"\"Questioning this isn't allowed here.\""}],"bins":[{"id":"respects","label":"Respects thinking","valence":"pos"},{"id":"shuts","label":"Shuts it down","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"respects","b":"shuts","c":"respects","d":"shuts","e":"respects","f":"shuts"},"relearn":"Sharing your view with a 'why' and inviting their thoughts respects a child; banning questions doesn't.","persona":"Priya","source":"respect thinking"},
  {"id":"tk-1011","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"frank question","hook":"On the drive home, your ten-year-old Farhan asks what 'having sex' means. He heard it on the school bus.","steps":[{"prompt":"There's no escape in the car. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Give a short, true answer, then say what your family believes","then":"Farhan listens, then asks, \"So that's why people get married?\"","best":true},{"text":"Recite the rule that it's only for married people, and stop there","then":"Farhan nods, none the wiser about what it actually is."},{"text":"Say he's far too young to be asking that","then":"Farhan stares out of the window. That night he searches it online."},{"text":"Give a calm, true answer, and keep your beliefs out of it","then":"Farhan gets the facts, but not a word about what you think."}],"why":"A true answer at his level, then your values, keeps him safe and guided."},{"prompt":"A week later, Farhan tells you a boy on the school bus showed him a video about it. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Thank him, say it's not his fault, and tell his school","then":"Farhan looks relieved. \"I didn't like it,\" he says. The school promises to look into it.","best":true},{"text":"Ban him from sitting next to that boy on the bus again","then":"Farhan goes quiet, sure he's in trouble for telling. The questions stay with him."},{"text":"Get angry that he watched something like that at all","then":"Farhan shrinks. \"I didn't want to,\" he mutters, and leaves the room."},{"text":"Say those videos are fake, and leave it at that","then":"Farhan nods, but still looks like he has questions."}],"why":"Thanks and 'not your fault' keep him telling you, and telling his school gets adults to help."},{"prompt":"Later, Farhan asks whether what he saw is what grown-ups really do. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say much of it isn't real or respectful, then share your view","then":"Farhan thinks. \"So real people are kinder?\" he asks. You nod.","best":true},{"text":"Say yes, and that's exactly why it's for adults only","then":"Farhan looks troubled, and decides what he saw must be normal."},{"text":"Say you'd rather not talk about that video ever again","then":"Farhan drops it. The video is left to answer his questions."},{"text":"Explain the facts properly, but skip what you believe about it","then":"Farhan understands more, but your view is missing from the picture."}],"why":"The truth about online content, plus your values, keeps you his trusted source."}],"debrief":"Answer honestly and age-right, then add your values.","relearn":"Answer truly, then add your values; dodging hands it to the feed."},
  {"id":"tk-1012","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"branch","persona":"Priya","source":"relative pressure","hook":"Your sister-in-law says explaining body facts to your eight-year-old Ruhi will 'spoil' her, and values are enough.","steps":[{"prompt":"She says it at a family lunch, in front of Ruhi. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say calmly you teach both, and suggest talking after lunch","then":"Your sister-in-law raises an eyebrow but agrees. Lunch carries on.","best":true},{"text":"Agree with her and drop the facts, just to keep her happy","then":"She nods. Ruhi learns the subject is something to keep quiet about."},{"text":"Argue with her loudly, right there at the table","then":"Voices rise. Ruhi stares at her plate, sure she caused the fight."},{"text":"Change the subject and never raise it with her","then":"Lunch moves on, but Ruhi heard every word, and your silence."}],"why":"A calm 'we do both', with the real talk saved for later, keeps Ruhi out of a fight."},{"prompt":"After lunch, your sister-in-law adds that facts will make Ruhi curious too early. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Explain kindly that honest facts make children safer, not earlier","then":"She's quiet. \"I was told nothing,\" she says. \"It didn't help me.\"","best":true},{"text":"Say she might be right, and you'll hold off for a while","then":"She smiles, relieved. Ruhi's questions go unanswered another year."},{"text":"Tell her to worry about her own children instead","then":"Her face hardens, and she doesn't call for weeks."},{"text":"Send her a long article link, and refuse to discuss it any further","then":"She reads the headline and replies with an angry emoji."}],"why":"Answering the worry itself, kindly, can bring a relative round."},{"prompt":"That evening, Ruhi asks if knowing about bodies will spoil her. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say no, the facts keep her safe and your values guide her","then":"Ruhi nods. \"Both, then,\" she says, pleased with the idea.","best":true},{"text":"Say her Bua worries too much, so she can ignore her","then":"Ruhi giggles. On the next visit, she tells Bua exactly that."},{"text":"Say maybe, so she should keep the facts to herself","then":"Ruhi nods, and decides her body is something shameful."},{"text":"Say not to worry about it, and ask what she'd like for dinner","then":"Ruhi picks paneer, but the worry stays with her."}],"why":"Telling her plainly that facts and values go together settles the worry."},{"prompt":"Next Diwali, Ruhi's Bua asks if Ruhi is still getting 'all those facts'. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say yes, facts plus your values, and leave it kindly there","then":"Bua sighs. \"You're as stubborn as your mother,\" she says, smiling a little.","best":true},{"text":"Laugh and tell her you stopped all of that long ago, of course","then":"Bua is pleased. Now you have a story to keep straight in front of Ruhi."},{"text":"Start the old argument all over again","then":"The festive mood sours, and your husband steps in to calm things."},{"text":"Say 'We'll see' and quickly change the subject","then":"Bua takes it as a win, and repeats her advice all evening."}],"why":"Holding steady, kindly, shows Ruhi the facts aren't up for bargaining."}],"debrief":"Hold to facts-plus-values and explain it kindly.","relearn":"Keep giving facts with your values under pressure; explain kindly, don't drop them."},
  {"id":"tk-1013","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"online false fact","hook":"At dinner, your fifteen-year-old Sid repeats an influencer's claim that when girls say no, they just want to be chased.","steps":[{"prompt":"He says it casually, reaching for the rice. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Calmly say it's false: no means no. Then add your view","then":"Sid pauses mid-scoop. \"Okay, but he says it's science,\" he argues.","best":true},{"text":"Say 'That's disgusting. We don't talk like that in this house.'","then":"Sid rolls his eyes. \"Chill. It's a joke,\" he says, and the claim stands."},{"text":"Laugh along so he doesn't feel judged or lectured","then":"Sid grins, and takes your laugh as agreement."},{"text":"Say it goes against your values, and leave it there","then":"Sid shrugs. \"Your values, not facts,\" he says, and keeps eating."}],"why":"Fixing the false fact first, then adding your values, leaves no lie standing."},{"prompt":"Later, Sid shows you another clip. \"Millions follow him,\" he says. \"He must know.\" What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say views don't make it true, and ask what he thinks","then":"Sid hesitates. \"I mean, I wouldn't want someone ignoring my no,\" he admits.","best":true},{"text":"Tell him to delete that app from his phone right now","then":"Sid clutches his phone. \"You don't even know what's on it,\" he says."},{"text":"Say you won't argue with a phone-addicted teenager","then":"Sid stands up. \"Fine,\" he says, and walks off."},{"text":"Say he's far too clever to believe that, and drop it","then":"Sid shrugs, flattered, but hasn't changed his mind."}],"why":"Questioning the source together teaches him to check claims, not just drop this one."},{"prompt":"A few days later, Sid says his friends think a girl who flirts has agreed to more. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say flirting isn't a yes. Consent is asked for, every time","then":"Sid frowns, thinking. \"Every time? Even if you're dating?\" he asks.","best":true},{"text":"Say girls who flirt like that are really asking for trouble","then":"Sid nods, and the idea settles in as a rule."},{"text":"Tell him those friends sound like a bad influence","then":"Sid bristles. \"You don't even know them,\" he snaps."},{"text":"Say he should just keep away from girls who flirt","then":"Sid laughs. \"That's not the point,\" he says, and the question hangs."}],"why":"Naming what consent actually is protects him and the people he'll date."},{"prompt":"Your wife says quietly, 'Just take his phone. He's getting ideas.' What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say a ban cuts you out, and keep talking with Sid instead","then":"She sighs, then nods. \"Fine. But I want to be part of the next talk.\"","best":true},{"text":"Agree, and take his phone away that night","then":"Sid is furious, and watches the same videos on a friend's phone."},{"text":"Start secretly checking his phone every night instead","then":"Sid finds out within a week, and goes quiet with you for days."},{"text":"Leave it to your wife to handle however she thinks best","then":"She takes the phone. Sid sulks, and the influencer's clips reach him at school anyway."}],"why":"Staying in the conversation keeps your voice louder than the algorithm."},{"prompt":"Weeks later, Sid asks how he can tell if a girl he likes feels the same. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say to ask her, and respect her answer, even a no","then":"Sid goes red. \"Just ask? That's so simple,\" he says, half smiling.","best":true},{"text":"Say girls play hard to get, so he should keep trying","then":"Sid nods, and plans to keep pushing."},{"text":"Say he's too young to be thinking about girls","then":"Sid sighs. \"Forget it,\" he says, and goes back to his videos."},{"text":"Tell him to read her signals closely, then go for it","then":"Sid looks unsure. \"What if I read her wrong?\" he asks."}],"why":"Asking, and respecting the answer, is what consent looks like in real life."}],"debrief":"Correct the false fact calmly first, then offer your values.","relearn":"Fix the false fact, then share your values; values alone leave the lie standing."},
  {"id":"tk-1014","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"branch","persona":"Divya","source":"where babies","hook":"After Maasi's godh bharai, your five-year-old Mira asks where babies come from. You worry the truth will spoil her innocence.","steps":[{"prompt":"Mira tugs at your sleeve, waiting. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say babies grow in a womb, and are welcomed with love","then":"Mira beams. \"So Maasi's baby is in her womb, being loved?\"","best":true},{"text":"Tell a stork story, to keep her innocent a bit longer","then":"Mira believes you, until a cousin laughs at her for it."},{"text":"Say it's a secret just for grown-ups, not little girls","then":"Mira's face falls, and she asks her cousin instead."},{"text":"Say 'From God's blessing, beta', and say nothing more","then":"Mira nods, then asks how the blessing gets into Maasi's tummy."}],"why":"A simple truth, warmed by your values, answers her and keeps her trust."},{"prompt":"At bedtime, Mira asks if she'll have a baby too one day. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say some grown-ups choose to, some don't, and she'll decide","then":"Mira considers it. \"I'll decide when I'm big,\" she says, and yawns.","best":true},{"text":"Say of course, because every girl becomes a mother","then":"Mira nods seriously. \"Every girl,\" she repeats."},{"text":"Say she's far too little to think about such things","then":"Mira pouts and pulls the blanket over her head."},{"text":"Joke that she'd better, since Dadi wants great-grandchildren","then":"Mira giggles, but remembers it as a promise she has to keep."}],"why":"An honest answer that leaves the choice hers shares your values without pressure."},{"prompt":"Next day, your mother says true answers about babies will rob Mira of her innocence. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say simple truths keep her safe, and keep her innocence too","then":"Your mother is quiet. \"She did seem happy asking you,\" she admits.","best":true},{"text":"Agree, and say you'll stick to sweet stories from now on instead","then":"Your mother nods, relieved. Mira's next question gets a fairy tale."},{"text":"Tell her the whole idea of 'innocence' is outdated now","then":"Your mother looks hurt, and changes the subject."},{"text":"Say you'll let her school handle all of it from now on","then":"Your mother agrees. Mira slowly stops asking at home."}],"why":"True, simple answers don't spoil a child but keep her trusting and safe."}],"debrief":"Answer simply and truly at their level, warmed by your values.","relearn":"A simple true answer keeps trust; a stork story or 'secret' sends them elsewhere."},
  {"id":"tk-1015","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"add the reason","hook":"Yesterday you told your eleven-year-old Neel, 'Never send photos of your body to anyone,' but gave no reason.","steps":[{"prompt":"Today he's on his new phone, chatting with game friends. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Explain the honest reason behind the rule","then":"Neel puts the phone down. \"Okay,\" he says, and actually listens.","best":true},{"text":"Leave it. The rule was clear enough on its own","then":"Neel keeps chatting. The rule sits there, with nothing holding it up."},{"text":"Take the phone away until he's a bit older","then":"Neel sulks, and borrows a friend's phone at school."},{"text":"Repeat the rule again, more firmly this time","then":"Neel sighs. \"Yes, I know,\" he says, without looking up."}],"why":"Going back with the reason turns a rule he'll forget into one he understands."},{"prompt":"Neel asks why a photo is such a big deal if it's just for a friend. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say photos can be copied and shared forever, even by friends","then":"Neel frowns. \"Forever? Even if I delete it?\" he asks.","best":true},{"text":"Say it's because good boys just don't do such things, beta","then":"Neel shrugs. \"I'm not doing anything,\" he says, and the point slips past."},{"text":"Say he'd be in huge trouble with you if he ever did","then":"Neel nods. Now he knows to hide it if it ever happens."},{"text":"Say you just don't trust anyone on the internet","then":"Neel rolls his eyes. \"You don't trust anyone,\" he says."}],"why":"The honest 'why' gives him a reason he can repeat to himself, and to friends."},{"prompt":"Neel asks what he should do if someone online asks him for a photo. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say don't send it, and tell you. He won't be in trouble","then":"Neel nods. \"Even if it's someone I know from the game?\" You say yes.","best":true},{"text":"Say to block them, and not bother telling anyone at all","then":"Neel nods. If it ever happens, you'll never know."},{"text":"Say that would never happen to a boy anyway","then":"Neel relaxes, and stops watching for it."},{"text":"Say he'd lose his phone for good if that happened","then":"Neel nods slowly, and decides he'd keep it to himself."}],"why":"Telling you, with no trouble attached, is the step that actually keeps him safe."}],"debrief":"Circle back and give the honest reason; a value with a 'why' lasts.","relearn":"Add the reason behind a bare rule; a 'why' makes a value stick, and going back models repair."},
  {"id":"tk-1016","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"fact now value forming","hook":"Your thirteen-year-old Aditi asks if using a menstrual cup makes her 'not a virgin'. Your own views on this are still forming.","steps":[{"prompt":"She's holding the box, waiting. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say a cup can't change that, and your views are still forming","then":"Aditi relaxes. \"Okay. You'll tell me when you've thought more?\"","best":true},{"text":"Say you'll answer once you've made up your own mind","then":"Aditi puts the box down, and asks her friends that evening."},{"text":"Say 'Of course it does', just to sound certain","then":"Aditi puts the box back, now afraid of something that isn't true."},{"text":"Say pads are simpler for now, and quietly step around the question","then":"Aditi shrugs and takes the pads. Her question goes unanswered."}],"why":"The fact can't wait for your views to settle, and honesty about them builds trust."},{"prompt":"A week later, Aditi asks what 'being a virgin' even means, and why aunties care so much. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Give the true meaning, and say you're still thinking it through","then":"Aditi nods. \"Can we think about it together?\" she asks.","best":true},{"text":"Pretend to hold a firm view that you don't really hold","then":"Aditi senses you're unsure, and trusts your answer a little less."},{"text":"Say it's not a topic for girls her age","then":"Aditi goes quiet, and looks it up on her phone."},{"text":"Give her the meaning, and leave the values part to her school","then":"Aditi gets the facts, but hears nothing of what you think."}],"why":"Facts plus honest, still-forming values show her how to think, not just what."},{"prompt":"That evening, your mother says a parent should never let a child see their doubts. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say honesty about unsure views teaches Aditi more than faking","then":"Your mother purses her lips. \"In my day...\" she starts, then stops.","best":true},{"text":"Agree, and give Aditi your mother's view as final","then":"Aditi hears a rule, not a conversation, and stops asking."},{"text":"Tell your mother to stay out of it","then":"Your mother looks hurt, and the house stays tense all evening."},{"text":"Say you'll have firm answers soon, and hold off on it till then","then":"Your mother nods. Aditi's next question waits for an answer that doesn't come."}],"why":"Truth now, with honest thinking out loud, beats certainty you don't feel."}],"debrief":"Give the fact now and be honest the value is still forming.","relearn":"Give the honest fact now even if your view is forming; truth needn't wait on a settled value."},
  {"id":"tk-1017","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"park at dinner","hook":"At a family dinner, your ten-year-old Pihu asks what a 'wet dream' is. Your father-in-law signals, 'Not here.'","steps":[{"prompt":"The whole table has gone quiet. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say it's a good question for a proper talk after dinner","then":"Pihu nods. \"After dinner, then,\" she says, and goes back to her dal.","best":true},{"text":"Shush her firmly, to keep the peace at the table","then":"Pihu goes red and stares at her plate for the rest of the meal."},{"text":"Insist on answering it fully, right there at the table","then":"Your father-in-law leaves the table. Pihu remembers the scene, not the answer."},{"text":"Laugh and ask her where she hears these things","then":"Everyone laughs. Pihu laughs too, unsure if she's in trouble."}],"why":"Honouring the question and parking it kindly keeps it safe to ask, without a scene."},{"prompt":"After dinner, your father-in-law says girls shouldn't hear about such things. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say kindly that knowing all bodies stops shame and teasing","then":"He grunts. \"In my day, nobody knew anything,\" he says, then shrugs.","best":true},{"text":"Agree, and say you'll only tell her about periods, not boys","then":"He nods. Pihu will hear about boys' changes from boys' jokes instead."},{"text":"Tell him his generation got all of this wrong","then":"He stiffens, and the evening ends in a chilly silence."},{"text":"Say nothing, and quietly do what you think is right","then":"He takes your silence as agreement, and tells the family so."}],"why":"Every child learning about everyone's puberty builds empathy, and that's worth explaining."},{"prompt":"At bedtime, Pihu asks if she embarrassed everyone at dinner. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Tell her it was a good question, and answer it simply now","then":"Pihu listens, then nods. \"So it's just normal? Like periods?\"","best":true},{"text":"Say yes, a little, so next time she should ask in private","then":"Pihu nods, and decides some questions are embarrassing."},{"text":"Say Dadaji overreacted, the way he always does","then":"Pihu giggles, and learns to roll her eyes at her grandfather."},{"text":"Say not to worry about it, and turn off the light","then":"Pihu turns over. The question is still waiting in the dark."}],"why":"Answering it simply now, calmly and in private, shows her the door really is open."},{"prompt":"A week later, Pihu's twelve-year-old cousin Arush laughs that girls shouldn't know 'boy stuff'. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say all kids learn about all bodies, so nobody gets teased","then":"Arush shrugs. \"Fine. As long as she doesn't laugh at my voice.\"","best":true},{"text":"Laugh along with him, and let the cousins sort it out themselves","then":"Arush grins. Pihu goes quiet, feeling she asked about something forbidden."},{"text":"Tell Arush off sharply in front of everyone","then":"Arush sulks, and later whispers to Pihu that she got him in trouble."},{"text":"Tell Pihu to just ignore him and his silly jokes","then":"Pihu shrugs, and Arush keeps believing girls shouldn't know."}],"why":"Normalising everyone's puberty for every child is what ends the teasing."}],"debrief":"Honour the question and park it kindly for a real talk.","relearn":"Honour the question and park it for a real talk; shushing teaches shame, and a scene teaches it's risky."},
  {"id":"tk-1018","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"keep opinions out","hook":"Your sixteen-year-old Aisha asks how contraception works for a school project. 'Just facts,' she adds. 'Keep your opinions out of it.'","steps":[{"prompt":"She's sitting across from you, arms folded. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Give the facts clearly, then offer your view as hers to weigh","then":"Aisha listens to the facts, then raises an eyebrow. \"And your view is?\"","best":true},{"text":"Give only the facts, and swallow your own view","then":"Aisha nods, relieved. Louder voices online will fill in the rest."},{"text":"Refuse to give facts until she hears what you think","then":"Aisha gets up. \"Forget it. I'll google it,\" she says."},{"text":"Give the facts, but slip your own view in as if it were a fact","then":"Aisha catches it. \"That's your opinion, not a fact,\" she says."}],"why":"Clear facts first, then a view she's free to weigh, respects her and still guides her."},{"prompt":"Next day, Aisha says she doesn't see why a parent's view should matter to a teenager. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say it doesn't have to, but you'd like her to know yours","then":"Aisha's arms loosen. \"Fine. Go on, then,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"Say it's because you're her father, full stop","then":"Aisha rolls her eyes. \"Right. Full stop,\" she mutters."},{"text":"Say it shouldn't, and let the whole thing drop","then":"Aisha shrugs. Your view never gets heard."},{"text":"Say it matters because you know better than her friends","then":"Aisha bristles. \"You don't even know my friends,\" she says."}],"why":"Offering a view, not imposing it, is what keeps a teen willing to hear it."},{"prompt":"A week later, Aisha says her friends think parents' views are outdated. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say some might be, and ask which of yours she'd question","then":"Aisha thinks, then names one. You end up talking for an hour.","best":true},{"text":"Say her friends are wrong about most things anyway","then":"Aisha goes cold. \"Wow. Okay,\" she says, and leaves."},{"text":"Agree, and say she should just do whatever her friends do","then":"Aisha looks surprised, then a little lost."},{"text":"Say maybe, but she'll understand when she's older","then":"Aisha rolls her eyes. \"That's what everyone says.\""}],"why":"Staying curious, not defensive, keeps you in the conversation she's already having."},{"prompt":"Months later, Aisha brings you a relationship question and asks what you honestly think. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Give the facts she needs, then your honest view, gently","then":"Aisha nods slowly. \"Thanks. That actually helps,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"Remind her she didn't want your opinion before","then":"Aisha's face falls. \"Never mind,\" she says, and turns away."},{"text":"Give a long speech of everything you've held back","then":"Aisha's eyes glaze over, and she edges towards the door."},{"text":"Give your honest view, but skip the facts she asked about","then":"Aisha listens, but leaves still unsure of the facts."}],"why":"Facts, then an honest view offered gently, is exactly what she came back for."}],"debrief":"Give the facts, then offer your view to weigh.","relearn":"Give the facts, then offer your value to weigh; silence on values lets louder voices win."},
  {"id":"tk-1019","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"match","hook":"Match the honest fact to the family value a parent might pair with it.","pairs":[{"left":"Consent means a free, clear yes","right":"We hope you treat people with care"},{"left":"Bodies develop on their own timeline","right":"No one should be rushed or shamed"},{"left":"A lot of online content isn't real","right":"We value seeing people as whole"},{"left":"You can always leave if it feels unsafe","right":"Come home rather than stay polite"},{"left":"Anyone can say no at any point","right":"We trust you to honour a no"}],"relearn":"Each fact pairs with a value: the fact keeps a child safe, the value carries your family's hope.","persona":"Vikram","source":"fact to value"},
  {"id":"tk-1020","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"match","hook":"Match the child's line to a 'facts then values' reply.","pairs":[{"left":"'What's a condom for?'","right":"It prevents this; here's our hope for you"},{"left":"'My friend has a crush'","right":"Crushes are normal; we value being kind"},{"left":"'Is it bad to feel this?'","right":"Feelings are normal; here's how we act"},{"left":"'Why wait?'","right":"The honest reasons, and what we believe"},{"left":"'Everyone's online dating'","right":"Here are the real risks; here's our view"}],"relearn":"Each line gets the honest fact first, then your value, so a child has the truth and your guidance.","persona":"any","source":"line to reply"},
  {"id":"tk-1021","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"match","hook":"Match a parent's fear to the reframe that lets facts and values sit together.","pairs":[{"left":"'Facts will rob their innocence'","right":"Facts protect; silence leaves them open"},{"left":"'My values will sound preachy'","right":"As your view, values invite, not push"},{"left":"'It's facts or our culture'","right":"Naming values is how culture passes on"},{"left":"'They can't hold both'","right":"Kids carry facts to stay safe, values to guide"},{"left":"'School will handle it'","right":"Be the first trusted voice; lessons run late"}],"relearn":"Each fear has a reframe: facts protect, values invite, both belong, your voice first.","persona":"any","source":"fear to reframe"},
  {"id":"tk-1022","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"match","hook":"Match the topic to a both-and line that gives the fact and your family's value.","pairs":[{"left":"Periods","right":"Here's what happens; we treat it as normal, never shameful"},{"left":"Saying no","right":"A no is always valid; we honour it, always"},{"left":"Online strangers","right":"Here's the real risk; we keep private things private"},{"left":"Respect","right":"Respect means real consent; we expect it both ways"},{"left":"Pornography","right":"Most of it isn't real; we value seeing people whole"}],"relearn":"Each topic gets a both-and line: the honest fact to stay safe and the family value you choose to share.","persona":"Vikram","source":"topic to bothand"},
  {"id":"tk-1023","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"match","hook":"Match what a parent says to whether it's giving a fact, a value, or both.","pairs":[{"left":"\"This is how the body works\"","right":"An honest fact"},{"left":"\"We hope you'll wait for trust\"","right":"A value you share"},{"left":"\"Here's the truth, and our view\"","right":"Both, together"},{"left":"\"No one may touch you here\"","right":"A safety fact"},{"left":"\"In our home we value honesty\"","right":"A family belief"}],"relearn":"Naming whether a line is a fact, a value, or both helps a parent make sure each answer carries both.","persona":"any","source":"label fact or value"},
  {"id":"tk-1024","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"match","hook":"Match the slip to the both-and repair.","pairs":[{"left":"Gave only the rule","right":"Go back and add the honest reason"},{"left":"Gave only the fact","right":"Return and share what you believe"},{"left":"Hid a fact to protect a belief","right":"Offer the fact, then name your belief honestly"},{"left":"Stayed silent to stay neutral","right":"Put your honest view into the mix"},{"left":"Outsourced it to the feed","right":"Be the next trusted voice they hear"}],"relearn":"Every facts-or-values slip has a repair: add what was missing, so a child ends up with both the truth and your view.","persona":"any","source":"slip to repair"},
  {"id":"tk-1025","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"match","hook":"Match the parent's worry about saying their values to the gentle truth that frees them.","pairs":[{"left":"'They'll think I'm controlling'","right":"Offered, not imposed, values respect choice"},{"left":"'I'll get the facts wrong'","right":"'Let's check' is an honest answer"},{"left":"'They won't listen anyway'","right":"A stated value lands quietly over time"},{"left":"'It'll start an argument'","right":"Calm 'here's my view' invites, not fights"},{"left":"'It's not my place'","right":"Your trusted voice is the one they need"}],"relearn":"Each worry about voicing values has a gentle truth: offered calmly, your view belongs.","persona":"Priya","source":"worry to truth"},
  {"id":"tk-1026","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: giving your child a clear fact today doesn't lock in their choices for later. It just means they decide informed. Sit right?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Sits right","They decide informed","Facts now, choices later"],"affirm":"Sharing an accurate fact equips a child to make informed choices later; it doesn't dictate what those choices will be.","relearn":"A fact today doesn't decide their future for them. It means they'll choose with their eyes open.","persona":"any","source":"informed not decided"},
  {"id":"tk-1027","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: sharing your honest view isn't preaching; it's a gift your child gets to weigh. Sit right?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Sits right","A gift to weigh","Not preaching"],"affirm":"Offered as your view rather than a verdict, your values invite a child to think, not feel pushed; they belong in the mix.","relearn":"Sharing your view, offered not imposed, isn't preaching; it's something honest your child gets to weigh.","persona":"Priya","source":"not preaching reflect"},
  {"id":"tk-1028","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: staying silent doesn't keep you neutral; it just lets someone else fill the gap. Land for you?","prompt":"Does that land?","options":["It lands","Silence isn't neutral","I'll speak up"],"affirm":"Silence on values isn't neutral; peers, media and the feed will fill the gap, so your honest voice belongs in the mix.","relearn":"Silence isn't neutral; it cedes the choice to others, so put your honest voice in the mix your child weighs.","persona":"any","source":"not neutral reflect"},
  {"id":"tk-1029","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: if you stay quiet, your child still learns about this, just from a screen or a classmate instead of you. Land?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Lands","Better from me","Someone fills the gap"],"affirm":"A child learns about these topics whether or not the parent speaks; silence simply hands the teaching to less trustworthy sources.","relearn":"Your silence isn't neutral: if you don't fill it, a screen or a classmate will.","persona":"any","source":"silence isn't neutral"},
  {"id":"tk-1030","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: 'here's how it works, and here's what we believe' is one sentence your child can hold whole. Feel true?","prompt":"How's that sit?","options":["Feels true","One whole sentence","I can say that"],"affirm":"Pairing the fact and your value in a single calm breath shows a child the two aren't rivals; they belong together.","relearn":"'Here's how it works, and here's what we believe' is one honest sentence; the fact and the value belong together.","persona":"any","source":"one sentence reflect"},
  {"id":"tk-1031","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: giving a fact isn't the same as approving of it; you can be honest and still say where you stand. True for you?","prompt":"Sound right?","options":["Sounds right","Fact isn't approval","I can do both"],"affirm":"Explaining how something works and saying clearly where your family stands are two separate, honest messages.","relearn":"Giving a fact isn't approval; you can explain how something works and still say where your family stands.","persona":"Vikram","source":"fact not approval reflect"},
  {"id":"tk-1032","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: not having a settled opinion yet is okay; you can still give your child the honest fact today. Resonate?","prompt":"What do you feel?","options":["Resonates","Truth needn't wait","I'll be honest"],"affirm":"An honest fact doesn't have to wait for a settled view; you can give the truth now and say the value is still forming.","relearn":"You can give the honest fact today even if your view is still forming; truth needn't wait on a settled opinion.","persona":"any","source":"value still forming reflect"},
  {"id":"tk-1033","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: the goal isn't to win agreement; it's to give the facts and your view, and trust your child to weigh them. Sit well?","prompt":"How's that feel?","options":["Sits well","Trust them to weigh","Not about winning"],"affirm":"Giving honest facts and your values, then trusting a child to weigh them, keeps the door open far better than demanding agreement.","relearn":"The aim isn't agreement; give the facts and your view and trust your child to weigh both, with the door open.","persona":"Priya","source":"not about winning"},
  {"id":"tk-1034","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"both honestly","hook":"Your thirteen-year-old Nitya comes home full of news about her classmate Zara.","setup":"She drops her school bag and follows you into the kitchen.","steps":[{"prompt":"Nitya asks: \"Zara has a boyfriend now. Is that even allowed at thirteen?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Lots of teens like someone. Here's what we hope for you.\"","then":"Nitya perches on the counter. \"Okay, tell me,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"\"Absolutely not. And you're to stop being friends with Zara.\"","then":"Nitya gapes. \"What? That's so unfair!\""},{"text":"\"Do whatever you want, beta. It's your life, really.\"","then":"Nitya blinks. \"Really? You don't even care?\""},{"text":"\"Never mind Zara. You just do as we say.\"","then":"Nitya frowns. \"But say what, though?\""}],"why":"Normal facts about crushes, then your hopes, is an answer she can actually use."},{"prompt":"Nitya asks: \"How would I even know if someone's good for me?\"","options":[{"text":"\"They respect your no, and you feel safe. That matters to me.\"","then":"Nitya nods. \"So not just someone cute,\" she says, grinning.","best":true},{"text":"\"You'll just know when you're older. Don't worry about it now.\"","then":"Nitya sighs. \"That's not helpful at all.\""},{"text":"\"If he's from a good family, then he's fine.\"","then":"Nitya frowns. \"So his family matters more than how he treats me?\""},{"text":"\"If he's nice to you and buys you nice things.\"","then":"Nitya raises an eyebrow. \"That's it?\""}],"why":"Respect and safety are the facts of a healthy relationship, and saying they matter to you is your value."},{"prompt":"Nitya asks: \"And if I do like someone? Will you be angry?\"","options":[{"text":"\"No. I'd want you to tell me, and I'd share what I think.\"","then":"Nitya smiles. \"Okay. You'll be the first to know,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"\"Yes, very. So don't even think about it.\"","then":"Nitya says, \"Okay,\" and quietly decides she'd hide it."},{"text":"\"No, but you'll be far too busy with your studies anyway.\"","then":"Nitya rolls her eyes. \"That's not really an answer.\""},{"text":"\"Only if you're silly enough to hide it from me.\"","then":"Nitya frowns. \"So I'd be in trouble either way?\""}],"why":"Being told first, and sharing your view, keeps you in her corner."}],"relearn":"Pairing the honest facts with your stated values gives a child both safety and your guidance to weigh."},
  {"id":"tk-1035","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"offer not impose roleplay","hook":"You've been explaining consent to your fifteen-year-old Rehaan, and added what you believe about waiting.","setup":"He tosses his phone onto the bed and looks up.","steps":[{"prompt":"Rehaan snaps: \"You're just forcing your beliefs on me.\"","options":[{"text":"\"The facts are yours to keep. My view is yours to weigh.\"","then":"Rehaan pauses. \"So I can disagree?\" he asks, suspicious.","best":true},{"text":"\"You'll believe what I believe. End of discussion.\"","then":"Rehaan reaches for his headphones, then stops. \"Seriously? Great talk.\""},{"text":"\"Fine. Just forget I said anything about it, then.\"","then":"Rehaan shrugs. \"Fine by me.\""},{"text":"\"I'm not forcing anything. I'm telling you what's right.\"","then":"Rehaan snorts. \"That's literally forcing.\""}],"why":"Separating the facts from your view, and leaving the view to him, respects a teen."},{"prompt":"Rehaan says: \"My friends' parents don't lecture them about this stuff.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Maybe. I'd rather you hear it from me than a feed.\"","then":"Rehaan half smiles. \"The feed is pretty weird,\" he admits.","best":true},{"text":"\"Then go and live with your friends' parents.\"","then":"Rehaan turns away. \"Wow. Okay.\""},{"text":"\"Your friends' parents clearly don't care enough.\"","then":"Rehaan bristles. \"Don't talk about them like that.\""},{"text":"\"Okay. I'll stop talking about it altogether, then.\"","then":"Rehaan shrugs. \"Good.\""}],"why":"Staying in the conversation, lightly, keeps your voice in the mix."},{"prompt":"After a pause, Rehaan asks: \"So what if I end up disagreeing with you?\"","options":[{"text":"\"You might. I'll still be here, and still want you safe.\"","then":"Rehaan nods slowly. \"Okay. That's actually fair.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Then you'll just have to learn it the hard way, won't you?\"","then":"Rehaan scoffs. \"Thanks for the confidence.\""},{"text":"\"You won't, beta, if you're smart about it.\"","then":"Rehaan frowns. \"So I'm stupid if I disagree?\""},{"text":"\"Then that's your problem, not mine, is it?\"","then":"Rehaan goes quiet. \"Right,\" he says."}],"why":"Love that doesn't depend on agreement keeps a teen talking to you."},{"prompt":"Rehaan asks, quieter: \"Can I ask you something without getting a lecture?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Yes. Facts first. My view only if you want it.\"","then":"Rehaan sits up. \"Okay. So, about this girl in my class...\"","best":true},{"text":"\"That depends on what it is, doesn't it?\"","then":"Rehaan looks away. \"Never mind, then.\""},{"text":"\"If it's about girls, then the answer is no.\"","then":"Rehaan groans. \"Forget it.\""},{"text":"\"Sure, but I'll have to tell you what I think.\"","then":"Rehaan hesitates. \"Maybe later, then.\""}],"why":"Facts first, views on request, is the deal that makes a teen come back."}],"relearn":"Offering your view as theirs to weigh, not a command, respects a teen and keeps them willing to keep talking."},
  {"id":"tk-1036","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"role-play","persona":"Priya","source":"back facts to relative","hook":"Mausi overheard you explaining periods to your nine-year-old Aarohi, and she isn't happy.","setup":"She corners you in the kitchen, voice lowered.","steps":[{"prompt":"Mausi says: \"Values are all a girl needs. Why fill her head with such things?\"","options":[{"text":"\"We teach both, Mausi. Facts keep her safe, and values guide her.\"","then":"Mausi purses her lips. \"Both? Hmm,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"\"You're right, Mausi. I'll stop explaining these things to her.\"","then":"Mausi nods. \"Good. She'll learn when it's time.\""},{"text":"\"She's my daughter, Mausi. Please stay out of it.\"","then":"Mausi draws back. \"I was only trying to help.\""},{"text":"\"The school asked us to do it. It wasn't my idea.\"","then":"Mausi tuts. \"Schools! What will they teach next?\""}],"why":"Naming 'both', kindly, backs the facts without a fight."},{"prompt":"Mausi adds, half to herself: \"In our time, girls found out when it happened. We coped.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Many of us were scared, Mausi. I want Aarohi ready.\"","then":"Mausi is quiet. \"I thought I was dying,\" she says softly.","best":true},{"text":"\"Your time was a disaster, honestly, Mausi.\"","then":"Mausi's face tightens. \"Is that so?\""},{"text":"\"True. Maybe I'll wait until she actually starts, then.\"","then":"Mausi smiles. \"Sensible girl.\""},{"text":"\"Let's just agree to disagree on this one, Mausi.\"","then":"Mausi sniffs. \"As you like,\" she says, unconvinced."}],"why":"Preparing before the changes is what keeps a first period from being frightening."},{"prompt":"Mausi asks: \"And what will people say if she talks about it openly?\"","options":[{"text":"\"That she knows her own body. That's nothing to hide.\"","then":"Mausi shakes her head, half smiling. \"Such a modern mother,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"\"You're right, Mausi. I'll tell her never to mention it.\"","then":"Mausi nods. \"Good. Some things stay private.\""},{"text":"\"Honestly, Mausi, who cares what people say?\"","then":"Mausi frowns. \"You will, when it's your family they talk about.\""},{"text":"\"She'll only talk about it with me. Don't worry.\"","then":"Mausi nods. \"Good. Keep it that way.\""}],"why":"Treating her knowledge as normal teaches Aarohi there's no shame in it."},{"prompt":"Aarohi walks in, and Mausi asks her: \"Did your mother tell you grown-up things?\"","options":[{"text":"\"I did. Aarohi, you can ask me or Mausi anything.\"","then":"Mausi blinks, then smiles at Aarohi. \"Anything, beta,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"\"No, no, nothing like that. Go and play, beta.\"","then":"Mausi nods, satisfied. \"Good girl. Off you go.\""},{"text":"\"Aarohi, don't answer that. Go to your room, please.\"","then":"Mausi stiffens. \"So now she can't even talk to me?\""},{"text":"\"Mausi, please, don't embarrass her like this.\"","then":"Mausi looks stung. \"Embarrass her? I only asked.\""}],"why":"Owning it openly, and inviting Mausi in, gives Aarohi one more safe adult."}],"relearn":"Backing the facts kindly in front of a relative keeps a child safe and shows the door to honest talk stays open."},
  {"id":"tk-1037","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"fact then value roleplay","hook":"Your eleven-year-old Ishita comes home worried about a classmate, Mehak.","setup":"She sits on the kitchen counter, swinging her legs.","steps":[{"prompt":"Ishita asks: \"Can you get pregnant from kissing? Mehak thinks she is.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Good question. No, you can't. Here's how it really works.\"","then":"Ishita lets out a breath. \"Phew. Okay, tell me,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"\"That's not something we talk about. Just trust the rule.\"","then":"Ishita frowns. \"What rule? Nobody told me a rule.\""},{"text":"\"Yes, it can happen, so don't let anyone kiss you.\"","then":"Ishita's eyes go wide. \"So Mehak really is pregnant?\""},{"text":"\"Of course not. Don't be so silly, Ishita.\"","then":"Ishita flushes. \"I only asked,\" she mumbles."}],"why":"A calm, honest answer to a frank question keeps you her trusted source."},{"prompt":"Ishita asks: \"So how does someone actually get pregnant?\"","options":[{"text":"\"A sperm and egg must meet. Kissing can't do that. Is Mehak okay?\"","then":"Ishita nods slowly. \"She's just scared. I'll tell her to talk to her mum too.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"You'll find out all about it when you're married, beta.\"","then":"Ishita groans. \"That's years away!\""},{"text":"\"Why do you want to know? Who have you been kissing?\"","then":"Ishita goes red. \"Nobody! I was asking for Mehak.\""},{"text":"\"Your biology teacher will cover all of that next year.\"","then":"Ishita sighs. \"Next year is ages away.\""}],"why":"A simple, true fact beats a lasting myth, and asking after Mehak makes sure she has help too."},{"prompt":"Ishita asks: \"What do you actually think about kissing and stuff?\"","options":[{"text":"\"I hope you'll wait till you're ready, and feel respected.\"","then":"Ishita thinks. \"Ready how?\" she asks, and you talk it through.","best":true},{"text":"\"I think it's disgusting, and so should you.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" Ishita says uncertainly, and looks away."},{"text":"\"My opinion doesn't matter, beta. Do whatever feels right.\"","then":"Ishita frowns. \"But I asked what you think.\""},{"text":"\"I'll tell you what I think when you're older.\"","then":"Ishita crosses her arms. \"I'm eleven. I'm older now.\""}],"why":"After the facts, your values give her something to steer by."}],"relearn":"Answering the frank question honestly, then adding your value, keeps you the trusted source instead of the feed."},
  {"id":"tk-1038","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"correct then view roleplay","hook":"Your fourteen-year-old Anvi repeats a claim her friend Riddhi saw online.","setup":"She's scrolling on the sofa while you fold clothes.","steps":[{"prompt":"Anvi says: \"Riddhi says boys can't control themselves, so girls must dress carefully.\"","options":[{"text":"\"That isn't true. Everyone controls their own actions.\"","then":"Anvi looks up. \"Wait, really? Riddhi was so sure.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"That's nonsense, and against our values. Just drop it.\"","then":"Anvi shrugs. \"Okay, okay,\" she says, and goes back to scrolling."},{"text":"\"Well, it's safer to dress carefully anyway.\"","then":"Anvi nods. \"So Riddhi's right, then.\""},{"text":"\"Don't listen to Riddhi. She says silly things.\"","then":"Anvi bristles. \"She's my best friend.\""}],"why":"Correcting the false fact calmly first leaves no lie for your values to fight."},{"prompt":"Anvi holds up her phone and asks: \"Why does everyone online keep saying it?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Some accounts get views by blaming girls. It's still false.\"","then":"Anvi frowns. \"That's so messed up,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"\"Because the whole internet is full of rubbish. Stay off it.\"","then":"Anvi rolls her eyes. \"Everyone's on it, though.\""},{"text":"\"Maybe they know something that we don't.\"","then":"Anvi frowns. \"So it could be true?\""},{"text":"\"I don't really know. Let's not get into all that.\"","then":"Anvi shrugs. \"Okay. Whatever,\" she says, still wondering."}],"why":"Showing her why a lie spreads helps her spot the next one."},{"prompt":"Anvi asks: \"So what do you actually believe about it?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Everyone deserves respect, whatever they wear.\"","then":"Anvi nods. \"I'm telling Riddhi that,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"\"Girls should still be careful. That's just life.\"","then":"Anvi frowns. \"That sounds like the same thing, though.\""},{"text":"\"It doesn't really matter what I believe, beta.\"","then":"Anvi looks down. \"It does to me,\" she says quietly."},{"text":"\"I believe you should just stay away from boys.\"","then":"Anvi rolls her eyes. \"That's not an answer.\""}],"why":"After the facts, a clear value gives her something to stand on."},{"prompt":"Anvi asks: \"Can I show you the next weird thing I see online?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Please do. We'll check it together, anytime.\"","then":"Anvi grins. \"Okay. There's a lot of weird stuff,\" she warns.","best":true},{"text":"\"Only if you promise to unfollow those people.\"","then":"Anvi looks away. \"Never mind, then.\""},{"text":"\"I'd rather you just stayed off those sites.\"","then":"Anvi frowns. \"So that's a no?\""},{"text":"\"Sure, but I'll probably be busy with work.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" Anvi says, unsure if you meant it."}],"why":"Welcoming the next claim keeps her bringing them to you, not the feed."}],"relearn":"Correcting the false fact calmly, then offering your view, fixes the error and keeps a teen bringing claims to you."},
  {"id":"tk-1039","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"add why roleplay","hook":"Yesterday your twelve-year-old Dhruv used a crude word for girls. You told him never to say it again, and left it there.","setup":"Today you find him doing homework at the table.","steps":[{"prompt":"Dhruv mutters: \"Are you still angry about yesterday?\"","options":[{"text":"\"No. I gave a rule without a reason. Can I explain?\"","then":"Dhruv looks up from his book. \"Okay,\" he says, warily.","best":true},{"text":"\"The rule's the rule. You don't need a reason.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" Dhruv says flatly, eyes on his book."},{"text":"\"Yes, and I'll be angry every time you say it.\"","then":"Dhruv shrugs. \"Fine. I won't say it near you.\""},{"text":"\"Let's just forget all about it, beta. It's done.\"","then":"Dhruv shrugs. \"Okay.\""}],"why":"Going back to add the reason models honest repair."},{"prompt":"Dhruv asks: \"Everyone says it. What's even wrong with it?\"","options":[{"text":"\"It turns girls into objects. It's meant to put them down.\"","then":"Dhruv frowns. \"I didn't think of it like that,\" he admits.","best":true},{"text":"\"It's dirty. Good boys don't say dirty words, Dhruv.\"","then":"Dhruv shrugs. \"So it's just about sounding good?\""},{"text":"\"If everyone jumped off a cliff, would you jump off too?\"","then":"Dhruv rolls his eyes. \"That's not an answer.\""},{"text":"\"Your teachers would be so shocked if they ever heard that.\"","then":"Dhruv shrugs. \"They're not there, though.\""}],"why":"The honest meaning of the word is the fact his rule was missing."},{"prompt":"Dhruv asks: \"So what do we believe, then?\"","options":[{"text":"\"That everyone deserves respect, in words too.\"","then":"Dhruv nods slowly. \"Okay. That makes sense,\" he says.","best":true},{"text":"\"That boys should always be careful around girls.\"","then":"Dhruv frowns. \"Careful how?\""},{"text":"\"That you should do as you're told in this house.\"","then":"Dhruv sighs. \"Right.\""},{"text":"\"That some words just aren't for our family.\"","then":"Dhruv shrugs. \"But why not, though?\""}],"why":"Linking the rule to respect gives it a 'why' he can carry with him."}],"relearn":"Going back to add the honest reason behind a rule gives a value a 'why' that lasts and models honest repair."},
  {"id":"tk-1040","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"role-play","persona":"Divya","source":"normalise roleplay","hook":"Feeding the baby, you flush when your six-year-old Laila asks how the milk comes out. She notices.","setup":"She edges closer, watching your face.","steps":[{"prompt":"Laila asks, unsure now: \"Is it a bad thing to ask?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Not at all. Breasts make milk for babies. It's amazing.\"","then":"Laila's face lights up. \"Like a fridge inside you?\" she asks.","best":true},{"text":"\"Shh. We don't talk about that. It's not nice.\"","then":"Laila shrinks back. \"Sorry,\" she whispers."},{"text":"\"Go and play, Laila. I'm busy with the baby right now.\"","then":"Laila trails to the door, then turns back, still curious."},{"text":"\"No, but it's a bit embarrassing, so let's not, okay?\"","then":"Laila frowns. \"Why is it embarrassing?\""}],"why":"Saying it's fine to ask, then giving the plain fact, turns your blush into trust."},{"prompt":"Laila asks: \"Did I drink milk like that too?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Yes, or from a bottle. Both help babies grow.\"","then":"Laila nods. \"And now I eat parathas,\" she says proudly.","best":true},{"text":"\"That's enough questions about that for today.\"","then":"Laila pouts. \"But I want to know.\""},{"text":"\"Chhi, beta, don't ask such things.\"","then":"Laila looks at the floor. \"Sorry.\""},{"text":"\"I don't remember. Go and ask your father.\"","then":"Laila frowns. \"But you were the one feeding me.\""}],"why":"A simple, true answer keeps the topic ordinary and warm."},{"prompt":"Laila asks: \"Can I tell my friends about it?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Yes. It's normal. Bodies are private, but never shameful.\"","then":"Laila nods. \"Private, not shameful,\" she repeats, trying it out.","best":true},{"text":"\"No! Never tell anyone about it, Laila.\"","then":"Laila's eyes go wide. \"Is it a secret, then?\""},{"text":"\"Better not. People might think you're being rude.\"","then":"Laila frowns. \"Why would it be rude?\""},{"text":"\"Tell them the baby drinks milk, and leave out the rest.\"","then":"Laila tilts her head. \"Why leave it out?\""}],"why":"Your value, private but not shameful, sits naturally beside the facts."}],"relearn":"Normalising the question and giving facts plus your values shows a child the topic is safe to bring to you."},
  {"id":"tk-1041","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two lines that drop either the facts or your values instead of giving both.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Here's how it works, and here's what we believe.\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"Just follow the rule; the facts don't matter.\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"The honest answer is this; my hope is that.\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"I'll give facts but keep my views to myself.\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"True answer first, then our family's view.\"","trick":false}],"why":"A bare rule with no facts, or facts with your values withheld, each gives a child only half.","relearn":"A both-and reply gives the fact and your value; dropping either leaves a child with half.","persona":"any","source":"spot dropped half"},
  {"id":"tk-1042","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two moves that cede the field instead of putting your voice in the mix.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Share your honest view on the hard topic","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Stay silent and call it staying neutral","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Answer the question before the feed does","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Leave it for the algorithm to explain","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Name what your family believes and why","trick":false}],"why":"Silence isn't neutral and the algorithm doesn't wait; both hand the lesson to others, not your voice.","relearn":"Silence and the feed cede the field; sharing your view and answering first keep your voice in the mix.","persona":"any","source":"spot cede the field"},
  {"id":"tk-1043","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two replies that hide a fact to protect a belief, instead of giving both.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"That's how it works; we believe in waiting.\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"Better you never learn that fact at all.\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"Here's the honest truth, and here's our hope.\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"We don't explain that; it's against our values.\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"The facts are these; here's our family's view.\"","trick":false}],"why":"Refusing a fact to guard a belief leaves a child unsafe; it gets learned anyway, minus you.","relearn":"Hiding a needed fact to guard a belief leaves a child unsafe; give the fact, then the belief.","persona":"Vikram","source":"spot hide fact"},
  {"id":"tk-1044","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two reactions that teach a child the topic is shameful rather than safe to ask.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Good question, let's talk about it properly.\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"Don't ever say that word again.\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"Here's the honest answer at your level.\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Gasping and changing the subject fast","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"No question is silly; ask me anything.\"","trick":false}],"why":"Snapping at a word or flinching teaches a child the topic is shameful and sends the next question elsewhere.","relearn":"Calm, welcoming answers keep a child asking you; shock or flinching teach shame and send them to the feed.","persona":"any","source":"spot shame reaction"},
  {"id":"tk-1045","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two myths this game exists to bust about facts and values.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Honest facts and your values both protect","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"Giving facts gives kids the wrong ideas\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Kids can hold the facts and your values","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"It's facts or our values, never both\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Your trusted voice belongs in the mix","trick":false}],"why":"'Facts give ideas' and 'it's one or the other' are the myths the game busts; both facts and your values protect.","relearn":"Facts don't 'give ideas', and it's never facts-or-values; the honest facts and your values protect a child together.","persona":"any","source":"spot the myths"},
  {"id":"tk-1046","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two ordering mistakes that shut a tricky answer down before the value can land.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Give the honest fact, then add your view","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Open with \"you're too young to know\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Answer first, then share what you hope","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Lecture for ten minutes before they ask","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Reassure with the fact, then guide gently","trick":false}],"why":"Leading with 'too young' or a long lecture shuts the child down, so the value never gets a chance to land.","relearn":"Give the honest fact first, then your value; leading with 'too young' or a lecture shuts the answer down.","persona":"any","source":"spot order mistake"},
  {"id":"tk-1047","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two replies that leave a teen's guidance to louder voices instead of yours.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Here are the facts, and here's my view.\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"Figure the values out yourself.\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"That's how it works; here's my hope.\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"No comment; your friends' view is fine.\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"True answer first, then where I stand.\"","trick":false}],"why":"Refusing to share your view hands a teen's guidance to friends and the feed; your voice belongs in the mix.","relearn":"Silence on values leaves a teen's guidance to louder voices; give the facts and your honest view.","persona":"Vikram","source":"spot leave to others"},
  {"id":"tk-1048","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: a true thing to confirm for your child, or an online myth to correct kindly?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"A clear 'no' must always be respected"},{"id":"b","text":"\"Real relationships look like what's on screen\""},{"id":"c","text":"Bodies vary, and that's normal"},{"id":"d","text":"\"Pressuring someone is just being confident\""},{"id":"e","text":"Consent can be taken back at any time"},{"id":"f","text":"\"If they liked you once, they always owe you\""}],"bins":[{"id":"true","label":"True, confirm it","valence":"pos"},{"id":"myth","label":"Online myth, correct it","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"true","b":"myth","c":"true","d":"myth","e":"true","f":"myth"},"relearn":"Confirm the true facts about consent and bodies; correct the online myths kindly, so your voice is the trusted one.","persona":"Vikram","source":"true or online myth"},
  {"id":"tk-1049","cat":"facts-and-values","type":"match","hook":"Match the child's stage to the facts-plus-values headline that fits it.","pairs":[{"left":"Early years","right":"Correct names and body safety, plus our kindness"},{"left":"Before puberty","right":"What's coming and why, plus 'never be ashamed'"},{"left":"Teen years","right":"Consent and online reality, plus respect both ways"},{"left":"Any age","right":"Honest answers, plus what our family believes"},{"left":"After a fumble","right":"The true correction, plus 'you can always ask me'"}],"relearn":"Each stage gets honest facts paired with your values; the facts shift with age, the both-and habit stays the same.","persona":"any","source":"stage to headline"},
  {"id":"tk-1080","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Divya","source":"start small now","hook":"\"I'll wait until my child is old enough to bring these things up themselves.\"","myth":{"un":"I'll wait until my child is old enough to bring these things up themselves.","re":"Start small now; a child who's never invited to ask usually stays quiet and learns from the feed instead.","why":"Waiting for them to start often means the talks never begin."},"relearn":"Don't wait for a child to raise it; start small, age-right chats now so they know they can come to you.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1081","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Vikram","source":"answering keeps you source","hook":"\"If I answer their questions, I'm just putting ideas in their head.\"","myth":{"un":"If I answer their questions, I'm just putting ideas in their head.","re":"Honest, age-right answers don't plant ideas; they keep you the trusted source instead of the internet.","why":"Answering protects; silence hands the topic to the algorithm."},"relearn":"Answering honestly doesn't put ideas in a child's head; it keeps you their trusted source over the feed.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1082","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Vikram","source":"both parents askable","hook":"\"These talks are really the mother's job, not mine.\"","myth":{"un":"These talks are really the mother's job, not mine.","re":"A child with two askable parents has two open doors; both of you being calm and willing doubles the safety.","why":"Two askable parents are better than one."},"relearn":"These talks aren't only a mother's job; both parents being askable gives a child two open doors.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1083","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"any","source":"plain words land","hook":"\"I have to explain it perfectly, like a textbook, or I'll get it wrong.\"","myth":{"un":"I have to explain it perfectly, like a textbook, or I'll get it wrong.","re":"Simple, plain words at the child's level land far better than a perfect textbook speech.","why":"Clear and simple beats correct-but-overwhelming."},"relearn":"You don't need textbook-perfect answers; simple, plain words at a child's level land best.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1084","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Divya","source":"fumbling is fine","hook":"\"If I blush or stumble over my words, I've ruined the whole conversation.\"","myth":{"un":"If I blush or stumble over my words, I've ruined the whole conversation.","re":"Blushing or fumbling doesn't ruin it; staying warm and open is what your child actually remembers.","why":"Children remember that you stayed open, not that you were smooth."},"relearn":"Stumbling doesn't ruin a talk; staying warm and open is what your child remembers, not your polish.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1085","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"any","source":"calm is the goal","hook":"\"If I stay calm and don't react, they'll think they can ask me anything.\"","myth":{"un":"If I stay calm and don't react, they'll think they can ask me anything.","re":"A child being able to ask you anything is exactly the goal; your calm is what keeps that door open.","why":"Being the one they can ask anything is the win, not the risk."},"relearn":"Staying calm so a child can ask you anything is the goal, not a danger; your calm keeps the door open.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1086","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Divya","source":"silence cedes field","hook":"\"They'll come and ask me when they're ready, so I don't need to start.\"","myth":{"un":"They'll come and ask me when they're ready, so I don't need to start.","re":"Most children won't raise it first; if you don't open the door, friends and screens answer instead.","why":"Your silence doesn't keep them neutral; it lets others teach them."},"relearn":"Most children won't bring it up first; if you stay silent, peers and screens fill the gap instead of you.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1087","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"any","source":"many not one","hook":"\"Once I've had one good talk about all this, my job is basically done.\"","myth":{"un":"Once I've had one good talk about all this, my job is basically done.","re":"It's never one-and-done; it's many small chats over years as your child grows and new questions arise.","why":"Children grow into new questions; the door stays useful for years."},"relearn":"One talk is never enough; it's many small, age-right chats over the years as a child keeps growing.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1088","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"any","source":"honour and park","hook":"\"I have to answer the very second they ask, and answer it perfectly.\"","myth":{"un":"I have to answer the very second they ask, and answer it perfectly.","re":"You can honour the question and park it briefly: 'great question, let's talk properly after dinner.'","why":"A warm 'let's talk later' keeps it safe to ask without rushing you."},"relearn":"You needn't answer perfectly on the spot; honour the question and park it warmly for a calmer moment.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1089","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Priya","source":"calm reassures","hook":"\"Talking about bodies and growing up will only frighten my child.\"","myth":{"un":"Talking about bodies and growing up will only frighten my child.","re":"Calm, honest, age-right answers reassure children; it's confusion and silence that leave them anxious.","why":"A calm answer settles a child; an avoided question worries them more."},"relearn":"Calm, age-right talks reassure rather than frighten; it's silence and confusion that leave a child anxious.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1090","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Vikram","source":"find out together","hook":"\"If I look unsure or don't know the answer, my child will lose trust in me.\"","myth":{"un":"If I look unsure or don't know the answer, my child will lose trust in me.","re":"'I don't know, let's find out together' builds trust; it models honesty and keeps you their go-to.","why":"Honest not-knowing earns more trust than a confident guess."},"relearn":"Not knowing won't cost you trust; 'let's find out together' models honesty and keeps you their go-to.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1091","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"branch","persona":"Divya","source":"babies at dinner","hook":"At dinner with your in-laws, your four-year-old Noor suddenly asks where babies come from.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your in-laws stop eating and look at you. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say calmly that babies grow in a womb, inside a mother","then":"Noor nods. \"Like Maasi's baby,\" she says, and goes back to her rice.","best":true},{"text":"Laugh it off and say 'Not at the table, ask later'","then":"Noor looks confused, then embarrassed, and doesn't ask again."},{"text":"Say the doctor brings them in a big bag","then":"Noor believes you, and tells all her playschool friends."},{"text":"Explain sperm, eggs and birth in full, there and then","then":"Noor loses interest halfway, and your in-laws look stunned."}],"why":"A simple, true answer, given calmly right there, makes it a normal thing to ask."},{"prompt":"Later, your mother-in-law says quietly that such questions should wait until Noor is older. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say a simple truth now makes the later talks easier","then":"She considers it. \"Well, she does ask a lot,\" she says, softening.","best":true},{"text":"Agree, and promise to keep such talk away from Noor","then":"She nods. Noor's next question will go somewhere else."},{"text":"Tell her things have changed a lot since her day","then":"She stiffens, and the rest of dinner is quiet."},{"text":"Say nothing, and quickly offer her more sabzi","then":"She takes the sabzi, and her view stands unanswered."}],"why":"Starting early with simple truths is what makes the harder talks easier later."},{"prompt":"At bedtime, Noor asks if she said something naughty at dinner. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Tell her it was a good question, and she can always ask","then":"Noor smiles and snuggles in. \"Can I ask another one tomorrow?\"","best":true},{"text":"Say yes, a little, so she should ask in private","then":"Noor nods, and learns that some questions make trouble."},{"text":"Say Dadi just got a bit shy, and leave it there","then":"Noor thinks about it, still unsure if asking was okay."},{"text":"Say she should think carefully before she speaks next time","then":"Noor's face falls, and she pulls the blanket up."}],"why":"Telling her plainly the question was welcome keeps her asking you."}],"debrief":"Answer 'where do babies come from' simply and truthfully at the child's level, not with shame.","relearn":"Meet 'where do babies come from' with a simple, true, calm answer at their level, not a brush-off."},
  {"id":"tk-1092","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"repair a fumble","hook":"Yesterday you snapped 'not now' at your child's body question, and it has bothered you since.","steps":[{"prompt":"This evening your child is doing homework at the table. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Bring home their favourite snack to make up for it","then":"They grin at the treat. Neither of you mentions the question."},{"text":"Say nothing and hope they've forgotten about it","then":"The evening passes quietly. The question hangs there, unasked and unanswered."},{"text":"Sit beside them, say sorry, and ask them to ask again","then":"They look up, surprised, then quietly ask it again. It was about where babies come out.","best":true},{"text":"Leave a children's body book on their bed without a word","then":"They flip through it later, unsure whether you'd welcome the question now."}],"why":"Saying sorry and inviting the question again shows your child the door really is open."},{"prompt":"Next evening your child hovers near you, starts to ask something, then says 'never mind'. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Let it go. They'll ask when they're ready","then":"They drift off to their room. Whatever it was stays with them."},{"text":"Ask their older cousin to find out what's on their mind","then":"The cousin reports back that it's a body question. Your child feels talked about."},{"text":"Say 'Only if it's quick. I'm really busy'","then":"They mumble 'forget it' and leave the room."},{"text":"Put your phone down and say 'Go on. I'm listening.'","then":"They sit down beside you and ask about the new baby next door.","best":true}],"why":"Noticing the hesitation and inviting it out shows your child the door is open."},{"prompt":"Later that week, your child asks if having a baby hurts. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"'No, it doesn't hurt at all. Don't worry.'","then":"They look relieved. Later a friend says otherwise, and they wonder why you said that."},{"text":"'Why are you even thinking about that? Who's been talking?'","then":"They flush and say 'nobody'. The talk ends there."},{"text":"'It can hurt, and doctors and nurses help. Good question.'","then":"They nod and ask how long it takes. The talk keeps going.","best":true},{"text":"'You don't need to worry about that for years'","then":"They shrug and go quiet."}],"why":"A short, true answer at their level keeps you the one they trust to ask."},{"prompt":"A month on, you snap 'not now' again as you rush out of the door. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Let it pass. Snapping once in a while doesn't matter","then":"They don't bring it up again that week."},{"text":"Go back later: 'Sorry about earlier. Ask me now.'","then":"They ask. It takes two minutes, and they hug you on the way to bed.","best":true},{"text":"Promise yourself you'll never snap at them again","then":"The promise feels good, but their question is still sitting unanswered."},{"text":"Explain at length how stressful your day was","then":"They listen patiently, and the talk ends up being about your day, not their question."}],"why":"Every parent slips. Going back each time is what keeps the door open."}],"debrief":"Repair a fumbled answer by going back to it; it models honesty and shows the door is open.","relearn":"If you shut a question down, circle back and repair it; it reopens the door and models honesty."},
  {"id":"tk-1093","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"question in traffic","hook":"Stuck in heavy traffic, your child asks from the back seat how babies get out of tummies.","steps":[{"prompt":"A bus is cutting in and you can't focus. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"'Stop asking me weird things while I'm driving'","then":"The car goes silent. In the mirror you see them look down at their lap."},{"text":"'Good question! I'll answer properly once we park.'","then":"'Okay!' they say, and go back to watching the traffic.","best":true},{"text":"Pretend you didn't hear and turn the radio up","then":"They ask once more, then give up and stare out of the window."},{"text":"Try to answer in bits between all the braking and honking","then":"Your half-answer comes out jumbled. They look more confused than before."}],"why":"Honouring the question and promising a proper answer keeps it welcome while you mind the road."},{"prompt":"Back home, you're carrying bags in and the question is still unanswered. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Hand them your phone to search for the answer","then":"They scroll through results you haven't checked, with no one to explain them."},{"text":"Wait to see whether they bring it up again","then":"They run off to play. The question slides away for now."},{"text":"Promise to explain it all properly at bedtime instead","then":"Bedtime brings a story and sleepy eyes. The question gets pushed again."},{"text":"Set the bags down and bring the question up yourself","then":"They look pleased you remembered, and sit on the step to listen.","best":true}],"why":"Raising it yourself shows your child the question mattered to you too."},{"prompt":"A few days later, your child asks whether they grew in a tummy too. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"'Yes, you grew in a womb, like every baby.'","then":"'Wow,' they say, and ask to see their baby photos.","best":true},{"text":"'Of course not. A stork dropped you off.'","then":"They laugh, unsure if you're joking. It won't match what friends tell them."},{"text":"'Yes, but that's enough questions for today'","then":"They nod, and the next question they had stays in their head."},{"text":"'Ask Dadi. She knows all about babies.'","then":"They shrug and wander off. The question never reaches Dadi either."}],"why":"A simple, true answer tells your child any question can come to you."}],"debrief":"If you can't answer well right now, honour the question and give a proper answer soon, rather than snapping.","relearn":"Can't answer well in the moment? Honour the question and promise a proper answer soon, not a snap."},
  {"id":"tk-1094","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"saw cousin's phone","hook":"Your child says they saw something on an older cousin's phone and wants to know what it meant.","steps":[{"prompt":"They say it showed grown-ups without clothes, and they look puzzled. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say 'That's disgusting. Forget you ever saw it.'","then":"They nod quickly, and you can see they're still confused."},{"text":"Stay calm, thank them for telling you, and explain simply","then":"Their shoulders drop. 'I thought I'd be in trouble,' they admit.","best":true},{"text":"Thank them, then change the subject to cheer them up","then":"They smile, but the picture and the question stay with them."},{"text":"Demand to know exactly what they saw there, and for how long","then":"They go red and start to cry. 'I only saw it for a second!'"}],"why":"Staying calm and thanking them keeps you the person they bring confusing things to."},{"prompt":"Later, your child asks why anyone would watch videos like that. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"'Some things just aren't for kids. We'll talk when you're older.'","then":"They nod. The 'why' they asked about is still unanswered."},{"text":"'Only bad people watch things like that'","then":"They look worried. 'Is Bhaiya bad, then?'"},{"text":"'Those videos are for grown-ups, and aren't how real life works'","then":"They think about it. 'So it's like a pretend film?' they ask.","best":true},{"text":"'You're far too young to understand this'","then":"They go quiet and file the question away for someone else."}],"why":"A simple, honest reason at their level answers the real question without scaring them."},{"prompt":"Before bed, your child asks whether they're in trouble for looking. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"'Just don't ever go near his phone again'","then":"They nod, still unsure whether they did something wrong."},{"text":"'You're not in trouble. Now let's forget all about it.'","then":"They settle, but they've learned this is something to forget, not ask about."},{"text":"'No, and it's not your fault. I'm glad you told me.'","then":"They let out a breath and snuggle down. 'Okay. Night.'","best":true},{"text":"'A little. You should have looked away at once.'","then":"Their face crumples. Next time, they may not mention it."}],"why":"Hearing it's not their fault makes it safe to bring you the next confusing thing."},{"prompt":"At the next family visit, the cousin is scrolling his phone with little ones crowded round. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Snatch his phone and scold him in front of everyone","then":"The room goes silent. He storms off, and the family talks about the scene instead."},{"text":"Say nothing. He isn't your child to correct","then":"The kids stay crowded round his phone. You watch, uneasy."},{"text":"Have a calm, private word with his parents about it","then":"His mother is embarrassed but thanks you. She says she'll talk to him.","best":true},{"text":"Keep your own child next to you all evening","then":"Your child stays by you, but the other little ones still crowd round his phone."}],"why":"A calm word with his parents protects every child. If it seems deliberate or keeps happening, call Childline 1098."}],"debrief":"Thank a child for bringing you something they saw and answer calmly, so they keep coming.","relearn":"When a child reports something they saw, stay calm and thank them, so they keep coming back."},
  {"id":"tk-1095","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"a word from school","hook":"Walking home from school, your child repeats a crude word they heard and asks what it means.","steps":[{"prompt":"They say it cheerfully, with no idea it's rude. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"'Where did you hear that? Never say it again!'","then":"They flinch and stay quiet for the rest of the walk."},{"text":"Laugh it off and change the subject","then":"They laugh too, and say the word again, louder."},{"text":"Say it's a rude word, and leave it at that for now","then":"They stop saying it near you. What it means, they'll ask a friend."},{"text":"Calmly explain what it means and why it can hurt","then":"They listen, wide-eyed. 'Oh. A boy in my class says it all the time.'","best":true}],"why":"A calm, honest explanation teaches the word and shows you can be asked anything."},{"prompt":"A few days later, your child says some kids use the word to tease a classmate. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Ask how that classmate might feel hearing it","then":"They think for a moment. 'Sad, probably. She always walks away.'","best":true},{"text":"'Just make sure you never use it yourself, okay?'","then":"They promise. The teasing in class carries on around them."},{"text":"'Stay away from those kids from now on'","then":"They nod, though they sit beside those kids every day."},{"text":"'That's between them. Don't get involved.'","then":"They shrug. The teasing becomes something they simply watch."}],"why":"Thinking about how a word lands helps your child choose kindness, not just avoid trouble."},{"prompt":"A week later, your child brings home another new word and asks what it means. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Tell them to look it up in the dictionary","then":"They find the meaning, but not why the kids laugh when they say it."},{"text":"Sigh and ask why they keep picking up these words","then":"They mumble 'sorry' and drop it."},{"text":"Explain it, then warn they'll be punished for using it","then":"They understand the word, and learn that asking comes with a warning."},{"text":"Thank them for asking, and explain it plainly","then":"They listen, then add, 'Okay. I'll ask you if I hear more.'","best":true}],"why":"Thanking them for asking makes you the first place new words come to."}],"debrief":"When a child repeats a word they don't understand, explain it calmly instead of scolding.","relearn":"Explain a word a child repeats calmly, not with a scolding; scolding just sends the next question away."},
  {"id":"tk-1096","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"don't know puberty","hook":"Your child asks why voices crack during puberty, and you realise you don't know the answer.","steps":[{"prompt":"They're waiting, eyes on you. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"'Good question. I'm not sure. Let's look it up together.'","then":"They grab the tablet and pull up a chair. 'Can we do it now?'","best":true},{"text":"'That's one for your science teacher'","then":"They shrug. The question goes on the pile they won't bring to you."},{"text":"Make up something that sounds about right","then":"They repeat it to a friend at school, who says that's not true at all."},{"text":"'I'm not sure. Search it online and tell me what you find.'","then":"They search alone and land on a forum full of jokes and half-truths."}],"why":"Admitting you don't know and finding out together shows honesty and keeps you their go-to."},{"prompt":"At a family lunch, your brother hears you didn't know and laughs that parents should know everything. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"'You're right. I'll read up so it never happens again.'","then":"He nods, satisfied. Your child hears that not knowing is something to hide."},{"text":"'I didn't, and that's fine. We can find out together.'","then":"He raises an eyebrow. Your child, listening, sits a little taller.","best":true},{"text":"Laugh along and make a joke about getting old","then":"Everyone laughs. Your child learns that not knowing is embarrassing."},{"text":"Snap at him to mind his own business","then":"The table goes tense, and lunch ends awkwardly."}],"why":"Owning 'I don't know' in front of others shows your child that honesty beats pretending."},{"prompt":"A month later, your child asks a harder body question, and you only half know the answer. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Answer confidently and hope the gaps don't show","then":"They take it as fact. Part of it turns out to be wrong."},{"text":"Say 'I don't know' and leave it at that","then":"They wait for more, then wander off with the question."},{"text":"Hand them a book and tell them to read it","then":"They skim a chapter and come away with their question still unanswered."},{"text":"Share what you know and check the rest together","then":"You look it up that evening. They correct you on one point, laughing.","best":true}],"why":"Saying what you know and checking the rest together keeps your answers honest and your door open."}],"debrief":"If you don't know, say so and find out together; willingness beats pretending to know.","relearn":"Don't fake an answer you lack; say 'let's find out together'; willingness beats false certainty."},
  {"id":"tk-1097","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"branch","persona":"Divya","source":"asked again","hook":"For the fourth time this week, your young child asks how babies come out.","steps":[{"prompt":"You're tired, and you've answered it three times already. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Answer warmly again, as simply as before","then":"They nod along, mouthing the words with you, then skip off, content.","best":true},{"text":"'Go and ask Nani this time'","then":"Nani laughs and says 'from the hospital'. They come back more puzzled."},{"text":"Give a longer, fuller answer to settle it for good","then":"Halfway through, they lose interest and start playing with your keys."},{"text":"'I've already told you. Stop asking me that.'","then":"They go quiet and look at the floor."}],"why":"Young children repeat questions to make sense of them. A warm, same answer makes them feel safe."},{"prompt":"At the park, your child loudly tells another child how babies come out, and that child's mother looks startled. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Hush your child and apologise to the mother","then":"Your child looks confused about what they did wrong."},{"text":"Laugh it off and quickly steer your child to the swings","then":"The moment passes. Your child isn't sure it was okay to say."},{"text":"Smile at her: 'We talk about bodies openly at home.'","then":"She hesitates, then smiles back. Your child goes back to the slide.","best":true},{"text":"Scold your child for saying it in public","then":"They burst into tears at the top of the slide."}],"why":"Staying calm shows your child that simple, true facts are nothing to be ashamed of."},{"prompt":"At dinner, your child asks it once more, and an older cousin groans, 'Not again!' What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Answer again, and say asking is how we all learn","then":"Your child beams. The cousin rolls her eyes but lets it go.","best":true},{"text":"Ask your child to save such questions for when you're alone","then":"They nod, and learn that body questions are something to hide."},{"text":"Tell the cousin off sharply for being mean","then":"The cousin sulks, and dinner turns tense for everyone."},{"text":"Laugh with the cousin and change the subject","then":"Your child's smile fades. They push their food around the plate."}],"why":"Answering again in front of others shows every question is welcome, however often it comes."}],"debrief":"Re-answer a repeated question warmly; repetition is how young children learn, not a reason to snap.","relearn":"Young children repeat questions to make sense of them; answer warmly again, not 'stop asking me'."},
  {"id":"tk-1098","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"branch","persona":"Priya","source":"partner waves it off","hook":"Your child asks your partner a body question, and your partner waves it off: 'You're too small.'","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child's face falls, and they turn to you. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Stay quiet so you don't contradict your partner","then":"Your child waits, then gives up and goes back to colouring."},{"text":"Whisper to your child that you'll answer it later, in private","then":"They nod, but they've still watched their question get shut down."},{"text":"Tell your partner off for being so dismissive","then":"Your partner bristles, and the question gets lost in your argument."},{"text":"Step in gently: 'It's a good question. Let me answer.'","then":"Your child brightens. Your partner looks surprised but lets you answer.","best":true}],"why":"Stepping in gently keeps one door open without turning it into a fight."},{"prompt":"Later, your partner says answering body questions this young just makes kids curious too early. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Agree to keep things vague until they're older","then":"Your partner looks relieved. The next question will meet two closed doors."},{"text":"Say that's just how they were raised, and it shows","then":"Your partner goes cold, and the talk ends there."},{"text":"Agree to disagree, and answer all the questions yourself","then":"Your partner shrugs. Your child learns only one of you can be asked."},{"text":"Explain that simple, true answers keep children safer","then":"Your partner listens. 'I never thought of it as safety,' they admit.","best":true}],"why":"Calmly sharing why talking protects can turn a second parent into a second open door."},{"prompt":"A week later, your child asks another body question at dinner with both of you there. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Answer, then look pointedly at your partner","then":"Your partner reddens. The answer lands, but dinner turns stiff."},{"text":"Answer simply, and nod to your partner to add a line","then":"Your partner adds a sentence. Your child looks from one to the other, delighted.","best":true},{"text":"Say 'Let's talk about it after dinner, just us two'","then":"Your child nods. Your partner stays out of it again."},{"text":"Wait to see whether your partner answers first","then":"Your partner freezes. The pause stretches, and your child says 'never mind'."}],"why":"Answering calmly and inviting your partner in shows your child both doors are open."},{"prompt":"That night, your partner quietly asks how you find the words for these questions. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Forward them a long article on the topic","then":"They mean to read it. It sits unopened among their messages."},{"text":"Share a few simple lines that help you","then":"Your partner repeats two of them to themselves. 'I can say that.'","best":true},{"text":"'Leave the questions to me. I'm better at it.'","then":"Your partner looks relieved, and your child now has one door, not two."},{"text":"'You just have to be brave and wing it'","then":"Your partner looks unconvinced and dreads the next question."}],"why":"A few ready phrases give a nervous parent the confidence to answer too."}],"debrief":"If a question gets waved off, gently keep the door open yourself so the child has an askable adult.","relearn":"If your partner brushes a question off, gently keep the door open; a child needs one askable adult."},
  {"id":"tk-1099","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"asked at a function","hook":"At a family function, your child loudly asks why their aunt's tummy is so big.","steps":[{"prompt":"Heads turn, and the aunt laughs nervously. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Joke loudly that she's been eating too many sweets","then":"Everyone laughs. Your child stares at the aunt's tummy, puzzled."},{"text":"Hush them sharply and apologise to everyone around you","then":"Your child shrinks behind you, cheeks burning."},{"text":"'She's growing a baby. I'll tell you more at home.'","then":"Your child's eyes go wide. 'A baby? In there?' The aunt smiles.","best":true},{"text":"Whisper 'Not here' and steer them away","then":"They follow you, confused about what they said wrong."}],"why":"A calm, true short answer meets the question without shaming your child."},{"prompt":"Over lunch, a relative says children shouldn't be told about babies at all. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Quickly change the subject to avoid a scene","then":"The talk moves on. Your child notices nobody backed their question."},{"text":"Nod along to keep the peace","then":"Your child, sitting close, hears that their question was a mistake."},{"text":"Say simply that you'll answer your child honestly","then":"The relative raises an eyebrow but lets it go. Your child is listening.","best":true},{"text":"Argue the point hotly with the relative in front of everyone","then":"Voices rise. Your child slips away from the table."}],"why":"A short, calm stand shows your child you'll keep answering, even when relatives disapprove."},{"prompt":"On the drive home, your child asks if Aunty has a baby inside, and how it got there. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"'A stork brings them. Everyone knows that.'","then":"They frown. 'Then why is her tummy so big?'"},{"text":"'It's a long story. Remind me about it another time.'","then":"They say 'okay'. Neither of you brings it up again."},{"text":"'You'll understand all this when you're much older'","then":"They sigh and look out of the window."},{"text":"'Yes. A tiny egg and sperm joined and grew into a baby.'","then":"They think hard. 'Like a seed?' they ask, and you talk it through.","best":true}],"why":"A simple, true answer at their level keeps you the one they bring questions to."},{"prompt":"Weeks later, the baby is born, and your child asks where it came out from. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"'Through her vagina, or sometimes doctors lift it out of her tummy.'","then":"They nod seriously. 'Can I hold the baby?' they ask.","best":true},{"text":"'From the hospital, of course. Where else would it be?'","then":"They laugh. 'But how did it get out?' The question is still there."},{"text":"'From her tummy. That's all you need to know.'","then":"They nod, and picture a baby popping out of a belly button."},{"text":"'That's not something nice children ask about'","then":"They look down, and the next question stays inside."}],"why":"Using the proper word calmly gives a clear, true answer and keeps your child safer."}],"debrief":"Give a calm, true short answer in public and offer more later, not a hushing in shame.","relearn":"In public, give a calm true short answer and offer more later, not a hushing in embarrassment."},
  {"id":"tk-1100","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"went quiet","hook":"Last month you overreacted to your child's question, and they haven't asked you anything since.","steps":[{"prompt":"Tonight you're tucking them into bed. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Wait. They'll start asking again on their own","then":"They say goodnight and roll over. Another quiet week goes by."},{"text":"Say 'You can ask me anything. I'll stay calm. I promise.'","then":"They study your face for a long moment, then nod slowly.","best":true},{"text":"Ask them straight out why they've stopped talking to you","then":"They shrug, mumble 'no reason', and turn to the wall."},{"text":"Apologise at great length for how badly you reacted last month","then":"They listen awkwardly and say 'It's okay.' The talk ends on your guilt, not their questions."}],"why":"A calm, clear invitation tells your child the door has opened again."},{"prompt":"A few days later, your child mentions a classmate got her period at school. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Jump straight into a full explanation of periods","then":"They listen politely, then slip away the moment you pause."},{"text":"Ask what the other kids said about it, and listen","then":"They say the boys were giggling. Then they ask what a period actually is.","best":true},{"text":"Let the comment pass without a word","then":"They wait a second, then start talking about cricket instead."},{"text":"Say 'That's not something for you to worry about'","then":"They nod and go back to their game."}],"why":"Picking up a small opening, and listening first, shows it's safe to talk again."},{"prompt":"Later that week, your child asks a question that makes you tense up again. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say it's a question for when they're older","then":"They go quiet again. 'Okay,' is all they say."},{"text":"Take a breath, thank them for asking, then answer","then":"Your calm surprises them. They ask a second question straight after.","best":true},{"text":"Answer fast so the awkward moment is over quickly","then":"The answer is fine, but they notice how badly you want it over."},{"text":"Ask where they heard about such things","then":"Their face closes. 'Nowhere,' they say."}],"why":"Staying calm when you feel tense shows your child the door is truly open again."},{"prompt":"Your sister says her son has stopped asking her anything too, and wants your advice. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"'Give it time. Kids come back on their own.'","then":"She relaxes and waits. Her son stays quiet a while longer."},{"text":"'Apologise to him for being strict. That's enough.'","then":"She does. He says 'okay', but no questions follow."},{"text":"'Say he can ask anything, then stay calm when he does'","then":"She nods slowly. 'I've never actually said that out loud,' she admits.","best":true},{"text":"'Get him a good book so he doesn't need to ask'","then":"She orders one that night. The silence between them stays."}],"why":"Reopening the door means saying it out loud, then staying calm to keep it open."},{"prompt":"Months later, your child brings you a big question they've clearly been saving. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Answer, then tease them a little to keep it light","then":"They laugh, but they don't ask the follow-up they had."},{"text":"Stop what you're doing and give it your full attention","then":"They talk for twenty minutes, then say, 'Thanks for not freaking out.'","best":true},{"text":"Answer them while you finish replying to your work messages","then":"They trail off with 'never mind' and drift away."},{"text":"Say 'Finally! Why didn't you ask me sooner?'","then":"They squirm and go pink. The question comes out half-asked."}],"why":"Full, calm attention on the big question shows the door is open for good."}],"debrief":"If a child has gone quiet after you overreacted, actively reopen the door instead of waiting.","relearn":"After overreacting, actively reopen the door with a calm invitation; don't just wait for them to try."},
  {"id":"tk-1101","type":"match","persona":"any","source":"line to effect","hook":"Match each thing a parent says to what it does for the child.","pairs":[{"left":"'Great question'","right":"Rewards them for coming to you"},{"left":"'Let's find out together'","right":"Models honesty when you don't know"},{"left":"'You can ask me anything'","right":"Opens the lifelong door"},{"left":"'Let's talk properly after dinner'","right":"Honours it while you find a calm moment"},{"left":"'That's normal and okay'","right":"Settles their worry"}],"relearn":"Phrases like 'great question' and 'you can ask me anything' reward curiosity and keep the door open.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1102","type":"match","persona":"any","source":"move to door effect","hook":"Match each parent move to its effect on the door staying open.","pairs":[{"left":"Staying calm and unshocked","right":"Keeps you their trusted source"},{"left":"Answering at the child's level","right":"Makes the answer actually land"},{"left":"Welcoming awkward questions","right":"Keeps them willing to ask"},{"left":"Repairing a fumbled answer","right":"Shows the door is truly always open"},{"left":"Many small chats over years","right":"Beats one dreaded big lecture"}],"relearn":"Calm answers, child-level wording, welcoming questions and repairing fumbles all keep the door open.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1103","type":"match","persona":"any","source":"moment to opener","hook":"Match each tricky moment to a calm way to open it.","pairs":[{"left":"You don't know the answer","right":"'Let's find out together'"},{"left":"A bad time to talk right now","right":"'Great question, let's talk after dinner'"},{"left":"You shut them down yesterday","right":"'Sorry, ask me again, I'm listening'"},{"left":"Starting the first conversation","right":"'You can always ask me anything'"},{"left":"They saw something confusing","right":"'Thanks for telling me, let's talk it through'"}],"relearn":"Each tricky moment has a calm opener that keeps you the askable parent, from 'let's find out together' on.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1104","type":"match","persona":"any","source":"reaction to message","hook":"Match each reaction to the hidden message a child takes from it.","pairs":[{"left":"Calm, warm answer","right":"'It's safe to ask my parent'"},{"left":"Shock or anger","right":"'I'd better not ask again'"},{"left":"'Ask your mother / father'","right":"'This door is closed'"},{"left":"'No question is silly'","right":"'My curiosity is welcome here'"},{"left":"Changing the subject","right":"'We don't talk about this at home'"}],"relearn":"A child reads your reaction: calm warmth says 'safe to ask'; shock or dodging says 'this door is closed'.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1105","type":"match","persona":"any","source":"tone to outcome","hook":"Match each tone a parent uses to where it leads.","pairs":[{"left":"Matter-of-fact and easy","right":"The topic feels ordinary, not shameful"},{"left":"Panicked and flustered","right":"The child senses danger in asking"},{"left":"Curious alongside them","right":"Learning together feels safe"},{"left":"Lecturing and long","right":"The child tunes out and stops asking"},{"left":"Gentle and unhurried","right":"There's room for the next question"}],"relearn":"A matter-of-fact, gentle tone makes the topic ordinary; panic or lecturing teaches a child to stop asking.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1106","type":"match","persona":"any","source":"habit to why","hook":"Match each open-door habit to why it works.","pairs":[{"left":"Little chats as things come up","right":"No single talk has to carry it all"},{"left":"Answering honestly, not perfectly","right":"Trust grows from honesty, not polish"},{"left":"Thanking them for asking","right":"Curiosity gets rewarded, so it continues"},{"left":"Staying askable through eye-rolls","right":"You remain a resource as they grow"},{"left":"Sharing your own gaps","right":"They learn not-knowing is normal"}],"relearn":"Open-door habits work because they reward curiosity and let trust grow from honesty over many small chats.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1107","type":"match","persona":"any","source":"style to effect","hook":"Match each answer style to its effect on a child.","pairs":[{"left":"Short and simple","right":"They take it in and come back for more"},{"left":"Long and anxious","right":"They feel overwhelmed and switch off"},{"left":"Honest 'I don't know'","right":"They trust you and learn to find out"},{"left":"Honouring and parking it","right":"It stays safe to ask later"},{"left":"Shaming the question","right":"They take it to friends instead"}],"relearn":"Short honest answers keep a child coming back; long anxious or shaming ones send them away from you.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1108","type":"reflect","persona":"any","source":"askable beats expert","hook":"Lensy: you don't have to be an expert on every topic, just the parent your child feels safe asking. Sit right?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Sits right","Askable over expert","Yes"],"affirm":"Being the askable, safe parent matters far more than knowing every answer; willingness beats expertise.","relearn":"You don't have to be an expert; being the askable parent your child feels safe with matters far more.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1109","type":"reflect","persona":"any","source":"each chat a deposit","hook":"Lensy: every small, calm chat is a little deposit in the trust that lets the big questions come later. Worth it?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Worth it","Small chats add up","Yes"],"affirm":"Each small calm chat deposits trust, so when the bigger, harder questions come, your child brings them to you.","relearn":"Every small, calm chat deposits trust, so the bigger questions later get brought to you, not the feed.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1110","type":"reflect","persona":"Vikram","source":"okay not to know","hook":"Lensy: it's completely okay not to have every answer ready; 'let's find out together' is a real answer. Agree?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Agree","Not-knowing is fine","Yes"],"affirm":"You don't need every answer ready; 'let's find out together' is honest, and it keeps you your child's guide.","relearn":"It's okay not to have every answer; 'let's find out together' is honest and keeps you your child's guide.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1111","type":"reflect","persona":"Divya","source":"calm is a gift","hook":"Lensy: your calm face when a child asks something hard is a gift, it tells them this is safe ground. Ring true?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Rings true","Calm is a gift","Yes"],"affirm":"A calm face when a child asks something hard tells them the topic is safe ground, and keeps them coming to you.","relearn":"Your calm when a child asks something hard tells them it's safe ground and keeps them coming to you.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1112","type":"reflect","persona":"any","source":"door reopens","hook":"Lensy: whatever's happened before, the door can reopen today with one calm 'you can always ask me'. Believe it?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Believe it","It's never too late","Yes"],"affirm":"It's never too late: whatever happened before, one calm invitation can reopen the door with your child today.","relearn":"Whatever happened before, the door reopens today with one calm 'you can always ask me'; it's never too late.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1113","type":"reflect","persona":"any","source":"honesty over perfect","hook":"Lensy: your child needs honest more than they need perfect; an honest fumble beats a polished silence. Sit right?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Sits right","Honest over perfect","Yes"],"affirm":"Children need honesty more than polish; an honest, fumbling answer beats a perfect-looking silence every time.","relearn":"Children need honest more than perfect; an honest, fumbling answer beats a polished silence every time.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1114","type":"reflect","persona":"Priya","source":"your voice belongs","hook":"Lensy: if you stay silent, the feed and the playground answer instead; your voice belongs in the mix. Agree?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Agree","My voice belongs","Yes"],"affirm":"Your voice belongs in the mix; staying silent doesn't keep a child neutral, it just lets others teach them.","relearn":"Staying silent doesn't keep a child neutral; the feed and peers fill the gap, so your voice belongs in it.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1115","type":"reflect","persona":"any","source":"curiosity is healthy","hook":"Lensy: a child's curiosity about bodies and growing up is healthy, not a problem to be managed. Ring true?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Rings true","Curiosity is healthy","Yes"],"affirm":"A child's curiosity about bodies and growing up is healthy and normal, not a problem; it's an invitation to talk.","relearn":"A child's curiosity about bodies and growing up is healthy and normal; treat it as an invitation to talk.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1116","type":"spot","persona":"any","source":"sends to internet","hook":"Spot the two reactions that send a child to the internet instead of to you.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Calm, honest answer at their level","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"'You're too young to know that'","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"'Great question, let's talk'","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Shock and a sharp 'who told you that?'","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Thanking them for asking you","trick":false}],"why":"'You're too young' and shocked interrogation are the door-closers that send a child to the feed for answers.","relearn":"Answer calmly and thank a child for asking; 'you're too young' and shock send them to the feed instead.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1117","type":"spot","persona":"any","source":"shuts a question down","hook":"Spot the two lines that shut a child's question down.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"'Let me explain that simply'","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"'We don't talk about that in this house'","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"'No question is silly'","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"'Ask me again after dinner, I'll answer'","trick":false},{"id":"e","text":"'Wait till you're older, not now'","trick":true}],"why":"'We don't talk about that' and 'wait till you're older' shut the door; the others keep it open.","relearn":"'We don't talk about that' and 'wait till you're older' shut a question down; keep the door open instead.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1118","type":"spot","persona":"any","source":"teaches shame","hook":"Spot the two responses that teach a child to feel ashamed for asking.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Answering warmly and matter-of-factly","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"'Chee, don't be dirty, why ask that?'","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Using the calm, correct words","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"A disgusted face and silence","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"'I'm glad you asked me'","trick":false}],"why":"Calling a question dirty and reacting with disgust teach shame; warm, matter-of-fact answers don't.","relearn":"Calling a question dirty or reacting with disgust teaches shame; answer warmly and matter-of-factly instead.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1119","type":"spot","persona":"any","source":"closes the door","hook":"Spot the two moves that quietly close the door for next time.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"'You can always come to me'","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Laughing at the child for asking","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Answering honestly, even if unsure","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"'Go ask someone else, not me'","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Staying calm and unshocked","trick":false}],"why":"Laughing at the child and 'go ask someone else' close the door; the rest keep you the askable parent.","relearn":"Laughing at a child or 'go ask someone else' quietly closes the door; stay calm and answer to keep it open.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1120","type":"spot","persona":"any","source":"harder next time","hook":"Spot the two reactions that make the next, harder question tougher to ask.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"A calm, simple answer","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Getting angry at the question","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"'Thanks for trusting me with that'","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Changing the subject in a panic","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Welcoming the awkwardness","trick":false}],"why":"Anger and panicked subject-changing make the next question harder; calm, welcoming answers make it easier.","relearn":"Anger and panicked subject-changing make the next question harder; calm, welcoming answers make it easier.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1121","type":"spot","persona":"Vikram","source":"sends to peers","hook":"Spot the two responses that hand the topic over to a teen's friends.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Staying open and non-lecturing","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"A long, judgemental lecture","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"'I won't freak out, you can tell me'","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"'That's disgusting, never mention it'","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Answering honestly without judging","trick":false}],"why":"Judgemental lectures and 'that's disgusting' send a teen to friends; staying open and honest keeps you in the loop.","relearn":"Judgemental lectures and 'that's disgusting' send a teen to friends; stay open and honest to keep them talking.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1122","type":"spot","persona":"any","source":"punishes curiosity","hook":"Spot the two reactions that punish a child for being curious.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"'What a thoughtful thing to wonder'","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Snapping 'stop asking me that!'","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Answering at their level","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Embarrassing them in front of others","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"A patient re-answer when they repeat it","trick":false}],"why":"Snapping and public embarrassment punish curiosity; patient, welcoming answers reward it instead.","relearn":"Snapping at or embarrassing a child punishes curiosity; patient, welcoming answers reward it instead.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1123","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"role-play","persona":"Divya","source":"how did baby get in","hook":"Your young child has just met a pregnant aunty and couldn't stop looking at her tummy.","setup":"At home, they climb into your lap, wide-eyed.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"How did the baby get inside Aunty's tummy?\"","options":[{"text":"\"She ate something special, and it turned into a baby.\"","then":"\"Can I eat it too?\" they ask, alarmed."},{"text":"\"Babies grow in a special place called the womb.\"","then":"\"The womb,\" they repeat carefully. \"Is it cosy in there?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"The stork brings it. Now stop asking silly things.\"","then":"\"But storks can't fit inside tummies,\" they frown."},{"text":"\"That's grown-up stuff. I'll tell you when you're bigger.\"","then":"They slide off your lap. \"Everything is when I'm bigger.\""}],"why":"A simple, true answer about the womb satisfies a young child and keeps them asking you."},{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"How does the baby eat in there?\"","options":[{"text":"\"It doesn't eat. It just sleeps in there until it's born.\"","then":"\"Doesn't it get hungry?\" they ask, worried."},{"text":"\"Through a tube. Your belly button is where yours was!\"","then":"They lift their shirt and poke their belly button. \"Here?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"You ask too many questions, you know that?\"","then":"\"Sorry,\" they whisper, fiddling with their shirt."},{"text":"\"Hmm, that's a question for Aunty, not for me.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, though they're far too shy to ask her."}],"why":"Answering each new question simply and truly keeps their curiosity coming to you."},{"prompt":"Later, your child asks: \"Did I grow in a tummy like that too?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Yes. Every baby grows in a womb, and you did too.\"","then":"\"Every baby?\" they marvel. \"Even Nani?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"No, silly. We just picked you up from the hospital.\"","then":"Their face falls. \"Was I lost there?\" they whisper."},{"text":"\"Yes, but don't talk about this at school.\"","then":"They nod solemnly. \"Is it a bad thing?\""},{"text":"\"Enough about babies now. Go and play.\"","then":"They blink. \"Did I say something bad?\""}],"why":"Linking the answer to them, simply and truly, shows bodies are nothing to hide."}],"relearn":"Give a simple, true answer about where a baby grows, not a stork story or a shutdown."},
  {"id":"tk-1124","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"role-play","persona":"Divya","source":"why bodies differ","hook":"Your young child watches you change a baby cousin's nappy, looking very puzzled.","setup":"Afterwards, they follow you into the kitchen.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"Why does he look different from me down there?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Don't look at that! It's dirty down there.\"","then":"\"Is my body dirty too?\" they ask, worried."},{"text":"\"Boys have a 'susu' and girls have a 'nunu'. That's all.\"","then":"They giggle. \"Nunu! That's a funny word.\""},{"text":"\"That's not something nice children ask about.\"","then":"Their cheeks go pink. \"Sorry,\" they whisper."},{"text":"\"Boys have a penis and girls have a vulva.\"","then":"\"Vulva,\" they repeat, testing the word. \"Okay.\"","best":true}],"why":"Proper names, said calmly, answer the question and help keep a child safe."},{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"Why do we keep those parts covered?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Because they're shameful. That's why.\"","then":"They look down. \"Is something wrong with me?\""},{"text":"\"Those parts are private. They're just for you.\"","then":"\"Just for me,\" they nod. \"Not for anyone else?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Because people will laugh at you otherwise.\"","then":"\"Would they laugh at me?\" they ask, anxious."},{"text":"\"Everyone does. That's just how it is.\"","then":"They shrug. \"Okay,\" they say, none the wiser."}],"why":"Calling them private and theirs teaches body ownership in words a young child understands."},{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"What if somebody wants to see them?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Say no, and tell me. You'll never be in trouble.\"","then":"\"Never in trouble,\" they repeat, and go back to their blocks.","best":true},{"text":"\"Just shout no, really loudly, and run away fast.\"","then":"\"Like this? NO!\" they shout, giggling."},{"text":"\"We'll talk about all that when you're a bit older.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, and the question stays open."},{"text":"\"Don't worry. Nobody would ever do that to you.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, relieved, with no idea what they'd do."}],"why":"Saying no and telling you, with no trouble, is the body-safety rule young children need."}],"relearn":"Explain body differences calmly with the proper names, not by shaming the child for wondering."},
  {"id":"tk-1125","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"open first talk","hook":"No awkward question has come up yet, but you want to open the door with your child first.","setup":"You're walking back from the park, just the two of you.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child says: \"You're quiet today. What are you thinking about?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Nothing much. Just boring work stuff.\"","then":"\"Boring,\" they agree, and run ahead to the gate."},{"text":"\"That you should come to me if something's ever wrong.\"","then":"\"Like if I fall off my bike?\" they ask."},{"text":"\"That we'll have big talks when you're much older.\"","then":"\"What talks?\" they ask, then lose interest."},{"text":"\"That you can ask me anything about your body, anytime.\"","then":"They look up, surprised. \"Anything? Even weird stuff?\"","best":true}],"why":"A clear invitation before any question comes makes the first one much easier to ask."},{"prompt":"A few steps on, your child asks: \"Why do grown-ups' armpits get hairy and smelly?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Because grown-ups don't wash enough. Ha!\"","then":"They laugh and hold their nose. \"Really?\""},{"text":"\"Ugh, what a disgusting question to ask me.\"","then":"They giggle nervously. \"Sorry. Forget it.\""},{"text":"\"Growing bodies sweat more, and hair grows there.\"","then":"\"Will mine?\" they ask, sniffing their own arm.","best":true},{"text":"\"Ask your teacher. They know all the science stuff.\"","then":"\"But I'm asking you,\" they say, disappointed."}],"why":"A simple, true answer to a small question shows any question is welcome with you."},{"prompt":"At the gate, your child asks: \"Will you tell anyone what I ask you?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Never. Everything you say stays a secret between us.\"","then":"\"Even big secrets?\" they whisper, pleased."},{"text":"\"Why? What are you planning to ask me?\"","then":"\"Nothing,\" they say quickly, and hurry inside."},{"text":"\"It stays with me, unless you're ever unsafe.\"","then":"They nod slowly. \"Okay. That's fair.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"If it's a funny one, I might tell the family.\"","then":"Their face falls. \"Then I won't ask the funny ones.\""}],"why":"Honest privacy, with safety as the one exception, lets your child trust your door."}],"relearn":"Open the lifelong door with a clear invitation that any question is welcome, rather than deferring it for years."},
  {"id":"tk-1126","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"asked while cooking","hook":"You're frying pakoras for guests. The oil is hot and both your hands are full.","setup":"Your child hovers in the kitchen doorway.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"Where do periods come from?\"","options":[{"text":"\"From the tummy, sort of. Pass me that plate, please.\"","then":"They pass the plate. \"The tummy? How?\""},{"text":"\"Good question! Two minutes, then I'll sit with you.\"","then":"\"Two minutes,\" they say, and start counting out loud.","best":true},{"text":"\"Go and ask Dadi. I'm in the middle of cooking.\"","then":"They come back later. \"Dadi just said 'chhi' and sent me off.\""},{"text":"\"Can't you see I'm busy? Don't bother me with that now.\"","then":"\"Sorry,\" they mumble, backing out of the kitchen."}],"why":"Honouring the question and naming a short wait keeps it welcome, even with your hands full."},{"prompt":"A bit later, your child asks: \"Do boys get periods too?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Periods are girls' business. Don't worry about them.\"","then":"\"Oh,\" they say, and drop it."},{"text":"\"No, they don't. Let's leave the rest for when you're older.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, though they clearly had more."},{"text":"\"Why do you want to know? Who's been talking?\"","then":"\"Nobody,\" they say quickly, going pink."},{"text":"\"No, but their bodies change in other ways as they grow.\"","then":"\"Like what?\" they ask, pulling up a stool.","best":true}],"why":"Every child learning about everyone's body builds understanding, not shame."},{"prompt":"That night, your child asks: \"Can I always ask you stuff, even when you're busy?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Only when I'm not busy, please.\"","then":"\"You're always busy,\" they mutter."},{"text":"\"Always, and I'll drop everything the second you ask.\"","then":"They grin. \"Even when there's hot oil?\""},{"text":"\"Always. If I'm busy, I'll tell you when I can talk.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, satisfied. \"Deal.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Sometimes. It depends on my mood.\"","then":"They look unsure. \"How will I know your mood?\""}],"why":"An honest 'always, and I'll say when' is a promise you can actually keep."}],"relearn":"Honour a question even when busy and promise a proper answer soon, instead of brushing the child off."},
  {"id":"tk-1127","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"word from a song","hook":"A film song is playing at home, and your child has been singing along to every word.","setup":"Suddenly they stop mid-line and turn to you.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"What does 'maal' mean? They keep singing it.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Glad you asked. It means 'goods', like things in a shop.\"","then":"\"But they're singing it about a girl,\" they say, puzzled.","best":true},{"text":"\"It's nothing. Just a word that fits the tune.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they shrug, and sing it again, louder."},{"text":"\"Where did you pick that up? Don't ever repeat it.\"","then":"\"From the song,\" they say, stung. \"Everyone sings it.\""},{"text":"\"It's a bad word. Let's put on a different song, okay?\"","then":"\"But why is it bad?\" they ask, as the new song starts."}],"why":"Welcoming the question and giving the meaning keeps you the one they check words with."},{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"So why do they call a girl that in the song?\"","options":[{"text":"\"It treats her like a thing, not a person. That hurts.\"","then":"They frown. \"That's not nice. She's a person.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"It's just a song. Don't think about it so much.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, and start humming along again."},{"text":"\"Film people are silly. Just ignore them.\"","then":"They laugh. \"Silly film people!\" they say, and hum on."},{"text":"\"Because some girls actually like being called that, maybe.\"","then":"\"Oh,\" they say slowly. \"So it's a compliment?\""}],"why":"Naming how a word treats people helps your child see respect, not just a rule."},{"prompt":"The next day, your child says: \"A boy at school called my friend that.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Well, at least you'd never say a word like that.\"","then":"\"No,\" they agree. Then, quietly: \"I still didn't help her, though.\""},{"text":"\"How did your friend feel? What did you do?\"","then":"\"She went quiet. I didn't know what to say,\" they admit.","best":true},{"text":"\"Boys will be boys. Just ignore it, beta.\"","then":"They look unsure. \"But she was really upset.\""},{"text":"\"What? I'm calling his parents right now!\"","then":"\"No!\" they gasp. \"Then everyone will know I told.\""}],"why":"Asking how their friend felt, and what they did, turns a lesson into kindness they can act on."},{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"What could I say next time?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Stay out of it. It's not your fight, is it, beta?\"","then":"They nod slowly. \"I guess,\" they say, not convinced."},{"text":"\"Call him something even worse right back.\"","then":"\"Like what?\" they giggle, already thinking of names."},{"text":"\"Say 'Don't call her that.' Tell a teacher if he goes on.\"","then":"\"Don't call her that,\" they practise. \"And I'll tell Miss if he keeps on.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Tell your friend to just ignore him, and he'll stop.\"","then":"\"She tried that,\" they say. \"He kept going.\""}],"why":"A short, calm line, and a teacher if it goes on, gives your child a safe way to back a friend."}],"relearn":"Welcome a question about a word a child heard and explain it, rather than scolding them for asking."},
  {"id":"tk-1128","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"repair after snapping","hook":"Earlier your child asked about a sore spot on their chest, and you snapped at them to stop fussing.","setup":"Now they're doing homework and won't look up.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child mutters: \"I'm not asking you anything anymore.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Want some ice cream? Let's cheer up a bit.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, and eat it quietly, the question still unanswered."},{"text":"\"Sorry I was short with you. It was a fair question.\"","then":"They look up slowly. \"You were really grumpy.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Don't sulk like that. I had a very long day at work.\"","then":"They shrug. \"Fine.\" The pencil keeps moving."},{"text":"\"Good. Let's just forget you ever asked that.\"","then":"\"Already forgotten,\" they say flatly."}],"why":"A plain apology shows you own a mistake, and that their question was fair."},{"prompt":"Your child says: \"It still feels sore, though.\"","options":[{"text":"\"It's probably nothing at all. Don't worry about it, beta.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, but keep pressing the spot when you're not looking."},{"text":"\"Right, get your shoes. We're going to the doctor this minute.\"","then":"\"The doctor?\" they gasp. \"Is something really wrong?\""},{"text":"\"I'll look it up sometime and get back to you.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, still rubbing the spot."},{"text":"\"Can I see? Growing can do that. If it stays sore, we'll see a doctor.\"","then":"They show you the spot, calmer now. \"Okay. We'll watch it.\"","best":true}],"why":"A calm, true answer to the question you shut down shows the door is open again."},{"prompt":"At bedtime, your child asks: \"Will you get cross if I ask more body stuff?\"","options":[{"text":"\"No. And if I ever do, remind me I promised.\"","then":"They smile. \"I will. I'll say 'you promised'.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Depends on what kind of stuff you mean.\"","then":"They pull the blanket up. \"Never mind, then.\""},{"text":"\"I'll never, ever get cross again. I swear.\"","then":"They look doubtful. \"You got cross today, though.\""},{"text":"\"Not if the questions are sensible ones.\"","then":"\"What's sensible?\" they ask, worried."}],"why":"Promising calm, and inviting them to hold you to it, keeps the door honestly open."}],"relearn":"Repair a snapped answer by apologising and reopening it; that shows the door is genuinely always open."},
  {"id":"tk-1129","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"standing invitation","hook":"It's bedtime, and your child is sleepy but chatty after a big day at school.","setup":"You switch off the light and sit on the edge of the bed.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child says: \"My friend's mummy says kids shouldn't ask about bodies.\"","options":[{"text":"\"In our home, you can ask me anything, big or small.\"","then":"\"Anything?\" they murmur. \"Even at night?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"She's right. Some things just aren't for kids.\"","then":"They go quiet. \"So where do I take my questions?\""},{"text":"\"Every family is different. Now go to sleep, beta.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they sigh, not sure which rule is theirs."},{"text":"\"Well, she's being very old-fashioned, isn't she?\"","then":"\"Should I tell her that?\" they ask, interested."}],"why":"A clear 'our home' rule tells your child where they can always bring questions."},{"prompt":"Your child yawns and asks: \"What if my question is really embarrassing?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Bring it to me. You'll never be in trouble for asking.\"","then":"They let out a big yawn. \"Okay. Good.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Then I'll try really hard not to laugh.\"","then":"\"You'd laugh?\" they ask, suddenly wide awake."},{"text":"\"Then maybe ask one of your friends about it instead, beta.\"","then":"\"Okay. My friends know lots of stuff,\" they yawn."},{"text":"\"Only come to me if it's really important.\"","then":"\"How important?\" they ask, frowning."}],"why":"Promising no trouble for any question is what makes the embarrassing ones reach you."},{"prompt":"As you stand up, your child whispers: \"Can I ask one right now?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Of course. Go on.\"","then":"\"Why do some grown-ups kiss on the lips?\" they whisper.","best":true},{"text":"\"Only if it's not a silly one.\"","then":"\"It's probably silly,\" they decide, and turn over."},{"text":"\"Is it a quick one? I'm really tired.\"","then":"\"Never mind,\" they mumble into the pillow."},{"text":"\"Tomorrow. Remind me if you remember.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they sigh. By morning, it's gone."}],"why":"Taking the question when it comes shows your child that asking you is always welcome."}],"relearn":"Leave a child with a standing, no-trouble invitation to ask anything, rather than a high bar that closes the door."},
  {"id":"tk-1130","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"kissing on TV","hook":"It's family film night, and the couple on screen suddenly kiss.","setup":"Your child turns to you, puzzled.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"What are they doing? Why?\"","options":[{"text":"\"It's just film stuff. None of it is real life, beta.\"","then":"\"So people don't kiss in real life?\" they ask."},{"text":"\"Kissing. Grown-ups who like each other sometimes do.\"","then":"\"Oh,\" they say, and turn back to the film.","best":true},{"text":"\"Don't look at that! Close your eyes, quickly.\"","then":"They squeeze their eyes shut, then peek. \"Why can't I look?\""},{"text":"\"Nothing. Let's just watch something else now.\"","then":"\"But what were they doing?\" they ask, as you flick channels."}],"why":"A calm, matter-of-fact answer tells your child affection isn't something to panic about."},{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"Will I kiss someone when I grow up?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Don't think about such things at your age.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, clearly still thinking about it."},{"text":"\"Maybe, if you both want to. That's for much later.\"","then":"\"Ew,\" they grin. \"Much, much later.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Never! Not in this family, you won't.\"","then":"\"Why not?\" they ask, suddenly more curious."},{"text":"\"Maybe. You'll know all about it when you're older.\"","then":"\"How will I know?\" they ask."}],"why":"A light, honest answer that includes 'if you both want to' plants consent early."},{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"Does everyone have to kiss if someone wants to?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Only if it's someone in the family.\"","then":"\"So I have to kiss everyone at Diwali?\" they groan."},{"text":"\"Don't worry about that. It's grown-up stuff.\"","then":"\"But what if someone wants to?\" they press."},{"text":"\"No. Nobody has to kiss or hug if they don't want to.\"","then":"\"Not even Bua?\" they ask, eyes wide.","best":true},{"text":"\"No, unless it would be rude to say no to them, of course.\"","then":"They frown. \"How do I know if it's rude?\""}],"why":"Teaching that no one has to kiss or hug is consent, in words a child can use."},{"prompt":"At the next family visit, Bua calls out: \"Come, give Bua a big kiss!\"","options":[{"text":"\"Bua, please stop forcing kids to kiss you. It's creepy.\"","then":"Bua's face falls. \"Creepy? I'm family!\" she says, hurt."},{"text":"\"They're just shy, Bua. Don't mind them.\"","then":"Bua smiles. \"Shy! Next time, then.\" She'll ask again."},{"text":"\"You can give Bua a wave or a high five, if you like.\"","then":"Bua laughs. \"A high five! Okay, clever one.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Don't be rude now. Go and give Bua a kiss.\"","then":"Bua beams. \"See? Not so hard!\" Your child wipes their cheek after."}],"why":"Offering a choice of greeting backs your child's say over their own body, kindly."}],"relearn":"Give a calm, matter-of-fact answer about affection on screen, not a panicked 'don't look'."},
  {"id":"tk-1131","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"saying I don't know","hook":"Your child is doing a school project on the human body and comes to you for help.","setup":"They slide their notebook across the table.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"Why do babies have more bones than grown-ups?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Stop asking things even I don't know. It's annoying.\"","then":"They pull the notebook back. \"Sorry.\""},{"text":"\"Because babies need them, obviously. Next question.\"","then":"\"But why do they need them?\" they press."},{"text":"\"Good question. Ask your teacher about it tomorrow.\"","then":"\"She said to ask at home,\" they sigh."},{"text":"\"Honestly, I'm not sure. Let's look it up together.\"","then":"\"You don't know?\" they grin. \"Okay, let's find out.\"","best":true}],"why":"Admitting you're not sure and finding out together keeps you their go-to."},{"prompt":"A while later, your child asks: \"Aren't grown-ups supposed to know everything?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Parents know what matters. That's enough.\"","then":"They shrug, unconvinced. \"Okay.\""},{"text":"\"I should, really. I'm a bit embarrassed I didn't know.\"","then":"They look worried. \"Is it bad not to know?\""},{"text":"\"Mostly, yes. I just forgot this one thing.\"","then":"\"Oh. So I'll know everything when I'm big?\" they ask."},{"text":"\"Nobody knows everything. Finding out is the fun part.\"","then":"They think about it. \"So you're still learning too?\"","best":true}],"why":"Showing that grown-ups still learn makes it safe for your child not to know too."},{"prompt":"The next week, your child asks: \"Can you help me find out another body thing?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Can't you just search it yourself now?\"","then":"\"I guess,\" they say, and wander off with the tablet."},{"text":"\"Only if it's for school, okay?\"","then":"\"It's not for school,\" they admit, and drop it."},{"text":"\"Maybe at the weekend, if there's time.\"","then":"\"You always say that,\" they grumble."},{"text":"\"Yes! What do you want to find out?\"","then":"\"Why hiccups happen,\" they say, already opening the laptop.","best":true}],"why":"Saying yes to finding out together makes learning side by side a habit."}],"relearn":"Saying 'I'm not sure. Let's find out together' models honesty and keeps you your child's go-to."},
  {"id":"tk-1132","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"role-play","persona":"Priya","source":"backed in front of family","hook":"It's Sunday lunch at your in-laws' house, with the whole family around the table.","setup":"Your child has been listening closely to the adults.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child asks loudly: \"Why do grown-ups have hair down there?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Good thing to wonder. I'll answer properly when it's just us.\"","then":"\"Okay!\" they say, and go back to their rice.","best":true},{"text":"\"How embarrassing! Don't ask such things in front of everyone.\"","then":"Their face goes red. \"Sorry,\" they whisper to their plate."},{"text":"\"Because bodies change. Now, who wants more dal?\"","then":"\"Oh,\" they say, unsure if they should ask more."},{"text":"\"Ask your Chacha. He seems to know everything.\"","then":"\"Chacha, why?\" they ask, and the whole table laughs at them."}],"why":"Backing the question calmly and promising a proper answer later keeps it safe to ask."},{"prompt":"Your mother-in-law says: \"In our time, children never asked such things.\"","options":[{"text":"\"And that silence did nobody any good, did it?\"","then":"Her face tightens. \"So now I'm the problem?\""},{"text":"\"Yes, Mummyji. I'll make sure it doesn't happen again.\"","then":"She nods, satisfied. \"Good. Better to stop it early.\""},{"text":"\"Kids these days, Mummyji! What can we do?\"","then":"She laughs. \"Too much TV. That's what it is.\""},{"text":"\"I'm glad they ask me. It helps keep them safe.\"","then":"She purses her lips. \"Hm. Times change, I suppose.\"","best":true}],"why":"A calm, respectful line backs your child without a fight with elders."},{"prompt":"Later, your child asks you quietly: \"Was that a naughty question?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Not naughty at all. I'm glad you asked me.\"","then":"They smile. \"So will you tell me now?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Yes. You embarrassed me in front of Dadi.\"","then":"Their eyes fill up. \"I didn't know.\""},{"text":"\"A bit. Save those for when we're alone.\"","then":"They nod. \"So body questions are secret ones?\""},{"text":"\"Let's not bring it up again, okay?\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they whisper, but they still look puzzled."}],"why":"Telling them the question wasn't naughty undoes the room's silence."},{"prompt":"At home, your child asks again: \"So why do grown-ups have hair down there?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Hmm, I forgot what you asked. Never mind.\"","then":"\"I remember it,\" they insist. \"Tell me!\""},{"text":"\"Stop thinking about that stuff. Go and play.\"","then":"\"Fine,\" they say, and go, still puzzled."},{"text":"\"You'll find out all about it when it happens.\"","then":"They frown. \"That's not an answer.\""},{"text":"\"Hair grows there as bodies grow up. It's normal.\"","then":"\"Will I get it too?\" they ask, curious.","best":true}],"why":"A simple, true answer when they ask again shows body questions are always welcome."}],"relearn":"Back a child's question calmly in front of others and promise a proper answer later, instead of shaming them."},
  {"id":"tk-1133","cat":"how-to-talk","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"only got one word out","hook":"A TV advert ends, and your child asks what a condom is. You freeze and manage only 'um'.","setup":"They're still looking at you, waiting.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"Why did you go all red? Is it a bad thing?\"","options":[{"text":"\"You caught me off guard. Fair question. Let me think.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, and wait patiently.","best":true},{"text":"\"It's nothing. Just a boring grown-up thing.\"","then":"\"Then why was it on TV?\" they ask."},{"text":"\"Not bad, just grown-up. Ask me when you're much older.\"","then":"\"How much older?\" they ask, disappointed."},{"text":"\"Never mind. Just don't ask me that again.\"","then":"\"Sorry,\" they mumble, and turn back to the TV."}],"why":"Naming that you were caught off guard buys time and keeps the question welcome."},{"prompt":"A minute later, your child asks: \"So what is it?\"","options":[{"text":"\"It's just for grown-ups. That's all you need to know for now.\"","then":"\"But what does it do?\" they press."},{"text":"\"Something grown-ups can use so a baby doesn't start.\"","then":"\"Oh,\" they nod. \"So people choose when to have babies?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"It's a kind of balloon. That's all.\"","then":"They giggle. \"A balloon? On TV?\""},{"text":"\"Something only married people need to know.\"","then":"\"So I'll learn when I get married?\" they ask."}],"why":"A short, true answer at their level beats a fib they'll later have to unlearn."},{"prompt":"At bedtime, your child says: \"You looked scared when I asked. Are you cross?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Not cross. Just surprised. Keep asking me.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they yawn. \"You're not scary, then.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"A little. That wasn't a very nice question.\"","then":"\"Sorry,\" they mumble, pulling the blanket over their face."},{"text":"\"Let's not talk about that advert ever again.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say quietly, and roll over."},{"text":"\"No, no, not at all. Now go to sleep, beta.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, still not quite sure."}],"why":"Saying you were surprised, not cross, keeps the door open after a wobble."}],"relearn":"If a question catches you off guard, name it and stay open; freezing then shutting down closes the door."},
  {"id":"tk-1134","type":"sort","persona":"any","source":"opens vs shuts","hook":"Sort each parent move: does it open the door or shut it?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Calm, honest answer at their level"},{"id":"b","text":"Shock and a raised voice"},{"id":"c","text":"'Great question, let's talk'"},{"id":"d","text":"'You're too young to ask that'"},{"id":"e","text":"Thanking them for coming to you"},{"id":"f","text":"Changing the subject in a panic"}],"bins":[{"id":"open","label":"Opens the door","valence":"pos"},{"id":"shut","label":"Shuts it down","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"open","b":"shut","c":"open","d":"shut","e":"open","f":"shut"},"relearn":"Calm honest answers and welcoming questions open the door; shock, 'too young' and panic shut it down.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1135","type":"sort","persona":"any","source":"source vs away","hook":"Sort each reaction: does it keep you the source, or send your child away?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Answering simply and truthfully"},{"id":"b","text":"'Go ask your friends'"},{"id":"c","text":"Staying calm and unshocked"},{"id":"d","text":"Getting angry at the question"},{"id":"e","text":"'Let's find out together'"},{"id":"f","text":"Disgust and a 'chee, don't'"}],"bins":[{"id":"source","label":"Keeps you the source","valence":"pos"},{"id":"away","label":"Sends them away","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"source","b":"away","c":"source","d":"away","e":"source","f":"away"},"relearn":"Calm, honest answers keep you a child's source; anger, disgust and 'ask your friends' send them away.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1136","type":"sort","persona":"any","source":"now vs later content","hook":"Sort what's age-right to answer NOW for a young child, versus saved for LATER.","items":[{"id":"a","text":"The correct names for body parts"},{"id":"b","text":"Explicit details of adult sex"},{"id":"c","text":"'Private parts are just for you'"},{"id":"d","text":"The complexities of adult relationships"},{"id":"e","text":"'You're the boss of your own body'"},{"id":"f","text":"Graphic specifics they didn't ask for"}],"bins":[{"id":"now","label":"Age-right now","valence":"pos"},{"id":"later","label":"Save for later","valence":"uhoh"}],"key":{"a":"now","b":"later","c":"now","d":"later","e":"now","f":"later"},"relearn":"Correct names, privacy and body ownership are age-right now; explicit adult details are saved for later.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1137","type":"sort","persona":"any","source":"builds vs erodes trust","hook":"Sort each habit: does it build a child's trust, or erode it?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Honest answers, even 'I don't know'"},{"id":"b","text":"Making up an answer to look sure"},{"id":"c","text":"Going back to repair a fumble"},{"id":"d","text":"Pretending the question never happened"},{"id":"e","text":"Keeping your calm every time"},{"id":"f","text":"Laughing the question off"}],"bins":[{"id":"builds","label":"Builds trust","valence":"pos"},{"id":"erodes","label":"Erodes trust","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"builds","b":"erodes","c":"builds","d":"erodes","e":"builds","f":"erodes"},"relearn":"Honesty, repairing fumbles and staying calm build trust; faking answers and laughing them off erode it.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1138","type":"sort","persona":"any","source":"invites vs deters","hook":"Sort each thing you say: does it invite the next question or deter it?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"'No question is silly'"},{"id":"b","text":"'We don't discuss such things'"},{"id":"c","text":"'You can ask me anything'"},{"id":"d","text":"'Wait until you're much older'"},{"id":"e","text":"'I'm glad you came to me'"},{"id":"f","text":"'That's not a nice thing to ask'"}],"bins":[{"id":"invites","label":"Invites the next question","valence":"pos"},{"id":"deters","label":"Deters it","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"invites","b":"deters","c":"invites","d":"deters","e":"invites","f":"deters"},"relearn":"'No question is silly' and 'ask me anything' invite the next question; 'we don't discuss that' deters it.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1139","type":"sort","persona":"any","source":"calm vs panicked","hook":"Sort each response into calm-and-askable, or panicked-and-closing.","items":[{"id":"a","text":"A steady, matter-of-fact tone"},{"id":"b","text":"A flustered, flushed shut-down"},{"id":"c","text":"'Let me think and answer properly'"},{"id":"d","text":"Snapping 'why would you ask that?'"},{"id":"e","text":"A warm 'thanks for asking'"},{"id":"f","text":"Quickly changing the subject"}],"bins":[{"id":"calm","label":"Calm and askable","valence":"pos"},{"id":"panic","label":"Panicked and closing","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"calm","b":"panic","c":"calm","d":"panic","e":"calm","f":"panic"},"relearn":"A steady, warm, matter-of-fact response stays askable; flustering, snapping and dodging close the door.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1140","type":"sort","persona":"any","source":"one talk myth vs truth","hook":"Sort each idea about RSE talks as a myth to drop, or a truth to keep.","items":[{"id":"a","text":"It's many small chats over years"},{"id":"b","text":"It's one big dreaded talk"},{"id":"c","text":"'I don't know' is a fine answer"},{"id":"d","text":"I must have every answer ready"},{"id":"e","text":"Willingness beats expertise"},{"id":"f","text":"Talking gives children ideas"}],"bins":[{"id":"keep","label":"True, keep it","valence":"pos"},{"id":"drop","label":"Myth, drop it","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"keep","b":"drop","c":"keep","d":"drop","e":"keep","f":"drop"},"relearn":"Truths to keep: many small chats, 'I don't know' is fine, willingness beats expertise; drop the dreaded-talk myths.","cat":"how-to-talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1170","cat":"middle-years","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If I mention periods early, I'll just scare her.\"","myth":{"un":"If I mention periods early, I'll just scare her.","re":"A calm heads-up before periods start makes the first one feel expected and supported, not a frightening shock.","why":"Warned in advance, she meets it ready, not afraid."},"relearn":"A warm, early heads-up about periods makes the first one feel expected, not frightening.","persona":"Divya","source":"early heads-up calms"},
  {"id":"tk-1171","cat":"middle-years","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"My son doesn't need to know anything about periods.\"","myth":{"un":"My son doesn't need to know anything about periods.","re":"Every child learns about everyone's puberty, periods and wet dreams alike, so they grow up with empathy instead of teasing.","why":"Knowing the facts ends the giggling and the shame."},"relearn":"All children learn about everyone's puberty; it builds empathy and ends teasing.","persona":"Vikram","source":"boys learn periods too"},
  {"id":"tk-1172","cat":"middle-years","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Hand a child a phone and they'll work the safety out themselves.\"","myth":{"un":"Hand a child a phone and they'll work the safety out themselves.","re":"Pair a first device with simple, ongoing talks about privacy and telling you about anything off; don't hand it over in silence.","why":"A device plus a conversation beats a device alone."},"relearn":"Pair a first device with simple online-safety talks, not a silent handover.","persona":"Vikram","source":"device needs a talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1173","cat":"middle-years","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"A wet dream means something is wrong with my child.\"","myth":{"un":"A wet dream means something is wrong with my child.","re":"Wet dreams are a normal, healthy part of growing up; a calm word beforehand stops a child thinking they've done something bad.","why":"Named as normal, it never feels like a fault."},"relearn":"Wet dreams are normal; a calm, matter-of-fact heads-up prevents needless shame.","persona":"any","source":"wet dreams are normal"},
  {"id":"tk-1174","cat":"middle-years","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If she reports a scary video, taking the phone away keeps her safe.\"","myth":{"un":"If she reports a scary video, taking the phone away keeps her safe.","re":"Thank a child for telling you and talk it through; punishing the messenger only teaches them to hide the next scary thing.","why":"Thanked, she keeps coming to you; punished, she goes quiet."},"relearn":"Thank a child for reporting scary content; punishment teaches them to hide it.","persona":"Vikram","source":"thank not punish"},
  {"id":"tk-1175","cat":"middle-years","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"There's plenty of time, I'll start once the changes actually begin.\"","myth":{"un":"There's plenty of time, I'll start once the changes actually begin.","re":"The pre-puberty years are the golden window; a child prepared before the changes start handles them far better.","why":"Prepared early, the changes arrive as no surprise."},"relearn":"Prepare before puberty starts; the pre-puberty years are the golden window.","persona":"any","source":"golden window"},
  {"id":"tk-1176","cat":"middle-years","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If I look unsure answering a frank question, I've already failed.\"","myth":{"un":"If I look unsure answering a frank question, I've already failed.","re":"\"I'm not sure, let's find out together\" is an honest answer; willingness to stay in the talk matters more than a perfect reply.","why":"Staying in the conversation is the real win."},"relearn":"\"Let's find out together\" is a good answer; willingness beats perfect expertise.","persona":"any","source":"let's find out together"},
  {"id":"tk-1177","cat":"middle-years","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Schools cover all the puberty talk, so I can leave it to them.\"","myth":{"un":"Schools cover all the puberty talk, so I can leave it to them.","re":"A lesson at school is a start, not the whole story; your calm answers at home make you the source your child keeps returning to.","why":"Home talks are where the real questions land."},"relearn":"School lessons help, but your home talks keep you the source your child returns to.","persona":"Priya","source":"home not just school"},
  {"id":"tk-1178","cat":"middle-years","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: prepare a child for this before puberty, or save it for the teen years?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Periods are a normal, healthy sign of growing up"},{"id":"b","text":"Wet dreams happen and nothing is wrong"},{"id":"c","text":"Basic privacy and online safety"},{"id":"d","text":"Detailed advice on adult relationships"},{"id":"e","text":"What sweat, hair and mood changes mean"},{"id":"f","text":"Navigating consent in a dating relationship"}],"bins":[{"id":"now","label":"Prep before puberty","valence":"pos"},{"id":"later","label":"Save for the teen years","valence":"uhoh"}],"key":{"a":"now","b":"now","c":"now","d":"later","e":"now","f":"later"},"relearn":"Periods, wet dreams, body changes and online basics suit pre-puberty; detailed adult relationship advice waits.","persona":"any","source":"now or teen years"},
  {"id":"tk-1179","cat":"middle-years","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each online habit: a green habit, or a risk to talk through?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Telling you about a creepy message"},{"id":"b","text":"Sending a stranger their address"},{"id":"c","text":"Keeping the account private"},{"id":"d","text":"Meeting an online 'friend' alone"},{"id":"e","text":"Asking before downloading an app"},{"id":"f","text":"Sharing location with everyone"}],"bins":[{"id":"green","label":"Green habit","valence":"pos"},{"id":"risk","label":"Risk to address","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"green","b":"risk","c":"green","d":"risk","e":"green","f":"risk"},"relearn":"Telling you, staying private and asking first are green; sharing details, meeting strangers and open location are risks.","persona":"Vikram","source":"green habit or risk"},
  {"id":"tk-1180","cat":"middle-years","type":"sort","hook":"Sort how you reacted when your pre-teen asked about bodies: kept the door open, or shut it?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Great question, let me explain simply\""},{"id":"b","text":"\"That's dirty, don't ask me that\""},{"id":"c","text":"\"You can ask me anything, anytime\""},{"id":"d","text":"\"You're too young to know\""},{"id":"e","text":"\"I'm not sure, let's look it up together\""},{"id":"f","text":"Laughing it off and changing the subject"}],"bins":[{"id":"open","label":"Keeps the door open","valence":"pos"},{"id":"shut","label":"Shuts the door","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"open","b":"shut","c":"open","d":"shut","e":"open","f":"shut"},"relearn":"Welcoming the question and offering to find out together keeps the door open; shaming or dismissing shuts it.","persona":"any","source":"door open or shut"},
  {"id":"tk-1181","cat":"middle-years","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: which belong in the 'before her first period' heads-up?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"What a period is, in simple words"},{"id":"b","text":"That it's normal and you'll help her"},{"id":"c","text":"Where pads are kept at home"},{"id":"d","text":"A long lecture on adult reproduction"},{"id":"e","text":"That she can come to you anytime"},{"id":"f","text":"A warning to keep it a secret"}],"bins":[{"id":"pack","label":"Include it","valence":"pos"},{"id":"leave","label":"Leave it out","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"pack","b":"pack","c":"pack","d":"leave","e":"pack","f":"leave"},"relearn":"A first-period heads-up gives simple facts, reassurance, where supplies are and an open invitation; no lectures, no secrecy.","persona":"Divya","source":"first-period kit"},
  {"id":"tk-1182","cat":"middle-years","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each line: a calm, normalising reply about body changes, or one that lands as shame?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Everyone's body changes, it's healthy\""},{"id":"b","text":"\"Why are you so obsessed with this?\""},{"id":"c","text":"\"That's a normal part of growing up\""},{"id":"d","text":"\"Nice children don't talk like that\""},{"id":"e","text":"\"Good question, here's how it works\""},{"id":"f","text":"\"Stop being so dramatic about it\""}],"bins":[{"id":"calm","label":"Calm and normalising","valence":"pos"},{"id":"shame","label":"Lands as shame","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"calm","b":"shame","c":"calm","d":"shame","e":"calm","f":"shame"},"relearn":"Naming changes as normal and healthy reassures; calling a child obsessed, dramatic or not-nice teaches shame.","persona":"any","source":"calm or shame"},
  {"id":"tk-1183","cat":"middle-years","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each first-phone move: a safety step to set up, or a habit to rethink?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Agreeing screen-time limits together"},{"id":"b","text":"Letting them follow back any stranger"},{"id":"c","text":"Setting up reporting and block buttons"},{"id":"d","text":"Keeping the phone secret from you"},{"id":"e","text":"Promising to tell you about anything scary"},{"id":"f","text":"Posting their daily location publicly"}],"bins":[{"id":"setup","label":"Set it up","valence":"pos"},{"id":"rethink","label":"Rethink it","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"setup","b":"rethink","c":"setup","d":"rethink","e":"setup","f":"rethink"},"relearn":"Shared limits, block/report tools and a promise to tell you are safety steps; secret phones, following strangers and public location are not.","persona":"Vikram","source":"phone setup or rethink"},
  {"id":"tk-1184","cat":"middle-years","type":"sort","hook":"Sort what a pre-teen is ready to understand about periods and puberty now.","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Periods are a normal monthly cycle"},{"id":"b","text":"Hair grows in new places as you grow"},{"id":"c","text":"How to manage cramps and supplies"},{"id":"d","text":"Graphic, explicit sexual detail"},{"id":"e","text":"Voices and bodies change at different paces"},{"id":"f","text":"Adult contraception choices in depth"}],"bins":[{"id":"ready","label":"Ready for it now","valence":"pos"},{"id":"wait","label":"Wait until older","valence":"uhoh"}],"key":{"a":"ready","b":"ready","c":"ready","d":"wait","e":"ready","f":"wait"},"relearn":"Cycles, body hair, managing periods and different paces suit now; explicit detail and in-depth contraception wait.","persona":"any","source":"ready now or wait"},
  {"id":"tk-1185","cat":"middle-years","type":"sort","hook":"Sort: when your child shows you something online, which reactions keep them telling you?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Thank you for showing me\""},{"id":"b","text":"Shouting and snatching the device"},{"id":"c","text":"\"Let's look at it together calmly\""},{"id":"d","text":"\"You're banned from the internet now\""},{"id":"e","text":"\"You did the right thing telling me\""},{"id":"f","text":"Mocking them for being upset by it"}],"bins":[{"id":"keeps","label":"Keeps them telling you","valence":"pos"},{"id":"silences","label":"Silences them","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"keeps","b":"silences","c":"keeps","d":"silences","e":"keeps","f":"silences"},"relearn":"Thanking them, looking together calmly and praising the telling keep the door open; shouting, banning and mocking close it.","persona":"Vikram","source":"keeps telling or silences"},
  {"id":"tk-1186","cat":"middle-years","type":"branch","persona":"Divya","source":"before they start","hook":"Your daughter is nearly ten. Her periods haven't started, and you haven't mentioned them yet.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your mother says there's no need to talk about it until it happens. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Ask her school to cover it in class for you","then":"The school says that's next year. Your daughter still knows nothing."},{"text":"Bring it up warmly with your daughter now","then":"Your daughter listens, curious, and asks if it hurts.","best":true},{"text":"Leave a leaflet on her bed and say nothing","then":"She reads it alone and comes away with more worries than answers."},{"text":"Wait, and explain it only once it begins","then":"Weeks pass. Your mother nods approvingly, and nothing is said."}],"why":"Talking before periods start means the first one feels expected, not frightening."},{"prompt":"A few days later, your daughter says a friend told her periods are dirty. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say periods are a normal, healthy part of growing up","then":"She looks relieved. 'So I can still go to school and play?'","best":true},{"text":"Tell her not to listen to silly friends","then":"She nods, but doesn't know what to believe instead."},{"text":"Say that's why girls keep them very secret","then":"She nods, now nervous about something that hasn't even started."},{"text":"Say 'We'll talk about all that when it actually happens'","then":"She shrugs. Her friend's word is the only one she has."}],"why":"A calm, clear 'it's normal and healthy' replaces shame before it takes root."},{"prompt":"At the weekend, you pass the pads shelf at the chemist together. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Show her the options and let her pick some for her bag","then":"She chooses a pack with a purple wrapper and tucks it in her school bag.","best":true},{"text":"Buy some quietly and hide them in your cupboard","then":"They're ready, but she doesn't know where they are or how to use them."},{"text":"Buy some, and say you'll show her how to use them later","then":"The pack goes into a drawer. 'Later' keeps slipping."},{"text":"Walk past quickly so she doesn't feel awkward","then":"She notices you hurrying, and learns this shelf is embarrassing."}],"why":"A ready kit she chose herself makes the first period feel prepared, not scary."},{"prompt":"Months later, she calls you from the school office: 'I think it started.' What do you say?","options":[{"text":"'Oh no! Leave school and come home straight away.'","then":"She leaves school early, flustered, and misses her test."},{"text":"'Okay. We'll talk about it properly this evening.'","then":"She gets through the day, unsure what she's meant to do."},{"text":"'Thanks for telling me. Use a pad. The office has some.'","then":"'Okay,' she says, sounding steadier. 'I can do that.'","best":true},{"text":"'Don't tell anyone about it. We'll talk at home.'","then":"She sits through class tense and alone with it."}],"why":"A calm, warm reply turns her first period into something she can handle."}],"debrief":"Prepare a child for periods before they begin so the first one feels expected, not a frightening surprise.","relearn":"Explain periods before they start so the first never comes as a shock."},
  {"id":"tk-1187","cat":"middle-years","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"end the teasing","hook":"Your son says boys at school teased a classmate who got her period in class.","steps":[{"prompt":"He tells it laughing, glancing at you to see if it's funny. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Laugh along. Boys will be boys, after all","then":"He grins, pleased, and tells the story again at dinner."},{"text":"Say it's girls' business and none of his concern","then":"He shrugs. Next time the boys laugh, he laughs too."},{"text":"Explain periods are normal, and teasing hurts","then":"His smile fades. 'I didn't think about how she felt,' he admits.","best":true},{"text":"Tell him teasing is wrong, and leave it there","then":"He nods, still unsure what a period is or why she was so upset."}],"why":"Knowing periods are normal, and that teasing hurts, builds empathy and ends shame."},{"prompt":"Later, your son asks what actually happens during a period. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"'Ask your aunty. That's more of a women's topic.'","then":"He never asks her. The question stays with him."},{"text":"'It's a kind of bleeding girls get. That's all, really.'","then":"He frowns. 'Does it hurt? Is she sick?'"},{"text":"Explain simply that the womb sheds a lining monthly","then":"He listens. 'So it's just the body working?' he asks.","best":true},{"text":"'You don't need to know. You're a boy.'","then":"He shrugs. His picture of periods stays a playground joke."}],"why":"Every child learning about everyone's puberty turns a joke into understanding."},{"prompt":"A week later, he says the boys are teasing her again. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Tell him to stay well out of it","then":"He does. The teasing carries on around him."},{"text":"Ask how he could stand by her, and which teacher to tell","then":"He thinks. 'I could sit with her at lunch. And tell Ma'am.'","best":true},{"text":"Say she should tell a teacher herself","then":"He passes it on, but she's too embarrassed to go."},{"text":"Say you're calling the principal about it right now","then":"He panics. 'Don't! They'll know it was me.'"}],"why":"Helping him plan how to stand by her, and which adult to tell, turns empathy into action."}],"debrief":"Teaching every child about everyone's puberty builds empathy and ends the teasing and shame.","relearn":"All children learn about everyone's puberty; it builds empathy and ends teasing."},
  {"id":"tk-1188","cat":"middle-years","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"first phone talk","hook":"Your pre-teen is about to get their first phone, mainly for the bus journey to school.","steps":[{"prompt":"It's the evening before their first bus ride with it. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Save the talk for if something goes wrong","then":"They head off happily, with no plan for when something feels off."},{"text":"Hand it over with no conversation at all, just a hug","then":"They're thrilled, and spend the evening downloading games."},{"text":"Warn them you'll be reading every single message","then":"Their excitement drops. 'So it's not really mine?' they ask."},{"text":"Hand it over with a short online-safety talk","then":"They listen, then save your number as 'Home' with a heart.","best":true}],"why":"Starting with simple talks gives them a safety net and keeps you in the loop."},{"prompt":"A fortnight later, your child says someone on the bus filmed them without asking. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say it's not their fault, and plan who to tell","then":"They relax a little. You agree to tell their class teacher tomorrow.","best":true},{"text":"Say they shouldn't have been on their phone either","then":"They go quiet. 'Forget it. It doesn't matter.'"},{"text":"Tell them to ignore it. It's only a video","then":"They nod, but check the class group nervously all evening."},{"text":"Storm off to the school to find whoever did it","then":"Your child begs you not to. 'Everyone will know I told.'"}],"why":"Hearing it's not their fault, and telling a teacher together, keeps them safe and still talking to you."},{"prompt":"A month in, you notice the phone comes out at meals and at bedtime. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say nothing. That's just how kids are now","then":"The phone creeps further into every evening."},{"text":"Write strict phone rules and stick them on the fridge","then":"They follow them at first, then find every gap you didn't write down."},{"text":"Agree a few phone-free times together as a family","then":"They grumble, then say the rule should apply to you too.","best":true},{"text":"Take the phone away for a whole week","then":"They sulk, and start hiding it in their school bag."}],"why":"Rules made together are easier to keep, and they keep the conversation going."}],"debrief":"Pair a first device with simple talks on privacy, kindness and telling you anything scary.","relearn":"Pair a first device with simple online-safety talks, not a silent handover."},
  {"id":"tk-1189","cat":"middle-years","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"calm and thank","hook":"Your child comes to you, upset. A video popped up on the tablet and frightened them.","steps":[{"prompt":"They're close to tears, holding the tablet out to you. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Get angry and confiscate the tablet as punishment","then":"They cry harder. 'But I didn't do anything!'"},{"text":"Say 'It's not real. Stop being such a baby.'","then":"They wipe their eyes and go quiet, still scared."},{"text":"Stay calm, thank them for telling you, and talk it through","then":"They climb into your lap and tell you about the scary face in it.","best":true},{"text":"Hug them, and put on a cartoon to take their mind off it all","then":"They cheer up a little, but the scary face comes back at bedtime."}],"why":"Thanking them and talking it through teaches that telling you is safe."},{"prompt":"That night, they're scared to sleep with the light off. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Let them watch videos until they fall asleep","then":"They doze off with the tablet still glowing beside them."},{"text":"Sit with them and talk about what's real","then":"They ask a few questions, then drift off holding your hand.","best":true},{"text":"Tell them firmly to stop being silly and sleep","then":"They lie awake in the dark, too scared to call you."},{"text":"Leave the light on for them and close the door","then":"The light helps, but they lie there alone with the scary face."}],"why":"Staying close and talking helps a scared child feel safe again."},{"prompt":"The next day, you think about how to stop it happening again. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Do nothing. These things just happen online sometimes, sadly","then":"A week later, another scary video pops up."},{"text":"Ban the tablet for good, and tell them why","then":"They're upset, and ask to use a friend's tablet instead."},{"text":"Set up the filters quietly on your own tonight","then":"The filters help, but your child doesn't know what to do if one slips through."},{"text":"Choose safer settings with them, and ask them to tell you","then":"They help choose the settings. 'I'll tell you if another one comes,' they say.","best":true}],"why":"Safer settings plus the habit of telling you keep them protected and talking."}],"debrief":"Thank a child for reporting scary content and talk it through; anger teaches them to hide it.","relearn":"Thank a child for reporting scary content; punishment teaches them to hide it."},
  {"id":"tk-1190","cat":"middle-years","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"simple true answer","hook":"Your nine-year-old asks you, point-blank, how babies actually get made.","steps":[{"prompt":"It's just the two of you in the car, and they're clearly serious. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Promise to give them a good book on it at home","then":"They read it alone that night and come away with more questions."},{"text":"Give a simple, true, age-right answer without shame","then":"They listen, then say, 'Oh. That's kind of weird. But okay.'","best":true},{"text":"Tell them a stork brought them and laugh it off","then":"They roll their eyes. 'I'm nine, not five.'"},{"text":"Say you'll explain it all when they're a teenager","then":"They sigh and look out of the window. A friend will explain first."}],"why":"A simple, true answer keeps you their trusted source for the harder questions ahead."},{"prompt":"At the weekend, they say a friend told them a very different story about it. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say friends' stories don't matter, and quickly change the subject","then":"They nod, still unsure which version is true."},{"text":"Say that friend is a bad influence on them","then":"They get defensive. 'He's my best friend!'"},{"text":"Ask what the friend said, and gently set the facts straight","then":"They tell you, and you untangle the myths together. A few make them laugh.","best":true},{"text":"Tell them to believe you, not their friend","then":"They say okay, but don't know which parts of the story were wrong."}],"why":"Hearing what they've heard lets you swap myths for facts."},{"prompt":"Your mother hears your child has been asking about babies, and says kids that age shouldn't be told anything. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Agree, and promise not to say any more","then":"She's pleased. You wonder what you'll say when the next question comes."},{"text":"Tell her she knows nothing about raising kids today","then":"She goes quiet and hurt, and the visit turns stiff."},{"text":"Say you only answer because they ask you","then":"She nods. 'Next time, just don't answer.'"},{"text":"Say simple, true answers help keep children safe","then":"She shakes her head, but doesn't argue. 'Just keep it simple,' she says.","best":true}],"why":"Calmly standing by honest answers keeps the talks going, even when family disagree."},{"prompt":"A month later, your child comes back with a follow-up question about babies. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Answer, but look uncomfortable the whole time","then":"They cut the question short, sensing your unease."},{"text":"Tell them to look it up themselves this time","then":"They search online and land on things you'd never have chosen."},{"text":"Welcome it, and give a simple, true answer","then":"It takes two minutes. They nod. 'Can I ask you other stuff too?'","best":true},{"text":"Say you've already covered all of that","then":"They look embarrassed and don't ask the next one."}],"why":"Welcoming each follow-up shows the first answer opened a door, not closed a topic."}],"debrief":"Answer \"where do babies come from?\" with a simple, true answer at the child's level, never a stork story.","relearn":"Give a simple, honest answer; never a stork story or a shutdown."},
  {"id":"tk-1191","cat":"middle-years","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"use the window","hook":"Your child is eight, and you realise puberty may begin before you've said a word about it.","steps":[{"prompt":"A friend says school will probably cover it anyway. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Hope school covers it, and say nothing yet","then":"Months pass. Your child's first questions go to the playground."},{"text":"Wait until you see the first signs of change","then":"The first changes arrive before your talk does, and your child is scared."},{"text":"Start small, age-right chats now","then":"The first chat is short and a bit awkward. Your child asks two questions.","best":true},{"text":"Plan one big talk for their next birthday","then":"The date looms. You both dread it, and it gets pushed back."}],"why":"The pre-puberty years are the golden window: small chats now prepare them for what's coming."},{"prompt":"A few weeks later, your child asks why a friend's voice suddenly sounds different. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Explain that voices deepen as bodies grow up","then":"They're fascinated. 'Will mine change too?' they ask.","best":true},{"text":"Say they're too young to worry about that","then":"They go quiet. The next question goes to a friend."},{"text":"Say it's a boys' thing, and leave it there for now","then":"They nod, but don't learn what's coming for everyone."},{"text":"Say it's nothing, and change the subject","then":"They shrug. Their friends explain it their own way."}],"why":"Answering small questions as they come builds the talk step by step."},{"prompt":"A few months later, your child seems moody and shuts their door more often. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Check in gently, and say they can ask you anything","then":"They mumble 'I'm fine', then later ask you about spots on their face.","best":true},{"text":"Demand to know what's wrong with them these days","then":"They snap back, and the door slams."},{"text":"Leave a book on puberty on their desk for them","then":"They read a bit, but the questions it raises have nowhere to go."},{"text":"Leave them be. It's just a phase they'll grow out of","then":"The door stays shut, and you're not sure what's going on."}],"why":"Gentle check-ins keep the door open as the changes begin."}],"debrief":"Use the pre-puberty golden window: small age-right chats now so the changes never shock them.","relearn":"Prepare before puberty starts; the pre-puberty years are the golden window."},
  {"id":"tk-1192","cat":"middle-years","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"don't know is fine","hook":"Your pre-teen asks if it's normal for one side of the chest to grow faster. You don't know.","steps":[{"prompt":"They look worried, waiting for your answer. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say it's nothing to worry about and move on","then":"They nod, but you can see the worry hasn't gone."},{"text":"Say you'll ask the doctor at the next visit","then":"They nod. The next doctor's visit is months away."},{"text":"Say \"I'm not sure. Let's find out together\"","then":"They nod, relieved you're taking it seriously, and fetch the laptop.","best":true},{"text":"Bluff a confident answer so you don't look unsure","then":"They relax for now. Later, a health site says something different."}],"why":"Finding out together is honest, and it shows the door stays open."},{"prompt":"That evening, you look into it and find trusted health sites beside scary forums. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Go through a trusted health site with your child","then":"It says uneven growth is common. Your child breathes out. 'Oh, good.'","best":true},{"text":"Read it yourself and give them the short version","then":"They get the answer, but not how to find a good source next time."},{"text":"Close the laptop. It's all too confusing","then":"The worry stays, and so does the question."},{"text":"Read the forums too, just to be thorough","then":"A horror story scares you both more than before."}],"why":"Checking a trusted source together teaches them where good answers live."},{"prompt":"A week later, you realise an answer you gave them earlier was wrong. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Slip in the right answer without admitting the mistake","then":"They look puzzled. 'But you said something different before.'"},{"text":"Let it go. It was only a small thing","then":"They repeat the wrong fact to their friends."},{"text":"Tell them plainly, and give the right answer","then":"They laugh. 'So parents get things wrong too,' they say.","best":true},{"text":"Blame the website you got it from","then":"They nod, and learn that mistakes are always someone else's."}],"why":"Owning a mistake shows honesty matters more than looking like an expert."}],"debrief":"\"I don't know. Let's find out together\" is an honest answer; willingness beats expertise.","relearn":"\"Let's find out together\" is a good answer; willingness beats perfect expertise."},
  {"id":"tk-1193","cat":"middle-years","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"online stranger rule","hook":"Your pre-teen mentions that an online 'friend' they've never met wants to video-call, just the two of them.","steps":[{"prompt":"They say it casually over dinner, watching your face. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Thank them, and talk it through calmly","then":"They relax. 'He's nice, though. He likes the same games,' they say.","best":true},{"text":"Panic, ban the internet, and lecture angrily","then":"They go red. 'I shouldn't have told you,' they mutter."},{"text":"Say no to the call, and leave it at that","then":"They nod, but don't understand why, and the chats carry on."},{"text":"Say it's probably fine if they're careful","then":"They grin. 'See? I said he was fine,' they say."}],"why":"Thanking them keeps them telling you, and that is what keeps them safe."},{"prompt":"That evening, you read the chat with your child. The 'friend' keeps asking which school they go to. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Delete the app at once without explaining","then":"They're upset, and download it again at a friend's house."},{"text":"Say a school name is harmless, and let it go","then":"They send it. The 'friend' now knows where to find them."},{"text":"Tell them to stop chatting, without saying why","then":"They agree, but still don't see what the problem was."},{"text":"Explain why personal details stay private online","then":"They frown. 'I didn't think a school name mattered,' they say, and don't reply.","best":true}],"why":"Explaining why details stay private helps them spot the risk themselves."},{"prompt":"Next day, the 'friend' messages: 'Don't tell your parents about us. They won't get it.' What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Message him yourself and threaten to go straight to the police","then":"He replies with a laughing emoji, and a new account appears."},{"text":"Name it a warning sign, then block and report it together","then":"Your child goes quiet, then nods. 'He did keep saying that.'","best":true},{"text":"Let it go. He's probably just a silly teenager too","then":"The messages keep coming, and your child feels torn."},{"text":"Block the account yourself without talking about it","then":"It's blocked, but your child doesn't learn why secret-asking matters."}],"why":"Secrecy is a warning sign. Block and report together, and call Childline 1098 if you're worried."},{"prompt":"Your child says they feel stupid for trusting him. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say it's fine, and change the subject to cheer them up","then":"They smile, but the feeling of being stupid stays."},{"text":"Say it's not their fault, and you're glad they told you","then":"Their shoulders drop, and they lean against you.","best":true},{"text":"Say let's never mention it again","then":"They nod. It becomes something they don't talk about."},{"text":"Say they really should have known better","then":"They look at the floor and say nothing more."}],"why":"When someone online tricks a child, it's never the child's fault. Telling you was brave."},{"prompt":"A week later, you sit down together to set online rules. What do you agree?","options":[{"text":"No strangers ever, and you'll read every chat each night","then":"They agree, and start deleting chats before you check."},{"text":"They can talk to anyone they like, as long as they're careful","then":"They nod, but 'careful' means different things to each of you."},{"text":"No solo chats with strangers, and tell you if anything's off","then":"They add a rule of their own: 'And you don't freak out.' You shake on it.","best":true},{"text":"No internet at all until they're much older","then":"They agree, then start using a friend's phone at school."}],"why":"Simple rules made together, plus the promise to tell you, keep them safer online."}],"debrief":"Video-calling online strangers alone is a risk; thank the child for telling and set the rule calmly.","relearn":"Talk through stranger-contact calmly; meeting strangers is a risk to address."},
  {"id":"tk-1194","cat":"middle-years","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"different paces","hook":"Your child is anxious that they're developing later than their friends.","steps":[{"prompt":"They say everyone in class looks older than them now. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say you were a late bloomer too, and leave it there","then":"They smile a little, but their real question hangs in the air."},{"text":"Say 'Don't worry about silly things like that'","then":"They nod and go quiet, but the worry is still there."},{"text":"Reassure them every body changes at its own pace","then":"They listen, then ask, 'But when will mine start?'","best":true},{"text":"Say they'll catch up if they eat more","then":"They start taking second helpings, still worried."}],"why":"Taking the worry seriously and reassuring them keeps them confiding in you."},{"prompt":"A few days later, a cousin teases them for being 'still a baby'. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Laugh it off. Cousins always tease each other","then":"Your child's face falls, and they leave the room."},{"text":"Tell your child to toughen up and just ignore the cousin","then":"They nod, and keep the hurt to themselves."},{"text":"Scold the cousin loudly in front of everyone there","then":"The cousin sulks. Your child squirms at all the attention."},{"text":"Tell the cousin it's unkind, then check on your child","then":"The cousin mutters sorry. Later, your child admits it hurt.","best":true}],"why":"Standing up for them kindly, then checking in, shows the worry matters."},{"prompt":"Your child asks whether they should see a doctor for being 'behind'. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Book an urgent appointment for them right away","then":"Their worry grows. 'So something is wrong with me?'"},{"text":"Say they're definitely normal, so there's no need at all","then":"They feel a bit better, but wonder how you can be so sure."},{"text":"Explain the usual range, and offer a check-up if wanted","then":"They think. 'Maybe just ask at my next check-up?' they say.","best":true},{"text":"Say doctors are only for when you're properly ill","then":"They nod, but the worry keeps nagging."}],"why":"Honest reassurance, with a doctor as an easy option, respects their worry without feeding it."}],"debrief":"Reassure a child that bodies change at different paces; taking the worry seriously keeps them confiding.","relearn":"Bodies change at different paces; take the worry seriously and reassure instead of dismissing it."},
  {"id":"tk-1195","cat":"middle-years","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"wet dream worry","hook":"Your son asks shyly what the boys mean by 'wet dreams', clearly worried about himself.","steps":[{"prompt":"He won't meet your eyes, and his voice is very quiet. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Calmly explain it's a normal part of growing up","then":"He finally looks up. 'So nothing's wrong with me?' he asks.","best":true},{"text":"Laugh and say he's becoming a man now","then":"He goes red and wishes he hadn't asked."},{"text":"Tell him that's not something to discuss with you","then":"He nods quickly and leaves. Later you hear him on the phone to a friend."},{"text":"Say it's normal, then quickly change the subject","then":"He nods, but the questions he had are still stuck."}],"why":"A calm, matter-of-fact answer lifts the worry and ends needless shame."},{"prompt":"Later, he asks, embarrassed, what he should do about the bedsheets. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say 'Just leave them. I'll sort it out.'","then":"He's relieved, but still feels it's something to hide."},{"text":"Say you'll handle it, and tell the whole family to ignore it","then":"He looks mortified at the thought of the family knowing."},{"text":"Tell him to hide them so nobody finds out","then":"He nods, and now it feels like a shameful secret."},{"text":"Show him where fresh sheets are, and say it's no big deal","then":"He relaxes. 'Okay. That's easy,' he says.","best":true}],"why":"Simple practical steps, said calmly, show there's nothing to be ashamed of."},{"prompt":"A week later, he asks whether girls have anything like this. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Explain that girls' bodies change too, with periods","then":"He nods slowly. 'So everyone has stuff going on,' he says.","best":true},{"text":"Say he's asking too many questions now","then":"He goes quiet and doesn't ask the next thing."},{"text":"Say he'll learn about girls when he's older","then":"He nods, but the playground gets there first."},{"text":"Say that's girls' business, and none of his concern","then":"He shrugs. The jokes at school fill in the gap."}],"why":"Learning about everyone's puberty builds empathy and ends shame for all."}],"debrief":"Explain wet dreams calmly as a normal part of growing up so a child knows nothing is wrong.","relearn":"Wet dreams are normal; a calm, matter-of-fact answer prevents needless shame."},
  {"id":"tk-1196","cat":"middle-years","type":"branch","persona":"Priya","source":"back the talks","hook":"Your aunt says you're 'spoiling' your pre-teen daughter by explaining puberty so openly.","steps":[{"prompt":"She says it at a family lunch, in front of your daughter. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Smile and change the subject to keep the peace","then":"Lunch moves on. Your daughter wonders if the talks were wrong."},{"text":"Calmly say preparing her keeps her safe and unafraid","then":"Your aunt sniffs, but your daughter gives you a small smile.","best":true},{"text":"Apologise and promise to stop the 'early' talks","then":"Your aunt nods, satisfied. Your daughter stares at her plate."},{"text":"Tell your aunt sharply to mind her own business, for once","then":"The table goes silent, and your daughter looks mortified."}],"why":"A calm, short stand keeps the talks going and shows your daughter you're behind her."},{"prompt":"On the way home, your daughter asks if knowing about periods makes her a bad girl. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say it's normal and smart to know about your own body","then":"She nods slowly. 'Okay. Aunty's just old-fashioned,' she says.","best":true},{"text":"Say 'Maybe we should keep it quieter from now on'","then":"She nods, and decides these are things to hide."},{"text":"Say Aunty is being silly and she shouldn't listen to her","then":"She giggles, but now she's learned to mock her aunt."},{"text":"Say 'Of course not', and leave it there","then":"She seems okay, but doesn't quite know why it's fine."}],"why":"Telling her why knowing her body is good undoes the shame."},{"prompt":"A week later, your mother phones to say the family is talking about your 'modern' ideas. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Carry on, but keep the talks a secret from the whole family","then":"The talks continue, and your daughter learns they're something to hide."},{"text":"Promise to stop the talks so the gossip dies down","then":"The gossip fades. So do your talks with your daughter."},{"text":"Refuse to discuss it at all, and hang up on her","then":"Your mother is hurt, and the family talk grows louder."},{"text":"Explain why you're preparing her, and hold your ground","then":"Your mother goes quiet. 'I just didn't want her embarrassed,' she admits.","best":true}],"why":"Explaining calmly can turn an elder's worry into support, without dropping the talks."},{"prompt":"Months later, your daughter calls from her cousin's house: her first period has started. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"'Oh no, not at your cousin's house, of all places!'","then":"Her voice wobbles. 'Is something wrong?'"},{"text":"'Thanks for telling me. It's normal. What do you need?'","then":"'Just a pad. Didi's got one,' she says, sounding steady.","best":true},{"text":"'Okay. We'll talk about it properly when you're home.'","then":"She manages, but feels alone with it all afternoon."},{"text":"'Don't tell anyone there. Come home right now.'","then":"She hangs up, flustered, and slips out without a word."}],"why":"A calm, warm reply turns a first period into something she can handle."}],"debrief":"Stand by age-right preparation calmly; it keeps a child safer, even if a relative disapproves.","relearn":"Preparing a child for puberty keeps them safer; hold the line if relatives disapprove."},
  {"id":"tk-1197","cat":"middle-years","type":"match","hook":"Match each pre-teen topic to a calm, normalising way to open it.","pairs":[{"left":"Periods","right":"\"A normal, healthy sign of growing up.\""},{"left":"Wet dreams","right":"\"This happens to bodies; nothing's wrong.\""},{"left":"Body odour","right":"\"Time to add a wash routine, that's all.\""},{"left":"Mood swings","right":"\"Big feelings come with these changes too.\""},{"left":"Growth spurts","right":"\"Everyone grows at their own pace.\""}],"relearn":"Periods, wet dreams, odour, moods and growth each have a calm, normalising line to open the conversation.","persona":"any","source":"normalising openers"},
  {"id":"tk-1198","cat":"middle-years","type":"match","hook":"Match each first-phone worry to the simple safety habit that answers it.","pairs":[{"left":"Strangers messaging","right":"Tell me about anyone who makes you uneasy"},{"left":"Oversharing details","right":"Keep your name, school and address private"},{"left":"Scary content","right":"Show me anything that frightens you"},{"left":"Account safety","right":"Use a private setting and a strong password"},{"left":"Endless scrolling","right":"Agree screen-time limits together"}],"relearn":"Each online worry has a simple habit: tell me, keep details private, show me scary things, lock accounts, agree limits.","persona":"Vikram","source":"worry to habit"},
  {"id":"tk-1199","cat":"middle-years","type":"match","hook":"Match each pre-teen question to a calm, honest opener you could use.","pairs":[{"left":"\"What's a period?\"","right":"\"It's a normal monthly cycle; let me explain.\""},{"left":"\"Why is my body changing?\"","right":"\"That's puberty, it happens to everyone.\""},{"left":"\"Where do babies come from?\"","right":"\"A simple, true answer at your level.\""},{"left":"\"What's that word online?\"","right":"\"Good you asked; here's what it really means.\""},{"left":"\"Am I normal?\"","right":"\"Yes, bodies change at their own pace.\""}],"relearn":"Each frank pre-teen question has a calm, honest opener that keeps you the trusted source.","persona":"any","source":"question to opener"},
  {"id":"tk-1200","cat":"middle-years","type":"match","hook":"Match each puberty change to the practical kit or routine that helps with it.","pairs":[{"left":"First period","right":"Pads kept somewhere she can reach"},{"left":"Body odour","right":"A daily wash-and-deodorant routine"},{"left":"Oily skin","right":"A gentle face-wash habit"},{"left":"Cramps","right":"A warm compress and rest"},{"left":"Faster growth","right":"Bigger clothes and good sleep"}],"relearn":"Each puberty change pairs with a simple, practical routine, so the changes feel manageable, not alarming.","persona":"Divya","source":"change to routine"},
  {"id":"tk-1201","cat":"middle-years","type":"match","hook":"Match each pre-teen reaction with the parent line that keeps the door open.","pairs":[{"left":"Embarrassed to ask","right":"\"No question is silly, ask me anything.\""},{"left":"Asked something you don't know","right":"\"Let's find out together.\""},{"left":"Showed you scary content","right":"\"Thank you for telling me.\""},{"left":"Worried they're 'late'","right":"\"Everyone changes at their own pace.\""},{"left":"Caught off-guard mid-chore","right":"\"Great question, let's talk after dinner.\""}],"relearn":"Each pre-teen reaction has a parent line, welcoming, honest, grateful, reassuring, that keeps the door open.","persona":"any","source":"reaction to line"},
  {"id":"tk-1202","cat":"middle-years","type":"match","hook":"Match each online red flag your pre-teen might meet to the safe move.","pairs":[{"left":"A stranger asks to meet up","right":"Say no and tell a parent"},{"left":"Someone asks for a photo","right":"Don't send it; show me"},{"left":"A message feels threatening","right":"Block, report and tell me"},{"left":"An app wants your location","right":"Keep it off unless we agree"},{"left":"A friend dares a risky post","right":"Pause and check with me first"}],"relearn":"Each online red flag has a safe move: refuse, don't send, block and report, keep location off, check first.","persona":"Vikram","source":"red flag to safe move"},
  {"id":"tk-1203","cat":"middle-years","type":"match","hook":"Match each pre-teen myth to the calm truth that replaces it.","pairs":[{"left":"\"Only girls learn about periods\"","right":"Every child learns; it builds empathy"},{"left":"\"Wait until puberty starts\"","right":"Prepare before, so it's no shock"},{"left":"\"A device needs no talk\"","right":"Pair a first phone with safety chats"},{"left":"\"Reporting scary content is punished\"","right":"Telling me is always thanked"},{"left":"\"Asking about bodies is shameful\"","right":"No body question is silly"}],"relearn":"Each pre-teen myth has a calm truth: everyone learns, prepare early, talk, thank reporting, no shame.","persona":"any","source":"myth to truth"},
  {"id":"tk-1204","cat":"middle-years","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: a child warned about periods before her first one feels ready, not terrified. What's your take?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Worth doing early","Ready, not scared","Yes, prepare her"],"affirm":"Preparing a child before periods start swaps fear and shame for readiness and confidence.","relearn":"A child prepared for periods before they start feels ready, not terrified.","persona":"Divya","source":"ready not scared"},
  {"id":"tk-1205","cat":"middle-years","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: when every child learns about everyone's puberty, the teasing fades. Agree?","prompt":"What's your view?","options":["Agree","Ends the teasing","Everyone should learn"],"affirm":"All children learning about everyone's puberty builds empathy and ends the shame and teasing.","relearn":"All children learn about everyone's puberty; it builds empathy and ends teasing.","persona":"Vikram","source":"empathy ends teasing"},
  {"id":"tk-1206","cat":"middle-years","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: a first phone is easier when it comes with a few simple safety chats. Sound right?","prompt":"What do you reckon?","options":["Sounds right","Phone plus a talk","Yes, talk it through"],"affirm":"Pairing a first device with simple safety talks gives a child a net instead of leaving them alone online.","relearn":"Pair a first device with simple online-safety talks, not a silent handover.","persona":"Vikram","source":"phone plus talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1207","cat":"middle-years","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: thanking a child for reporting something scary makes them likelier to tell you again. True for you?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["True","Thanks keeps them telling","Yes, stay calm"],"affirm":"Thanking a child for reporting scary content, and staying calm, keeps them coming to you next time.","relearn":"Thank a child for reporting scary content; calm keeps them telling you.","persona":"any","source":"thanks keeps telling"},
  {"id":"tk-1208","cat":"middle-years","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: \"I don't know, let's find out together\" is a perfectly good answer to a pre-teen. Agree?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Agree","Honest beats perfect","Yes, find out together"],"affirm":"Admitting you don't know and finding out together models honesty and keeps the conversation open.","relearn":"\"Let's find out together\" is a good answer; willingness beats perfect expertise.","persona":"any","source":"honest beats perfect"},
  {"id":"tk-1209","cat":"middle-years","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: the years just before puberty are the golden window to prepare a child. Worth using?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Worth using","Catch the window","Yes, start now"],"affirm":"The pre-puberty years are the ideal window to prepare a child so the changes feel manageable.","relearn":"The years just before puberty are the golden window; prepared kids cope far better.","persona":"any","source":"catch the window"},
  {"id":"tk-1210","cat":"middle-years","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: a frank pre-teen question answered calmly makes the next, harder one easier to ask. Ring true?","prompt":"What's your view?","options":["Rings true","Each answer opens the next","Yes, stay calm"],"affirm":"Every calmly answered question makes the next, harder one easier to ask, and keeps you the source.","relearn":"A calm answer now makes the next, harder question easier to ask.","persona":"any","source":"next question easier"},
  {"id":"tk-1211","cat":"middle-years","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: telling a child their body changes at its own pace eases a lot of quiet pre-teen worry. Agree?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Agree","Own pace reassures","Yes, reassure them"],"affirm":"Reassuring a child that bodies change at their own pace eases worry and keeps them confiding in you.","relearn":"Bodies change at different paces; saying so eases pre-teen worry.","persona":"any","source":"own pace reassures"},
  {"id":"tk-1212","cat":"middle-years","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two lines that would shame a pre-teen for asking about their changing body.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Great question, here's how it works\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"We don't talk about dirty things like that\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"Everyone's body changes; it's healthy\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"You're disgusting for even asking\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"You can ask me anything, anytime\"","trick":false}],"why":"\"Dirty things\" and \"you're disgusting\" shame a child for asking and send them elsewhere; the others keep the door open.","relearn":"Welcoming a body question keeps the door open; shaming it sends a child to peers and the feed.","persona":"any","source":"spot the shame lines"},
  {"id":"tk-1213","cat":"middle-years","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two online habits that put a pre-teen at risk.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Telling you about a creepy message","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Sending a stranger their home address","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Keeping accounts private","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Agreeing to meet an online 'friend' alone","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Asking before downloading an app","trick":false}],"why":"Sharing an address and meeting a stranger alone are the real risks; telling you, staying private and asking first are healthy.","relearn":"Sharing personal info with, or meeting, online strangers are the risks to address.","persona":"Vikram","source":"spot the online risks"},
  {"id":"tk-1214","cat":"middle-years","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two reactions that would teach a child to hide scary online content next time.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Thank you for showing me\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Shouting and snatching the phone away","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"Let's look at it together calmly\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"You're banned from the internet now\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"You did the right thing telling me\"","trick":false}],"why":"Shouting/snatching and a blanket ban punish the telling, so a child hides it next time; thanks and calm keep them reporting.","relearn":"Punishing a child for reporting teaches them to hide it; thank them instead.","persona":"Vikram","source":"spot the silencing reactions"},
  {"id":"tk-1215","cat":"middle-years","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two myths a parent should never pass on about pre-teen puberty.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Prepare before the changes begin","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"Wait until puberty starts to explain it\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Periods and wet dreams are normal","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"Only girls need to know about periods\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"All children learn about everyone's puberty","trick":false}],"why":"\"Wait until it starts\" and \"only girls need to know\" are the myths; preparing early and teaching everyone are the truths.","relearn":"Prepare early and teach every child about everyone's puberty; don't wait or split it by gender.","persona":"any","source":"spot the puberty myths"},
  {"id":"tk-1216","cat":"middle-years","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two replies that would scare a child about a normal body change.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Periods are normal; I'll help you\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"Something must be wrong with you\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"Wet dreams happen; nothing's wrong\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"That's shameful, don't tell anyone\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"Everyone's body grows differently\"","trick":false}],"why":"\"Something's wrong with you\" and \"that's shameful\" frighten and shame; the others name the change as normal and supported.","relearn":"Name body changes as normal and supported; never frame them as wrong or shameful.","persona":"any","source":"spot the scary replies"},
  {"id":"tk-1217","cat":"middle-years","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two first-phone setups that leave a pre-teen exposed.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Agreeing screen-time limits together","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Letting them follow any stranger back","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Setting up block and report buttons","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Posting their daily location publicly","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"A promise to tell you anything scary","trick":false}],"why":"Following strangers and public location expose a child; shared limits, block/report tools and an open promise protect them.","relearn":"Set shared limits, safety tools and an open promise; following strangers and public location expose a child.","persona":"Vikram","source":"spot the exposed setups"},
  {"id":"tk-1218","cat":"middle-years","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two answers that would shut down a pre-teen's frank question.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Good you asked; here's the simple answer\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"You're far too young to ask that\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"I'm not sure, let's find out together\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"Don't be disgusting, never ask again\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"Great question; let's talk after dinner\"","trick":false}],"why":"\"Too young\" and \"don't be disgusting\" shut the door; answering simply, learning together or parking it warmly keep it open.","relearn":"Answer simply, find out together or park it warmly; \"too young\" or shaming shuts the door.","persona":"any","source":"spot the shutdowns"},
  {"id":"tk-1219","cat":"middle-years","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two moves that leave a pre-teen unprepared for the changes ahead.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Honest heads-up before changes begin","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Leaving them to learn from peers and feeds","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"An open door for any worry","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Saying \"you'll find out when it happens\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Pairing a first phone with safety chats","trick":false}],"why":"Leaving them to peers/feeds and \"find out when it happens\" leave a child unprepared; honest prep and an open door ready them.","relearn":"Prepare a pre-teen with honest prep and an open door, not by leaving them to peers and the feed.","persona":"any","source":"spot the unprepared moves"},
  {"id":"tk-1220","cat":"middle-years","type":"role-play","persona":"Divya","source":"open about periods","hook":"You've decided to talk to your daughter about her first period before it arrives.","setup":"You're walking home together from her dance class.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your daughter says: \"You've gone quiet. Is something wrong?\"","options":[{"text":"\"No, nothing. Let's go and get some ice cream.\"","then":"\"Yay!\" she says, and the moment slips by."},{"text":"\"I've bought you a book about growing up. Read it later.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" she says, and starts chatting about her dance steps."},{"text":"\"It's nothing. I'll tell you when you're a bit older.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" she says, a little worried, and walks on quietly."},{"text":"\"Nothing's wrong. I want to tell you about periods.\"","then":"\"Oh,\" she says, surprised, and slows down to listen.","best":true}],"why":"Naming the topic plainly and warmly makes it easy to begin."},{"prompt":"Near home, your daughter asks: \"Meera missed dance for her period. Can't you dance then?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Yes. Better to rest at home on those days.\"","then":"Her face falls. \"I'll miss class every month?\""},{"text":"\"No. You can do everything you usually do.\"","then":"\"So Meera could have come,\" she says, relieved.","best":true},{"text":"\"Some people say so. Ask your dance teacher.\"","then":"\"I don't want to ask him that,\" she says, embarrassed."},{"text":"\"Let's not get into all the details now.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" she says, still unsure."}],"why":"Clearing up myths early stops them turning into fear and missed days."},{"prompt":"Your daughter asks: \"How will I know it's started?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Something will feel really wrong.\"","then":"She stops walking. \"Wrong how? Will it hurt?\""},{"text":"\"Some blood in your underwear. It's normal.\"","then":"\"Blood?\" she says, then nods slowly. \"Okay. If it's normal.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"You'll just know. Don't worry about it.\"","then":"\"But what if I don't?\" she asks."},{"text":"\"Your teacher will explain all that at school.\"","then":"\"When? What if it starts before that?\" she asks."}],"why":"A plain, calm description means the first sign won't frighten her."},{"prompt":"At home, your daughter asks: \"Can I tell my friends we talked about this?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Of course. It's nothing to hide.\"","then":"\"My friends will be so jealous,\" she grins.","best":true},{"text":"\"Only tell the girls, never the boys.\"","then":"\"Why not the boys?\" she asks, puzzled."},{"text":"\"If you like, but their mums might not be happy.\"","then":"\"Oh,\" she says. \"So maybe I shouldn't.\""},{"text":"\"Better not. Keep it between us.\"","then":"She nods. \"So periods are a secret thing.\""}],"why":"Treating periods as normal to talk about ends shame for her and her friends."}],"relearn":"A warm, matter-of-fact heads-up makes a first period feel expected and supported, not frightening."},
  {"id":"tk-1221","cat":"middle-years","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"answer about wet dreams","hook":"Your son has heard the words 'wet dreams' at school and wants to know what they mean.","setup":"He brings it up while you're washing up after dinner.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your son asks: \"What's a wet dream? The boys keep joking about it.\"","options":[{"text":"\"That's not something we talk about in this house, beta.\"","then":"He goes red, then mumbles: \"But I need to know.\""},{"text":"\"During sleep, the body can release fluid. It's normal.\"","then":"\"Oh,\" he says. \"So it's not like wetting the bed?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"It's a growing-up thing. You'll understand later.\"","then":"\"Later when?\" he asks, frowning."},{"text":"\"Ignore those boys. They're being really disgusting.\"","then":"\"But what does it mean?\" he asks again."}],"why":"A calm, matter-of-fact answer tells him it's normal before the jokes teach him shame."},{"prompt":"Your son asks: \"If it happens to me, does it mean something's wrong?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Not at all. It's a normal part of growing up.\"","then":"His shoulders drop a little. \"Okay. Good.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"No, but it's private, so don't mention it again.\"","then":"He nods. \"Got it. Private and secret.\""},{"text":"\"Let's not go into all that right now.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" he says, still frowning."},{"text":"\"Only if it happens a lot, I think.\"","then":"\"How much is a lot?\" he asks, worried."}],"why":"Saying clearly that nothing is wrong lifts a worry he may not say out loud."},{"prompt":"Your son asks: \"Why do the boys laugh about it, then?\"","options":[{"text":"\"People often joke about things they feel shy about.\"","then":"He thinks about that. \"Yeah. That makes sense.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Just laugh along, so they leave you alone.\"","then":"\"Even if I don't get the joke?\" he asks."},{"text":"\"Boys are just silly like that at your age.\"","then":"He laughs. \"Yeah, but why, though?\""},{"text":"\"Because it's embarrassing, and it should stay that way.\"","then":"He looks down. \"So I shouldn't talk about it.\""}],"why":"Explaining the jokes helps him see shame for what it is, and keep talking to you."}],"relearn":"Wet dreams are normal; a calm, matter-of-fact answer prevents needless shame."},
  {"id":"tk-1222","cat":"middle-years","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"first-phone deal","hook":"You're handing your child their first phone, and you want to start the online-safety habit.","setup":"They're practically bouncing with excitement.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"Is it really mine now? Can I download anything?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Only apps I approve. That's the one rule.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, and wait for your list."},{"text":"\"Yours, with one deal: tell me if anything feels off.\"","then":"\"Deal,\" they say. \"What counts as off?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Here's the phone. Just don't get into any trouble.\"","then":"\"What kind of trouble?\" they ask, already opening the app store."},{"text":"\"Anything you like. It's your phone now.\"","then":"\"Yes!\" they say, and start downloading games."}],"why":"A simple deal as you hand it over starts the telling habit from day one."},{"prompt":"Later, your child asks: \"Do you need to know what I do on it?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Yes. I'm your parent. That's why.\"","then":"They roll their eyes. \"Fine,\" they say, back to the screen."},{"text":"\"Only so I can help if something goes wrong online.\"","then":"They think. \"Like if someone's mean to me?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Not really. Just use it sensibly.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they shrug, and that's the end of it."},{"text":"\"Yes, because I don't trust you with it just yet.\"","then":"Their face falls. \"Then why give it to me?\""}],"why":"Framing it as help, not control, keeps them coming to you."},{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"Can I put my school and address on my profile?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Keep those private. Strangers could see them.\"","then":"\"Oh. Just my first name, then,\" they say.","best":true},{"text":"\"Your school is fine, but not the address.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, and type in their school's name."},{"text":"\"Why would you even ask that? Give me the phone.\"","then":"\"Never mind!\" they say, clutching it."},{"text":"\"Sure. Everyone puts that stuff up.\"","then":"\"Cool,\" they say, filling in every box."}],"why":"Explaining why details stay private builds a habit they'll keep online."},{"prompt":"A week later, your child says: \"Someone I don't know sent me a weird message.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Block them, and don't mention it again.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, and delete the whole chat."},{"text":"\"See? This is exactly why you shouldn't have a phone yet.\"","then":"They pull the phone back. \"Forget it.\""},{"text":"\"Thanks for telling me. Let's look at it together.\"","then":"They hand you the phone, relieved. \"I didn't reply.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Just ignore it. It's probably nothing.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, but keep glancing at the screen."}],"why":"Thanking them for telling you makes them more likely to tell you next time."}],"relearn":"Pair a first device with simple online-safety talks, not a silent handover."},
  {"id":"tk-1223","cat":"middle-years","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"thank for showing","hook":"Your child comes to you, shaken by a frightening video they found online.","setup":"They hold the screen out so you can see.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child says: \"I didn't mean to watch it. It just played.\"","options":[{"text":"\"It's fine. Just delete it and forget about it.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, but they don't look fine."},{"text":"\"Thank you for showing me. You did the right thing.\"","then":"Their lip wobbles. \"It was really scary.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Why were you even watching that? Give me the phone.\"","then":"They hand it over, eyes filling. \"I said I didn't mean to.\""},{"text":"\"Ugh, turn it off. Don't show me that stuff.\"","then":"They switch it off. \"Sorry,\" they whisper."}],"why":"Thanking them first makes telling you feel safe, not risky."},{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"Am I in trouble?\"","options":[{"text":"\"That depends on what else you've been watching.\"","then":"They freeze. \"Nothing! I promise.\""},{"text":"\"No. You're not in trouble for telling me.\"","then":"They let out a long breath. \"Okay.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"No. But no phone for you tonight, okay?\"","then":"\"But you said I'm not in trouble,\" they say, confused."},{"text":"\"Not this time. But be more careful.\"","then":"\"I'll try,\" they say, now worried about next time."}],"why":"Saying clearly there's no trouble for telling keeps them telling you."},{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"Why do people make videos like that?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Some do it for clicks. Let's report it together.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, and press the report button with you.","best":true},{"text":"\"Because the internet is full of bad people.\"","then":"They look alarmed. \"Is it safe to go online at all?\""},{"text":"\"Who knows. Try not to think about it.\"","then":"\"I can't stop thinking about it,\" they whisper."},{"text":"\"To scare kids. Now let's watch something funny.\"","then":"They giggle. \"This one's better,\" they say, and the question fades."}],"why":"A calm, honest reason plus reporting it gives them something to do with the fear."},{"prompt":"At bedtime, your child whispers: \"Can I tell you if it happens again?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Yes, but try not to let it happen again.\"","then":"\"How do I stop it?\" they ask, worried."},{"text":"\"Always. Every single time.\"","then":"They smile sleepily. \"Okay. Night.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"It won't happen again. I'll make sure of that.\"","then":"\"Promise?\" they ask, holding you to it."},{"text":"\"Only if it's something really scary.\"","then":"\"How scary is really scary?\" they ask."}],"why":"An 'always' makes you the first place they bring anything upsetting."}],"relearn":"Thank a child for reporting scary content and talk it through; anger teaches them to hide it."},
  {"id":"tk-1224","cat":"middle-years","type":"role-play","persona":"Divya","source":"normalise the changes","hook":"Your pre-teen has started changing behind a locked bathroom door and seems embarrassed about their body.","setup":"At bedtime, they finally bring it up.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child says quietly: \"I hate how my body's changing.\"","options":[{"text":"\"You're being far too sensitive about all this.\"","then":"They turn to the wall, then mumble: \"I even sweat all the time now.\""},{"text":"\"What's happening is normal and healthy. Tell me more?\"","then":"They hesitate. \"Everything feels different. And I get sweaty.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"It's just hormones. It'll all pass soon enough.\"","then":"\"Soon when?\" they ask, not comforted."},{"text":"\"Don't say that, beta. You're beautiful just as you are.\"","then":"\"You have to say that,\" they mumble."}],"why":"Calling the changes normal, and asking for more, opens the talk they need."},{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"Why do I sweat so much now? It's embarrassing.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Everyone smells a bit at your age. Ha!\"","then":"They go red. \"See? Even you think so.\""},{"text":"\"Don't worry. Honestly, nobody else even notices.\"","then":"\"They do notice,\" they say quietly."},{"text":"\"Maybe just stop running around so much.\"","then":"\"So it's my fault?\" they ask."},{"text":"\"Growing bodies sweat more. A wash and deo help.\"","then":"\"Can I choose my own deo?\" they ask, brightening.","best":true}],"why":"A plain reason plus a simple fix turns embarrassment into something they can handle."},{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"Do my friends feel like this too?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Don't go discussing your body with friends.\"","then":"They nod. \"So I should keep it to myself.\""},{"text":"\"Lots of them, I bet. Most people just don't say.\"","then":"They smile a little. \"Maybe I'll ask my best friend.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Probably not. You're just more sensitive.\"","then":"\"Great,\" they say. \"So it's just me.\""},{"text":"\"It doesn't matter what they feel. You're fine.\"","then":"\"It matters to me,\" they say."}],"why":"Knowing others feel it too makes the changes less lonely."}],"relearn":"Warmly normalising the changes and inviting questions replaces embarrassment with reassurance."},
  {"id":"tk-1225","cat":"middle-years","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"find out together","hook":"Your pre-teen asks how the contraceptive pill actually works. You realise you don't really know.","setup":"They're perched on the kitchen counter, swinging their legs.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child adds: \"A girl in class said it's dangerous. Is it?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Yes, very dangerous. Never, ever touch it.\"","then":"They look alarmed. \"Even when I'm grown up?\""},{"text":"\"I'm not sure. Let's find out together.\"","then":"\"You don't know?\" they grin. \"Okay, deal.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Stop asking me things like that.\"","then":"They slide off the counter. \"Fine. I'll ask someone else.\""},{"text":"\"Your friend's probably wrong. Don't worry about it.\"","then":"\"But how do you know?\" they ask."}],"why":"Admitting you're not sure and finding out together is honest, and keeps you their go-to."},{"prompt":"A bit later, your child asks: \"How do you tell if a website is telling the truth?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Just ask me instead of looking things up online.\"","then":"\"But what if you don't know either?\" they ask."},{"text":"\"If lots of people share it, it's probably true.\"","then":"\"Cool,\" they say. \"The most-shared one, then.\""},{"text":"\"See who made it. Hospitals and doctors are safest.\"","then":"\"So not random videos?\" they ask. \"Got it.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"You can't, really. Just don't look things up.\"","then":"\"Then how do I find anything out?\" they ask."}],"why":"Teaching them to check the source protects them long after this one question."},{"prompt":"A week later, your child says: \"My friend's mum never talks about this stuff.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Tell your friend to look it up herself, then.\"","then":"\"She doesn't know where to look,\" they say."},{"text":"\"Maybe we talk about it too much, then.\"","then":"\"Oh,\" they say. \"Should we stop?\""},{"text":"\"I'm glad we can. You can bring me anything.\"","then":"\"Anything?\" they say. \"Okay. I've got another one.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Well, her mum is very old-fashioned.\"","then":"\"I'll tell her you said that,\" they grin."}],"why":"Reminding them your door is open makes the next question easier to ask."}],"relearn":"\"Let's find out together\" is a good, honest answer; willingness beats perfect expertise."},
  {"id":"tk-1226","cat":"middle-years","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"own pace reassurance","hook":"After swimming class, your child seems upset about developing later than their friends.","setup":"In the car home, they stare out of the window.","steps":[{"prompt":"Your child says: \"Everyone else looks older. What's wrong with me?\"","options":[{"text":"\"You'll catch up by next year. I'm sure of it.\"","then":"\"And if I don't?\" they ask."},{"text":"\"Nothing. Every body changes at its own pace.\"","then":"\"Really?\" they ask, turning to you. \"Even mine?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Don't worry about silly things like that.\"","then":"\"It's not silly,\" they mutter, and turn back to the window."},{"text":"\"Ha! Enjoy being young while you still can.\"","then":"They don't laugh. \"You don't get it.\""}],"why":"Saying nothing is wrong, and that bodies keep their own time, eases the worry."},{"prompt":"Your child asks: \"How long until I catch up, then?\"","options":[{"text":"\"There's no set time. We can ask the doctor if you're worried.\"","then":"They nod slowly. \"Okay. I'll wait and see first.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Any day now, I promise you.\"","then":"\"You can't know that,\" they say."},{"text":"\"Eat more, and maybe you'll grow faster.\"","then":"\"So it's my fault for not eating?\" they ask."},{"text":"\"That sounds worrying. We'd better see a doctor tomorrow.\"","then":"\"Worrying? Is something wrong with me?\" they ask, alarmed."}],"why":"Saying there's no set time, with a doctor there if needed, eases the worry without alarm."},{"prompt":"As you pull up at home, your child asks: \"Can I talk to you if it still bothers me?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Sure, but try not to think about it so much.\"","then":"\"I'll try,\" they say, sounding unsure."},{"text":"\"You shouldn't let it bother you.\"","then":"They nod. \"Okay. I'll keep it to myself.\""},{"text":"\"Only if it's really bothering you.\"","then":"\"How much is 'really'?\" they ask."},{"text":"\"Anytime. I'm always glad when you tell me.\"","then":"\"Okay,\" they say, and give you a quick hug.","best":true}],"why":"An open invitation keeps them bringing their worries to you."}],"relearn":"Bodies change at different paces; reassuring a child eases worry and keeps them confiding."},
  {"id":"tk-1227","cat":"middle-years","type":"role-play","persona":"Priya","source":"back the approach","hook":"You've started telling your daughter Anaya, 8, about periods. Kusum Mausi overhears.","setup":"She pulls you aside in the kitchen.","steps":[{"prompt":"Kusum Mausi hisses: \"At eight? You'll scare her and put ideas in her head.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Sorry, Mausi. You're right. I'll wait until she's older.\"","then":"She nods, satisfied. \"Good. These things come in their own time.\""},{"text":"\"Knowing ahead is exactly what stops her being scared.\"","then":"Mausi pauses. \"Scared? Hm. I hadn't thought of it like that.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"This is my child, Mausi. Please don't interfere in this.\"","then":"Her face tightens. \"I was only trying to help.\" She leaves the kitchen."},{"text":"\"It was just a little chat. She won't even remember it.\"","then":"\"Then why tell her at all?\" she asks, and waits."}],"why":"Explaining why you prepare early backs your approach calmly and keeps Anaya's talks going."},{"prompt":"At dinner, Kusum Mausi tells the table: \"In our day nobody told girls anything. We managed.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Mausi, let's not get into this at the dinner table, please.\"","then":"She shrugs. \"As you like. I've said what I think.\" The topic hangs there."},{"text":"\"Times have changed, Mausi. You really wouldn't understand this.\"","then":"\"Oh, so I'm old-fashioned now?\" she says, and the table goes quiet."},{"text":"\"Plenty of girls were terrified by surprise. I want her ready.\"","then":"Mausi pauses. \"Well. I did cry the first time. Nobody explained a thing.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Maybe you're right. Her school can cover it when the time comes.\"","then":"She smiles. \"Good. Let the teachers handle such things.\""}],"why":"Naming what silence cost many girls turns a lecture into common ground."},{"prompt":"Next morning, Kusum Mausi asks: \"What exactly are you telling a child that age?\"","options":[{"text":"\"The basics of periods, and that she can always come to me.\"","then":"Mausi nods slowly. \"That's all? I thought you meant something else.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Only what her school would say anyway. Nothing more.\"","then":"\"Then why do it at home at all?\" she asks, unconvinced."},{"text":"\"That's really between Anaya and me, Mausi. Let's leave it.\"","then":"She purses her lips. \"Fine. Don't come to me when she has questions.\""},{"text":"\"Oh, just general things. Nothing for you to worry about.\"","then":"Mausi narrows her eyes. \"General things? That tells me nothing.\""}],"why":"A simple, honest answer shows the talks are age-right, not shocking."},{"prompt":"As she leaves, Kusum Mausi adds: \"At least keep the boys' side of it out. That's too much.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Fine. I'll only tell her what happens to girls.\"","then":"\"Good,\" she says, and pats your arm on the way out."},{"text":"\"Mausi, I really don't want to discuss this any more today.\"","then":"She sighs. \"As you wish.\" The door closes a little harder than usual."},{"text":"\"I'll think about it and see what her teacher says.\"","then":"\"Yes, ask the teacher,\" she says, pleased to have had a say."},{"text":"\"She'll learn about everyone's changes. It stops the teasing.\"","then":"\"Everyone's?\" She thinks. \"Hm. My sons did tease their sister terribly.\"","best":true}],"why":"When every child learns about everyone's puberty, shame and teasing lose their grip."}],"relearn":"Preparing a child for puberty keeps them safer; hold the line calmly if relatives disapprove."},
  {"id":"tk-1260","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Vikram","source":"ban controls porn","hook":"\"If I just block porn on the wifi, my teen will never see it and we don't need to talk.\"","myth":{"un":"\"If I just block porn on the wifi, my teen will never see it and we don't need to talk.\"","re":"Filters help, but teens find content on friends' phones; only your honest porn-literacy talk truly prepares them.","why":"A block is a wall a curious teen walks around; understanding is what stays with them."},"relearn":"Filters help, but teens find content on friends' phones; only your honest porn-literacy talk truly prepares them."},
  {"id":"tk-1261","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Vikram","source":"manosphere antidote","hook":"\"Those 'alpha male' influencers my son watches are just harmless entertainment.\"","myth":{"un":"\"Those 'alpha male' influencers my son watches are just harmless entertainment.\"","re":"Much of that content quietly teaches contempt for girls and consent; your calm, honest voice is the antidote.","why":"If you stay silent, those voices become his only teachers about respect."},"relearn":"Much of that content quietly teaches contempt for girls and consent; your calm, honest voice is the antidote."},
  {"id":"tk-1262","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"any","source":"consent not romance-killer","hook":"\"Teaching consent will make relationships awkward and unromantic for my teen.\"","myth":{"un":"\"Teaching consent will make relationships awkward and unromantic for my teen.\"","re":"Checking that both people freely want it makes closeness safer and kinder, not less romantic.","why":"Respect is what makes intimacy feel safe, never what spoils it."},"relearn":"Checking that both people freely want it makes closeness safer and kinder, not less romantic."},
  {"id":"tk-1263","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Vikram","source":"not too late at sixteen","hook":"\"My kid's already sixteen and dating, so it's far too late for me to start these talks.\"","myth":{"un":"\"My kid's already sixteen and dating, so it's far too late for me to start these talks.\"","re":"It's never too late; an open, non-judgemental parent still matters most to a teen, even one already dating.","why":"The door you open at sixteen still leads somewhere they'll walk through."},"relearn":"It's never too late; an open, non-judgemental parent still matters most to a teen, even one already dating."},
  {"id":"tk-1264","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"any","source":"girls and boys both","hook":"\"Consent and respect talks are really only for parents of sons, not daughters.\"","myth":{"un":"\"Consent and respect talks are really only for parents of sons, not daughters.\"","re":"Every teen needs both: to give respect and to expect it; consent and boundaries protect daughters and sons alike.","why":"A daughter who knows her 'no' counts is as protected as a son who honours it."},"relearn":"Every teen needs both: to give respect and to expect it; consent and boundaries protect daughters and sons alike."},
  {"id":"tk-1265","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Vikram","source":"heartbreak worth talking","hook":"\"A teen breakup is just drama; there's nothing for me to actually talk about there.\"","myth":{"un":"\"A teen breakup is just drama; there's nothing for me to actually talk about there.\"","re":"How they treat an ex, and recover from heartbreak, is real relationship learning your steady support shapes.","why":"How a teen handles a breakup is rehearsal for every relationship after."},"relearn":"How they treat an ex, and recover from heartbreak, is real relationship learning your steady support shapes."},
  {"id":"tk-1266","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"any","source":"sexting shame backfires","hook":"\"If my teen ever sends a risky photo, shaming them hard is what keeps them safe.\"","myth":{"un":"\"If my teen ever sends a risky photo, shaming them hard is what keeps them safe.\"","re":"Shame makes a teen hide the next mistake; staying a calm, problem-solving parent is what actually keeps them safe.","why":"A teen who fears your reaction stops telling you when they're in real trouble."},"relearn":"Shame makes a teen hide the next mistake; staying a calm, problem-solving parent is what actually keeps them safe."},
  {"id":"tk-1267","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Vikram","source":"privacy isn't secrecy","hook":"\"Reading my teen's chats in secret is just good parenting; I have a right to everything.\"","myth":{"un":"\"Reading my teen's chats in secret is just good parenting; I have a right to everything.\"","re":"Some privacy is healthy at this age; secret snooping, once found, costs the trust that keeps them talking to you.","why":"Trust is the thing that brings them to you; snooping spends it for nothing."},"relearn":"Some privacy is healthy at this age; secret snooping, once found, costs the trust that keeps them talking to you."},
  {"id":"tk-1268","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Vikram","source":"fun dad steps up","hook":"\"I'm the fun parent; the serious relationship and consent talks are my partner's job.\"","myth":{"un":"\"I'm the fun parent; the serious relationship and consent talks are my partner's job.\"","re":"A teen needs both parents askable; your fun, easy bond is exactly what makes a hard talk land lighter.","why":"Being the easy parent is a reason to do the talk, not to skip it."},"relearn":"A teen needs both parents askable; your fun, easy bond is exactly what makes a hard talk land lighter."},
  {"id":"tk-1269","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"any","source":"one talk myth teen","hook":"\"I gave my teen one big sex talk years ago, so my job there is done.\"","myth":{"un":"\"I gave my teen one big sex talk years ago, so my job there is done.\"","re":"It's many small, evolving chats as they grow; consent and online life keep changing and need you to keep talking.","why":"Teens face new questions every year; one old talk can't answer them all."},"relearn":"It's many small, evolving chats as they grow; consent and online life keep changing and need you to keep talking."},
  {"id":"tk-1270","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"strike-rewrite","persona":"Priya","source":"queer teen still talks","hook":"\"My teen came out as gay, so the usual consent and relationship talks don't really apply to them.\"","myth":{"un":"\"My teen came out as gay, so the usual consent and relationship talks don't really apply to them.\"","re":"Consent, respect and online safety matter for every teen; an affirmed, openly-guided child is a safer one.","why":"Every teen deserves the same words about respect, whoever they love."},"relearn":"Consent, respect and online safety matter for every teen; an affirmed, openly-guided child is a safer one."},
  {"id":"tk-1271","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"sort","persona":"any","source":"green or red flag","hook":"Sort each dating sign your teen describes: green flag or red flag?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Asks before posting a photo of you"},{"id":"b","text":"Checks your phone and demands passwords"},{"id":"c","text":"Respects it when you say not yet"},{"id":"d","text":"Sulks until you give in"},{"id":"e","text":"Likes your other friendships"},{"id":"f","text":"Says jealousy means real love"}],"bins":[{"id":"green","label":"Green flag","valence":"pos"},{"id":"red","label":"Red flag","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"green","b":"red","c":"green","d":"red","e":"green","f":"red"},"relearn":"Asking, respecting a no and liking your friendships are green flags; controlling phones, sulking and jealousy are red."},
  {"id":"tk-1272","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"sort","persona":"Vikram","source":"real or porn-myth","hook":"Sort what your teen might believe: a real fact about sex, or a porn-fed myth to gently correct?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Both partners' comfort matters"},{"id":"b","text":"Real bodies look like the ones online"},{"id":"c","text":"A clear no means stop, always"},{"id":"d","text":"Pressuring is normal and expected"},{"id":"e","text":"Consent can be withdrawn anytime"},{"id":"f","text":"Roughness without asking is fine"}],"bins":[{"id":"real","label":"Real fact","valence":"pos"},{"id":"myth","label":"Porn-fed myth","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"real","b":"myth","c":"real","d":"myth","e":"real","f":"myth"},"relearn":"Comfort, a respected no and withdrawable consent are real; matching online bodies, pressure and unasked roughness are myths."},
  {"id":"tk-1273","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"sort","persona":"any","source":"keeps door open","hook":"Your teen just told you something hard. Sort each reply: keeps the door open, or slams it?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Thanks for trusting me with this"},{"id":"b","text":"I'm disgusted, don't tell me more"},{"id":"c","text":"Let's figure this out together"},{"id":"d","text":"Wait till your father hears this"},{"id":"e","text":"You're not in trouble for telling me"},{"id":"f","text":"I always knew you'd mess up"}],"bins":[{"id":"open","label":"Keeps the door open","valence":"pos"},{"id":"slam","label":"Slams it shut","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"open","b":"slam","c":"open","d":"slam","e":"open","f":"slam"},"relearn":"Thanks, working it out together and 'not in trouble' keep the door open; disgust, threats and 'I knew it' slam it."},
  {"id":"tk-1274","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"sort","persona":"Vikram","source":"now or wait teen","hook":"Sort each teen topic: have it openly now, or it's genuinely fine to wait?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"What enthusiastic consent means"},{"id":"b","text":"Staying safe with online dating apps"},{"id":"c","text":"Picking their exact wedding date"},{"id":"d","text":"Handling porn they'll likely see"},{"id":"e","text":"Naming every future career choice"},{"id":"f","text":"How to leave a pressuring partner"}],"bins":[{"id":"now","label":"Talk now","valence":"tell"},{"id":"wait","label":"Can wait","valence":"neutral"}],"key":{"a":"now","b":"now","c":"wait","d":"now","e":"wait","f":"now"},"relearn":"Consent, app safety, porn-literacy and leaving pressure are now talks; wedding dates and far-off careers can wait."},
  {"id":"tk-1275","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"sort","persona":"any","source":"respect or control online","hook":"Your teen shows you messages from their partner. Sort each: respectful, or a controlling sign?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Asks how your day went"},{"id":"b","text":"Demands you reply within a minute"},{"id":"c","text":"Says have fun with your friends"},{"id":"d","text":"Guilt-trips you for being offline"},{"id":"e","text":"Sends a kind good-morning note"},{"id":"f","text":"Threatens to leave if you don't share locations"}],"bins":[{"id":"respect","label":"Respectful","valence":"pos"},{"id":"control","label":"Controlling","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"respect","b":"control","c":"respect","d":"control","e":"respect","f":"control"},"relearn":"Caring questions, encouraging friends and kind notes are respectful; demanding instant replies, guilt-trips and location threats are control."},
  {"id":"tk-1276","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"sort","persona":"Vikram","source":"my response teen disclosure","hook":"Your teen admits they sent a risky photo. Sort your possible reactions: helps, or harms?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Stay calm and ask what happened"},{"id":"b","text":"Yell and confiscate everything in rage"},{"id":"c","text":"Help them report it being shared"},{"id":"d","text":"Tell relatives to shame them"},{"id":"e","text":"Reassure them you'll face it together"},{"id":"f","text":"Call them ruined and dirty"}],"bins":[{"id":"helps","label":"Helps","valence":"pos"},{"id":"harms","label":"Harms","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"helps","b":"harms","c":"helps","d":"harms","e":"helps","f":"harms"},"relearn":"Staying calm, helping them report and facing it together help; yelling, shaming to relatives and 'ruined' harm."},
  {"id":"tk-1277","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"sort","persona":"any","source":"facts or feelings teen","hook":"A teen asks why a friend got pregnant. Sort each part of a good reply: honest fact, or your family value?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"How contraception actually works"},{"id":"b","text":"When we believe is the right time"},{"id":"c","text":"What consent and safety mean"},{"id":"d","text":"Our hopes for your future first"},{"id":"e","text":"Where to get reliable health help"},{"id":"f","text":"Why we value commitment"}],"bins":[{"id":"fact","label":"Honest fact","valence":"neutral"},{"id":"value","label":"Family value","valence":"tell"}],"key":{"a":"fact","b":"value","c":"fact","d":"value","e":"fact","f":"value"},"relearn":"Contraception, consent and where to get help are honest facts; the right time, your hopes and commitment are values you share."},
  {"id":"tk-1278","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"sort","persona":"Vikram","source":"listen or lecture teen","hook":"Your teen opens up about a crush. Sort each move: keeps them talking, or shuts them up?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Ask gentle, curious questions"},{"id":"b","text":"Launch into a long warning lecture"},{"id":"c","text":"Take their feelings seriously"},{"id":"d","text":"Tease them in front of cousins"},{"id":"e","text":"Share a short, honest story of your own"},{"id":"f","text":"Forbid all crushes until they're older"}],"bins":[{"id":"talk","label":"Keeps them talking","valence":"pos"},{"id":"shut","label":"Shuts them up","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"talk","b":"shut","c":"talk","d":"shut","e":"talk","f":"shut"},"relearn":"Curious questions, taking feelings seriously and a short honest story keep them talking; lecturing, teasing and forbidding shut them up."},
  {"id":"tk-1279","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"found porn history","hook":"On the family laptop, you find porn in the browser history. Your son Ishaan, 14, used it last.","steps":[{"prompt":"Ishaan walks in, sees the screen and goes red. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Shout at him and take his phone away on the spot","then":"Ishaan's eyes fill. He hands over the phone and says nothing at all."},{"text":"Shut the laptop fast, and act as though nothing happened at all","then":"Ishaan backs out. Neither of you mentions it, but it hangs over dinner."},{"text":"Laugh it off and say every boy his age does it","then":"Ishaan laughs nervously. He learns that you know, and nothing else."},{"text":"Take a breath and say you'll talk about it calmly later","then":"Ishaan nods, mortified, and escapes to his room.","best":true}],"why":"Pausing to calm down keeps shame out of it, so a real talk can happen."},{"prompt":"Later that night, Ishaan hovers at your door, anxious. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Tell him you're very disappointed and ban the laptop","then":"Ishaan nods at the floor, and his door stays shut to you for days."},{"text":"Say curiosity is normal, and that most porn isn't real life","then":"Ishaan looks up, surprised. \"Wait, it's fake?\" he asks quietly.","best":true},{"text":"Say it's normal, and leave it there so he's not embarrassed","then":"Ishaan exhales, relieved. What he saw stays his only picture of sex."},{"text":"Ask him exactly what he watched, and for how long","then":"Ishaan mumbles \"nothing much\" and backs out of the room."}],"why":"Calling curiosity normal removes shame, and the honest fact gives him a better guide than the screen."},{"prompt":"On a drive the next weekend, you have time alone with Ishaan. What do you raise?","options":[{"text":"What respect looks like: both people wanting it, every time","then":"Ishaan listens, then asks how you'd know if someone really wants to.","best":true},{"text":"That he'll be punished if it ever happens again, full stop","then":"Ishaan says \"Okay\" to the window, and clears his history more carefully after."},{"text":"A long list of the sites he must never visit again","then":"He nods through the list, knowing his friends' phones have all of them."},{"text":"Nothing. It's been handled, so why bring it back up","then":"The drive is easy. What he learned from the screen stays unchallenged."}],"why":"Talking about respect gives him what porn leaves out, so the screen isn't his only teacher."},{"prompt":"Months later, Ishaan says a friend sent him a video he didn't want to see. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Thank him, then phone the friend's parents yourself tonight","then":"The friend's parents are furious, and at school everyone knows Ishaan told."},{"text":"Take his phone away to check what else might be on it","then":"Ishaan hands it over, jaw tight, and decides not to tell you next time."},{"text":"Thank him, and ask how it felt and what he'd like to do","then":"Ishaan says it felt weird, and that he'll tell his friend to stop sending them.","best":true},{"text":"Tell him to drop that friend, since he's a bad influence","then":"\"He's my best friend,\" Ishaan says, and changes the subject."}],"why":"Thanking him keeps him coming to you, and asking what he wants builds his own judgement."}],"debrief":"Meet discovered porn with calm honesty: rage teaches hiding, and silence leaves the lesson to the screen.","relearn":"Meet discovered porn with calm honesty, not rage or silence."},
  {"id":"tk-1280","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"teen partner pressuring","hook":"Your daughter Zoya, 16, confides that her boyfriend keeps pressuring her to go further physically.","steps":[{"prompt":"She's twisting her sleeve, not meeting your eyes. What do you say first?","options":[{"text":"She has to end it with him tonight, no discussion","then":"\"You don't even know him,\" Zoya says, and starts defending him."},{"text":"Ask what she did that made him think it was okay","then":"Zoya's face crumples. \"So it's my fault?\" she says, and goes quiet."},{"text":"No one should pressure her, and you're glad she told you","then":"Zoya's shoulders drop. \"I thought you'd be angry,\" she whispers.","best":true},{"text":"Say you'll go and speak to his parents first thing tomorrow","then":"Zoya panics. \"Please don't. Everyone will know.\" She regrets telling you."}],"why":"Believing her and naming the pressure as wrong tells her it's not her fault, and keeps her talking."},{"prompt":"Zoya says she still really likes him and doesn't want to lose him. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Ask what she wants, and say a caring partner accepts a no","then":"Zoya thinks. \"I want to be with him. I just don't want to be pushed.\"","best":true},{"text":"Say you understand, and let her decide without saying more","then":"Zoya nods, relieved, and nothing changes the next time he pushes."},{"text":"Forbid her from seeing him until she's older","then":"Zoya says \"Fine,\" and starts meeting him after tuition instead."},{"text":"Warn her that boys like him only want one thing","then":"\"He's not like that,\" Zoya snaps, defending him harder."}],"why":"Asking what she wants respects her choices, and the fact about a no gives her a clear line."},{"prompt":"A few days later, a text from him makes Zoya's face fall. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Take her phone and read the whole chat yourself","then":"Zoya snatches it back. \"That's private!\" Her phone gets a new lock that night."},{"text":"Say nothing for now. She'll come to you if she needs you","then":"Zoya goes to her room. Later you hear her crying behind the door."},{"text":"Text him yourself from her phone to warn him off","then":"He shows your message to his friends, and Zoya is mortified at school."},{"text":"Ask if she wants to talk, or to practise what to say","then":"Zoya sighs. \"Can we practise? I never know what to say.\" You try a few lines.","best":true}],"why":"Offering to help her find her words supports her without taking over."},{"prompt":"Weeks later, Zoya says he got angry when she said no, and she's scared. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say couples fight, and he'll calm down in a day or two","then":"Zoya nods, unsure. She stops mentioning him, and you stop knowing."},{"text":"Say it's not her fault, and plan together how to keep her safe","then":"Zoya cries, then agrees to call Childline 1098 with you and tell a teacher she trusts.","best":true},{"text":"Go to his house and have it out with him yourself","then":"His family calls you, furious, and Zoya feels humiliated at school."},{"text":"Tell her to block him everywhere tonight, and leave it there","then":"Zoya blocks him, then unblocks him at midnight to explain herself."}],"why":"Saying it's not her fault and planning safety with her keeps her safe and keeps her coming to you."}],"debrief":"Back a pressured teen: believe them, say it's not their fault, respect their choices and offer help.","relearn":"Back a pressured teen's agency and offer help, rather than ordering them."},
  {"id":"tk-1281","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"first phone teen","hook":"Tonight you're giving your son Aarav, 13, his first smartphone.","steps":[{"prompt":"He's bouncing with excitement. How do you hand it over?","options":[{"text":"With a list of strict rules he must sign before he can use it","then":"Aarav signs without reading a word and asks if he can go now."},{"text":"With a short chat about photos, and telling you anything odd","then":"Aarav rolls his eyes but listens, and repeats back the \"tell me\" part.","best":true},{"text":"Just hand it over. He knows phones better than you","then":"Aarav vanishes into his room. You don't see him till dinner."},{"text":"With secret tracking installed, and no word about it","then":"Two days later, Aarav finds the tracking app. \"You're spying on me?\" he asks, hurt."}],"why":"A short chat gives the phone a guide, and makes telling you part of owning it."},{"prompt":"A week later, Aarav says a stranger in a game asked for his photo. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Take the phone back until he's old enough to handle it","then":"Aarav hands it over, furious, and decides the next odd message stays secret."},{"text":"Tell him to ignore it. It happens to everyone online","then":"Aarav shrugs and keeps playing. The account messages him again that night."},{"text":"Thank him, then block and report the account together","then":"Aarav watches you report it. \"That's it? Okay. I'll tell you if it happens again.\"","best":true},{"text":"Ask him why he was talking to strangers in the first place","then":"\"It's a game. Everyone talks,\" Aarav says, sorry he told you."}],"why":"It's not his fault a stranger asked. Thanking him rewards telling you, and acting together shows what to do."},{"prompt":"Months later, Aarav mentions that an edited photo mocking a classmate is going round his group chat. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Tell him to leave that group chat right now, no questions","then":"Aarav leaves, and the photo keeps going round without him."},{"text":"Say it's not his problem, since he didn't send it","then":"Aarav shrugs. The photo gets forwarded again and again."},{"text":"Demand to see the chat so you can check the photo","then":"Aarav hesitates, then says it's already deleted. You doubt it."},{"text":"Ask how the classmate feels, and what he could do to help","then":"Aarav goes quiet. \"Pretty awful.\" He won't forward it, and says he'll tell his class teacher.","best":true}],"why":"Asking how the classmate feels builds the empathy to stop it spreading and to get help."}],"debrief":"Pair a first phone with an open safety chat, not silence or secret spyware.","relearn":"Pair a first phone with an honest safety talk, not silent surveillance."},
  {"id":"tk-1282","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"teen comes out","hook":"Your son Dev, 15, nervously tells you he thinks he likes boys, not girls.","steps":[{"prompt":"He's watching you closely, barely breathing. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Tell him gently that it's probably a phase he'll outgrow","then":"Dev nods slowly. \"Yeah. Maybe.\" He goes quiet for the rest of the evening."},{"text":"Look shocked, then change the subject to dinner","then":"Dev laughs awkwardly and agrees about dinner. His door stays shut that night."},{"text":"Say it's fine, but ask him to keep it from the family","then":"Dev agrees, but his face falls. He hears that it's something to hide."},{"text":"Thank him for trusting you, and say you love him","then":"Dev lets out a long breath and his eyes fill. \"I was so scared to tell you.\"","best":true}],"why":"Thanks and love tell him first that he's safe with you, which is what he most needed."},{"prompt":"A few days later, Dev quietly asks whether you're disappointed in him. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say no, and that you're proud he trusted you","then":"Dev smiles for the first time in days. \"Really? Okay.\"","best":true},{"text":"Say no, then ask if he's really sure about all this","then":"\"I knew you'd say that,\" Dev mutters. \"I am sure.\""},{"text":"Say you'd rather not talk about it again for a while","then":"Dev nods, and the topic goes back into hiding."},{"text":"Say you're fine, but you worry what the relatives will say","then":"Dev's smile fades. Now he's worrying about the relatives too."}],"why":"Pride, not doubt, tells him he is still fully loved."},{"prompt":"At a family function, Bua asks loudly why Dev has no girlfriend yet. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Tell Bua that Dev likes boys, so she can stop asking","then":"The room goes silent. Dev leaves the function without a word."},{"text":"Laugh and say the girls will come along soon enough","then":"Bua laughs along. Dev stares at his plate for the rest of the meal."},{"text":"Say lightly there's no rush, and pass Bua the sweets","then":"Bua laughs and takes a laddoo. Dev catches your eye across the room.","best":true},{"text":"Glare at Bua and tell her it's none of her business","then":"Bua takes offence, and now everyone is looking at Dev."}],"why":"A light deflection that hints at nothing protects him, and leaves when to share up to him."},{"prompt":"Months later, Dev asks for advice about a boy he likes in class. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say you're not the right person for that kind of advice","then":"Dev shrugs. \"Okay.\" He asks his friends instead."},{"text":"Warn him to be careful, since people can be cruel","then":"Dev's excitement drains. \"I know,\" he says quietly."},{"text":"Tell him to focus on his studies for now, not crushes","then":"Dev rolls his eyes and goes back to his room."},{"text":"Give the same honest advice you'd give about anyone","then":"Dev talks for ages, laughing. It feels like any other crush chat.","best":true}],"why":"Treating his crush like any other keeps you the askable parent he came out to."}],"debrief":"Meet a coming-out with thanks, love and an open door; dismissal or shock pushes a teen away.","relearn":"Meet a teen coming out with love and openness, not dismissal or shock."},
  {"id":"tk-1283","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"teen says know everything","hook":"Your daughter Meher, 15, insists she knows everything about sex from friends and online.","steps":[{"prompt":"She says she won't sit through a talk. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Make her sit through it anyway, since it matters","then":"Meher sits, arms crossed, and answers \"I know\" to everything."},{"text":"Agree, then add one thing: a lot online isn't real","then":"Meher sighs. \"I know that.\" She pauses. \"Mostly.\"","best":true},{"text":"Give up. She clearly doesn't need you for this","then":"Meher heads to her room, relieved. Her phone stays her main teacher."},{"text":"Hand her a good book instead, and leave it at that","then":"The book sits on her shelf, unopened, under a pile of notes."}],"why":"One honest thought gets through, and backing off the lecture keeps you askable."},{"prompt":"A few weeks later, Meher repeats a wrong 'fact' about sex from a reel. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Take the chance to finally give her the whole talk now","then":"Five minutes in, Meher's eyes glaze over."},{"text":"Say you've heard that too, and gently share what's true","then":"Meher frowns, then looks it up. \"Huh. I didn't know that,\" she mutters.","best":true},{"text":"Laugh and tell her she's got that completely wrong","then":"\"Whatever,\" Meher says, cheeks burning, and leaves the table."},{"text":"Let it go. Correcting her will only start a fight","then":"The wrong fact stays, and she passes it on to her friends."}],"why":"Meeting a myth calmly corrects it without shaming her, so she keeps checking with you."},{"prompt":"Late one night, Meher knocks and asks if she can ask you something weird. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Tease her that she said she already knew everything","then":"Meher groans. \"Forget it.\" She closes the door."},{"text":"Ask why she's still up at this hour before anything else","then":"Meher mumbles something about homework and goes back to her room."},{"text":"Say she can ask you anything at all, and listen","then":"Meher sits on the bed and asks. It's a real question, and you answer it.","best":true},{"text":"Say yes, but warn her you'll be upset if it's about boys","then":"Meher hesitates. \"It's nothing,\" she says, and leaves."}],"why":"Welcoming a late-night question rewards her for coming to you, even after the eye-rolls."}],"debrief":"Stay warm and available with a know-it-all teen; lectures or quitting close the door.","relearn":"With a know-it-all teen, stay warm; lecturing or quitting lose them."},
  {"id":"tk-1284","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"relative shames teen","hook":"At a family lunch, Tauji loudly scolds your daughter Kavya, 16, for having a boyfriend.","steps":[{"prompt":"Kavya's face burns as the whole table turns to look. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Agree with Tauji, so the family sees you're strict too","then":"Tauji nods approvingly. Kavya stares at her plate, blinking hard."},{"text":"Calmly say Kavya's fine, and you'll talk about it privately","then":"Tauji grumbles, but the talk moves on. Kavya breathes out.","best":true},{"text":"Say nothing and wait for the moment to pass on its own","then":"The scolding goes on another minute. Kavya excuses herself from the table."},{"text":"Snap at Tauji, in front of everyone, that he's way out of line","then":"Tauji bristles, the table erupts, and Kavya is now the centre of a family fight."}],"why":"Backing her calmly and moving it private protects her dignity without a public fight."},{"prompt":"On the drive home, Kavya is silent, staring out of the window. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Tell her she should have kept it quieter from the family","then":"Kavya turns further to the window. \"So it's my fault,\" she says."},{"text":"Put on music and leave her be. She'll be fine by tomorrow","then":"The song plays on. Kavya puts her earphones in and shuts you out."},{"text":"Ask her to explain the boyfriend, since he's the issue now","then":"Kavya sighs. \"Great. Now you too.\" She doesn't say another word."},{"text":"Tell her you're on her side, whenever she wants to talk","then":"Kavya glances at you. \"You weren't embarrassed of me?\" she asks quietly.","best":true}],"why":"Telling her you're on her side eases the sting and keeps her coming to you."},{"prompt":"At home, Kavya asks whether you're angry about the boyfriend too. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say you're not, and ask her to tell you about him","then":"Kavya hesitates, then smiles and starts telling you about him.","best":true},{"text":"Say you're not angry, but she must end it to keep the peace","then":"Kavya's face falls. \"So Tauji wins,\" she says, and goes to her room."},{"text":"Say you'll decide how you feel once you've met him","then":"Kavya nods, unsure where she stands, and changes the subject."},{"text":"Say yes, since she's embarrassed the whole family","then":"Kavya's eyes fill. \"I knew it,\" she says, and shuts her door."}],"why":"Showing interest, not anger, keeps her talking to you about the relationship."},{"prompt":"A week later, Tauji phones to ask whether you've dealt with Kavya. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Assure him you've told her off and it's all sorted","then":"Tauji is pleased. Kavya, in the next room, hears your side of the call."},{"text":"Thank him for caring, and ask him to come to you, not her","then":"Tauji pauses. \"Hm. Fine. I only worry,\" he says, more quietly.","best":true},{"text":"Tell him firmly to mind his own family and stay out of yours","then":"Tauji hangs up, and the family WhatsApp group hears about it by evening."},{"text":"Change the subject fast, so there's no row with him","then":"Tauji raises it again at the next function, in front of everyone."}],"why":"A kind, clear boundary protects Kavya's dignity and keeps family ties intact."}],"debrief":"Back your teen against public shaming and take the talk private; joining the shaming breaks their trust.","relearn":"Back your teen against public shaming and keep talks private."},
  {"id":"tk-1285","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"teen sent risky photo","hook":"Your daughter Tara, 15, tearfully admits a private photo she sent is being passed around school.","steps":[{"prompt":"She can barely get the words out. What do you say first?","options":[{"text":"How could she, when she's shamed the whole family","then":"Tara flinches and goes silent. An hour later she's back, shaking, with nowhere else to turn."},{"text":"To delete everything and never speak of it again","then":"Tara nods, but the photo keeps moving from phone to phone."},{"text":"That it's not her fault, and you'll help her","then":"Tara sobs harder, then leans into you. \"I didn't know who else to tell.\"","best":true},{"text":"Ask who she sent it to, and why she'd do that","then":"Tara whispers a name, then shuts down. \"I knew you'd blame me.\""}],"why":"Saying it's not her fault first tells her she's safe with you, so she lets you help."},{"prompt":"Tara says she's scared everyone at school has seen it. What do you do next?","options":[{"text":"Tell her to stay home from school until it blows over","then":"Tara stays home. The photo keeps spreading while she hides."},{"text":"Help her report it on the app and get it taken down","then":"Tara shows you the accounts. Together you report the posts and save the links.","best":true},{"text":"Say it'll blow over soon if she just ignores it","then":"Tara tries. By Monday, two more groups have it."},{"text":"Message the parents of the boy she sent it to, tonight","then":"The parents deny everything, and Tara feels her life slipping out of her hands."}],"why":"Reporting it together starts to stop the spread and shows her she isn't facing it alone."},{"prompt":"The next day, Tara begs you not to tell anyone else, not even her school. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Promise you won't tell anyone at all, whatever happens","then":"Tara is relieved, but the photo keeps spreading and your hands are tied."},{"text":"Go straight to her principal tomorrow without telling her","then":"The school acts, but Tara feels betrayed and barely speaks to you for days."},{"text":"Explain why Childline 1098 can help, and decide with her","then":"Tara listens, then nods. You call Childline 1098 together and ask what happens next.","best":true},{"text":"Say she lost the right to decide when she sent it","then":"Tara goes white. \"So this is my punishment,\" she says, and walks away."}],"why":"Getting help while including her in the choice keeps her safe and in charge of her own story."},{"prompt":"A week later, Tara finally says she keeps thinking it was all her own fault. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Everyone makes mistakes, so try to forget it now","then":"Tara nods, but she hears that it was her mistake, and carries it."},{"text":"Well, maybe this will teach her to be more careful","then":"Tara's face crumples, and she stops talking about it at all."},{"text":"It wasn't. Sharing her photo was someone else's choice","then":"Tara looks up. \"Someone else's choice,\" she repeats slowly.","best":true},{"text":"Change the subject gently, so she stops dwelling on it","then":"Tara goes along with it, then lies awake replaying it alone."}],"why":"Putting the blame where it belongs helps her heal: it was never her fault."},{"prompt":"Months later, Tara starts seeing someone new, and you feel anxious. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Ask to check her phone every week, just to be safe","then":"Tara hands it over, but starts using a second app you don't know about."},{"text":"Remind her every day never to send another photo","then":"By the third reminder, Tara rolls her eyes and stops telling you about her day."},{"text":"Say nothing, so she doesn't feel judged all over again","then":"Tara wonders if you're still upset, and keeps her new crush to herself."},{"text":"Say you trust her, and she can come to you with anything","then":"Tara smiles. \"Okay. I'll remember that.\"","best":true}],"why":"Trust and an open door after a crisis keep her coming to you first."}],"debrief":"When a photo spreads, say it isn't their fault and help them report it; blame or silence leaves them alone.","relearn":"When a photo spreads, reassure your teen and help them report."},
  {"id":"tk-1286","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"teen disagrees values","hook":"Your daughter Simran, 17, calls her boyfriend 'the one'. To you it feels too serious, too soon.","steps":[{"prompt":"She wants to bring him home to meet you on Sunday. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say she ends it before her board exams, or else","then":"Simran goes pale. \"He's coming on Sunday anyway,\" she says coldly."},{"text":"Say yes, and share your worry with her once, honestly","then":"Simran listens. \"I hear you. Just meet him first?\" You agree.","best":true},{"text":"Agree, then quietly plan to put him off at lunch","then":"Simran is thrilled and tells Nikhil you're on their side. She'd never trust you again if she knew."},{"text":"Say yes warmly, and keep your worry to yourself for now","then":"Simran hugs you. Your worry stays unsaid, and grows."}],"why":"Saying your view once, honestly, keeps both your influence and her trust."},{"prompt":"On Sunday, Nikhil comes to lunch, polite and clearly nervous. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Grill him about his plans and his family's income","then":"Nikhil stumbles through his answers. Simran glares at you across the table."},{"text":"Stay polite but cold, so he quietly gets the message","then":"Nikhil leaves early. Simran doesn't speak to you that evening."},{"text":"Be warm, and ask him about himself like any guest","then":"Nikhil relaxes and tells you about his cricket team. Simran looks grateful.","best":true},{"text":"Be friendly, but drop hints that it's all too early","then":"Nikhil laughs awkwardly. Simran hears every hint and says nothing."}],"why":"Welcoming him keeps you close to her world, where your view still counts."},{"prompt":"Weeks later, Simran says they're thinking of applying to the same college. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say you'll only pay the fees if she chooses separately","then":"Simran goes silent. From then on, she tells you only what she must."},{"text":"Say it's her life, and stay out of it completely","then":"Simran nods, a little hurt that you have nothing to say."},{"text":"Ask what she wants for herself, and share your view once","then":"Simran thinks. \"I'd still pick it. But I'll look at others too.\"","best":true},{"text":"Remind her of every worry you've ever had about him","then":"\"You've said all this,\" Simran snaps, and stops sharing her plans."}],"why":"Centring her own goals and sharing your view once guides her without taking the choice away."}],"debrief":"Share your view once and stay connected; ultimatums and sabotage cost trust.","relearn":"On choices you dislike, share your view and keep the door open."},
  {"id":"tk-1287","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"match","persona":"any","source":"teen worry to opener","hook":"Match each teen situation to a calm opener.","pairs":[{"left":"They seem heartbroken","right":"\"Rough day? I'm here if you want to talk.\""},{"left":"They saw something explicit","right":"\"A lot of that isn't real. Let's unpack it.\""},{"left":"A partner is controlling them","right":"\"You always get a say in your own life.\""},{"left":"They're curious about dating","right":"\"Ask me anything, no judgement.\""},{"left":"They made an online mistake","right":"\"Thanks for telling me. Let's sort it.\""}],"relearn":"Heartbreak, explicit content, control, curiosity and a slip each have a calm opener that keeps a teen talking."},
  {"id":"tk-1288","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"match","persona":"Vikram","source":"myth to truth teen","hook":"Match each thing your teen picks up online to the honest truth you can offer.","pairs":[{"left":"Real bodies look like porn","right":"\"Most of that is edited and performed.\""},{"left":"Jealousy proves love","right":"\"Trust, not control, is love.\""},{"left":"A no can be worn down","right":"\"A no means stop, every time.\""},{"left":"Pleasure is one-sided","right":"\"Both people's comfort matters.\""},{"left":"Asking ruins the mood","right":"\"Checking in is part of respect.\""}],"relearn":"Edited bodies, jealousy, worn-down nos, one-sided pleasure and asking-ruins-it each have an honest truth to counter."},
  {"id":"tk-1289","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"match","persona":"any","source":"reaction to repair","hook":"You reacted badly to a teen's question. Match each fumble to the repair.","pairs":[{"left":"You snapped 'too young'","right":"\"Sorry I shut you down. Ask me again.\""},{"left":"You looked shocked and froze","right":"\"That surprised me, but I'm glad you asked.\""},{"left":"You lectured instead of listening","right":"\"I talked over you. Tell me your view.\""},{"left":"You said 'ask your mother'","right":"\"Let's figure this one out together.\""},{"left":"You laughed it off","right":"\"A real question deserves a real answer.\""}],"relearn":"Snapping, freezing, lecturing, deflecting and laughing each have a warm repair that reopens it."},
  {"id":"tk-1290","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"match","persona":"Vikram","source":"topic to age-right line","hook":"Match each teen topic to a clear, respectful thing to say about it.","pairs":[{"left":"Consent","right":"\"Both people freely wanting it, every time.\""},{"left":"Breakups","right":"\"You can end things kindly and still be okay.\""},{"left":"Online strangers","right":"\"People online aren't always who they claim.\""},{"left":"Peer pressure","right":"\"Real friends never push you past your limits.\""},{"left":"Privacy","right":"\"Your body and choices are yours to share or not.\""}],"relearn":"Consent, breakups, online strangers, peer pressure and privacy each have a clear, respectful line a parent can offer."},
  {"id":"tk-1291","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"match","persona":"any","source":"value to honest fact","hook":"A teen asks a hard question. Match each family value to the fact it pairs with.","pairs":[{"left":"We value commitment","right":"How contraception and safety work"},{"left":"We believe in the right time","right":"What consent really requires"},{"left":"We value respect for women","right":"How to spot a controlling partner"},{"left":"We honour your privacy","right":"Where to find reliable health info"},{"left":"We want you safe online","right":"How to spot and report grooming"}],"relearn":"Each family value pairs with an honest fact: commitment with safety, respect with spotting control."},
  {"id":"tk-1292","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"match","persona":"Vikram","source":"controlling sign to response","hook":"Match each controlling thing a partner does to a steady thing you can say.","pairs":[{"left":"Demands constant location sharing","right":"\"Trust doesn't need a tracker.\""},{"left":"Isolates them from friends","right":"\"A partner who likes your friends is a keeper.\""},{"left":"Threatens to leave to get their way","right":"\"Love isn't a threat over you.\""},{"left":"Reads all their messages","right":"\"You're allowed private space.\""},{"left":"Blames them for the anger","right":"\"Their feelings aren't yours to manage.\""}],"relearn":"Tracking, isolating, threatening, snooping and blame-shifting each have a steady reframe to name."},
  {"id":"tk-1293","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"match","persona":"any","source":"feeling to safe action","hook":"Match each thing your teen might be feeling to a safe next step you can offer.","pairs":[{"left":"Pressured by a partner","right":"\"You can always say not yet, or no.\""},{"left":"Ashamed of an online slip","right":"\"Mistakes are fixable. Let's act now.\""},{"left":"Confused by mixed messages online","right":"\"Let's sort what's real from what's performed.\""},{"left":"Scared by a stranger's messages","right":"\"Block, screenshot, and show me.\""},{"left":"Hurt by a breakup","right":"\"This pain is real and it does ease.\""}],"relearn":"Pressure, shame, confusion, fear and heartbreak each have a calm, safe next step a parent can offer."},
  {"id":"tk-1294","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"reflect","persona":"any","source":"door open wider","hook":"Lensy: in the teen years the door to your child matters more, not less. Sit with that?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["I feel it","The door stays open","Still their parent"],"affirm":"Your teen still wants a trusted adult; staying askable matters most exactly when they pull away.","relearn":"The door to your teen matters more in the teen years, not less."},
  {"id":"tk-1295","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"reflect","persona":"Vikram","source":"antidote to algorithm","hook":"Lensy: every honest answer you give is one the algorithm doesn't get to give instead. Worth it?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Worth it","Be the antidote","Out-talk the feed"],"affirm":"Your calm, honest voice is the antidote to what the feed teaches; silence simply hands over the lesson.","relearn":"Your honest voice is the antidote to what the algorithm teaches a teen."},
  {"id":"tk-1296","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"reflect","persona":"any","source":"not a perfect speech","hook":"Lensy: you don't need the perfect talk, just to be the parent they keep coming back to. Easier?","prompt":"How does that land?","options":["Easier","Just stay askable","I can do that"],"affirm":"It was never one flawless speech; being the askable, open-door parent is what truly protects a teen.","relearn":"You don't need a perfect talk, just to stay the askable parent a teen returns to."},
  {"id":"tk-1297","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"reflect","persona":"Vikram","source":"calm beats control","hook":"Lensy: a teen who isn't scared of your reaction is a teen who'll tell you the scary stuff. See it?","prompt":"What's your read?","options":["I see it","Calm keeps them talking","Less fear, more truth"],"affirm":"When a teen doesn't fear your reaction, they bring you the hard things; calm keeps the truth coming.","relearn":"A teen unafraid of your reaction is one who tells you what really matters."},
  {"id":"tk-1298","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"reflect","persona":"any","source":"both not either","hook":"Lensy: you get to give honest facts AND your family's values, never just one. Feel the relief?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Relief","Both, not either","Facts and values"],"affirm":"It's never facts-or-values; a teen can hold both: the facts to stay safe and your values to guide them.","relearn":"Give a teen honest facts and your values both, never just one."},
  {"id":"tk-1299","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"reflect","persona":"any","source":"respect is the lesson","hook":"Lensy: the heart of every teen talk is one idea: both people always matter. Worth repeating?","prompt":"Your take?","options":["Worth it","Both always matter","That's the core"],"affirm":"Underneath consent, dating and online life sits one lesson: both people's wants and limits always matter.","relearn":"The core of every teen talk is that both people's wants and limits always matter."},
  {"id":"tk-1300","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"reflect","persona":"Vikram","source":"fun dad can do hard","hook":"Lensy: being the easy, fun parent is exactly what lets a hard talk land gently. Reframe it?","prompt":"How does that sit?","options":["Reframed","My bond helps","I'm the right one"],"affirm":"Your easy, trusting bond is the very thing that lets a serious talk land softly; the fun parent can do this.","relearn":"Your fun, easy bond is what lets a hard teen talk land gently."},
  {"id":"tk-1301","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"reflect","persona":"any","source":"trust over surveillance","hook":"Lensy: trust brings a teen to you; surveillance just teaches them to hide better. Notice the difference?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["I notice","Trust over spying","Keep them coming"],"affirm":"Trust is what brings a teen to you with the truth; secret surveillance only teaches them to hide it better.","relearn":"Trust brings a teen to you; surveillance teaches them to hide."},
  {"id":"tk-1302","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"spot","persona":"any","source":"two red flags chat","hook":"Read your teen's partner's messages. Spot the two red flags.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Hope your exams went okay today\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"Why didn't you reply in five minutes?\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"Have fun with your friends tonight\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"Send your location or we're done\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"No rush, talk whenever you're free\"","trick":false}],"why":"Demanding instant replies and threatening over location are control red flags; the others respect a teen's freedom.","relearn":"Demands for instant replies and location threats are red flags, not signs of love."},
  {"id":"tk-1303","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"spot","persona":"Vikram","source":"two porn myths","hook":"Your teen lists 'facts' they picked up online. Spot the two myths to gently correct.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Both people's comfort should matter","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Real bodies look just like the videos","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"A no means stop, every time","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Pressuring someone is just normal","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Consent can be taken back anytime","trick":false}],"why":"That real bodies match videos and that pressuring is normal are porn-fed myths; the rest are true and worth affirming.","relearn":"Real bodies match the screen and pressure-is-normal are myths to correct, not facts."},
  {"id":"tk-1304","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"spot","persona":"any","source":"two shut-down replies","hook":"Your teen just confided something hard. Spot the two replies that slam the door.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Thank you for telling me this\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"That's disgusting, stop talking\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"You're not in trouble for being honest\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"Wait till the whole family hears this\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"Let's work through it together\"","trick":false}],"why":"Disgust and threatening to tell everyone slam the door; thanks, reassurance and teamwork keep it open.","relearn":"Disgust and threats to expose them slam the door a teen just opened."},
  {"id":"tk-1305","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"spot","persona":"Vikram","source":"two grooming signs","hook":"An adult is messaging your teen online. Spot the two grooming red flags.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Let's keep this chat our little secret\"","trick":true},{"id":"b","text":"\"You can tell your parents about me anytime\"","trick":false},{"id":"c","text":"\"Send me a private photo, no one'll know\"","trick":true},{"id":"d","text":"\"We met in the open class group\"","trick":false},{"id":"e","text":"\"It's fine to block me if you're uneasy\"","trick":false}],"why":"Pushing secrecy and asking for a private photo are grooming red flags; the safe lines welcome parents and a block.","relearn":"Demands for secrecy and private photos are grooming red flags a teen should bring to you."},
  {"id":"tk-1306","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"spot","persona":"any","source":"two pressure lines","hook":"Spot the two lines a partner uses to pressure a teen into 'yes'.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"If you loved me you'd just do it\"","trick":true},{"id":"b","text":"\"We can stop anytime you want\"","trick":false},{"id":"c","text":"\"Everyone's done it, don't be a baby\"","trick":true},{"id":"d","text":"\"Only if you're completely sure\"","trick":false},{"id":"e","text":"\"Your comfort matters more to me\"","trick":false}],"why":"'If you loved me' and 'everyone's done it' are pressure tactics; the others respect a teen's right to choose.","relearn":"'If you loved me' and 'everyone's done it' are pressure tactics, never proof of love."},
  {"id":"tk-1307","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"spot","persona":"Vikram","source":"two manosphere lies","hook":"Your son repeats lines from influencers. Spot the two lies that dishonour consent.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Girls owe you nothing for being nice\"","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"\"A real man takes what he wants\"","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"\"Respect means hearing a no the first time\"","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"\"Women secretly want to be pressured\"","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"\"Strength is controlling yourself, not others\"","trick":false}],"why":"'A real man takes what he wants' and 'women want pressure' dishonour consent; the rest model genuine respect.","relearn":"'Take what you want' and 'women want pressure' are manosphere lies, not strength."},
  {"id":"tk-1308","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"spot","persona":"any","source":"two snooping moves","hook":"Spot the two parenting moves that break a teen's trust instead of building it.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Asking openly how the relationship is going","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Secretly reading every private chat","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Agreeing on reasonable phone limits together","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Installing hidden spyware on their phone","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Keeping the door open without judgement","trick":false}],"why":"Secret chat-reading and hidden spyware break trust once found; open questions and shared limits build it.","relearn":"Secret snooping and hidden spyware break the trust that keeps a teen talking to you."},
  {"id":"tk-1309","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"porn calmly","hook":"Your son Samar, 15, wants to know if a video his friends shared is how it really is.","setup":"He asks while you're both washing up.","steps":[{"prompt":"Samar asks: \"Like, is that actually what people do?\"","options":[{"text":"\"You shouldn't be watching that filth at your age.\"","then":"Samar goes red. \"I didn't even want to watch it,\" he mutters."},{"text":"\"Good that you asked. A lot of that is acted and edited.\"","then":"Samar pauses, a plate in his hand. \"Wait, so it's fake? All of it?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"We're not discussing this now. Ask me again when you're older.\"","then":"Samar shrugs. \"Fine.\" He goes back to the videos for answers."},{"text":"\"Pretty much, yes. That's just what grown-ups do.\"","then":"Samar nods, and files it away as the truth."}],"why":"Calm honesty keeps you the source he trusts, instead of the screen."},{"prompt":"Later that evening, Samar asks: \"So how do you know if the other person actually wants to?\"","options":[{"text":"\"You'll find out when you're married. Not before.\"","then":"Samar rolls his eyes. The video stays his only picture."},{"text":"\"You ask, and you respect the answer. Both people must want it.\"","then":"Samar thinks. \"So the girl in the video maybe didn't want it?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"You'll just know. It's not something anyone can explain.\"","then":"Samar frowns. \"That's not really an answer,\" he says, and drops it."},{"text":"\"Honestly, it's embarrassing. Let's not go there.\"","then":"Samar laughs awkwardly. \"Yeah. Sorry I asked.\""}],"why":"Naming respect and mutual wanting gives him what the video leaves out."},{"prompt":"A week later, Samar says: \"My friends say when a girl says no, she's playing hard to get.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Your friends are idiots. Stop hanging around them.\"","then":"Samar bristles. \"They're my friends.\" The point gets lost."},{"text":"\"Some girls do that, so you have to read the signs.\"","then":"Samar nods. The myth now has your approval too."},{"text":"\"No means no. If you're ever unsure, stop and ask.\"","then":"Samar nods. \"Stop and ask. Okay. That's easy enough.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Well, that's between them. Don't get into it.\"","then":"Samar shrugs, and the idea goes unchallenged."}],"why":"A plain rule about no, and stopping to ask, protects him and everyone he dates."}],"relearn":"Meeting a porn question with calm honesty keeps you the trusted source over the screen."},
  {"id":"tk-1310","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"heartbreak support","hook":"Your daughter Nisha, 16, is sobbing in her room after a breakup.","setup":"You knock, and she lets you in.","steps":[{"prompt":"Nisha sobs: \"He ended it over a text. I feel so stupid.\"","options":[{"text":"\"It's puppy love. You'll forget him by next week.\"","then":"\"You don't get it,\" Nisha says, and turns to the wall."},{"text":"\"Honestly, good. He was never right for you anyway.\"","then":"Nisha stiffens. \"You never even liked him.\""},{"text":"\"Let's get you some ice cream and not think about him.\"","then":"Nisha eats a spoonful, then goes back to crying later, alone."},{"text":"\"I'm so sorry. That really hurts. I'm right here.\"","then":"Nisha leans against you and cries harder, then slowly quietens.","best":true}],"why":"Naming the hurt and staying close lets her grieve instead of hiding it."},{"prompt":"After a while, Nisha asks: \"Should I text him and ask why?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Absolutely not. Have some self-respect, Nisha.\"","then":"Nisha flushes, and texts him later when you're asleep."},{"text":"\"What do you hope his answer would give you?\"","then":"Nisha thinks. \"That it wasn't my fault, I guess.\" She puts the phone down.","best":true},{"text":"\"Yes, text him now and tell him how you feel.\"","then":"Nisha sends a long message. The two blue ticks sit there, unanswered."},{"text":"\"Give me the phone. I'll tell him what I think.\"","then":"Nisha grabs it back, horrified. \"Are you mad?\""}],"why":"A gentle question helps her find her own answer, which sticks better than advice."},{"prompt":"A week later, Nisha says: \"I'm never going to like anyone again.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Good. Focus on your studies instead of boys.\"","then":"Nisha rolls her eyes and changes the subject."},{"text":"\"Of course you will. There are plenty of fish in the sea.\"","then":"Nisha groans. \"Please don't say that.\" She stops talking."},{"text":"\"Come on. It's been a week. Time to move on.\"","then":"Nisha goes quiet, and learns to hide her sadness from you."},{"text":"\"It feels that way now. It won't always. I'll be here.\"","then":"Nisha gives a small, wet laugh. \"You have to say that.\" She looks lighter.","best":true}],"why":"Honouring the feeling while offering hope keeps you her safe place."}],"relearn":"Taking a teen's heartbreak seriously, without minimising it, keeps you their safe place."},
  {"id":"tk-1311","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"consent in words","hook":"After a talk at school, your son Aditya, 15, wants to know what 'consent' really means.","setup":"He's lounging on the sofa, half on his phone.","steps":[{"prompt":"Aditya asks: \"Like, in real life. How do you actually know?\"","options":[{"text":"\"It's complicated grown-up stuff. Don't worry about it yet.\"","then":"Aditya shrugs. \"Okay.\" He goes back to scrolling."},{"text":"\"It just means she said yes once. Then you're fine.\"","then":"Aditya nods. One yes now sounds like enough to him."},{"text":"\"Both people freely want it, every time. Anyone can stop.\"","then":"Aditya looks up from his phone. \"Every time? Even if you're together?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"You'll just know. You can always tell from someone's face.\"","then":"Aditya frowns. \"What if you can't tell, though?\""}],"why":"A plain rule he can remember gives him something clear to act on."},{"prompt":"A minute later, Aditya asks: \"What if someone says yes and then changes their mind?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Then you stop. Changing your mind is always allowed.\"","then":"Aditya nods. \"So it's not a one-time thing. Got it.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Well, once you've started, it's a bit late for that.\"","then":"Aditya takes that in, and it quietly becomes his rule."},{"text":"\"Then check once more if they're really, truly sure.\"","then":"Aditya nods. He hears that a no is something to argue with."},{"text":"\"That hardly ever happens. Don't overthink it.\"","then":"Aditya shrugs, and his question stays unanswered."}],"why":"Saying anyone can stop at any time is the heart of consent."},{"prompt":"A few days later, Aditya says: \"My friend says if a girl doesn't say no, that means yes.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Your friend is an idiot. Stop listening to him.\"","then":"Aditya bristles. \"He's not an idiot,\" he says, and the point is lost."},{"text":"\"Well, if she's not objecting, then that's usually fine, I think.\"","then":"Aditya shrugs. His friend's rule now has your stamp on it."},{"text":"\"Let's not get into what your friends think, okay?\"","then":"Aditya shrugs, and the myth wins by default."},{"text":"\"Not saying no isn't a yes. You need a clear, happy yes.\"","then":"Aditya nods slowly. \"I'll tell him. He won't like it, though.\"","best":true}],"why":"Silence isn't consent. A clear yes is the rule that keeps everyone safe."}],"relearn":"Explaining consent plainly, as both people freely wanting it every time, gives a teen a clear protective rule."},
  {"id":"tk-1312","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"partner pressure script","hook":"Your daughter Pooja, 17, says her girlfriend keeps pushing her further than she wants.","setup":"She's on the stairs, hugging her knees.","steps":[{"prompt":"Pooja says: \"I keep saying maybe later. I can't say no.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Well, maybe you're leading her on without meaning to.\"","then":"Pooja's face falls. \"So it's my fault?\" she whispers."},{"text":"\"No one should pressure you. 'I'm not ready' is enough.\"","then":"Pooja looks up. \"That's enough? I thought I needed a reason.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"That's for you two to sort out between yourselves.\"","then":"Pooja nods, and goes back to saying \"maybe later\"."},{"text":"\"Just tell her you're busy. That buys you some time.\"","then":"Pooja nods. It works for a week, and then the pushing starts again."}],"why":"Saying no one should pressure her, and 'not ready' is enough, tells her it's not her fault."},{"prompt":"Pooja asks: \"But what if she gets upset and leaves me?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Then she's not worth it. Let her go, honestly.\"","then":"Pooja flinches. \"You don't know her,\" she says quietly."},{"text":"\"Don't worry. She won't leave you over something as small as this.\"","then":"Pooja nods, but the fear stays, and so does the pressure."},{"text":"\"That would hurt. But someone who cares won't punish a no.\"","then":"Pooja wipes her eyes. \"Yeah. If she did, that tells me something.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Want me to talk to her and sort this out for you?\"","then":"Pooja looks horrified. \"No! That would be so much worse.\""}],"why":"Naming that a caring partner accepts a no helps her see the pressure clearly."},{"prompt":"A few days later, Pooja asks: \"Can we practise what I'd actually say?\"","options":[{"text":"\"You don't need practice. Just be firm with her.\"","then":"Pooja nods, unsure what \"firm\" is supposed to sound like."},{"text":"\"Here's a script. Read it to her word for word.\"","then":"Pooja reads it, then says it doesn't sound like her."},{"text":"\"Yes. I'll play her. You say it your own way.\"","then":"You practise twice. The second time, Pooja's voice is steady.","best":true},{"text":"\"Isn't this a bit much? It's not that serious.\"","then":"Pooja drops her eyes. \"Forget it,\" she says."}],"why":"Practising in her own words builds the confidence to say it for real."},{"prompt":"A week later, Pooja says: \"I told her. She sulked, but she said okay.\"","options":[{"text":"\"I'm proud of you. How are you feeling about it all?\"","then":"Pooja smiles. \"Relieved. A bit scared. But mostly relieved.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"See? I told you it was nothing to worry about.\"","then":"Pooja's smile fades. It didn't feel like nothing to her."},{"text":"\"Sulked? Then you should end it with her now.\"","then":"Pooja stiffens. \"I didn't ask you that,\" she says."},{"text":"\"Good. Now let's not talk about this stuff again for a while.\"","then":"Pooja nods, and the door you opened quietly closes."}],"why":"Praising her courage and asking how she feels keeps the door open for next time."}],"relearn":"Affirming a teen's right to say no and offering backup keeps a pressured teen talking to you."},
  {"id":"tk-1313","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"manosphere counter","hook":"Your son Yash, 14, has been watching a lot of one 'alpha male' influencer lately.","setup":"At dinner, he repeats one of his lines.","steps":[{"prompt":"Yash says: \"Women love a man who takes charge. Everyone knows that.\"","options":[{"text":"\"What rubbish. Only an idiot believes those losers online.\"","then":"Yash's face hardens. \"You just don't get it,\" he mutters."},{"text":"\"Ha, maybe you're right. Now pass me the dal, please.\"","then":"Yash grins, and the line settles in as something you agreed with."},{"text":"\"I get why that sounds cool. But real strength is respect.\"","then":"Yash smirks. \"Respect is boring, though. He says women want strong men.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Give me that phone. You're done watching that man.\"","then":"Yash hands it over, then watches the videos at a friend's place."}],"why":"Seeing the appeal without mocking him keeps him listening to your point."},{"prompt":"Later, Yash says: \"He also says real men don't cry. Crying is weak.\"","options":[{"text":"\"That's true, but only in front of other people.\"","then":"Yash nods. Hiding feelings now has your approval."},{"text":"\"I cry sometimes. Feelings are human, not weak.\"","then":"Yash looks surprised. \"You cry? Seriously?\" He goes quiet for a moment.","best":true},{"text":"\"That man is a fraud. I forbid you to watch him.\"","then":"Yash rolls his eyes, and finds one more reason to trust the influencer."},{"text":"\"Well, he has a lot of followers. He must know something.\"","then":"Yash nods, satisfied. The influencer gains one more point."}],"why":"Sharing your own truth shows him that someone strong he trusts has feelings."},{"prompt":"The next week, Yash asks: \"So what does taking charge even mean, then?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Being the boss. Just be nicer about it than he is.\"","then":"Yash nods. The idea of being the boss stays, just softer."},{"text":"\"Whatever you want it to mean. It doesn't matter.\"","then":"Yash shrugs, and the influencer's version fills the gap."},{"text":"\"Stop asking about that man. I'm sick of hearing him.\"","then":"Yash goes quiet, and takes his questions back to the videos."},{"text":"\"Leading with care. And never ignoring anyone's no.\"","then":"Yash thinks. \"So like a captain. Not a dictator.\"","best":true}],"why":"Giving him a respectful meaning of strength replaces the distorted one."},{"prompt":"A month later, Yash shows you a clip mocking a girl and asks: \"Is this funny or messed up?\"","options":[{"text":"\"It's messed up. I told you these guys are poison.\"","then":"Yash's face closes. \"Forget I asked.\""},{"text":"\"It's just a joke. Don't take things so seriously.\"","then":"Yash laughs along, and forwards it to his group."},{"text":"\"What do you think? How would she feel watching it?\"","then":"Yash watches it again. \"Pretty messed up, actually,\" he says.","best":true},{"text":"\"Why are you still watching this stuff? Delete it.\"","then":"Yash deletes it, and stops showing you what he watches."}],"why":"Asking him to think it through builds his own judgement, the real antidote."}],"relearn":"Countering manosphere lines warmly, without shaming your son, keeps the conversation open and teaches real respect."},
  {"id":"tk-1314","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"stranger online","hook":"Your daughter Diya, 13, mentions an older 'friend' from a game who wants to chat privately.","setup":"She says it casually, while doing homework.","steps":[{"prompt":"Diya says: \"He's really nice. He says I'm mature for my age.\"","options":[{"text":"\"That's it. You're banned from the internet. I knew it.\"","then":"Diya's face falls. \"I shouldn't have told you.\" An hour later, she comes back, worried."},{"text":"\"Thanks for telling me. Can we look at the chat together?\"","then":"Diya shrugs and opens the app. \"Sure. He's not weird or anything.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"That's sweet of him. Just be a bit careful, okay?\"","then":"Diya smiles and keeps chatting with him that night."},{"text":"\"Who is he? Where does he live? Tell me everything.\"","then":"Diya shrinks back. \"I don't know. Forget it.\""}],"why":"Staying calm and looking together keeps her telling you, with no trouble for her."},{"prompt":"Diya says quietly: \"He keeps asking me to move to a private app.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Fine, as long as you show me the chats every now and then.\"","then":"Diya moves to the app. The chats you see are the ones she picks."},{"text":"\"Absolutely not! Why are you even still talking to him?\"","then":"Diya flinches. \"Okay, okay,\" she mutters, and stares at the floor."},{"text":"\"Adults who want private chats with kids aren't safe.\"","then":"Diya hesitates. \"He did say not to tell anyone,\" she admits.","best":true},{"text":"\"You're old enough now to judge that for yourself.\"","then":"Diya moves to the private app that night."}],"why":"Naming secret chats with adults as unsafe gives her a clear rule to follow."},{"prompt":"Later, Diya asks: \"He told me not to tell you. Am I in trouble?\"","options":[{"text":"\"You should have told me the moment he said that.\"","then":"Diya's face crumples. \"So it is my fault,\" she whispers."},{"text":"\"No. You did nothing wrong. I'm glad you told me.\"","then":"Diya's eyes fill with relief. \"I was scared you'd be angry.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Not if you promise to stop talking to strangers.\"","then":"Diya promises, but she's unsure what she did wrong."},{"text":"\"We'll see. First show me everything you sent him.\"","then":"Diya hands over the phone, shaking, and stops talking."}],"why":"It is never a child's fault when an adult asks for secrets, and hearing that keeps her telling you."},{"prompt":"That evening, Diya asks: \"What happens now? Will he get in trouble?\"","options":[{"text":"\"I'll message him myself and give him a real scare.\"","then":"He deletes his profile, and could simply start again somewhere else."},{"text":"\"We'll block and report him, and call Childline 1098.\"","then":"Diya nods. The Childline counsellor listens and explains what to do next.","best":true},{"text":"\"Nothing. Just block him and we'll forget all about it.\"","then":"Diya blocks him. A week later, a new account says hello."},{"text":"\"I'll ask the family group what we should do about it.\"","then":"The family group fills with panic and advice, and Diya feels exposed."}],"why":"Reporting and getting expert help protects Diya, and other children too."}],"relearn":"Staying calm and curious about an online stranger keeps a teen reporting risks instead of hiding them."},
  {"id":"tk-1315","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"sexting mistake","hook":"Your son Veer, 15, admits he sent a private photo to a girl he likes, and now regrets it.","setup":"He can't look at you.","steps":[{"prompt":"Veer says: \"I don't know why I did it. I feel sick.\"","options":[{"text":"\"How could you be so stupid? You've shamed this whole family.\"","then":"Veer's face shuts. \"Forget it,\" he says, and leaves the room."},{"text":"\"Well, what's done is done. Try not to think about it.\"","then":"Veer nods, but he lies awake checking his phone all night."},{"text":"\"I'm glad you told me. You're not in trouble. We'll handle it.\"","then":"Veer lets out a shaky breath. \"I thought you'd kill me.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Why would you send that? What were you thinking?\"","then":"Veer shrugs miserably. \"I don't know. I told you I don't know.\""}],"why":"Saying he's not in trouble keeps him working the problem with you, not alone."},{"prompt":"Later, Veer asks: \"Should I ask her to delete it?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Yes, ask her calmly. And tell me how she replies.\"","then":"Veer sends a short message. \"She says okay,\" he tells you, unsure.","best":true},{"text":"\"Give me her number. I'll speak to her parents myself.\"","then":"Veer panics. \"Please don't. That's the worst thing you could do.\""},{"text":"\"No. Just stay quiet and hope she forgets about it.\"","then":"Veer waits, and the worry sits with him for weeks."},{"text":"\"Tell her she'll be in big trouble if she shows anyone.\"","then":"She screenshots the threat and shows it to her friends."}],"why":"A calm request is his best chance to stop it, and keeping you told keeps him supported."},{"prompt":"A few weeks later, Veer says: \"Someone says they've seen it. What do I do?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Just deny it's you. Nobody can prove anything, anyway.\"","then":"Veer tries, but the rumours grow, and he faces them alone."},{"text":"\"We'll report it together and call Childline 1098 for help.\"","then":"Veer nods, pale but steadier. The counsellor walks you both through next steps.","best":true},{"text":"\"Well, this is exactly what happens when you send photos.\"","then":"Veer's eyes fill. He stops telling you what's happening at school."},{"text":"\"Stay home from school until it all dies down, okay?\"","then":"Veer stays home, and the photo keeps moving without him."}],"why":"Getting real help fast, together, protects him. Someone else sharing it is not his fault."}],"relearn":"Meeting a sexting mistake with safety not blame keeps a teen working the problem with you."},
  {"id":"tk-1316","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"both facts and values","hook":"Your daughter Ira, 18, has been seeing Kiran for a year. She finds you alone in the kitchen.","setup":"She closes the door behind her.","steps":[{"prompt":"Ira asks: \"Honestly, do you think I should have sex with him?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Absolutely not. End of discussion. Don't ask me that.\"","then":"Ira's face closes. \"Fine,\" she says, but she doesn't leave."},{"text":"\"It's your life, beta. Whatever you decide is fine with me.\"","then":"Ira nods, a bit let down. \"Okay. I thought you'd say more.\""},{"text":"\"Has something already happened? Tell me the truth.\"","then":"Ira stiffens. \"No. And now I'm sorry I asked.\""},{"text":"\"I'll give you the facts and what we believe. Both matter.\"","then":"Ira sits down. \"Okay. Both, then.\" She looks relieved you didn't panic.","best":true}],"why":"Offering facts and your values together respects her and keeps the talk going."},{"prompt":"After a pause, Ira asks: \"So what do I actually need to know?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Consent both ways, every time, and how to stay protected.\"","then":"Ira nods, listening closely, and asks two clear questions about protection.","best":true},{"text":"\"That it can ruin your life. That's all you need.\"","then":"Ira rolls her eyes. \"That's not a fact. That's a threat.\""},{"text":"\"Don't ask me about that. It's not a parent's job.\"","then":"Ira shrugs. \"Fine. I'll look it up online, then.\" But she stays put."},{"text":"\"Just that you're too young, whatever your friends might say.\"","then":"Ira sighs. \"That's not what I asked.\""}],"why":"Honest safety facts protect her whatever she decides."},{"prompt":"Ira asks: \"And what do you actually think? Honestly.\"","options":[{"text":"\"If you do, I'll be very disappointed in you.\"","then":"Ira's shoulders drop. She hears a threat, not a value."},{"text":"\"We hope you'll wait till you're older. Here's why.\"","then":"Ira listens. \"I don't fully agree. But I get why you think that.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"I don't have an opinion. It's totally up to you.\"","then":"Ira frowns. \"Really? Nothing?\" Your values stay a mystery to her."},{"text":"\"Whatever your friends are doing is probably fine.\"","then":"Ira looks surprised, and unsure what you mean."}],"why":"Sharing your values openly, with your reasons, guides her without forcing her."},{"prompt":"A week later, Ira says: \"I think I'll wait a bit. But I want to decide myself.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Good. And I'll be keeping an eye on the two of you.\"","then":"Ira stiffens, and starts meeting Kiran where you won't see."},{"text":"\"Good girl. I knew you'd come round and see sense.\"","then":"Ira's smile fades. She hears that only one answer was allowed."},{"text":"\"That's fair. Whatever you decide, you can talk to me.\"","then":"Ira smiles. \"Thanks for not freaking out.\" The door stays open.","best":true},{"text":"\"Just don't tell your grandparents we talked about this.\"","then":"Ira nods, and learns that these talks are something to hide."}],"why":"Respecting her right to decide keeps her coming back to you, whatever she chooses."}],"relearn":"Answering a big question with honest facts and your values, not a shutdown, is what truly protects a teen."},
  {"id":"tk-1317","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"stay askable eye-roll","hook":"You mention a news story about teens blackmailed online. Your daughter Tanvi, 14, groans.","setup":"She doesn't even look up from her book.","steps":[{"prompt":"Tanvi says: \"Ugh, not another talk. I know, I know.\"","options":[{"text":"\"You'll sit here and listen whether you like it or not.\"","then":"Tanvi slumps in her chair and tunes out after one sentence."},{"text":"\"Fair enough. No lecture. Just know I'm always around.\"","then":"Tanvi glances up. \"Okay,\" she says. The eye-roll is smaller this time.","best":true},{"text":"\"Fine. Don't come crying to me when it happens to you.\"","then":"Tanvi's jaw tightens, and she goes back to her book."},{"text":"\"Okay, okay. Sorry for caring about you so much, then.\"","then":"Tanvi sighs. \"Now you're upset.\" The moment turns into a sulk."}],"why":"Backing off without a lecture keeps you askable, which matters more than this one talk."},{"prompt":"A few days later, Tanvi asks: \"Can someone really blackmail you with a photo?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Only if you're silly enough to send one in the first place.\"","then":"Tanvi goes quiet, and files away that it would be her fault."},{"text":"\"Why do you ask? Has someone been asking you for one?\"","then":"Tanvi rolls her eyes. \"No. God. It was just a question.\""},{"text":"\"Sometimes. If it happens, it's never your fault. Tell me.\"","then":"Tanvi nods slowly. \"Never my fault. Okay. Good to know.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"See? That's why I wanted to have that talk with you.\"","then":"Tanvi groans. \"Forget I asked,\" she says."}],"why":"Answering straight, and saying it's never her fault, means she'll come to you if it happens."},{"prompt":"Months later, Tanvi says: \"My friend got a creepy message. Can I show you?\"","options":[{"text":"\"See? I told you this sort of thing happens.\"","then":"Tanvi's face falls. \"Forget it. I'll handle it.\""},{"text":"\"Of course. Thanks for trusting me with it.\"","then":"Tanvi hands you her phone, and together you work out how her friend can block and report.","best":true},{"text":"\"That's really her parents' business, not ours.\"","then":"Tanvi hesitates. \"But she's scared to tell them.\""},{"text":"\"Show me, and then you're staying off that app.\"","then":"Tanvi pulls the phone back. \"Never mind.\""}],"why":"Thanking her for trusting you proves that coming to you was worth it."}],"relearn":"Staying light and available with an eye-rolling teen keeps you a resource without forcing a lecture."},
  {"id":"tk-1318","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"repair a fumble","hook":"Yesterday your son Om, 13, asked about wet dreams, and you snapped that he's too young.","setup":"Today he's avoiding your eyes at breakfast.","steps":[{"prompt":"Om mumbles: \"Can you pass the bread?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Here you go. Eat up or you'll be late for school.\"","then":"Om nods and eats in silence. The question stays buried."},{"text":"\"Here. And about yesterday, let's pretend it didn't happen.\"","then":"Om shrugs. \"Sure.\" He looks relieved and let down at once."},{"text":"\"Here. And sorry about yesterday. That was a real question.\"","then":"Om looks up, surprised. \"It's fine,\" he says, but he's listening.","best":true},{"text":"\"Here. And you shouldn't be asking such things anyway.\"","then":"Om's ears go red. He leaves half his breakfast."}],"why":"Naming the brush-off yourself shows him it's safe to ask again."},{"prompt":"After school, Om says: \"My friend says wet dreams mean something's wrong with you.\"","options":[{"text":"\"We're not talking about that sort of thing, Om.\"","then":"Om nods, and keeps his friend's version."},{"text":"\"Not at all. They're a normal part of growing up.\"","then":"Om exhales. \"Oh. Okay. He was really scaring me.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Your friend should really mind his own business.\"","then":"Om shrugs, unsure who to believe now."},{"text":"\"Ask your uncle. He's better at this stuff than me.\"","then":"Om frowns. \"I'm not asking him,\" he says, and drops it."}],"why":"A calm, true answer replaces the myth and shows the door is really open."},{"prompt":"That night, Om asks: \"Why did you get so cross yesterday?\"","options":[{"text":"\"I wasn't cross at all, Om. You're just imagining things now.\"","then":"Om frowns, confused, and trusts his own memory a little less."},{"text":"\"Because some things aren't for children to ask.\"","then":"Om's face closes. The door you'd reopened swings shut again."},{"text":"\"Let's not go over all that again. It's done now.\"","then":"Om shrugs, still unsure whether asking is safe."},{"text":"\"I was caught off guard. That's on me, not your question.\"","then":"Om nods. \"Okay. So I can still ask you stuff?\" You tell him yes.","best":true}],"why":"Owning your part models honesty and shows him the door is always open."}],"relearn":"Going back to repair a fumbled answer models honesty and shows a teen the door is genuinely always open."},
  {"id":"tk-1319","cat":"the-teen-talks","type":"role-play","persona":"Priya","source":"affirm queer teen","hook":"Your daughter Mahi, 15, quietly tells you she thinks she might be bisexual.","setup":"She's sitting on the edge of your bed.","steps":[{"prompt":"Mahi whispers: \"Please don't be weird about it.\"","options":[{"text":"\"You're just confused, beta. It's only a phase.\"","then":"Mahi's face shuts. \"Yeah. Okay.\" She stays, picking at the bedsheet."},{"text":"\"How can you know that already? You're only fifteen.\"","then":"Mahi shrugs. \"I just do. I knew you wouldn't get it.\""},{"text":"\"Thank you for trusting me. I love you exactly as you are.\"","then":"Mahi's eyes fill, and she laughs with relief. \"Okay. Not weird.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Okay. Does that mean you have a girlfriend now?\"","then":"Mahi goes red. \"No! That's not what this is about.\""}],"why":"Thanks and unconditional love are what she most needs to hear first."},{"prompt":"Mahi glances at the door and asks: \"Are you going to tell Papa?\"","options":[{"text":"\"I have to. We don't keep secrets in this house.\"","then":"Mahi panics. \"Please, not yet. I'm not ready.\""},{"text":"\"Not unless you want me to. It's your news to share.\"","then":"Mahi nods. \"Maybe later. When I'm ready.\" She sounds steadier.","best":true},{"text":"\"Never. He wouldn't cope, so let's keep it between us.\"","then":"Mahi's face falls. She hears that her father can't love this part of her."},{"text":"\"I'll tell him tonight myself, so you don't have to.\"","then":"Mahi grabs your hand. \"No! I want to do it myself.\""}],"why":"Letting her choose who knows, and when, keeps her in charge of her own story."},{"prompt":"A few weeks later, Mahi asks: \"What if I'm wrong and I change my mind?\"","options":[{"text":"\"See? It's probably just a phase, then.\"","then":"Mahi's shoulders drop. \"Never mind,\" she says."},{"text":"\"Then pick one and stick with it, so people don't get confused.\"","then":"Mahi frowns. \"It doesn't work like that,\" she says quietly."},{"text":"\"Then that's okay too. You don't have to have it figured out.\"","then":"Mahi relaxes. \"Okay. That's a relief, honestly.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Let's not keep talking about labels. It's all so new.\"","then":"Mahi nods, and takes her questions to the internet instead."}],"why":"Letting her explore without pressure keeps you the parent she brings it all to."},{"prompt":"Months later, Mahi says: \"A girl in class said bi people are just greedy. Is that true?\"","options":[{"text":"\"No. That's a myth. Who you're drawn to is just part of you.\"","then":"Mahi nods. \"I knew it was rubbish. I just needed to hear it.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Just ignore her, sweetheart. People like that don't matter at all.\"","then":"Mahi shrugs. \"Easy for you to say.\" The comment still stings."},{"text":"\"Maybe keep it to yourself at school for now, then.\"","then":"Mahi goes quiet, and hears that hiding is the safe option."},{"text":"\"Give me her name. I'll call her parents tomorrow.\"","then":"Mahi groans. \"Please don't. That would make it so much worse.\""}],"why":"Busting the myth plainly protects her from the shame others try to hand her."}],"relearn":"Affirming a teen who shares their identity keeps them safe and close; dismissal teaches them to stop confiding."},
  {"id":"tk-1351","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"The school's sex-ed class means I don't need to say anything at home.\"","myth":{"un":"The school's sex-ed class means I don't need to say anything at home.","re":"School lessons help, but your everyday voice and values are the tool a class can't replace; do both.","why":"Home talks and school lessons work together, not instead."},"relearn":"A school class helps but doesn't replace your voice; your everyday talks and values are tools no class can give.","persona":"any","source":"school plus home"},
  {"id":"tk-1352","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"A good book left in their room does the whole job for me.\"","myth":{"un":"A good book left in their room does the whole job for me.","re":"A book is a useful tool, but your willingness to talk about it is what makes it land; pair the book with a chat.","why":"A book opens the topic; your conversation seals it."},"relearn":"A book is a helpful tool, but pairing it with your willingness to talk is what makes it work; don't rely on it alone.","persona":"Divya","source":"book plus talk"},
  {"id":"tk-1353","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"If I fumbled one answer, I've lost my chance and shouldn't try again.\"","myth":{"un":"If I fumbled one answer, I've lost my chance and shouldn't try again.","re":"You can always go back and repair a fumble; doing so models honesty and shows the door is genuinely open.","why":"A repaired fumble teaches more than a perfect answer."},"relearn":"A fumbled answer isn't the end; you can go back and repair it, which models honesty and reopens the door.","persona":"Divya","source":"repair not lose"},
  {"id":"tk-1354","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"These talks are the mother's job; fathers don't need to be involved.\"","myth":{"un":"These talks are the mother's job; fathers don't need to be involved.","re":"A child gains when both parents are askable; a second calm, open door doubles their trusted support.","why":"Two askable parents are stronger than one."},"relearn":"These talks aren't only a mother's job; when both parents stay askable, a child gains a second trusted door.","persona":"Vikram","source":"both parents"},
  {"id":"tk-1355","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"My child never asks, so there's clearly nothing I need to bring up.\"","myth":{"un":"My child never asks, so there's clearly nothing I need to bring up.","re":"A child who never asks may have learned it's unwelcome; gently opening the topic yourself is a key tool.","why":"Silence isn't 'no questions'; it can mean a closed door."},"relearn":"A child not asking may mean the door feels closed; gently raising topics yourself is a tool you can use.","persona":"any","source":"open it yourself"},
  {"id":"tk-1356","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"Worrying about my child's safety is overreacting; I should just let it go.\"","myth":{"un":"Worrying about my child's safety is overreacting; I should just let it go.","re":"A safety worry is worth taking seriously; seek guidance from Be the Safe Adult and Childline 1098 rather than brushing it off.","why":"Acting on a worry is care, not overreaction."},"relearn":"A safety worry is never overreacting; take it seriously and seek guidance, routing to Be the Safe Adult and Childline 1098.","persona":"Meena","source":"take it seriously"},
  {"id":"tk-1357","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"strike-rewrite","hook":"\"There's a single right script that works for every child and every age.\"","myth":{"un":"There's a single right script that works for every child and every age.","re":"Each age has its own headline focus; you fit the words to the child in front of you, not one fixed script.","why":"Age-right beats one-size-fits-all."},"relearn":"No single script fits every child; each age has its own focus, so you tune the words to the child in front of you.","persona":"any","source":"age-right words"},
  {"id":"tk-1358","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"low-pressure moment","hook":"You want to ask your son Reyansh, 12, how he's feeling about the changes of puberty.","steps":[{"prompt":"You're wondering when to bring it up. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Sit him down at the dining table for a proper talk","then":"Reyansh sits stiffly, answering \"fine\" to everything."},{"text":"Bring it up at family dinner, so it feels normal","then":"His cousins snigger, and Reyansh goes red to the ears."},{"text":"Wait for a relaxed drive or walk, side by side","then":"You hold off, and plan to raise it on your next drive with him.","best":true},{"text":"Send him a long WhatsApp message about it instead","then":"Reyansh replies with a thumbs-up and nothing else."}],"why":"Side by side, with no eye contact, it's easier for a child to open up."},{"prompt":"A few days later, you're driving Reyansh to cricket, just the two of you. How do you start?","options":[{"text":"Open with: 'We need to have a serious talk about puberty.'","then":"Reyansh stiffens and turns up the radio."},{"text":"Ask lightly if anything about growing up is on his mind","then":"Reyansh shrugs, then asks if it's normal that his voice keeps cracking.","best":true},{"text":"Say nothing, and hope he'll bring it up on his own","then":"The drive passes in easy silence, and the moment goes."},{"text":"Put on a podcast about puberty and let it do the talking","then":"Reyansh listens, says \"Okay,\" and asks nothing."}],"why":"A light, open question lets him lead, so he raises what actually worries him."},{"prompt":"After cricket, on the way home, Reyansh asks if everyone feels as awkward as he does. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Tell him not to be silly. It's all perfectly normal","then":"Reyansh nods, but looks embarrassed that he asked."},{"text":"Tell him boys shouldn't worry about such small things","then":"Reyansh goes quiet, and keeps the rest to himself."},{"text":"Say yes, and share a story from your own teen years","then":"Reyansh laughs at your story, and asks two more questions before you reach home.","best":true},{"text":"Turn it into a joke about his squeaky, cracking voice","then":"Reyansh laughs weakly, then puts his earphones in."}],"why":"Sharing your own awkward years shows him it's normal and keeps him talking."}],"debrief":"Pick a relaxed side-by-side moment, like a car ride, rather than a tense formal sit-down.","relearn":"A side-by-side moment, like a car ride, lowers pressure and helps a child talk; a formal sit-down shuts it down."},
  {"id":"tk-1359","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"teachable moment","hook":"You're watching a film with your daughter Aisha, 12. The hero keeps chasing a girl who's said no.","steps":[{"prompt":"Aisha is watching closely. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Switch the channel fast and say nothing about it","then":"Aisha looks puzzled, and the question she had goes unasked."},{"text":"Ask her lightly what she makes of how he treats her","then":"Aisha thinks. \"It's kind of creepy, actually. She said no.\"","best":true},{"text":"Say nothing. It's just a film, and she's enjoying it","then":"The film ends with them together, and the chase looks romantic."},{"text":"Pause it and explain at length why stalking is wrong","then":"Aisha sighs. \"I know.\" She asks if you can unpause it."}],"why":"A light question lets her think it through, so the lesson is hers."},{"prompt":"The next day, Aisha says her friends think the hero is so romantic. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Tell her that her friends are being silly about it","then":"\"They're not silly,\" Aisha says, and changes the subject."},{"text":"Agree that it's romantic, since it's only a story","then":"Aisha nods happily, and the chasing starts to look like love."},{"text":"Warn her never to go near a boy like that, ever","then":"Aisha rolls her eyes. \"It's a film,\" she says, and the talk ends."},{"text":"Ask her if it's romantic when someone ignores a no","then":"Aisha pauses. \"No. It'd be scary if it was real.\"","best":true}],"why":"A question links the story to real life without making her defend her friends."},{"prompt":"Weeks later, Aisha says a boy in class won't stop messaging her after she said no. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say it's not her fault, and ask how you can help","then":"Aisha relaxes. Together you block and report him, and she chooses to tell her teacher.","best":true},{"text":"Say he probably likes her, and she should be flattered","then":"Aisha looks unsure, and wonders if she should reply after all."},{"text":"March into school tomorrow and demand he's punished","then":"Aisha is mortified, and the whole class hears about it."},{"text":"Say to ignore him. He'll lose interest eventually","then":"Aisha tries, but the messages keep coming, and she stops mentioning them."}],"why":"Saying it's not her fault and letting her choose the help backs her no without taking over."}],"debrief":"Use everyday cues, like a film scene, as natural openings to talk, rather than switching away in silence.","relearn":"Everyday cues like a TV scene are natural openings to talk; switching away silently wastes the chance."},
  {"id":"tk-1360","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"find out together","hook":"Your son Kiaan, 10, asks if shaving makes hair grow back thicker. You're honestly not sure.","steps":[{"prompt":"He's waiting for your answer. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say yes, confidently. Everyone seems to say so","then":"Kiaan nods, and passes the claim on to his friends at school."},{"text":"Tell him to look it up on his phone himself later","then":"Kiaan finds a video by someone selling razors."},{"text":"Say it's a good question, and look it up together","then":"Kiaan grabs the tablet. \"Can we check now?\"","best":true},{"text":"Guess 'probably not', and move on to dinner","then":"Kiaan shrugs. He's still not sure, and neither are you."}],"why":"Finding out together is honest, and shows him how to check facts."},{"prompt":"Kiaan asks how you know which answers online to trust. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say anything with lots of views is probably right","then":"Kiaan nods, and starts trusting the loudest videos."},{"text":"Tell him to trust only you, and never look online","then":"Kiaan nods, then looks online anyway when you're busy."},{"text":"Show him how to check who wrote it, and why","then":"Kiaan tries it on a video. \"Oh. They're selling something,\" he says.","best":true},{"text":"Say it's too complicated to explain right now","then":"Kiaan shrugs, and goes back to scrolling."}],"why":"Teaching him to check sources builds a skill he'll use long after this question."},{"prompt":"A week later, Kiaan asks what a wet dream is. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say you're not sure, so you can skip the awkward bit","then":"\"Let's look it up, then!\" Kiaan says, and you're stuck."},{"text":"Tell him he'll learn all about that when he's older","then":"Kiaan shrugs, and asks his friends instead."},{"text":"Laugh nervously and ask him where he heard that word","then":"Kiaan goes red. \"Nowhere. Forget it.\""},{"text":"Answer simply and calmly, as you would any question","then":"Kiaan nods. \"Okay. So it's normal.\" He goes back to his homework.","best":true}],"why":"A calm, simple answer shows him no question is too awkward to bring to you."}],"debrief":"Admit you don't know and find a reliable answer together, rather than inventing one.","relearn":"'Let's find out together' models honesty and good information-finding; making one up risks teaching wrong facts."},
  {"id":"tk-1361","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"shared line","hook":"Your partner Neha feels your daughter Sara, 8, is too young to learn about periods. You disagree.","steps":[{"prompt":"Sara asks about a pad she found, with Neha right there. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Answer Sara in full, right there, whatever Neha thinks","then":"Sara listens, but Neha goes silent, and the evening turns frosty."},{"text":"Argue it out with Neha, then and there, in front of Sara","then":"Sara looks from one of you to the other, and quietly leaves the room."},{"text":"Tell Sara it's a good question you'll answer after dinner","then":"Sara nods and goes back to her colouring. Neha looks grateful.","best":true},{"text":"Let Neha say 'it's nothing', and drop it for good","then":"Sara shrugs, but she keeps the pad and looks puzzled all evening."}],"why":"Honouring the question and parking it briefly buys time to agree a line with Neha."},{"prompt":"That night, alone, Neha says Sara will only get scared. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Ask what worries her, and share why early is less scary","then":"Neha admits her own first period terrified her. \"Maybe that's why,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"Tell her she's being old-fashioned, like her mother","then":"Neha's face hardens, and the talk becomes a fight."},{"text":"Give in to keep the peace. Sara can surely wait a few more years","then":"Neha relaxes. The next day, Sara asks her about the pad again."},{"text":"Say you'll tell Sara yourself, whatever she thinks","then":"Neha goes quiet. \"Then why ask me at all?\""}],"why":"Hearing her worry first, then sharing why, turns a standoff into teamwork."},{"prompt":"The next evening, Neha admits Sara keeps asking, and says you must agree an answer together. What do you propose?","options":[{"text":"Every detail at once, so she never needs to ask again","then":"Neha looks worried. \"That's a lot for an eight-year-old.\""},{"text":"A vague line about 'growing up', nothing specific","then":"Neha agrees, but you both know it won't answer Sara's questions."},{"text":"Each of you answers in your own way, whatever comes up","then":"You nod, but Sara will now get two different stories."},{"text":"A short, true outline of periods that you'll both use","then":"You write down a few lines together. Neha looks relieved.","best":true}],"why":"One shared, age-right line gives Sara a calm, consistent message."},{"prompt":"A few days later, Sara asks about the pad again at dinner. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Let Neha answer it alone, and keep quiet yourself this time","then":"Neha answers, glancing at you for backup that doesn't come."},{"text":"Answer her together, calmly, with a short and true outline","then":"Sara listens, asks one question, then says, \"Okay. Can I tell Nani?\"","best":true},{"text":"Tell her you'll explain it all when she's older","then":"Sara frowns, and asks a friend at school the next day."},{"text":"Hand her a book about it, and leave her to read","then":"Sara flips through the pictures, confused, and puts it away."}],"why":"Speaking together shows Sara that both of you are safe people to ask."}],"debrief":"Agree a shared, age-right line with your co-parent privately, rather than arguing in front of your child.","relearn":"Agree a shared, age-right line privately so a child gets one calm message; don't argue in front of them."},
  {"id":"tk-1362","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","persona":"Meena","source":"route a worry","hook":"Your son Ayaan, 9, says his friend Rudra is scared of a man who visits their building.","steps":[{"prompt":"Ayaan looks worried. Rudra made him promise not to tell. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Tell him to stay out of it. It's Rudra's family's business","then":"Ayaan nods, but lies awake worrying about his friend."},{"text":"Ask Ayaan to tell you every detail that Rudra told him","then":"Ayaan gets flustered and muddles what Rudra said."},{"text":"Thank him, and say this is a secret it's right to tell","then":"Ayaan breathes out. \"I didn't want to be a snitch,\" he says.","best":true},{"text":"Say Rudra is probably exaggerating to get attention","then":"Ayaan frowns. \"He wasn't. He was really scared.\""}],"why":"Hearing that an unsafe secret is okay to tell keeps him speaking up for his friend."},{"prompt":"Later, you can't stop thinking about what Ayaan said. What do you do next?","options":[{"text":"Wait and see whether Ayaan brings it up again","then":"A week passes. Ayaan says Rudra has stopped coming down to play."},{"text":"Take it seriously and call Childline 1098 for guidance","then":"The counsellor listens, takes the details, and explains how they'll help Rudra.","best":true},{"text":"Question Rudra yourself next time he comes over","then":"Rudra goes pale, runs home, and won't come over again."},{"text":"Tell the building WhatsApp group to watch out for the man","then":"Rumours fly, the man hears of it, and Rudra's family is upset."}],"why":"Expert guidance protects Rudra without putting him on the spot. None of this is his fault."},{"prompt":"Ayaan asks whether he's got Rudra into trouble. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Maybe, so he mustn't tell anyone else about it","then":"Ayaan's eyes widen, and he decides never to repeat anything again."},{"text":"Tell him it's handled, and not to think about it","then":"Ayaan nods, but lies awake worrying about Rudra."},{"text":"Tell him he did the right thing, then change the subject","then":"Ayaan nods, but asks the same question again at bedtime."},{"text":"No. Telling a grown-up is how children get help","then":"Ayaan nods. \"So I helped?\" You tell him yes.","best":true}],"why":"Hearing that telling is how children get help means he'll speak up again."},{"prompt":"Weeks later, Ayaan asks what to do if something like this happens again. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Stay out of other children's problems next time","then":"Ayaan nods, and learns that a friend in trouble is none of his business."},{"text":"Tell a safe grown-up, even if someone says keep it secret","then":"Ayaan repeats it. \"Even if they make me promise.\" You nod.","best":true},{"text":"Try to sort it out himself, with his friend, first","then":"Ayaan looks unsure. He's nine, and some things are too big for him."},{"text":"Only ever tell you, and never tell a teacher or anyone else","then":"Ayaan nods, but if you're not around, he has no one."}],"why":"A simple rule gives him a safe plan, whatever he faces next."}],"debrief":"Take a worry about another child seriously and seek guidance via Be the Safe Adult and Childline 1098.","relearn":"If a child hints another child is harmed, take it seriously and seek guidance via Be the Safe Adult and Childline 1098."},
  {"id":"tk-1363","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","persona":"Divya","source":"go back and repair","hook":"Yesterday your son Rehaan, 5, asked why his friend has two mums. You snapped at him to stop.","steps":[{"prompt":"Today he's quiet and keeps away from you. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Pretend it never happened, and hope he soon forgets","then":"Rehaan stays quiet all day, and asks his teacher instead."},{"text":"Buy him a treat to make up for it, and say nothing","then":"Rehaan grins at the chocolate, but his question stays buried."},{"text":"Say sorry you snapped, and that he can ask you again","then":"Rehaan peeks up at you. \"Can I ask now?\" he says.","best":true},{"text":"Explain that you were tired, so it wasn't really your fault","then":"Rehaan nods, and learns it's his job to catch you at the right time."}],"why":"Saying sorry and inviting the question again reopens the door you closed."},{"prompt":"At bedtime, Rehaan asks again why his friend has two mums. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"That families come in many shapes, and all can be loving","then":"Rehaan nods. \"Like Aryan lives with his Nani,\" he says, satisfied.","best":true},{"text":"That it's complicated, and he'll understand when older","then":"Rehaan frowns. \"But why?\" The question stays open."},{"text":"That it's not something we talk about in our house","then":"Rehaan goes quiet, and learns this topic is off limits."},{"text":"That his friend's family is just a bit different, that's all","then":"Rehaan thinks. \"Different bad or different good?\" he asks."}],"why":"A simple, warm answer at his level satisfies him and models respect."},{"prompt":"A week later, before asking something, Rehaan checks whether you'll get cross again. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Say that depends on what sort of question it is","then":"Rehaan hesitates, then decides it's not worth the risk."},{"text":"Laugh and promise you'll never, ever be cross again","then":"Rehaan looks unsure. He remembers last week."},{"text":"Tell him to stop fussing about it and just ask","then":"Rehaan mumbles \"never mind\" and runs off to play."},{"text":"Say his questions are always welcome, and listen","then":"Rehaan beams and asks his question. You answer it simply.","best":true}],"why":"Showing his questions are welcome, after a slip, keeps the door truly open."}],"debrief":"Go back and repair a snapped-at moment; it reopens the door and shows mistakes can be fixed.","relearn":"Going back to repair after you snapped reopens the door and shows mistakes are fixable; pretending leaves it shut."},
  {"id":"tk-1364","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","persona":"any","source":"kindly hold the line","hook":"Nanaji lives with you, and he's upset that you teach your son Advik, 6, about body safety.","steps":[{"prompt":"He says it will put dirty thoughts in Advik's head. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Drop the talks for now, to keep the peace at home","then":"Nanaji nods, pleased. Advik's lessons stop halfway."},{"text":"Kindly explain that it keeps Advik safe, and carry on","then":"Nanaji grumbles, \"In my day...\" but listens to the end.","best":true},{"text":"Tell him he doesn't understand modern parenting","then":"Nanaji's face falls. \"So I'm a fool now?\" he says."},{"text":"Keep teaching, but only when he's not around to see","then":"Nanaji is content. Advik notices you go quiet whenever Nanaji walks in."}],"why":"Explaining kindly why the facts protect Advik holds your line without a fight."},{"prompt":"At dinner, Advik proudly tells Nanaji that his body belongs to him. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Hush him quickly, before Nanaji has a chance to react","then":"Advik looks confused, and wonders if he said something wrong."},{"text":"Change the subject to his homework before a scene starts","then":"Advik answers about his homework, his proud moment gone."},{"text":"Smile and back him: 'That's right, beta. It does.'","then":"Advik beams. Nanaji raises an eyebrow, then says nothing.","best":true},{"text":"Laugh it off as something he picked up at school","then":"\"No, you taught me,\" Advik says, frowning."}],"why":"Backing Advik calmly shows him his safety words are something to be proud of."},{"prompt":"Later, Nanaji says children in his day learned all this on their own. What do you say?","options":[{"text":"Say times are different now, and leave it at that","then":"Nanaji shrugs, unconvinced, and the gap between you stays."},{"text":"Tell him that silence is exactly how children get hurt","then":"Nanaji stiffens, hurt. \"Are you saying I failed you?\""},{"text":"Ask what he wishes he'd been told, and listen","then":"Nanaji is quiet. \"No one told us anything,\" he says at last.","best":true},{"text":"Agree with him, just to bring the argument to an end","then":"Nanaji nods, satisfied, and brings it up again next week."}],"why":"Asking about his own past turns an argument into shared understanding."},{"prompt":"A month later, Nanaji asks what exactly you tell Advik. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Walk him through the few simple rules you've taught","then":"Nanaji listens. \"Tell a safe grown-up. Hm. That's sensible,\" he admits.","best":true},{"text":"Say it's between you and Advik, so he needn't worry","then":"Nanaji feels shut out, and his doubts grow."},{"text":"Water it down so it sounds like nothing much at all","then":"Nanaji nods, but later tells Advik to forget \"all that\"."},{"text":"Hand him an article, and let that do the convincing","then":"Nanaji puts on his glasses, skims it, and sets it aside."}],"why":"Sharing the simple rules openly can turn a doubter into another safe adult."}],"debrief":"Kindly hold your line on your child's safety facts, even when a grandparent disapproves.","relearn":"Kindly keep your child's safety facts in place even if a grandparent disapproves; dropping them for peace leaves a child exposed."},
  {"id":"tk-1365","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"branch","persona":"Vikram","source":"reliable source","hook":"Your daughter Gurleen, 13, wants to read up on periods and body changes by herself.","steps":[{"prompt":"She asks where she can find information she can trust. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Tell her to just search online and figure it out herself","then":"Gurleen's first result is a forum full of scary stories."},{"text":"Find a reliable, age-right source, and offer to read along","then":"Gurleen picks a book with you, and asks if you'll read one chapter together.","best":true},{"text":"Say she doesn't need to be reading about all that yet","then":"Gurleen shrugs, and looks it up on her friend's phone."},{"text":"Give her a good book, and leave her to it privately","then":"Gurleen reads it alone, and gets stuck on a word she won't ask about."}],"why":"A trusted source plus your company gives her facts and someone to ask."},{"prompt":"A few days later, Gurleen shows you a reel saying girls on their period shouldn't exercise. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Laugh and say all reels are complete rubbish anyway","then":"\"Not all of them,\" Gurleen says, and keeps scrolling."},{"text":"Agree, since Nani always said the same thing","then":"Gurleen nods, and sits out football that week."},{"text":"Check it together against a reliable source","then":"You look it up together. Gurleen grins. \"So I can still play football.\"","best":true},{"text":"Tell her to stop watching reels altogether","then":"Gurleen rolls her eyes, and keeps watching them anyway."}],"why":"Checking claims together teaches her how to test what she sees."},{"prompt":"Weeks later, Gurleen asks something her reading doesn't cover. What do you do?","options":[{"text":"Tell her to keep searching on her own, since it's all out there","then":"Gurleen shrugs, and asks her friends instead."},{"text":"Make up a quick answer, so she's not left hanging","then":"Gurleen believes you, and repeats it to her friends at school."},{"text":"Say it's not something you're comfortable talking about","then":"Gurleen nods, and decides not to bother anyone about it."},{"text":"Say you're glad she asked, and find out the answer together","then":"Gurleen settles in beside you, and the two of you read up on it.","best":true}],"why":"Staying involved as her questions grow keeps you her trusted co-reader."}],"debrief":"Point a teen to a reliable, age-right source and offer to explore it together.","relearn":"Point a teen to a reliable, age-right source and offer to read it together, not a blind online search."},
  {"id":"tk-1366","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each parent's hard moment to the tool that helps.","pairs":[{"left":"You freeze on a sudden question","right":"A simple script you readied earlier"},{"left":"You don't know the answer","right":"'Let's find out together' and a good source"},{"left":"You snapped and regret it","right":"Go back and repair the moment"},{"left":"Something said worries you","right":"Be the Safe Adult and Childline 1098"},{"left":"Your co-parent feels left out","right":"Invite them to be askable too"}],"relearn":"Each hard moment has a tool: a script, finding out together, repair, the safeguarding route, or a co-parent.","persona":"any","source":"moment to tool"},
  {"id":"tk-1367","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each age to a ready first-line to keep handy.","pairs":[{"left":"A curious four-year-old","right":"'That's the proper name, like elbow.'"},{"left":"A pre-teen before puberty","right":"'Your body will change soon; that's normal.'"},{"left":"A teen on relationships","right":"'No judgement; you can always ask me.'"},{"left":"Any child, after you fumbled","right":"'I didn't answer well; let's talk now.'"},{"left":"A child who shares a scary thing","right":"'Thank you for telling me, you're safe.'"}],"relearn":"Each age has a first-line: proper names, normalising changes, no-judgement for teens, repair, thanking a disclosure.","persona":"any","source":"ready first-lines"},
  {"id":"tk-1368","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each parenting goal to the everyday habit that builds it.","pairs":[{"left":"Stay your child's go-to source","right":"Answer calmly, every time"},{"left":"Make hard questions easier","right":"Welcome the easy ones warmly first"},{"left":"Keep talks low-pressure","right":"Chat side-by-side, in the car or kitchen"},{"left":"Show the door is always open","right":"Repair it openly when you get one wrong"},{"left":"Cover the right things in time","right":"Follow the age-by-age headline focus"}],"relearn":"Habits build the goals: calm answers, welcoming small questions, side-by-side chats, open repair, and an age-by-age focus.","persona":"any","source":"goal to habit"},
  {"id":"tk-1369","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each real India worry to a calm, doable response.","pairs":[{"left":"'Log kya kahenge if I teach this?'","right":"Your child's safety comes before opinions"},{"left":"'My elders never told me anything'","right":"You can give what you never got"},{"left":"'I'll say the wrong thing'","right":"Repair it; an honest fix beats silence"},{"left":"'I'm too embarrassed'","right":"Start with one small, factual sentence"},{"left":"'No time in our busy home'","right":"Use car rides and bedtimes for tiny talks"}],"relearn":"Worries each have a response: safety over opinions, breaking the silence, repairing, starting small, tiny moments.","persona":"any","source":"worry to response"},
  {"id":"tk-1370","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each thing a parent says to whether it opens or closes the door, and why.","pairs":[{"left":"'Great question, let's talk'","right":"Opens it: rewards coming to you"},{"left":"'You'll understand when older'","right":"Closes it: tells them not to ask"},{"left":"'I don't know, let's find out'","right":"Opens it: models honest learning"},{"left":"'We don't discuss such things'","right":"Closes it: sends them online"},{"left":"'Thanks for telling me, you're safe'","right":"Opens it: makes telling feel safe"}],"relearn":"Welcoming, honest, reassuring lines open the door; 'you're too young' and 'we don't discuss that' close it.","persona":"any","source":"open or close"},
  {"id":"tk-1371","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each child age to the safe route or support that fits a worry.","pairs":[{"left":"Any child says someone hurt them","right":"Stay calm, believe them, call Childline 1098"},{"left":"You need guidance on a safety worry","right":"Be the Safe Adult (g69)"},{"left":"An emergency right now","right":"112"},{"left":"You fumbled and want a redo","right":"Go back and repair the talk"},{"left":"You feel alone in the talks","right":"Invite your co-parent to be askable too"}],"relearn":"Match the route: Childline 1098 if a child was hurt, Be the Safe Adult for guidance, 112 in an emergency, repair, or a co-parent.","persona":"any","source":"route to support"},
  {"id":"tk-1372","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each ready script to the question it answers calmly.","pairs":[{"left":"'Where do babies come from?'","right":"A simple, true answer at their level"},{"left":"'What's a period?'","right":"'A normal, healthy sign of growing up'"},{"left":"'What does that rude word mean?'","right":"Define it plainly, then share your view"},{"left":"'Is what I saw online real?'","right":"'A lot of it isn't; let's talk about what is'"},{"left":"'Can I say no to a hug?'","right":"'Yes, your body is yours'"}],"relearn":"Questions each have a script: a simple true answer, normalising periods, plain definitions, porn-literacy, 'your body is yours'.","persona":"any","source":"script to question"},
  {"id":"tk-1373","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each part of the parent's kit to what it does.","pairs":[{"left":"Be askable","right":"Keeps your child bringing questions to you"},{"left":"Keep it age-right","right":"Makes each answer land at their level"},{"left":"Give facts and your values","right":"Offers safety and your guidance together"},{"left":"Route real worries to help","right":"Gets a child support when safety's at risk"},{"left":"Repair your fumbles","right":"Shows the door is genuinely always open"}],"relearn":"The kit: be askable, keep it age-right, give facts and values, route real worries to help, and repair fumbles, each doing its own job.","persona":"any","source":"the kit"},
  {"id":"tk-1374","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each 'I can't because...' to the reframe that frees a parent to start.","pairs":[{"left":"'I'm not an expert'","right":"Learn alongside; willingness is enough"},{"left":"'I had one bad attempt'","right":"Repair it; the door reopens any time"},{"left":"'It's the school's job'","right":"Your voice is what school can't give"},{"left":"'My child never asks'","right":"Gently open the topic yourself"},{"left":"'Too late, they're teens'","right":"The door matters more in the teen years"}],"relearn":"Every 'I can't' has a reframe: learn alongside, repair, your voice matters, open it yourself, never too late.","persona":"any","source":"reframe to start"},
  {"id":"tk-1375","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each everyday opening to the topic it makes easy to raise.","pairs":[{"left":"A relative's new baby","right":"Where babies come from, simply"},{"left":"A wedding in the family","right":"Relationships, consent and respect"},{"left":"A news story about online scams","right":"Online safety and telling you about 'off' things"},{"left":"A cousin starting her period","right":"Periods as a normal sign of growing up"},{"left":"A film about a crush","right":"Feelings, boundaries and saying no"}],"relearn":"Everyday life offers openings: a new baby, a wedding, online-scam news, a cousin's period, or a film each makes a topic easy.","persona":"any","source":"opening to topic"},
  {"id":"tk-1376","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"match","hook":"Match each sign you're becoming more askable to the move that builds it.","pairs":[{"left":"They bring you the small stuff","right":"You stayed calm last time"},{"left":"They tell you scary online things","right":"You thanked them, not punished"},{"left":"They ask the awkward questions","right":"You answered earlier ones without shame"},{"left":"They come back after a misstep","right":"You went back and repaired it"},{"left":"They trust your facts over the feed","right":"You gave honest answers before"}],"relearn":"You grow more askable by staying calm, thanking disclosures, answering without shame, repairing, and honest answers.","persona":"any","source":"sign to move"},
  {"id":"tk-1377","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each move: keeps you askable, or quietly closes the door?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Answering calmly, every time"},{"id":"b","text":"Reacting with anger or panic"},{"id":"c","text":"Going back to repair a fumble"},{"id":"d","text":"Saying 'you're too young' to dodge it"},{"id":"e","text":"Thanking them for a hard question"},{"id":"f","text":"Mocking a question as silly"}],"bins":[{"id":"askable","label":"Keeps you askable","valence":"pos"},{"id":"closes","label":"Closes the door","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"askable","b":"closes","c":"askable","d":"closes","e":"askable","f":"closes"},"relearn":"Calm answers, repair and thanking hard questions keep you askable; anger, 'you're too young' and mockery close the door.","persona":"any","source":"askable or closes"},
  {"id":"tk-1378","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each one: a real tool in the parent's kit, or a myth that holds you back?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"A few ready, age-right scripts"},{"id":"b","text":"'I must be an expert first'"},{"id":"c","text":"Learning alongside your child"},{"id":"d","text":"'One book does the whole job'"},{"id":"e","text":"The safeguarding route for real worries"},{"id":"f","text":"'The school handles all of it'"}],"bins":[{"id":"tool","label":"Real tool","valence":"pos"},{"id":"myth","label":"Myth to drop","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"tool","b":"myth","c":"tool","d":"myth","e":"tool","f":"myth"},"relearn":"Ready scripts, learning alongside and a safeguarding route are real tools; 'be an expert first', 'a book does it' and 'the school handles it' are myths.","persona":"any","source":"tool or myth"},
  {"id":"tk-1379","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each worry by where it belongs: call Childline 1098, seek guidance, or just keep talking.","items":[{"id":"a","text":"A child says someone hurt them"},{"id":"b","text":"You're unsure if it's a red flag"},{"id":"c","text":"An awkward but innocent question"},{"id":"d","text":"A disclosure of ongoing abuse"},{"id":"e","text":"You worry but have no clear sign"},{"id":"f","text":"Just curious about bodies"}],"bins":[{"id":"call","label":"Call Childline 1098","valence":"tell"},{"id":"guide","label":"Seek guidance (g69)","valence":"uhoh"},{"id":"talk","label":"Keep talking","valence":"pos"}],"key":{"a":"call","b":"guide","c":"talk","d":"call","e":"guide","f":"talk"},"relearn":"A child hurt means call Childline 1098; an unclear worry, seek guidance (g69); ordinary curiosity, keep talking calmly.","persona":"any","source":"where it belongs"},
  {"id":"tk-1380","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each habit: a sustainable everyday tool, or one that burns out fast?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Tiny talks at bedtime or in the car"},{"id":"b","text":"One long, scheduled lecture a year"},{"id":"c","text":"Answering questions as they come up"},{"id":"d","text":"Waiting till you feel fully expert"},{"id":"e","text":"Using everyday cues to start"},{"id":"f","text":"Cramming everything into one talk"}],"bins":[{"id":"sustain","label":"Sustainable tool","valence":"pos"},{"id":"burns","label":"Burns out","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"sustain","b":"burns","c":"sustain","d":"burns","e":"sustain","f":"burns"},"relearn":"Tiny everyday talks, answering as questions arise and using cues are sustainable; one yearly lecture, waiting to feel expert and cramming burn out.","persona":"any","source":"sustainable or burns"},
  {"id":"tk-1381","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each response to 'I don't know the answer': a good tool, or one to avoid?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"'Let's find a reliable answer together'"},{"id":"b","text":"Making up an answer to look sure"},{"id":"c","text":"'Good question, give me a day to check'"},{"id":"d","text":"'Stop asking me things like that'"},{"id":"e","text":"Looking it up with them in a good source"},{"id":"f","text":"Pretending you didn't hear"}],"bins":[{"id":"good","label":"Good move","valence":"pos"},{"id":"avoid","label":"Avoid it","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"good","b":"avoid","c":"good","d":"avoid","e":"good","f":"avoid"},"relearn":"Finding out together, honestly buying time and looking it up in a good source are good moves; inventing answers, snapping and ignoring are not.","persona":"Vikram","source":"i dont know move"},
  {"id":"tk-1382","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each into the age its headline focus fits best.","items":[{"id":"a","text":"Correct names and safe-vs-unsafe touch"},{"id":"b","text":"Preparing for periods and wet dreams"},{"id":"c","text":"Consent and respect in relationships"},{"id":"d","text":"'You're the boss of your body'"},{"id":"e","text":"First online-safety basics"},{"id":"f","text":"Porn-literacy and the manosphere"}],"bins":[{"id":"young","label":"Early years","valence":"neutral"},{"id":"before","label":"Before puberty","valence":"neutral"},{"id":"teen","label":"Teen years","valence":"neutral"}],"key":{"a":"young","b":"before","c":"teen","d":"young","e":"before","f":"teen"},"relearn":"Correct names and body ownership are early-years; period prep and online basics come before puberty; consent and porn-literacy are teen-years.","persona":"any","source":"age focus sort"},
  {"id":"tk-1383","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each move: brings your co-parent into the talks, or pushes them out?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"'Let's agree a line, then talk to them'"},{"id":"b","text":"'You always say the wrong thing'"},{"id":"c","text":"Sharing a ready script with them"},{"id":"d","text":"Doing every talk alone, resentfully"},{"id":"e","text":"'Even just being calm and askable helps'"},{"id":"f","text":"Mocking their attempt in front of the child"}],"bins":[{"id":"brings","label":"Brings them in","valence":"pos"},{"id":"pushes","label":"Pushes them out","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"brings","b":"pushes","c":"brings","d":"pushes","e":"brings","f":"pushes"},"relearn":"Agreeing a line, sharing a script and 'just be calm and askable' bring a co-parent in; criticising, going it alone and mocking push them out.","persona":"any","source":"co-parent in or out"},
  {"id":"tk-1384","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"sort","hook":"Sort each: a ready, age-right script, or one to rework before you use it?","items":[{"id":"a","text":"'That's the proper name, like elbow.'"},{"id":"b","text":"'Only bad children ask about that.'"},{"id":"c","text":"'No judgement, you can always ask me.'"},{"id":"d","text":"'We never speak of such dirty things.'"},{"id":"e","text":"'Thanks for telling me, you're not in trouble.'"},{"id":"f","text":"'You'll find out the hard way one day.'"}],"bins":[{"id":"ready","label":"Ready to use","valence":"pos"},{"id":"rework","label":"Rework it","valence":"neg"}],"key":{"a":"ready","b":"rework","c":"ready","d":"rework","e":"ready","f":"rework"},"relearn":"Calm, naming and no-judgement lines are ready to use; shaming, 'we don't speak of that' and scare-lines need reworking before you use them.","persona":"any","source":"ready or rework"},
  {"id":"tk-1385","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: the words you give your child are often the ones nobody gave you, and that's the cycle ending. Feel it?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Feel it","Cycle ending","Giving what I missed"],"affirm":"Handing your child the openness and words you never received is how the silence ends with you, on purpose.","relearn":"The words you give your child may be ones nobody gave you; that's the silence cycle ending with you.","persona":"any","source":"cycle ends here"},
  {"id":"tk-1386","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: you don't need every answer ready, just the willingness to find it with them. Sit right?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Sits right","Willingness is enough","Learn together"],"affirm":"Being willing to learn alongside your child matters more than having every answer; your openness is the real tool.","relearn":"You don't need every answer ready; the willingness to find it with your child is the tool that counts.","persona":"Vikram","source":"willingness is the tool"},
  {"id":"tk-1387","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: a fumbled talk you go back to repair teaches more than a perfect one ever could. Agree?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Agree","Repair teaches","Worth going back"],"affirm":"Going back to repair a fumble shows your child the door is genuinely open and that honesty beats perfection.","relearn":"A fumble you go back and repair teaches honesty and that the door is genuinely always open.","persona":"Divya","source":"repair teaches more"},
  {"id":"tk-1388","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: a second calm, askable parent in the home doubles your child's trusted doors. Worth bringing them in?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Worth it","Two doors","Bring them in"],"affirm":"When both parents stay calm and askable, a child has two trusted doors instead of one, and that's real protection.","relearn":"A second calm, askable parent doubles a child's trusted doors; it's worth bringing your co-parent in.","persona":"any","source":"two trusted doors"},
  {"id":"tk-1389","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: keeping a few ready scripts means a hard question meets calm, not a freeze. Useful tool?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Useful","No more freeze","Ready helps"],"affirm":"Readying a few simple scripts ahead of time lets a sudden hard question meet your calm instead of a panicked freeze.","relearn":"A few ready scripts mean a hard question meets your calm, not a freeze; preparing ahead is a real tool.","persona":"Divya","source":"ready beats freeze"},
  {"id":"tk-1390","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: routing a real safety worry to help isn't failing as a parent, it's exactly the right move. Land?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Lands","Right move","Get them help"],"affirm":"Taking a safety worry seriously and seeking guidance via Be the Safe Adult and Childline 1098 is good parenting, not failure.","relearn":"Routing a real safety worry to Be the Safe Adult and Childline 1098 is the right move, not a parenting failure.","persona":"Meena","source":"routing is right"},
  {"id":"tk-1391","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: the whole kit is just this, be askable, age-right, give facts and values, route real worries. Feel ready?","prompt":"What's your take?","options":["Ready","I hold the kit","Got this"],"affirm":"Being askable, age-appropriate, honest with your values, and ready to route real worries is the whole kit, and it's yours.","relearn":"The kit is simple: be askable, age-right, give facts and values, and route real worries to help; you already hold it.","persona":"any","source":"hold the kit"},
  {"id":"tk-1392","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"reflect","hook":"Lensy: tiny talks in the car or at bedtime add up to more than one big dreaded lecture ever would. Resonate?","prompt":"What do you think?","options":["Resonates","Tiny adds up","Small and steady"],"affirm":"Lots of tiny, low-pressure talks over time build more trust and safety than one big, dreaded lecture ever could.","relearn":"Tiny talks at bedtime or in the car add up to more than one dreaded lecture; small and steady is the tool.","persona":"any","source":"tiny adds up"},
  {"id":"tk-1393","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two red-flag moves that quietly close a child's door, among calm, askable ones.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Answering the question calmly and simply","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Snapping 'why would you ask that?'","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Thanking them for coming to you","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Laughing the question off as silly","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Saying 'good question, let's talk'","trick":false}],"why":"Snapping and laughing a question off are the red flags; they teach a child not to ask you again, unlike calm, welcoming answers.","relearn":"Snapping and mocking a question close the door; calm, welcoming, thankful answers keep a child coming to you.","persona":"any","source":"spot door-closers"},
  {"id":"tk-1394","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"A child shares something worrying. Spot the two responses that fail to keep them safe.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Staying calm and believing them","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Telling them they must be exaggerating","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Saying 'thank you for telling me'","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Promising to keep it a total secret","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Seeking guidance via Be the Safe Adult","trick":false}],"why":"Doubting the child and promising total secrecy are the red flags.","relearn":"Doubting a child or promising secrecy fails them; stay calm, believe them, thank them and seek guidance via Be the Safe Adult.","persona":"Meena","source":"spot unsafe responses"},
  {"id":"tk-1395","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two myths that keep a parent from using the tools, among the true reassurances.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"You can learn alongside your child","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"You must be an expert before you start","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"A fumble can always be repaired","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"One bad talk means you've lost your chance","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Small everyday talks really do add up","trick":false}],"why":"'Be an expert first' and 'one bad talk ends it' are the myths to catch.","relearn":"'Be an expert first' and 'one fumble ends it' are myths; you can learn alongside your child, repair, and small talks add up.","persona":"Vikram","source":"spot the myths"},
  {"id":"tk-1396","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two unhelpful 'tools' a parent might reach for, among the genuinely useful ones.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"A few simple, age-right ready scripts","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"A scare story to frighten them into care","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Everyday cues like a TV scene to start","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Shaming them so they never ask again","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"The safeguarding route for real worries","trick":false}],"why":"A scare story and shaming are the red flags; real tools are ready scripts, everyday cues and the safeguarding route.","relearn":"Scaring or shaming a child aren't tools; ready scripts, everyday cues and the safeguarding route are.","persona":"any","source":"spot unhelpful tools"},
  {"id":"tk-1397","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two moves that push a co-parent out of the talks, among the inviting ones.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Agreeing a shared, age-right line together","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Saying 'you always ruin these talks'","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Sharing a ready script with them","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Mocking their attempt in front of the child","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"'Even just being calm and askable helps'","trick":false}],"why":"Criticising and mocking are the red flags that push a co-parent out.","relearn":"Criticising or mocking a co-parent pushes them out; agreeing a line, sharing a script and a warm invite bring them in.","persona":"any","source":"spot co-parent push-outs"},
  {"id":"tk-1398","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two scripts that should be reworked, among the calm, age-right ones.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"'That's the proper name, like elbow or knee'","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"'Only dirty-minded kids ask such things'","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"'No judgement, you can always ask me'","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"'You'll learn the hard way, don't ask me'","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"'Thanks for telling me, you're not in trouble'","trick":false}],"why":"The shaming line and the 'learn the hard way' brush-off are the red flags.","relearn":"Shaming and brush-off scripts need reworking; naming plainly, 'no judgement' and 'you're not in trouble' are ready to use.","persona":"any","source":"spot scripts to rework"},
  {"id":"tk-1399","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two responses to 'I don't know' that backfire, among the honest ones.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"'Good question, let's find a reliable answer'","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Making up an answer to seem sure","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"'Give me a day, I'll check and tell you'","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"'Stop bothering me with these questions'","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Looking it up together in a good source","trick":false}],"why":"Inventing an answer and snapping are the red flags to catch.","relearn":"Inventing an answer or snapping backfires; 'let's find out together', buying time honestly and a reliable source work.","persona":"Vikram","source":"spot i-dont-know backfires"},
  {"id":"tk-1400","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"spot","hook":"Spot the two unsafe moves when a worry comes up, among the protective ones.","scene":[{"id":"a","text":"Taking the worry seriously","trick":false},{"id":"b","text":"Brushing it off so you needn't deal with it","trick":true},{"id":"c","text":"Seeking guidance via Be the Safe Adult","trick":false},{"id":"d","text":"Telling the child to keep it quiet","trick":true},{"id":"e","text":"Calling Childline 1098 if a child was hurt","trick":false}],"why":"Brushing the worry off and telling a child to stay quiet are the red flags.","relearn":"Brushing off a worry or silencing a child is unsafe; take it seriously, seek guidance, and call Childline 1098 if a child was hurt.","persona":"Meena","source":"spot unsafe worry moves"},
  {"id":"tk-1401","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","persona":"Divya","source":"ready line in the moment","hook":"At dinner, your son Arnav, 6, asks how the baby will get out of Chachi's tummy.","setup":"Everyone at the table turns to you.","steps":[{"prompt":"Arnav asks: \"Does it just pop out of her belly button?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Uh, why do you want to know? Go ask someone else.\"","then":"Arnav turns to his cousin, who tells him something wild. He looks back at you, unsure."},{"text":"\"Good question. Here's the simple version.\"","then":"Arnav leans in, waiting. Chachi smiles at you across the table.","best":true},{"text":"\"Yes, beta, it comes out of the belly button.\"","then":"Arnav nods, then frowns. \"But her belly button is so tiny.\""},{"text":"\"Eat your food. We don't talk like this at dinner.\"","then":"Arnav pokes at his dal, still glancing at Chachi's tummy."}],"why":"A ready, calm opener buys you a breath and keeps his question welcome."},{"prompt":"Arnav asks: \"So how does the baby really get out?\"","options":[{"text":"\"The doctor takes it out. That's all you need to know.\"","then":"Arnav nods, but his \"how\" is still there."},{"text":"\"A stork brings it to the hospital once it's ready.\"","then":"Arnav believes you, until a friend laughs at him for it."},{"text":"\"Usually out through her vagina. Sometimes doctors help.\"","then":"Arnav thinks. \"Oh. Okay.\" Then he asks if the baby will like him.","best":true},{"text":"\"You'll learn about all that when you're much older.\"","then":"Arnav sighs. \"Everyone says that.\""}],"why":"Simple, true words at his level answer him without any fuss."},{"prompt":"At bedtime, Arnav asks: \"Can I ask you more things like that?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Maybe. But not at the dinner table again, okay?\"","then":"Arnav nods, unsure which questions are allowed where."},{"text":"\"Only if it's important. Some things are private.\"","then":"Arnav looks puzzled, and decides to keep more to himself."},{"text":"\"Better to ask your teacher. She knows more than me.\"","then":"Arnav shrugs, and you've handed your place to someone else."},{"text":"\"Always. No question is silly. Ask me anything.\"","then":"Arnav grins and snuggles down. \"Okay. Tomorrow I have three.\"","best":true}],"why":"Saying no question is silly keeps him coming back with the next one."}],"relearn":"A ready, calm line lets you answer instead of freezing or pushing your child away to ask someone else."},
  {"id":"tk-1402","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"model finding out","hook":"Your son Vihaan, 12, asks if girls have wet dreams too. You honestly don't know.","setup":"He's waiting, half curious, half embarrassed.","steps":[{"prompt":"Vihaan asks: \"Do they? Or is it only boys?\"","options":[{"text":"\"No, only boys get them. Girls have periods instead.\"","then":"Vihaan nods, then frowns. \"My friend said girls can too.\""},{"text":"\"Why do you even want to know about girls' stuff?\"","then":"Vihaan goes red. \"Forget it.\" A minute later, he opens his laptop anyway."},{"text":"\"Honestly, I'm not sure. Let's look it up together.\"","then":"Vihaan pulls up a chair. \"Okay. Where do we even look?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"I'll ask a doctor friend, and tell you some other time.\"","then":"Vihaan nods, but doesn't want to wait, and opens his laptop."}],"why":"Admitting you don't know, and finding out together, models honesty."},{"prompt":"Vihaan turns his laptop to you: \"Which of these sites can we trust?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Whichever has the most views. They must know.\"","then":"Vihaan clicks a video with loud music and very little truth."},{"text":"\"Let's find a proper health source, not someone selling stuff.\"","then":"Vihaan finds a health page. \"It says girls can too. Huh.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"This is taking too long. Let's just go with that one.\"","then":"Vihaan reads the sketchy site, and a myth comes with it."},{"text":"\"You choose one. I really don't know much about these websites.\"","then":"Vihaan picks the flashiest link, and you both take it at its word."}],"why":"Choosing a reliable source together shows him how to find good information."},{"prompt":"Vihaan says: \"That was actually kind of fun. Can we do that again?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Sure, but next time just ask your teacher first.\"","then":"Vihaan shrugs. \"Okay.\" Next time, he doesn't come to you."},{"text":"\"Any time. I don't need to know everything to help.\"","then":"Vihaan grins. \"Cool. I've got another one already.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Let's hope you don't ask me anything that hard again!\"","then":"Vihaan laughs, but files away that hard questions are a burden."},{"text":"\"Maybe. But don't tell anyone we looked that up.\"","then":"Vihaan nods, and learns that these questions are something to hide."}],"why":"Showing you'll learn alongside him keeps him bringing you questions."}],"relearn":"Finding out together models honesty and the skill of seeking good information, unlike bluffing an answer."},
  {"id":"tk-1403","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","persona":"Divya","source":"open repair","hook":"Yesterday your daughter Anvi, 5, said 'vagina' at lunch, and you told her it's a dirty word.","setup":"Today she's in the bath, singing.","steps":[{"prompt":"Anvi whispers: \"Is vagina a bad word? You said it was.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Let's just forget all about yesterday, okay, beta?\"","then":"Anvi nods, still unsure whether the word is bad."},{"text":"\"Yes. Good girls don't say words like that out loud.\"","then":"Anvi goes quiet, and stops singing."},{"text":"\"No. I was wrong yesterday. It's the proper name. Sorry.\"","then":"Anvi splashes happily, and starts singing again.","best":true},{"text":"\"It's not bad exactly, but just say 'down there' instead.\"","then":"Anvi nods, but she looks puzzled."}],"why":"Owning the mistake and giving the proper name repairs it, and keeps her safer."},{"prompt":"Anvi asks: \"My teacher uses the proper names. Why do we need them?\"","options":[{"text":"\"So you can tell me clearly if anything feels wrong.\"","then":"Anvi nods. \"And you won't be cross?\" You promise you won't.","best":true},{"text":"\"Because your teacher says so, and that's that.\"","then":"Anvi shrugs, and the reason never lands."},{"text":"\"You don't, really. Our funny nicknames are cuter.\"","then":"Anvi giggles, then frowns. \"But my teacher says vagina.\""},{"text":"\"So you sound grown-up and nobody laughs at you.\"","then":"Anvi nods, pleased, but misses why it really matters."}],"why":"Knowing correct names helps a child tell clearly, which keeps her safer."},{"prompt":"At lunch the next day, Anvi says it again, and Dadi gasps: \"Chhi! What is this child saying?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Sorry about that. She won't say it again. I promise.\"","then":"Anvi's face falls. She hears that the word is shameful after all."},{"text":"\"Anvi, beta, we don't say that word at the table.\"","then":"Anvi goes quiet, confused about which rule is true."},{"text":"\"Please don't gasp at my child. You're scaring her.\"","then":"Dadi takes offence, and lunch turns tense."},{"text":"\"It's the proper name. We teach it to keep her safe.\"","then":"Dadi blinks. \"To keep her safe?\" she asks, and listens.","best":true}],"why":"Backing her calmly, and saying why, keeps the correct names in place."}],"relearn":"Openly repairing a fumbled answer reopens the door and shows your child mistakes can be fixed."},
  {"id":"tk-1404","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","persona":"Meena","source":"respond to a disclosure","hook":"At bedtime, your daughter Lakshmi, 6, says her tuition uncle touches her in a way she doesn't like.","setup":"She says he calls it their secret.","steps":[{"prompt":"Lakshmi whispers: \"Am I in trouble for telling?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Are you sure? Don't make up stories about people.\"","then":"Lakshmi's eyes fill. \"I'm not lying,\" she whispers, and pulls the sheet up."},{"text":"\"No. I'm glad you told me. This is not your fault.\"","then":"Lakshmi relaxes a little. \"I didn't like it,\" she says quietly.","best":true},{"text":"\"Show me exactly where he touched you, and how.\"","then":"Lakshmi freezes, and says \"I don't know\" to every question."},{"text":"\"What? I'm going straight to his house right now!\"","then":"Lakshmi starts to cry, frightened that she's caused something terrible."}],"why":"Believing her calmly, and saying it's not her fault, is what keeps a child telling."},{"prompt":"Lakshmi asks: \"Do I have to go to tuition tomorrow?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Yes, but sit far away from him, and you'll be fine.\"","then":"Lakshmi nods, but her tummy hurts all the next morning."},{"text":"\"Let's see. Maybe he didn't mean anything by it.\"","then":"Lakshmi goes silent, unsure if telling you changed anything."},{"text":"\"No. You don't have to go. I'll keep you safe.\"","then":"Lakshmi hugs you tight. \"Okay,\" she whispers, and closes her eyes.","best":true},{"text":"\"Only if I sit right outside the door the whole time.\"","then":"Lakshmi nods, but she's scared to walk past him."}],"why":"Keeping her away from him at once keeps her safe, and shows that telling works."},{"prompt":"Later, your partner says quietly: \"Let's keep this in the family. People will talk.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Her safety comes first. I'm calling Childline 1098 tonight.\"","then":"Your partner hesitates, then nods. The counsellor explains the next steps.","best":true},{"text":"\"You're right. We'll just quietly change her tuition.\"","then":"The tuition uncle carries on teaching other children, and no one knows."},{"text":"\"Then let's go and sort him out ourselves, tonight.\"","then":"The confrontation turns ugly, and he loudly denies everything."},{"text":"\"Let's just wait a few days and see if she mentions it again.\"","then":"Lakshmi doesn't mention it again. She's decided telling doesn't help."}],"why":"Getting expert help fast protects Lakshmi, and other children at that tuition too."},{"prompt":"Next day, Dadi asks: \"Are you sure the child isn't imagining things?\"","options":[{"text":"\"I'm not sure any more. Maybe she got it a bit wrong.\"","then":"Lakshmi, at the door, hears you doubt her."},{"text":"\"I believe her. She needs all of us to believe her.\"","then":"Dadi is quiet, then nods. \"Then we protect her,\" she says.","best":true},{"text":"\"Let's ask Lakshmi to tell you everything, so you can judge.\"","then":"Lakshmi has to tell it all again, and cries all evening."},{"text":"\"How dare you doubt her! Just stay out of this, please.\"","then":"Dadi walks out, hurt, and the family splits into sides."}],"why":"Standing calmly in your belief protects Lakshmi and brings the family with you."},{"prompt":"A week later, Lakshmi says: \"I still feel scared sometimes.\"","options":[{"text":"\"There's nothing to be scared of any more. Forget it.\"","then":"Lakshmi nods, and keeps the fear to herself."},{"text":"\"You're a big girl. Big girls don't stay scared.\"","then":"Lakshmi tries to be brave, and stops telling you when she's scared."},{"text":"\"Let's not talk about all that, beta. It only makes you sad.\"","then":"Lakshmi goes quiet, and the feelings stay bottled up."},{"text":"\"That's okay. You're safe, and we'll find someone to help.\"","then":"Lakshmi holds your hand a little tighter. You book a counsellor that week.","best":true}],"why":"Her feelings are okay, and help to heal is part of keeping her safe."}],"relearn":"Believing a child, reassuring them and getting the right help keeps them talking; doubting them silences future disclosures."},
  {"id":"tk-1405","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"warm co-parent invite","hook":"Your partner Kavita wants to leave all 'the talks' with your daughter Myra, 9, to you.","setup":"She says it after Myra's asleep.","steps":[{"prompt":"Kavita says: \"My parents never said a word to me, and I turned out fine.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Fine, sit it out. I'll carry all of this on my own.\"","then":"Kavita shrugs, relieved, and the load lands on you alone."},{"text":"\"You did. But I'd love Myra to have both of us to ask.\"","then":"Kavita pauses. \"Both of us,\" she repeats. \"I wouldn't know where to start.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Your parents got it wrong, and honestly, you're doing the same.\"","then":"Kavita's face tightens. \"Thanks a lot,\" she says, and turns away."},{"text":"\"Did you, though? You never talk about any of it.\"","then":"Kavita goes quiet, stung, and changes the subject."}],"why":"Honouring her story while inviting her in makes room for her to join."},{"prompt":"Later, Kavita admits: \"What if Myra asks me something and I get it wrong?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Then just send her to me, and I'll fix it for you.\"","then":"Kavita nods, relieved, and plans to send Myra to you if it ever comes up."},{"text":"\"You don't have to be perfect. Just calm and askable.\"","then":"Kavita exhales. \"Calm and askable. That I can do.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"You'll be fine. Honestly, it's not a big deal at all.\"","then":"Kavita isn't convinced, and still dreads the first question."},{"text":"\"Then read up on everything before she asks you anything.\"","then":"Kavita looks overwhelmed, and puts it off for months."}],"why":"Lowering the bar to calm and askable makes it feel possible for her."},{"prompt":"Weeks later, Kavita says: \"Myra asked me about periods today. I actually answered.\"","options":[{"text":"\"What exactly did you say? I hope you got it right.\"","then":"Kavita's smile fades. \"I thought I did,\" she says quietly."},{"text":"\"Good. Then you can take the next few as well.\"","then":"Kavita laughs, a little wary. \"Let's not rush it.\""},{"text":"\"That's wonderful. Now she has two of us she trusts.\"","then":"Kavita smiles. \"It felt good, actually. She hugged me after.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Really? I thought you'd leave that one to me.\"","then":"Kavita shrugs, deflated by the surprise in your voice."}],"why":"Celebrating her step shows her how much a second trusted door matters."}],"relearn":"Inviting a co-parent to simply be calm and askable shares the load and gives a child a second trusted door."},
  {"id":"tk-1406","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"hold the line kindly","hook":"Your daughter Fatima, 4, won't hug Chachi, and says her body belongs to her.","setup":"Chachi turns to you, offended.","steps":[{"prompt":"Chachi says: \"You're spoiling her with all this body talk. It's rude.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Sorry, Chachi. Fatima, go and give her a hug now.\"","then":"Fatima hugs Chachi stiffly, and learns her no doesn't count."},{"text":"\"You're right. I'll stop confusing her with all that.\"","then":"Chachi nods, satisfied. Fatima looks at you, confused."},{"text":"\"She can wave instead. We teach this to keep her safe.\"","then":"Fatima waves happily. Chachi sniffs, but waves back.","best":true},{"text":"\"It's her body. She doesn't owe anyone a hug. Accept it.\"","then":"Chachi's face reddens, and the room goes quiet."}],"why":"Offering a wave keeps Fatima's choice and Chachi's dignity, and names why it matters."},{"prompt":"Later, Chachi says: \"In our family, children show respect by hugging elders.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Fine, Fatima. Just this once, then, for the family's sake.\"","then":"Fatima is steered into a hug, and her face crumples."},{"text":"\"Respect matters to us too. She can show it another way.\"","then":"Chachi thinks. \"Another way. Hm. As long as she greets me.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Those old customs don't matter any more, Chachi.\"","then":"Chachi bristles. \"So our ways are nothing now?\""},{"text":"\"Let's not argue about it. It's just a small thing.\"","then":"Chachi shrugs, and brings it up again at the next visit."}],"why":"Joining her value of respect with Fatima's choice turns a clash into agreement."},{"prompt":"Chachi asks: \"And what else are you teaching a four-year-old?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Nothing much, really. Just a few little things here and there.\"","then":"Chachi nods, and assumes the talks will fade."},{"text":"\"That's really our business, Chachi, not yours.\"","then":"Chachi stiffens, and leaves early."},{"text":"\"Proper names, and to tell us if anything feels wrong.\"","then":"Chachi pauses. \"So she can tell you,\" she says slowly. \"Hm.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"All sorts. Should I list the body parts for you?\"","then":"Chachi goes red, and the whole room goes silent."}],"why":"Naming the simple safety rules openly shows the talks are age-right, not shocking."},{"prompt":"Months later, Chachi laughs: \"Fatima scolded me for tickling her after she said stop!\"","options":[{"text":"\"Sorry about that! She's getting a bit too cheeky.\"","then":"Chachi laughs, and next time she keeps tickling after the stop."},{"text":"\"Ha! Well, it was only tickling. She'll get over it.\"","then":"Chachi shrugs, and Fatima's stop starts to mean less."},{"text":"\"See? And you were the one who called it spoiling.\"","then":"Chachi's smile fades. \"No need to rub it in,\" she says."},{"text":"\"Thank you for stopping. That shows her stop counts.\"","then":"Chachi smiles. \"She's a strong one. I stopped straight away.\"","best":true}],"why":"Thanking an adult for respecting a child's no makes stop mean stop in your family."}],"relearn":"Kindly holding your line keeps your child's safety facts in place, rather than apologising away the protection they give."},
  {"id":"tk-1407","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","persona":"Vikram","source":"point and stay in","hook":"Your son Jai, 14, asks where he can read honest stuff about bodies and relationships.","setup":"He asks from the doorway, trying to sound casual.","steps":[{"prompt":"Jai says: \"Everything online is either weird or a lecture.\"","options":[{"text":"\"Just search online yourself. I'd rather not be part of this.\"","then":"Jai nods, and ends up on a forum full of myths."},{"text":"\"You really don't need to be reading about all that yet.\"","then":"Jai rolls his eyes, and searches anyway on his phone."},{"text":"\"Here, have my old biology textbook. It's all in there.\"","then":"Jai flips through diagrams from decades ago, and gives up."},{"text":"\"I'll find a reliable one, and read it with you if you like.\"","then":"Jai shrugs. \"Maybe. If it's not cringe.\" He doesn't say no.","best":true}],"why":"A trusted source plus your offer keeps you involved without a lecture."},{"prompt":"A few days later, Jai asks: \"I read that it's normal to not feel ready for a relationship. True?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Totally true. There's no timeline. What made you ask?\"","then":"Jai relaxes. \"My friends make it sound like I'm late,\" he says.","best":true},{"text":"\"Of course. You're much too young for all that anyway.\"","then":"Jai shrugs, and the chance to talk passes."},{"text":"\"Hmm. Most boys your age seem pretty ready, though.\"","then":"Jai's face falls, and he feels more behind than ever."},{"text":"\"Why do you ask? Is something going on with a girl?\"","then":"Jai goes red. \"No. Forget it.\""}],"why":"Confirming the fact and asking gently opens up the real worry behind his question."},{"prompt":"A week later, Jai asks: \"Can you send me a couple of good links? Ones you trust?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Sure, but you've read enough for now, don't you think?\"","then":"Jai hesitates. \"Never mind,\" he says."},{"text":"\"Sure. Just don't tell your friends that I helped you.\"","then":"Jai nods, and senses these talks are something to hide."},{"text":"\"Sure. And ask me about anything on there, any time.\"","then":"Jai grins. \"Cool. Thanks.\" Later, he sends you a question.","best":true},{"text":"\"Sure. And I'll check your history to see what you read.\"","then":"Jai's smile vanishes, and he switches to private browsing."}],"why":"Staying available as he reads keeps you part of his learning."}],"relearn":"Pointing a teen to a reliable source and offering to read along keeps you involved, unlike sending them off to a blind search."},
  {"id":"tk-1408","cat":"tools-and-help","type":"role-play","persona":"any","source":"easy car moment","hook":"You're on a long drive to Nani's with your daughter Saanvi, 10.","setup":"She's gazing out of the window, humming.","steps":[{"prompt":"Saanvi says: \"This drive is so boring. Talk to me about something.\"","options":[{"text":"\"At home, we'll sit down for a proper talk about growing up.\"","then":"Saanvi groans. \"A sit-down talk? What did I do?\""},{"text":"\"Okay. Anything about growing up you've been wondering about?\"","then":"Saanvi thinks. \"Actually, why do some girls in my class wear a bra already?\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Let's play antakshari instead. Something fun for a change.\"","then":"You sing for an hour. The moment slides past."},{"text":"\"You're ten now. It's time we talked about periods properly.\"","then":"Saanvi stiffens. \"Ugh. Do we have to?\" She puts her earphones in."}],"why":"A light, open question in a relaxed moment lets her lead with what's really on her mind."},{"prompt":"A little later, Saanvi asks: \"When will my body start changing, anyway?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Not for years and years yet, so don't worry about it now.\"","then":"Saanvi frowns. \"But Tanya's already started,\" she says, confused."},{"text":"\"When you become a woman. That's all you need to know.\"","then":"Saanvi rolls her eyes. \"That's not an answer.\""},{"text":"\"Anytime from about eight to thirteen. Everyone's different.\"","then":"Saanvi nods. \"So some of my friends are just early. Okay.\"","best":true},{"text":"\"Why? Has something started already? You can tell me.\"","then":"Saanvi shrinks. \"No! I was just asking.\""}],"why":"A simple, true answer makes the changes feel expected, not frightening."},{"prompt":"As you pull up at Nani's, Saanvi asks: \"Can I ask you more stuff on the way back?\"","options":[{"text":"\"Sure, but no more awkward stuff in front of Nani.\"","then":"Saanvi nods, and senses that some questions are embarrassing."},{"text":"\"Maybe. I think we've covered plenty for one day.\"","then":"Saanvi shrugs. The drive home is quiet."},{"text":"\"Only if you promise not to tell your friends.\"","then":"Saanvi looks puzzled, and wonders what's secret about it."},{"text":"\"Yes. I love these chats. Save up your questions.\"","then":"Saanvi grins. \"I've already got one,\" she says, and hops out.","best":true}],"why":"Welcoming more chats turns one easy moment into a habit."}],"relearn":"A relaxed side-by-side opening invites a child to share, where a formal, tense sit-down makes them clam up."},
];

